export const CURATED: Readonly<Record<string, CuratedQ[][]>> = {"BUDDHISM":[[{"id":"BUDDHISM-s00-01","day":6,"d":2,"q":"In Theravada countries such as Sri Lanka, Thailand and Myanmar, which events in the Buddha's life does the full moon of Vesak commemorate?","o":["his birth, his awakening and his passing away","his birth, his first sermon and his passing away","his leaving home, his awakening and his first sermon","his awakening, his first sermon and his passing away"],"a":0,"es":{"q":"En los países theravada como Sri Lanka, Tailandia y Myanmar, ¿qué hechos de la vida del Buda conmemora la luna llena de Vesak?","o":["su nacimiento, su despertar y su partida final","su nacimiento, su primer sermón y su partida final","su salida del hogar, su despertar y su primer sermón","su despertar, su primer sermón y su partida final"]}},{"id":"BUDDHISM-s00-02","day":9,"d":2,"q":"In the Buddha's first sermon, the Dhammacakkappavattana Sutta, what does the second noble truth name as the origin of dukkha (suffering, unsatisfactoriness)?","o":["past deeds ripening from earlier lives","craving, or tanha, literally thirst","the body and its contact with the world","doubt about the Buddha and his teaching"],"a":1,"es":{"q":"En el primer sermón del Buda, el Dhammacakkappavattana Sutta, ¿qué nombra la segunda noble verdad como el origen de dukkha (sufrimiento, insatisfacción)?","o":["actos pasados que maduran desde vidas anteriores","el anhelo, o tanha, literalmente sed","el cuerpo y su contacto con el mundo","la duda sobre el Buda y su enseñanza"]}},{"id":"BUDDHISM-s00-03","day":7,"d":3,"q":"In the Milindapanha (The Questions of King Milinda), the monk Nagasena compares rebirth to lighting one lamp from another. What point does the image make about the one who is reborn?","o":["an unchanging soul passes from one body to the next","the new life has no connection to the one before","it is neither the same person nor a different one","the body is reborn while the mind fades away"],"a":2,"es":{"q":"En el Milindapanha (Las preguntas del rey Milinda), el monje Nagasena compara el renacimiento con encender una lámpara con otra. ¿Qué muestra esa imagen sobre quien renace?","o":["un alma inmutable pasa de un cuerpo al siguiente","la nueva vida no tiene relación con la anterior","no es la misma persona ni tampoco una distinta","el cuerpo renace mientras la mente se apaga"]}},{"id":"BUDDHISM-s00-04","day":10,"d":3,"q":"In the Aggivacchagotta Sutta (Majjhima Nikaya 72), the Buddha asks the wanderer Vacchagotta which direction a fire went when it went out. What is he showing about where a Tathagata, a fully awakened one, goes after death?","o":["he is reborn in the highest of the heaven realms","he simply ceases to exist, as fire turns to nothing","he is reborn once more to teach in a later age","the question of where he goes does not apply"],"a":3,"es":{"q":"En el Aggivacchagotta Sutta (Majjhima Nikaya 72), el Buda le pregunta al asceta errante Vacchagotta en qué dirección se fue un fuego cuando se apagó. ¿Qué muestra sobre adónde va un Tathagata, alguien plenamente despierto, después de la muerte?","o":["renace en el más alto de los reinos celestiales","simplemente deja de existir, como el fuego en la nada","renace una vez más para enseñar en otra era","la pregunta de adónde va no se aplica a su caso"]}},{"id":"BUDDHISM-s00-05","day":20,"d":2,"q":"In the Sona Sutta (Anguttara Nikaya 6.55), the Buddha asks the monk Sona, once a skilled lute player, how his lute sounded with strings too tight or too loose. What is the Buddha teaching him?","o":["to balance his effort, neither straining nor slack","to leave the monks and go back to his music","to push harder, since slack effort is the real danger","to drop his other practices and keep only one"],"a":0,"es":{"q":"En el Sona Sutta (Anguttara Nikaya 6.55), el Buda le pregunta al monje Sona, que antes tocaba muy bien el laúd, cómo sonaba su laúd con las cuerdas demasiado tensas o demasiado flojas. ¿Qué le está enseñando el Buda?","o":["a equilibrar su esfuerzo, ni tenso ni flojo","a dejar a los monjes y volver a su música","a esforzarse más, pues el esfuerzo flojo es el peligro","a dejar sus otras prácticas y quedarse con una"]}},{"id":"BUDDHISM-s00-06","day":12,"d":2,"q":"Under the five precepts (pañcasīla) recited by lay Buddhists, a man takes a coworker's lunch from the office fridge without asking. Which of the five training rules does this go against?","o":["refraining from speaking what is false","refraining from harming living beings","refraining from taking what is not given","refraining from drink that clouds the mind"],"a":2,"es":{"q":"Según los cinco preceptos (pañcasīla) que recitan los budistas laicos, un hombre toma el almuerzo de un compañero del refrigerador de la oficina sin preguntar. ¿Contra cuál de las cinco reglas de entrenamiento va esto?","o":["abstenerse de decir lo que es falso","abstenerse de dañar a los seres vivos","abstenerse de tomar lo que no ha sido dado","abstenerse de bebidas que nublan la mente"]}}],[{"id":"BUDDHISM-s01-01","day":53,"d":2,"q":"in the bhumisparsha mudra, the Buddha's right hand reaching down to touch the ground, whom does he call on to witness his right to the seat under the bodhi tree when Mara challenges him?","o":["the earth he sat upon","the god Brahma Sahampati","his five old companions","the serpent king Mucalinda"],"a":0,"es":{"q":"en la bhumisparsha mudra, la mano derecha del Buda que baja a tocar el suelo, ¿a quién llama como testigo de su derecho al asiento bajo el árbol bodhi cuando Mara lo desafía?","o":["la tierra sobre la que se sentaba","el dios Brahma Sahampati","sus cinco antiguos compañeros","el rey serpiente Mucalinda"]}},{"id":"BUDDHISM-s01-02","day":42,"d":3,"q":"in the Ariyapariyesana Sutta (MN 26), the future Buddha masters the meditative states taught by Alara Kalama and Uddaka Ramaputta, then leaves both teachers. why does he leave?","o":["they refused to teach him the highest state they knew","he never managed to reach the states they taught him","their states did not lead to the end of suffering","they sent him away for questioning their teaching"],"a":2,"es":{"q":"en el Ariyapariyesana Sutta (MN 26), el futuro Buda domina los estados meditativos que enseñan Alara Kalama y Uddaka Ramaputta, y luego deja a ambos maestros. ¿por qué se va?","o":["se negaron a enseñarle el estado más alto que conocían","nunca logró alcanzar los estados que ellos le enseñaban","esos estados no llevaban al fin del sufrimiento","lo echaron por cuestionar lo que ellos enseñaban"]}},{"id":"BUDDHISM-s01-03","day":62,"d":2,"q":"in the Buddha's first sermon, the Dhammacakkappavattana Sutta, the middle way is the path between which two extremes?","o":["worship of the many gods and denial of all gods","devotion to sense pleasures and to self-torment","life as a wandering monk and life as a householder","nonstop study of texts and nonstop meditation"],"a":1,"es":{"q":"en el primer sermón del Buda, el Dhammacakkappavattana Sutta, el camino medio es el camino entre ¿qué dos extremos?","o":["el culto a muchos dioses y la negación de todo dios","la entrega a los placeres y el tormento de uno mismo","la vida de monje errante y la vida de jefe de hogar","estudiar textos sin parar y meditar sin parar"]}},{"id":"BUDDHISM-s01-04","day":75,"d":1,"q":"in the story of Kisa Gotami, who brought her dead son to the Buddha asking for medicine, what did the Buddha ask her to fetch from the city?","o":["water from a well that had never once run dry","a healing herb from a garden in the high mountains","a lamp lit in a house where no one had ever lied","a mustard seed from a house where no one had died"],"a":3,"es":{"q":"en el relato de Kisa Gotami, que llevó a su hijo muerto ante el Buda pidiéndole una medicina, ¿qué le pidió el Buda que trajera de la ciudad?","o":["agua de un pozo que nunca se hubiera secado","una hierba curativa de un jardín en lo alto de los montes","una lámpara de una casa donde nadie hubiera mentido","un grano de mostaza de una casa donde nadie hubiera muerto"]}},{"id":"BUDDHISM-s01-05","day":79,"d":3,"q":"in the Mahaparinibbana Sutta (DN 16), Ananda hopes the aging Buddha will leave instructions for the community. what does the Buddha tell the monks to take as their refuge?","o":["themselves and the dhamma, with no other refuge","Sariputta, named as the next leader of the order","Ananda, chosen to lead the order after him","the royal house of Magadha, as its protector"],"a":0,"es":{"q":"en el Mahaparinibbana Sutta (DN 16), Ananda espera que el Buda, ya anciano, deje instrucciones para la comunidad. ¿qué les dice el Buda a los monjes que tomen como refugio?","o":["a sí mismos y al dhamma, sin ningún otro refugio","a Sariputta, nombrado próximo líder de la orden","a Ananda, elegido para guiar la orden después de él","a la casa real de Magadha, como su protectora"]}},{"id":"BUDDHISM-s01-06","day":62,"d":3,"q":"a woman notices that her constant restlessness is fed by always wanting more: the next purchase, the next bit of praise. which of the four noble truths names what she has seen about where that restlessness comes from?","o":["the first truth: dukkha, that life is unsatisfactory","the second truth: its cause is craving, tanha","the third truth: suffering can come to an end","the fourth truth: the eightfold path to its end"],"a":1,"es":{"q":"una mujer nota que su inquietud constante se alimenta de querer siempre más: la próxima compra, el próximo elogio. ¿cuál de las cuatro nobles verdades nombra lo que ella vio sobre el origen de esa inquietud?","o":["la primera verdad: dukkha, la vida es insatisfactoria","la segunda verdad: su causa es el ansia, tanha","la tercera verdad: el sufrimiento puede terminar","la cuarta verdad: el óctuple sendero hacia su fin"]}}],[{"id":"BUDDHISM-s02-01","day":105,"d":2,"q":"in the Karaniya Metta Sutta, the Theravada discourse on loving-kindness, what image shows the boundless heart one should cultivate toward all beings?","o":["a king who shares his whole treasury with his people","a mother who protects her only child with her life","a farmer who waters every field in the valley alike","a lamp that lights every room of a great house"],"a":1,"es":{"q":"en el Karaniya Metta Sutta, el discurso theravada sobre la bondad amorosa, ¿qué imagen muestra el corazón sin límites que hay que cultivar hacia todos los seres?","o":["un rey que reparte todo su tesoro entre su pueblo","una madre que protege con su vida a su único hijo","un campesino que riega igual cada campo del valle","una lámpara que ilumina cada cuarto de una gran casa"]}},{"id":"BUDDHISM-s02-02","day":150,"d":3,"q":"Magha Puja, kept on the full moon of February or March in Thailand, Laos and Cambodia, remembers which event in the Theravada tradition?","o":["the Buddha's first sermon to the five ascetics at the Deer Park","the Buddha's birth, awakening and final passing, on one full moon","the Buddha's return to earth after teaching his mother in heaven","1,250 awakened monks gathering before the Buddha, uncalled"],"a":3,"es":{"q":"Magha Puja, que se celebra en la luna llena de febrero o marzo en Tailandia, Laos y Camboya, ¿qué acontecimiento recuerda en la tradición theravada?","o":["el primer sermón del Buda a los cinco ascetas en el Parque de los Ciervos","el nacimiento, el despertar y la muerte final del Buda, en una luna llena","el regreso del Buda a la tierra tras enseñar a su madre en el cielo","1.250 monjes despiertos que se reunieron ante el Buda sin ser llamados"]}},{"id":"BUDDHISM-s02-03","day":115,"d":3,"q":"in the Samyutta Nikaya (SN 46.55), the Buddha compares the five hindrances to a bowl of water that is dyed, boiling, mossy, wind-stirred or muddy. what does the simile teach?","o":["while a hindrance is present, the mind can't see clearly","the hindrances are the mind's true nature and stay for good","the hindrances come from impure food eaten before sitting","the mind must be emptied of all thought before it can sit"],"a":0,"es":{"q":"en el Samyutta Nikaya (SN 46.55), el Buda compara los cinco obstáculos con un cuenco de agua teñida, hirviendo, con musgo, agitada por el viento o turbia. ¿qué enseña el símil?","o":["mientras hay un obstáculo, la mente no puede ver con claridad","los obstáculos son la naturaleza verdadera de la mente y se quedan","los obstáculos vienen de comida impura tomada antes de sentarse","hay que vaciar la mente de todo pensamiento antes de sentarse"]}},{"id":"BUDDHISM-s02-04","day":136,"d":3,"q":"in the story of the poor woman's lamp, kept in the Sutra of the Wise and the Foolish (a story collection in the Chinese and Tibetan canons), her one small lamp burns on after the king's many lamps go out. what is the story teaching?","o":["the merit of a gift grows with how much is given","offerings of light are the highest form of giving","a small, wholehearted gift can outshine a great show","kings gain the most merit because they can give the most"],"a":2,"es":{"q":"en el relato de la lámpara de la mujer pobre, recogido en el Sutra del Sabio y el Necio (una colección de relatos de los cánones chino y tibetano), su única lamparita sigue ardiendo cuando las muchas lámparas del rey se apagan. ¿qué enseña el relato?","o":["el mérito de un regalo crece con la cantidad que se da","las ofrendas de luz son la forma más alta de dar","un regalo pequeño y sincero puede superar a un gran lujo","los reyes ganan más mérito porque pueden dar más"]}},{"id":"BUDDHISM-s02-05","day":143,"d":3,"q":"at the end of a Theravada ceremony, lay people slowly pour water into a bowl while the monks chant (in Thailand, kruat nam). what does the pouring express?","o":["washing away the bad karma of the givers' past deeds","sharing the merit just made with the dead and all beings","cleansing the monks' bowls after the morning alms meal","offering cool water to the Buddha image in the heat"],"a":1,"es":{"q":"al final de una ceremonia theravada, los laicos vierten agua despacio en un cuenco mientras los monjes cantan (en Tailandia, kruat nam). ¿qué expresa ese gesto?","o":["lavar el mal karma de las acciones pasadas de los donantes","compartir el mérito recién hecho con los muertos y todos los seres","limpiar los cuencos de los monjes tras la comida de la ronda","ofrecer agua fresca a la imagen del Buda por el calor"]}},{"id":"BUDDHISM-s02-06","day":133,"d":3,"q":"a woman offers food to monks, glad as she prepares it and bright-hearted as she gives it, but for weeks afterward she resents what it cost. by the Buddha's account of Nandamata's gift (AN 6.37), which factor of the giver is missing?","o":["being glad before the giving","being bright-hearted while giving","receivers free of greed and hate","being uplifted after the giving"],"a":3,"es":{"q":"una mujer ofrece comida a los monjes, alegre mientras la prepara y con el corazón luminoso al darla, pero durante semanas resiente lo que le costó. según lo que dice el Buda del regalo de Nandamata (AN 6.37), ¿qué factor del donante falta?","o":["estar alegre antes de dar","tener el corazón luminoso al dar","receptores libres de codicia y odio","sentirse elevado después de dar"]}}],[{"id":"BUDDHISM-s03-01","day":159,"d":2,"q":"Dhammapada verse 5 calls it \"an eternal law\": hatred never ceases by hatred in this world. by what does hatred cease, according to the verse?","o":["by a hatred repaid in kind","by non-hatred, that is, by love","by a fair and just punishment","by the slow passing of the years"],"a":1,"es":{"q":"el verso 5 del Dhammapada lo llama \"una ley eterna\": el odio nunca cesa con odio en este mundo. según el verso, ¿con qué cesa el odio?","o":["con un odio devuelto igual","con el no-odio, es decir, con amor","con un castigo justo y merecido","con el paso lento y largo de los años"]}},{"id":"BUDDHISM-s03-02","day":210,"d":2,"q":"Dhammapada 277–279 say that one who sees three things with wisdom turns away from suffering. which three marks of existence do these verses name?","o":["greed, hatred and delusion","virtue, concentration and wisdom","impermanence, suffering and not-self","the Buddha, the dhamma and the sangha"],"a":2,"es":{"q":"los versos 277–279 del Dhammapada dicen que quien ve tres cosas con sabiduría se aparta del sufrimiento. ¿qué tres marcas de la existencia nombran estos versos?","o":["la codicia, el odio y la ignorancia","la virtud, la concentración y la sabiduría","la impermanencia, el sufrimiento y el no-yo","el Buda, el dharma y la sangha"]}},{"id":"BUDDHISM-s03-03","day":158,"d":3,"q":"the Dhammapada opens: \"mind goes before all things\" (manopubbangama); pain follows an evil thought as the wheel follows the ox, and happiness follows a pure one like a shadow. what are verses 1–2 teaching?","o":["the intention behind words and deeds shapes what follows from them","deeds alone matter, and the thoughts behind them make no difference","a person's lot is fixed by the deeds of earlier lives alone","thinking pleasant thoughts brings good luck, whatever one does"],"a":0,"es":{"q":"el Dhammapada comienza: \"la mente precede a todas las cosas\" (manopubbangama); el dolor sigue a un pensamiento malo como la rueda sigue al buey, y la felicidad sigue a uno puro como una sombra. ¿qué enseñan los versos 1–2?","o":["la intención detrás de palabras y actos moldea lo que viene después","importan los actos, y los pensamientos detrás no cambian nada","la suerte de una persona la fijan solo los actos de vidas pasadas","pensar cosas agradables trae buena suerte, sin importar lo que hagas"]}},{"id":"BUDDHISM-s03-04","day":172,"d":3,"q":"Dhammapada 64 says a fool may wait on a wise person all his life and still not know the dhamma, as a spoon never tastes the soup. what is the image teaching?","o":["fools should keep away from wise teachers so as not to waste their own time","the wise must patiently spoon-feed the teaching to those who are foolish","being near wisdom does not make one wise without one's own understanding","the dhamma passes to a disciple simply by living close to a wise teacher"],"a":2,"es":{"q":"el verso 64 del Dhammapada dice que un necio puede servir a un sabio toda su vida y aun así no conocer el dharma, como la cuchara nunca prueba la sopa. ¿qué enseña la imagen?","o":["los necios deben alejarse de los sabios para no perder su tiempo con ellos","el sabio debe darle la enseñanza en la boca, con paciencia, al necio","estar cerca de la sabiduría no hace sabio a nadie sin su propia comprensión","el dharma pasa al discípulo con solo vivir cerca de un maestro sabio"]}},{"id":"BUDDHISM-s03-05","day":190,"d":3,"q":"Dhammapada 165 says: \"by oneself is evil done; by oneself is one purified.\" what does the verse go on to say about purity?","o":["purity and impurity depend on oneself; no one purifies another","a teacher's blessing can wash away the evil a student has done","the gods will purify those who offer them all the proper sacrifices","bathing in a sacred river cleanses a person of evil deeds"],"a":0,"es":{"q":"el verso 165 del Dhammapada dice: \"por uno mismo se hace el mal; por uno mismo se purifica uno\". ¿qué dice después el verso sobre la pureza?","o":["la pureza y la impureza dependen de uno; nadie purifica a otro","la bendición de un maestro puede borrar el mal que hizo un alumno","los dioses purifican a quienes les ofrecen los sacrificios debidos","bañarse en un río sagrado limpia a la persona de sus malos actos"]}},{"id":"BUDDHISM-s03-06","day":202,"d":3,"q":"Dhammapada 223 names four ways to overcome what opposes us: anger by non-anger, evil by good, and two more. by its teaching, how should someone overcome a stingy neighbor?","o":["by refusing to share with him in turn","by speaking nothing but the truth to him","by staying silent as a broken gong","by being generous and giving to him"],"a":3,"es":{"q":"el verso 223 del Dhammapada nombra cuatro maneras de vencer lo que se nos opone: la ira con la no-ira, el mal con el bien, y dos más. según su enseñanza, ¿cómo se vence a un vecino tacaño?","o":["negándose también a compartir con él","diciéndole nada más que la verdad","callando como un gong roto","siendo generoso y dándole a él"]}}],[{"id":"BUDDHISM-s04-01","day":234,"d":2,"q":"Buddhaghosa's Visuddhimagga (the Theravada \"Path of Purification\") gives loving-kindness (metta) a \"near enemy\" that can pass for it and a \"far enemy\" that is its plain opposite. what is its near enemy?","o":["envy at another person's good luck","cruelty toward someone who suffers","greed, a clinging kind of affection","ill will, wishing that someone suffer"],"a":2,"es":{"q":"el Visuddhimagga de Buddhaghosa (el \"Camino de la Purificación\" theravada) le da a la bondad amorosa (metta) un \"enemigo cercano\" que puede hacerse pasar por ella y un \"enemigo lejano\" que es su opuesto claro. ¿cuál es su enemigo cercano?","o":["la envidia ante la buena suerte ajena","la crueldad hacia alguien que sufre","la codicia, un afecto que se aferra","la malevolencia, desear que alguien sufra"]}},{"id":"BUDDHISM-s04-02","day":249,"d":3,"q":"in the Satipatthana Sutta (Majjhima Nikaya 10), the Buddha compares someone mindful of breathing to a skilled turner working at a lathe. what does the comparison illustrate?","o":["knowing each breath as long or short, as it happens","lengthening each breath, as a turner lengthens a pull","counting the breaths in tens, then starting over again","turning the attention from the breath toward a word"],"a":0,"es":{"q":"en el Satipatthana Sutta (Majjhima Nikaya 10), el Buda compara a quien está atento a la respiración con un tornero hábil que trabaja en su torno. ¿qué ilustra la comparación?","o":["conocer cada respiración como larga o corta, tal como ocurre","alargar cada respiración, como el tornero alarga su tirón","contar las respiraciones de diez en diez y empezar de nuevo","desviar la atención de la respiración hacia una palabra"]}},{"id":"BUDDHISM-s04-03","day":257,"d":3,"q":"in the Sallatha (\"Arrow\") Sutta, Samyutta Nikaya 36.6, the Buddha speaks of a first and a second arrow. a woman gets a painful injection, then spends the evening resenting the nurse and dreading the next one. in the sutta's terms, what is the second arrow?","o":["the sting of the needle in her arm","the illness the injection is meant to stop","the soreness in her arm the next day","the resentment and dread she adds"],"a":3,"es":{"q":"en el Sallatha Sutta (\"la flecha\"), Samyutta Nikaya 36.6, el Buda habla de una primera y una segunda flecha. una mujer recibe una inyección dolorosa y luego pasa la tarde resentida con la enfermera y temiendo la próxima. en los términos del sutta, ¿cuál es la segunda flecha?","o":["el pinchazo de la aguja en su brazo","la enfermedad que la inyección busca evitar","el dolor en el brazo al día siguiente","el resentimiento y el temor que ella añade"]}},{"id":"BUDDHISM-s04-04","day":269,"d":3,"q":"the Heart Sutra says \"form is emptiness\" (Sanskrit shunyata). as Mahayana teaching, especially the Madhyamaka school of Nagarjuna, explains it, what is form empty of?","o":["any reality at all, so that nothing exists in any way","own-being (svabhava), existence apart from conditions","suffering, once a bodhisattva has looked at it deeply","worth, so that ordinary things deserve no care at all"],"a":1,"es":{"q":"el Sutra del Corazón dice \"la forma es vacuidad\" (en sánscrito shunyata). según la enseñanza mahayana, en especial la escuela madhyamaka de Nagarjuna, ¿de qué está vacía la forma?","o":["de toda realidad, de modo que nada existe de ninguna manera","de ser propio (svabhava), existir aparte de las condiciones","del sufrimiento, una vez que un bodisatva la mira a fondo","de valor, de modo que las cosas comunes no merecen cuidado"]}},{"id":"BUDDHISM-s04-05","day":280,"d":3,"q":"in the Zen koan of Baizhang's fox (Gateless Gate, case 2), an old teacher was reborn as a fox for five hundred lives after saying that a person of great practice does not fall into cause and effect. what point does Baizhang's freeing \"turning word\" make?","o":["an awakened person stands wholly above cause and effect","cause and effect are only an illusion made by the mind","an awakened person is not blind to cause and effect","the fox's bad karma had at last been entirely used up"],"a":2,"es":{"q":"en el koan zen del zorro de Baizhang (La puerta sin puerta, caso 2), un antiguo maestro renació como zorro durante quinientas vidas por decir que una persona de gran práctica no cae en la causa y el efecto. ¿qué señala la \"palabra que da vuelta\" con que Baizhang lo libera?","o":["una persona despierta está por encima de la causa y el efecto","la causa y el efecto son solo una ilusión creada por la mente","una persona despierta no es ciega a la causa y el efecto","el mal karma del zorro por fin se había agotado por completo"]}},{"id":"BUDDHISM-s04-06","day":299,"d":3,"q":"in Theravada teaching, which three fetters (samyojana) are cut when someone becomes a stream-enterer (sotapanna), the first of the four stages of awakening?","o":["self-view, doubt, and clinging to rites and rituals","sensual desire, ill will, and restlessness of mind","conceit, restlessness, and ignorance of the truths","lust for form realms, lust for formless realms, conceit"],"a":0,"es":{"q":"en la enseñanza theravada, ¿qué tres ataduras (samyojana) se cortan cuando alguien entra en la corriente (sotapanna), la primera de las cuatro etapas del despertar?","o":["la idea de un yo, la duda y el apego a ritos y rituales","el deseo sensual, la malevolencia y la inquietud mental","la vanidad, la inquietud y la ignorancia de las verdades","el apego a los reinos de forma, a los sin forma, la vanidad"]}}],[{"id":"BUDDHISM-s05-01","day":343,"d":2,"q":"in the Buddha's first sermon (SN 56.11, the Dhammacakkappavattana Sutta), each noble truth comes with a task. what is the task given for the fourth truth, the path leading to the end of dukkha?","o":["to be realized (sacchikatabba)","to be fully understood (pariññeyya)","to be developed (bhavetabba)","to be abandoned (pahatabba)"],"a":2,"es":{"q":"en el primer sermón del Buda (SN 56.11, el Dhammacakkappavattana Sutta), cada noble verdad trae una tarea. ¿cuál es la tarea de la cuarta verdad, el camino que lleva al fin de dukkha?","o":["ser realizada (sacchikatabba)","ser comprendida a fondo (pariññeyya)","ser desarrollada (bhavetabba)","ser abandonada (pahatabba)"]}},{"id":"BUDDHISM-s05-02","day":353,"d":3,"q":"in MN 44 (Culavedalla Sutta), the nun Dhammadinna sorts the factors of the noble eightfold path into three trainings. in which training does she place right speech, right action and right livelihood?","o":["the training in meditation (samadhi)","the training in conduct (sila)","the training in wisdom (panna)","the practice of giving (dana)"],"a":1,"es":{"q":"en MN 44 (Culavedalla Sutta), la monja Dhammadinna ordena los factores del noble óctuple sendero en tres entrenamientos. ¿en cuál pone el habla correcta, la acción correcta y el modo de vida correcto?","o":["el entrenamiento en meditación (samadhi)","el entrenamiento en conducta (sila)","el entrenamiento en sabiduría (panna)","la práctica de la generosidad (dana)"]}},{"id":"BUDDHISM-s05-03","day":367,"d":3,"q":"a man knows something true and helpful that his brother will not want to hear. in MN 58 (Abhayarajakumara Sutta), what does the Buddha say he himself does with words that are true, beneficial and unwelcome?","o":["he keeps silent, since unwelcome words count as harsh speech","he waits for the right time to speak them, and then speaks","he speaks them at once, whatever the moment or the mood","he speaks them if the listener first asks to hear them"],"a":1,"es":{"q":"un hombre sabe algo verdadero y útil que su hermano no querrá oír. en MN 58 (Abhayarajakumara Sutta), ¿qué dice el Buda que hace él mismo con las palabras verdaderas, beneficiosas y mal recibidas?","o":["calla, porque las palabras mal recibidas cuentan como habla dura","espera el momento oportuno para decirlas, y entonces las dice","las dice de inmediato, sin importar el momento ni el ánimo","las dice si quien escucha primero pide oírlas"]}},{"id":"BUDDHISM-s05-04","day":372,"d":3,"q":"in AN 6.63 the Buddha says, \"it is intention (cetana), monks, that I call kamma.\" what does this say about how kamma works?","o":["deeds of the body make kamma, but words and thoughts do not","every feeling a person has is the fruit of past intention","kamma is fixed at birth, and choices made now cannot change it","the will behind a deed of body, speech or mind is what counts"],"a":3,"es":{"q":"en AN 6.63 el Buda dice: \"es a la intención (cetana), monjes, a lo que llamo kamma\". ¿qué dice esto sobre cómo funciona el kamma?","o":["los actos del cuerpo hacen kamma, pero las palabras y los pensamientos no","todo lo que una persona siente es fruto de una intención pasada","el kamma queda fijado al nacer y lo que se elige ahora no lo cambia","lo que cuenta es la voluntad detrás del acto de cuerpo, habla o mente"]}},{"id":"BUDDHISM-s05-05","day":388,"d":3,"q":"in AN 6.55, the monk Sona has walked in meditation until his feet bleed and is thinking of giving up. why does the Buddha ask him how his lute sounded when its strings were too tight or too loose?","o":["to teach that Sona should leave the robe and return to his music","to teach that awakening comes from straining as hard as one can","to teach that the mind does best when left slack and fully at ease","to teach that effort should be even, neither too tight nor slack"],"a":3,"es":{"q":"en AN 6.55, el monje Sona ha caminado en meditación hasta sangrarle los pies y piensa en rendirse. ¿por qué el Buda le pregunta cómo sonaba su laúd con las cuerdas muy tensas o muy flojas?","o":["para enseñarle que debe dejar los hábitos y volver a su música","para enseñarle que el despertar viene de esforzarse al máximo","para enseñarle que la mente rinde mejor floja y del todo relajada","para enseñarle que el esfuerzo debe ser parejo, ni tenso ni flojo"]}},{"id":"BUDDHISM-s05-06","day":397,"d":4,"q":"in the Pali Canon's MN 39, the Buddha likens the second jhana to a lake with no streams flowing in and no rain, fed by a cool spring welling up from below. what does the image convey?","o":["joy born of concentration wells up within and fills the body","joy flows in from pleasant sights and sounds outside the body","the mind grows still because all joy and feeling have dried up","calm depends on a quiet place, free of every outside disturbance"],"a":0,"es":{"q":"en MN 39 del Canon Pali, el Buda compara el segundo jhana con un lago sin arroyos que entren ni lluvia, alimentado por un manantial fresco que brota desde abajo. ¿qué transmite la imagen?","o":["el gozo nacido de la concentración brota adentro y llena el cuerpo","el gozo entra desde vistas y sonidos agradables fuera del cuerpo","la mente se aquieta porque todo gozo y toda sensación se secaron","la calma depende de un lugar quieto, libre de toda molestia externa"]}}],[{"id":"BUDDHISM-s06-01","day":420,"d":2,"q":"in the simile of the raft in the Majjhima Nikaya (MN 22), a man ties a raft of grass and branches and crosses a great river. what does the Buddha say he should do with it on the far shore?","o":["carry it on his head wherever he goes next","hand it to a traveler waiting on that bank","leave it on the shore and go on his way","break it apart so nobody can reuse it"],"a":2,"es":{"q":"en el símil de la balsa del Majjhima Nikaya (MN 22), un hombre ata una balsa de hierba y ramas y cruza un gran río. ¿qué dice el Buda que debe hacer con ella en la otra orilla?","o":["cargarla sobre la cabeza adondequiera que vaya","dársela a un viajero que espera en esa orilla","dejarla en la orilla y seguir su camino","desarmarla para que nadie pueda volver a usarla"]}},{"id":"BUDDHISM-s06-02","day":437,"d":3,"q":"in the Culavedalla Sutta (MN 44), the layman Visakha asks a series of hard questions about identity, meditation and feeling, and the Buddha later says he would have answered them the same way. who answers Visakha?","o":["the nun Dhammadinna","the nun Uppalavanna","the elder Sariputta","the elder Moggallana"],"a":0,"es":{"q":"en el Culavedalla Sutta (MN 44), el laico Visakha hace una serie de preguntas difíciles sobre la identidad, la meditación y la sensación, y después el Buda dice que él habría respondido igual. ¿quién le responde a Visakha?","o":["la monja Dhammadinna","la monja Uppalavanna","el anciano Sariputta","el anciano Moggallana"]}},{"id":"BUDDHISM-s06-03","day":433,"d":3,"q":"in the Mahatanhasankhaya Sutta (MN 38), the monk Sati claims that \"this same consciousness\" runs on and wanders from life to life. why does the Buddha reject this?","o":["consciousness stops at death and nothing at all carries on","only a fully awakened one's consciousness stays the same","consciousness is the true self, but it rests between lives","consciousness arises from conditions, not apart from them"],"a":3,"es":{"q":"en el Mahatanhasankhaya Sutta (MN 38), el monje Sati afirma que \"esta misma conciencia\" sigue y vaga de vida en vida. ¿por qué lo rechaza el Buda?","o":["la conciencia se detiene al morir y nada en absoluto continúa","solo la conciencia de un ser plenamente despierto sigue igual","la conciencia es el verdadero yo, pero descansa entre vidas","la conciencia surge de condiciones, no separada de ellas"]}},{"id":"BUDDHISM-s06-04","day":417,"d":2,"q":"in the simile of the saw (MN 21), the Buddha says that even if bandits cut someone apart limb by limb with a two-handled saw, a monk should keep a certain state of mind. which one?","o":["a calm face, while hiding the anger inside","a mind of goodwill, with no hate within","a firm resolve to repay them in a later life","a mind so absorbed that it feels no pain"],"a":1,"es":{"q":"en el símil de la sierra (MN 21), el Buda dice que aunque unos bandidos cortaran a alguien miembro por miembro con una sierra de dos mangos, un monje debe mantener cierto estado mental. ¿cuál?","o":["una cara tranquila, mientras esconde el enojo por dentro","una mente de buena voluntad, sin odio por dentro","una firme decisión de pagarles en una vida futura","una mente tan absorta que no siente ningún dolor"]}},{"id":"BUDDHISM-s06-05","day":463,"d":4,"q":"in the Aggivacchagotta Sutta (MN 72), the wanderer Vacchagotta asks where a fully freed mind reappears after death, and the Buddha asks him which direction a fire went when it went out. what is the point of the fire?","o":["the freed mind rises to the highest heaven, just as flame rises","the freed one is wiped out, as a fire is destroyed for good","\"reappears\" doesn't fit, as no direction fits a fire gone out","the freed mind is reborn later, as a fire can be lit again"],"a":2,"es":{"q":"en el Aggivacchagotta Sutta (MN 72), el asceta errante Vacchagotta pregunta dónde reaparece después de la muerte una mente plenamente liberada, y el Buda le pregunta en qué dirección se fue un fuego cuando se apagó. ¿qué quiere mostrar el fuego?","o":["la mente liberada sube al cielo más alto, así como sube la llama","el liberado queda borrado, como un fuego destruido para siempre","\"reaparece\" no encaja, como ninguna dirección encaja con un fuego apagado","la mente liberada renace más tarde, como un fuego que se vuelve a encender"]}},{"id":"BUDDHISM-s06-06","day":478,"d":3,"q":"in the Devadaha Sutta (MN 101), an arrow-maker heats a crooked shaft between two flames. a monk's hard effort has already cleared away the unwholesome habit it was aimed at. what does the simile say comes next?","o":["he keeps the heat on, since pain itself burns away his old deeds","he eases off, as the fletcher stops once the shaft is straight","he drops all effort, since effort never changes the mind","he heats it harder, so the habit can never come back again"],"a":1,"es":{"q":"en el Devadaha Sutta (MN 101), un fabricante de flechas calienta un astil torcido entre dos llamas. el esfuerzo intenso de un monje ya eliminó el hábito dañino al que apuntaba. ¿qué dice el símil que sigue?","o":["mantiene el calor, porque el dolor mismo quema los actos pasados","afloja, como el flechero se detiene cuando el astil queda recto","deja todo esfuerzo, porque el esfuerzo nunca cambia la mente","calienta todavía más, para que el hábito no vuelva nunca"]}}],[{"id":"BUDDHISM-s07-01","day":525,"d":2,"q":"The Brahmajala Sutta, the first discourse of the Digha Nikaya, compares speculative views about the self and the world to fish caught in a fine net. How many such views does it list?","o":["thirty-two views","fifty-two views","sixty-two views","eighty-four views"],"a":2,"es":{"q":"El Brahmajala Sutta, el primer discurso del Digha Nikaya, compara las opiniones especulativas sobre el yo y el mundo con peces atrapados en una red fina. ¿Cuántas de esas opiniones enumera?","o":["treinta y dos opiniones","cincuenta y dos opiniones","sesenta y dos opiniones","ochenta y cuatro opiniones"]}},{"id":"BUDDHISM-s07-02","day":585,"d":2,"q":"In the Karaniya Metta Sutta, the discourse on loving-kindness (Sutta Nipata 1.8), what image does the poem give for a boundless heart toward all beings?","o":["a mother guarding her one child with her own life","a lamp that lights a thousand others and stays bright","a full moon shining on every pond the same way","a river carrying every boat to the far shore"],"a":0,"es":{"q":"En el Karaniya Metta Sutta, el discurso sobre la bondad amorosa (Sutta Nipata 1.8), ¿qué imagen da el poema de un corazón sin límites hacia todos los seres?","o":["una madre que protege con su vida a su único hijo","una lámpara que enciende otras mil y sigue brillando","una luna llena que brilla igual sobre cada estanque","un río que lleva cada barca a la otra orilla"]}},{"id":"BUDDHISM-s07-03","day":548,"d":3,"q":"In the Mahaparinibbana Sutta's four great references (mahapadesa), a monk claims he heard a teaching from the Buddha himself. What are the other monks told to do with it?","o":["accept it at once, since it came from the Buddha's own mouth","compare its words with the discourses and the discipline","ask the most senior elder to rule on whether it is true","accept it if a whole community of elders agrees with it"],"a":1,"es":{"q":"En las cuatro grandes referencias (mahapadesa) del Mahaparinibbana Sutta, un monje afirma que oyó una enseñanza del propio Buda. ¿Qué se les pide a los demás monjes que hagan con ella?","o":["aceptarla enseguida, porque salió de la boca del propio Buda","comparar sus palabras con los discursos y la disciplina","pedir al anciano de más edad que decida si es verdadera","aceptarla si toda una comunidad de ancianos está de acuerdo"]}},{"id":"BUDDHISM-s07-04","day":547,"d":3,"q":"In the Mahaparinibbana Sutta, the ill and aging Buddha tells Ananda that he has no \"teacher's closed fist\" (acariya-mutthi). What does he mean?","o":["he has kept a few teachings for his closest disciples","he will name a successor to hold the teaching after him","his last teaching is saved for Ananda to pass on","he has taught everything, with nothing held back"],"a":3,"es":{"q":"En el Mahaparinibbana Sutta, el Buda, enfermo y anciano, le dice a Ananda que no tiene \"puño cerrado de maestro\" (acariya-mutthi). ¿Qué quiere decir?","o":["que guardó enseñanzas para sus discípulos más cercanos","que nombrará a un sucesor que custodie la enseñanza","que su última enseñanza queda para que Ananda la transmita","que lo enseñó todo, sin guardarse nada para el final"]}},{"id":"BUDDHISM-s07-05","day":584,"d":2,"q":"In the Vasala Sutta (Sutta Nipata 1.7), a brahmin shouts \"outcast!\" at the Buddha. According to the Buddha's reply, what makes someone an outcast or a brahmin?","o":["the family a person is born into","the deeds a person does in life","the sacrifices a person performs","the sacred verses a person knows"],"a":1,"es":{"q":"En el Vasala Sutta (Sutta Nipata 1.7), un brahmán le grita \"¡paria!\" al Buda. Según la respuesta del Buda, ¿qué hace que alguien sea paria o brahmán?","o":["la familia en la que nace la persona","los actos que la persona lleva a cabo","los sacrificios que la persona realiza","los versos sagrados que la persona sabe"]}},{"id":"BUDDHISM-s07-06","day":571,"d":3,"q":"A shop owner gives her workers tasks suited to their strength, fair wages, care when they are sick, and time off. In the six directions of the Sigalovada Sutta (Digha Nikaya 31), which direction is she honoring?","o":["the zenith: monks and brahmins","the west: wife and children","the north: friends and companions","the nadir: servants and workers"],"a":3,"es":{"q":"La dueña de una tienda les da a sus trabajadores tareas acordes con sus fuerzas, un sueldo justo, cuidado cuando se enferman y días libres. En las seis direcciones del Sigalovada Sutta (Digha Nikaya 31), ¿qué dirección está honrando?","o":["el cenit: monjes y brahmanes","el oeste: esposa e hijos","el norte: los amigos y compañeros","el nadir: siervos y trabajadores"]}}],[{"id":"BUDDHISM-s08-01","day":613,"d":3,"q":"in the Udana (1.10), the ascetic Bahiya stops the Buddha on his alms round and begs three times for a teaching. what short instruction does the Buddha give him there in the street?","o":["in the seen, see the fruit of past karma","in the seen, let there be only the seen","in the seen, search for the one who sees","in the seen, turn away and close the eyes"],"a":1,"es":{"q":"en el Udana (1.10), el asceta Bahiya detiene al Buda durante su ronda de limosnas y le ruega tres veces una enseñanza. ¿qué instrucción breve le da el Buda ahí en la calle?","o":["en lo visto, ve el fruto del karma pasado","en lo visto, que haya solo lo visto","en lo visto, busca a quien está viendo","en lo visto, apártate y cierra los ojos"]}},{"id":"BUDDHISM-s08-02","day":616,"d":3,"q":"in the Udana (5.1), King Pasenadi and Queen Mallika agree that no one is dearer to them than their own self. what conclusion does the Buddha draw in his verse?","o":["since the king is dearest to all, his people should serve him","since no self exists, holding anyone dear is a mistake","since others hold themselves as dear, one should harm none","since the self is dearest, one should care for it before others"],"a":2,"es":{"q":"en el Udana (5.1), el rey Pasenadi y la reina Mallika coinciden en que nadie les es más querido que su propio ser. ¿qué conclusión saca el Buda en su verso?","o":["como el rey es el más querido, su pueblo debe servirle","como no existe un ser, querer a alguien es un error","como los demás se quieren igual, no hay que dañar a nadie","como uno mismo es lo más querido, hay que cuidarse antes que a otros"]}},{"id":"BUDDHISM-s08-03","day":645,"d":2,"q":"in the Sallatha Sutta (Samyutta Nikaya 36.6), an untaught person struck by bodily pain is said to be hit by two arrows. what is the second arrow?","o":["the same pain coming back the next day","the karma that caused the first pain","the bodily pain felt by a loved one","the mental distress piled on top"],"a":3,"es":{"q":"en el Sallatha Sutta (Samyutta Nikaya 36.6), se dice que una persona sin instrucción, golpeada por un dolor del cuerpo, recibe dos flechas. ¿cuál es la segunda flecha?","o":["el mismo dolor que vuelve al día siguiente","el karma que causó el primer dolor","el dolor físico que siente un ser querido","la angustia mental añadida encima"]}},{"id":"BUDDHISM-s08-04","day":656,"d":4,"q":"in the Anguttara Nikaya (1.51–52), the Buddha calls the mind luminous (pabhassara) and its defilements agantuka, \"arriving\" like visiting guests. what does calling the defilements visitors imply?","o":["they come from outside, so the mind can be freed of them","they are the mind's nature, so they can never be removed","they come from past lives, so this life cannot touch them","they visit only monks, so lay people are already pure"],"a":0,"es":{"q":"en el Anguttara Nikaya (1.51–52), el Buda llama a la mente luminosa (pabhassara) y a sus impurezas agantuka, \"que llegan\", como huéspedes de visita. ¿qué implica llamar visitantes a las impurezas?","o":["vienen de afuera, y la mente puede liberarse de ellas","son la naturaleza de la mente, así que nunca se quitan","vienen de vidas pasadas, así que esta vida no las toca","solo visitan a los monjes, así que los laicos ya son puros"]}},{"id":"BUDDHISM-s08-05","day":660,"d":4,"q":"in the Anguttara Nikaya's salt crystal simile (AN 3.100), a lump of salt makes a cup of water undrinkable but leaves the Ganges river drinkable. what is the simile teaching about karma?","o":["a bad deed is erased by a good deed of the same size","a small bad deed weighs less in a well-developed mind","small bad deeds bring no result at all for anyone","the result of a bad deed is shared by the whole village"],"a":1,"es":{"q":"en el símil del grano de sal del Anguttara Nikaya (AN 3.100), un puñado de sal vuelve imbebible una taza de agua pero deja potable el río Ganges. ¿qué enseña el símil sobre el karma?","o":["una mala acción se borra con una buena del mismo tamaño","una mala acción pequeña pesa poco en una mente cultivada","las malas acciones pequeñas no dan ningún resultado","el resultado de una mala acción lo comparte toda la aldea"]}},{"id":"BUDDHISM-s08-06","day":669,"d":3,"q":"a teacher is thanked warmly by one parent in the morning and criticized sharply by another that afternoon. which pair of the eight worldly conditions (lokadhamma) in the Anguttara Nikaya (8.6) does her day show?","o":["gain and loss","pleasure and pain","praise and blame","hope and fear"],"a":2,"es":{"q":"a una maestra la agradece con calidez un padre por la mañana y la critica con dureza otro por la tarde. ¿qué par de las ocho condiciones mundanas (lokadhamma) del Anguttara Nikaya (8.6) muestra su día?","o":["ganancia y pérdida","placer y dolor","elogio y censura","esperanza y miedo"]}}],[{"id":"BUDDHISM-s09-01","day":697,"d":3,"q":"Which poet does tradition credit with the Buddhacarita, the Sanskrit epic poem on the life of the Buddha?","o":["Nagarjuna","Aryashura","Ashvaghosha","Chandrakirti"],"a":2,"es":{"q":"¿A qué poeta atribuye la tradición el Buddhacarita, el poema épico en sánscrito sobre la vida del Buda?","o":["Nagarjuna","Aryashura","Ashvaghosha","Chandrakirti"]}},{"id":"BUDDHISM-s09-02","day":727,"d":3,"q":"In the Vinaya's Mahavagga, which monk recites the short verse on causes that opens the way for Upatissa, later called Sariputta?","o":["Assaji, one of the first five monks","Ananda, the Buddha's own young cousin","Upali, the former court barber","Kassapa, the elder of the forest"],"a":0,"es":{"q":"En el Mahavagga del Vinaya, ¿qué monje recita el breve verso sobre las causas que le abre el camino a Upatissa, más tarde llamado Sariputta?","o":["Assaji, uno de los cinco primeros monjes","Ananda, el propio primo del Buda","Upali, el antiguo barbero de la corte","Kassapa, el anciano del bosque"]}},{"id":"BUDDHISM-s09-03","day":730,"d":3,"q":"In the Anguttara Nikaya (AN 9.11), falsely accused of striking a monk, Sariputta says his mind is like the earth. What is the point of the comparison?","o":["it stays unmoved while the world spins around it","it feeds every creature without asking anything back","it hides what is buried in it and keeps it secret","it takes whatever is thrown on it without ill will"],"a":3,"es":{"q":"En el Anguttara Nikaya (AN 9.11), acusado falsamente de golpear a un monje, Sariputta dice que su mente es como la tierra. ¿Cuál es el sentido de la comparación?","o":["se queda inmóvil mientras el mundo gira a su alrededor","alimenta a toda criatura sin pedir nada a cambio","esconde lo que se entierra en ella y lo guarda en secreto","recibe todo lo que le echan encima sin mala voluntad"]}},{"id":"BUDDHISM-s09-04","day":746,"d":3,"q":"In the Vinaya's Cullavagga, why do the Sakyan princes ask the Buddha to ordain their barber Upali before they are ordained?","o":["Upali was the eldest man in their party","so they must honor him as their senior","Upali had been a wandering ascetic before","so he could shave their heads for the rite"],"a":1,"es":{"q":"En el Cullavagga del Vinaya, ¿por qué los príncipes sakya le piden al Buda que ordene a su barbero Upali antes que a ellos?","o":["Upali era el mayor de todo el grupo","para tener que honrarlo como su superior","Upali ya había sido asceta errante antes","para que él les rapara la cabeza en el rito"]}},{"id":"BUDDHISM-s09-05","day":756,"d":4,"q":"In the Samyutta Nikaya (SN 44.1), King Pasenadi asks the nun Khema whether the Tathagata exists after death. What is her answer?","o":["he lives on in a pure, radiant realm","he simply ceases and is no more","the Buddha left this undeclared","he both is and is not, in two senses"],"a":2,"es":{"q":"En el Samyutta Nikaya (SN 44.1), el rey Pasenadi le pregunta a la monja Khema si el Tathagata existe después de la muerte. ¿Qué responde ella?","o":["sigue viviendo en un reino puro y radiante","simplemente cesa y ya no existe más","el Buda ha dejado esto sin declarar","es y no es a la vez, en dos sentidos"]}},{"id":"BUDDHISM-s09-06","day":750,"d":4,"q":"In MN 61, the Buddha tells the novice Rahula to reflect on an act like looking in a mirror. A novice about to speak sees the words would harm someone. By that teaching, what should he do?","o":["hold back and not say those words","say them, then confess it afterward","say them if he means them kindly","say them, but in a gentle voice"],"a":0,"es":{"q":"En el MN 61, el Buda le dice al novicio Rahula que reflexione sobre cada acto como quien se mira en un espejo. Un novicio a punto de hablar ve que sus palabras harían daño a alguien. Según esa enseñanza, ¿qué debe hacer?","o":["contenerse y no decir esas palabras","decirlas y confesarlo después","decirlas si su intención es amable","decirlas, pero con voz suave"]}}],[{"id":"BUDDHISM-s10-01","day":882,"d":3,"q":"The scholar Buddhaghosa came from India to the Great Monastery (Mahavihara) at Anuradhapura in Sri Lanka. Which Theravada manual of virtue, concentration and wisdom did he write there?","o":["the Visuddhimagga, the Path of Purification","the Milindapanha, the Questions of King Milinda","the Dipavamsa, the Chronicle of the Island","the Lalitavistara, the Unfolding Play"],"a":0,"es":{"q":"El erudito Buddhaghosa llegó desde la India al Gran Monasterio (Mahavihara) de Anuradhapura, en Sri Lanka. ¿Qué manual theravada sobre la virtud, la concentración y la sabiduría escribió allí?","o":["el Visuddhimagga, el Camino de la Purificación","el Milindapanha, las Preguntas del rey Milinda","el Dipavamsa, la Crónica de la Isla","el Lalitavistara, el Juego Desplegado"]}},{"id":"BUDDHISM-s10-02","day":868,"d":3,"q":"In the Questions of King Milinda (Milindapanha), the monk Nagasena shows that \"chariot\" is not the pole, the axle or the wheels, nor something apart from them. What does he use this to teach about a person?","o":["the self is a lasting driver hidden behind body and mind","a person, like a chariot, is a name for parts come together","only the mind is the real person; the body is a mere vehicle","names are false, so neither chariot nor person exists at all"],"a":1,"es":{"q":"En las Preguntas del rey Milinda (Milindapanha), el monje Nagasena muestra que \"carro\" no es la lanza, ni el eje, ni las ruedas, ni algo aparte de ellos. ¿Qué enseña con esto sobre una persona?","o":["el yo es un conductor duradero escondido tras el cuerpo y la mente","una persona, como un carro, es un nombre para partes que se juntan","solo la mente es la persona real; el cuerpo es un simple vehículo","los nombres son falsos, así que ni el carro ni la persona existen"]}},{"id":"BUDDHISM-s10-03","day":857,"d":3,"q":"In his Rock Edict 13, the emperor Ashoka looks back on his conquest of Kalinga. What does the edict say came of that war for him?","o":["pride in a victory that made him master of every land in India","an order that his sons push on and conquer the lands past Kalinga","remorse at the slaughter, and a turn to conquest by dhamma","a decree that only Buddhists could serve as officials in his empire"],"a":2,"es":{"q":"En su Edicto de Roca 13, el emperador Ashoka mira atrás a su conquista de Kalinga. ¿Qué dice el edicto que le dejó esa guerra?","o":["orgullo por una victoria que lo hizo dueño de todas las tierras de la India","una orden para que sus hijos siguieran y conquistaran más allá de Kalinga","remordimiento por la matanza, y un giro hacia la conquista por el dhamma","un decreto para que solo los budistas sirvieran como funcionarios del imperio"]}},{"id":"BUDDHISM-s10-04","day":818,"d":3,"q":"In the Theravada list of ten perfections (paramis), a man is insulted and struck, yet bears it without anger and without seeking revenge. Which perfection is he practicing?","o":["dana, giving freely","adhitthana, resolve","nekkhamma, renunciation","khanti, forbearance"],"a":3,"es":{"q":"En la lista theravada de las diez perfecciones (paramis), un hombre es insultado y golpeado, pero lo soporta sin enojo y sin buscar venganza. ¿Qué perfección está practicando?","o":["dana, la generosidad","adhitthana, la determinación","nekkhamma, la renuncia","khanti, la paciencia"]}},{"id":"BUDDHISM-s10-05","day":861,"d":2,"q":"According to the Mahavamsa, Sri Lanka's great chronicle, who brought the Buddha's teaching to King Devanampiya Tissa of Anuradhapura?","o":["Nagasena, the monk who answered King Milinda","Mahinda, a monk who was the son of Ashoka","Buddhaghosa, the commentator from Magadha","Moggaliputta Tissa, elder of the third council"],"a":1,"es":{"q":"Según el Mahavamsa, la gran crónica de Sri Lanka, ¿quién llevó la enseñanza del Buda al rey Devanampiya Tissa de Anuradhapura?","o":["Nagasena, el monje que respondió al rey Milinda","Mahinda, un monje que era hijo de Ashoka","Buddhaghosa, el comentarista de Magadha","Moggaliputta Tissa, anciano del tercer concilio"]}},{"id":"BUDDHISM-s10-06","day":890,"d":3,"q":"Borobudur in Java is a stupa raised in terraces, its galleries carved with relief panels of the Buddha's life and past lives. How is a pilgrim meant to read the panels?","o":["by circling each terrace clockwise, keeping the monument on the right","by circling each terrace counterclockwise, with the monument on the left","by going into the great hall inside, where the panels line the walls","by climbing straight to the top, then reading the terraces downward"],"a":0,"es":{"q":"Borobudur, en Java, es una estupa levantada en terrazas, con galerías talladas con relieves de la vida del Buda y de sus vidas pasadas. ¿Cómo debe leer los relieves un peregrino?","o":["rodeando cada terraza en el sentido del reloj, con el monumento a la derecha","rodeando cada terraza al revés del reloj, con el monumento a la izquierda","entrando en la gran sala interior, donde los relieves cubren los muros","subiendo directo hasta la cima y leyendo luego las terrazas hacia abajo"]}}],[{"id":"BUDDHISM-s11-01","day":903,"d":2,"q":"which monk, born in the oasis kingdom of Kucha and later brought to the Chinese capital Chang'an, made the Chinese versions of the Lotus, Diamond and Vimalakirti sutras that are still the ones most chanted and studied?","o":["An Shigao","Xuanzang","Kumarajiva","Dharmaraksa"],"a":2,"es":{"q":"¿qué monje, nacido en el reino oasis de Kucha y llevado después a la capital china, Chang'an, hizo las versiones chinas de los sutras del Loto, del Diamante y de Vimalakirti que siguen siendo las más recitadas y estudiadas?","o":["An Shigao","Xuanzang","Kumarajiva","Dharmaraksa"]}},{"id":"BUDDHISM-s11-02","day":915,"d":3,"q":"in the Platform Sutra's verse contest, the head monk Shenxiu writes that the mind is like a bright mirror on a stand that must be wiped clean again and again. what does Huineng's answering verse say?","o":["the mirror has no stand, so where could dust land?","the mirror is wiped once, then stays bright for good","the mirror needs a teacher's hand to wipe it clean","the body is its stand, and it must be wiped daily"],"a":0,"es":{"q":"en el concurso de versos del Sutra del Estrado, el monje principal, Shenxiu, escribe que la mente es como un espejo brillante sobre un soporte que hay que limpiar una y otra vez. ¿qué dice el verso con que responde Huineng?","o":["el espejo no tiene soporte, ¿dónde caería el polvo?","el espejo se limpia una vez y queda brillante ya siempre","el espejo necesita la mano de un maestro para limpiarse","el cuerpo es su soporte, y hay que limpiarlo cada día"]}},{"id":"BUDDHISM-s11-03","day":922,"d":3,"q":"in Secrets on Cultivating the Mind (Susim gyeol), how does the Korean Seon master Chinul order awakening and practice?","o":["gradual cultivation first, then a sudden awakening","sudden awakening first, then gradual cultivation","sudden awakening, with no further practice needed","gradual cultivation, with awakening in a later life"],"a":1,"es":{"q":"en Secretos para cultivar la mente (Susim gyeol), ¿en qué orden pone el maestro coreano de Seon Chinul el despertar y la práctica?","o":["primero el cultivo gradual, luego un despertar súbito","primero el despertar súbito, luego el cultivo gradual","un despertar súbito, sin que haga falta más práctica","cultivo gradual, con el despertar en una vida futura"]}},{"id":"BUDDHISM-s11-04","day":934,"d":3,"q":"in the Tibetan accounts of the debate at Samye, the Indian scholar Kamalashila argues against the Chinese Chan master Hashang Mahayana. what does Kamalashila hold is the way to awakening?","o":["stopping all thought, since every thought clouds the mind","calling on Amida Buddha's name with trust in his vow","receiving tantric initiation before studying any texts","moving through stages, with careful study and analysis"],"a":3,"es":{"q":"en los relatos tibetanos del debate de Samye, el erudito indio Kamalashila discute con el maestro chino de Chan Hashang Mahayana. según Kamalashila, ¿cuál es el camino al despertar?","o":["detener todo pensamiento, pues cada uno nubla la mente","invocar el nombre del Buda Amida confiando en su voto","recibir la iniciación tántrica antes de estudiar textos","avanzar por etapas, con estudio y análisis cuidadosos"]}},{"id":"BUDDHISM-s11-05","day":938,"d":3,"q":"a commentary by an Indian master explaining Nagarjuna's teaching on emptiness is translated into Tibetan. in which part of the Tibetan Buddhist canon do the editors place it?","o":["the Tengyur, the translated treatises","the Kangyur, the translated word of the Buddha","the terma, the hidden treasure teachings","the Vinaya, the rules for monks and nuns"],"a":0,"es":{"q":"un comentario de un maestro indio que explica la enseñanza de Nagarjuna sobre la vacuidad se traduce al tibetano. ¿en qué parte del canon budista tibetano lo colocan los editores?","o":["el Tengyur, los tratados traducidos","el Kangyur, la palabra traducida del Buda","los terma, las enseñanzas del tesoro oculto","el Vinaya, las reglas de monjes y monjas"]}},{"id":"BUDDHISM-s11-06","day":943,"d":2,"q":"a printed scroll of the Diamond Sutra, found sealed in a cave library near Dunhuang, is now kept at the British Library. what is it famous for?","o":["the first sutra ever put into Chinese","a copy in Kumarajiva's own handwriting","the earliest dated printed book known","the oldest copy of the sutra in Sanskrit"],"a":2,"es":{"q":"un rollo impreso del Sutra del Diamante, hallado sellado en una biblioteca de una cueva cerca de Dunhuang, se guarda hoy en la Biblioteca Británica. ¿por qué es famoso?","o":["es el primer sutra traducido al chino","es una copia escrita por Kumarajiva","es el libro impreso fechado más antiguo","es la copia más antigua en sánscrito"]}}],[{"id":"BUDDHISM-s12-01","day":956,"d":3,"q":"In Nagarjuna's Mulamadhyamakakarika (24.18), the root text of the Madhyamaka school, dependent arising is said to be the same as what?","o":["mind-only (cittamatra)","emptiness (shunyata)","true suchness (tathata)","storehouse mind (alaya)"],"a":1,"es":{"q":"En el Mulamadhyamakakarika de Nagarjuna (24.18), el texto raíz de la escuela Madhyamaka, ¿con qué se identifica el surgimiento dependiente?","o":["solo mente (cittamatra)","la vacuidad (shunyata)","la talidad (tathata)","la mente almacén (alaya)"]}},{"id":"BUDDHISM-s12-02","day":965,"d":2,"q":"Buddhaghosa's Visuddhimagga (Path of Purification), the great Theravada manual, is built around which three trainings, in order?","o":["generosity, virtue and meditation","faith, effort and mindfulness","virtue, concentration and wisdom","right view, intention and speech"],"a":2,"es":{"q":"El Visuddhimagga (Camino de purificación) de Buddhaghosa, el gran manual theravada, se organiza en torno a ¿qué tres entrenamientos, en orden?","o":["generosidad, virtud y meditación","fe, esfuerzo y atención plena","virtud, concentración y sabiduría","recta visión, intención y habla"]}},{"id":"BUDDHISM-s12-03","day":966,"d":2,"q":"In the Indian and Tibetan Mahayana tradition, which work is Shantideva, the monk of Nalanda, remembered for composing?","o":["the Bodhicharyavatara","the Abhidharma Treasury","the Lamp for the Path","the Precious Garland"],"a":0,"es":{"q":"En la tradición mahayana india y tibetana, ¿qué obra se recuerda que compuso Shantideva, el monje de Nalanda?","o":["el Bodhicharyavatara","el Tesoro del Abhidharma","la Lámpara para el camino","la Guirnalda preciosa"]}},{"id":"BUDDHISM-s12-04","day":986,"d":3,"q":"In the Chan records, when the monk Damei (\"Great Plum\") hears that Mazu now teaches \"no mind, no Buddha\", why does Mazu then say \"the plum is ripe\"?","o":["Damei gave up his old words for Mazu's new ones","Damei held to \"this mind is Buddha\", unshaken","Damei left his mountain to rejoin Mazu's hall","Damei sent Mazu a gift of plums from the hill"],"a":1,"es":{"q":"En los registros chan, cuando el monje Damei (\"Gran Ciruelo\") oye que Mazu ahora enseña \"ni mente ni Buda\", ¿por qué Mazu dice entonces \"el ciruelo está maduro\"?","o":["Damei cambió sus viejas palabras por las nuevas de Mazu","Damei se mantuvo en \"esta mente es Buda\", sin vacilar","Damei dejó su montaña para volver a la sala de Mazu","Damei le mandó a Mazu un regalo de ciruelas del monte"]}},{"id":"BUDDHISM-s12-05","day":996,"d":4,"q":"A Soto Zen monastery must choose its tenzo (head cook). Following Dogen's Tenzo Kyokun (Instructions for the Cook), who should hold the post?","o":["a lay servant hired for skill at the stove","the newest novice, as training in humility","the monk who struggles most in zazen","a senior monk with a mind set on the Way"],"a":3,"es":{"q":"Un monasterio zen soto debe elegir a su tenzo (cocinero principal). Según el Tenzo Kyokun (Instrucciones para el cocinero) de Dogen, ¿quién debe ocupar el puesto?","o":["un sirviente laico contratado por su oficio","el novicio más nuevo, para aprender humildad","el monje al que más le cuesta el zazen","un monje veterano con la mente en el Camino"]}},{"id":"BUDDHISM-s12-06","day":1036,"d":3,"q":"In the Pali Vinaya's Cullavagga, what does it mean when the sangha formally turns its bowls down (patta nikkujjana) toward a layperson?","o":["he is barred from taking refuge for life","the monks will fast until he says sorry","he must ordain as a novice for one season","monks will not take his alms or visit him"],"a":3,"es":{"q":"En el Cullavagga del Vinaya pali, ¿qué significa que la sangha vuelva formalmente sus cuencos boca abajo (patta nikkujjana) hacia un laico?","o":["le prohíben tomar refugio de por vida","los monjes ayunan hasta que se disculpe","debe ordenarse de novicio por una temporada","no aceptarán sus ofrendas ni lo visitarán"]}}],[{"id":"BUDDHISM-s13-01","day":1066,"d":3,"q":"In the Theravada Abhidhamma, which four things are counted as ultimate realities (paramattha dhamma), what is left when experience is fully analysed?","o":["the self, consciousness, matter and nibbana","consciousness, mental factors, matter, nibbana","the five aggregates, the sense bases and kamma","the four great elements: earth, water, fire, wind"],"a":1,"es":{"q":"En el Abhidhamma theravada, ¿qué cuatro cosas se cuentan como realidades últimas (paramattha dhamma), lo que queda cuando la experiencia se analiza por completo?","o":["el yo, la conciencia, la materia y el nibbana","la conciencia, los factores mentales, la materia, el nibbana","los cinco agregados, las bases de los sentidos y el kamma","los cuatro grandes elementos: tierra, agua, fuego, viento"]}},{"id":"BUDDHISM-s13-02","day":1080,"d":3,"q":"At dinner, a woman is about to make a cutting remark about an absent friend and holds it back. In the Theravada Abhidhamma, which mental factor arises in that moment of holding back?","o":["the abstinence (virati) of right speech","conceit (mana), measuring self against others","remorse (kukkucca), regret over a deed done","torpor (middha), a dullness of the mind"],"a":0,"es":{"q":"En una cena, una mujer está por hacer un comentario hiriente sobre una amiga ausente y se lo guarda. En el Abhidhamma theravada, ¿qué factor mental surge en ese momento de contenerse?","o":["la abstención (virati) del habla correcta","la presunción (mana), compararse con otros","el remordimiento (kukkucca), pesar por algo hecho","el sopor (middha), un embotamiento de la mente"]}},{"id":"BUDDHISM-s13-03","day":1085,"d":4,"q":"In the Theravada Abhidhamma's account of a single sense process, at which stage is kamma actually made?","o":["in the first moment, when the object strikes the sense door","in the bhavanga, the quiet life-continuum between processes","in the receiving moment, when the object is taken in","in the javana (impulsion) moments, where intention acts"],"a":3,"es":{"q":"En la descripción del Abhidhamma theravada de un solo proceso de los sentidos, ¿en qué etapa se genera realmente el kamma?","o":["en el primer momento, cuando el objeto toca la puerta del sentido","en el bhavanga, la corriente vital tranquila entre procesos","en el momento de recibir, cuando se capta el objeto","en los momentos de javana (impulsión), donde actúa la intención"]}},{"id":"BUDDHISM-s13-04","day":1103,"d":3,"q":"In the Mahayana teaching of the three bodies of a Buddha (trikaya), what is the nirmanakaya?","o":["the Buddha who appears in the world as a human life","the Buddha as truth itself, with no edges or form","the radiant Buddha teaching bodhisattvas in pure lands","the relics kept in stupas after the Buddha's cremation"],"a":0,"es":{"q":"En la enseñanza mahayana de los tres cuerpos de un Buda (trikaya), ¿qué es el nirmanakaya?","o":["el Buda que aparece en el mundo como una vida humana","el Buda como la verdad misma, sin bordes ni forma","el Buda radiante que enseña a bodhisattvas en tierras puras","las reliquias guardadas en estupas tras la cremación del Buda"]}},{"id":"BUDDHISM-s13-05","day":1110,"d":3,"q":"In the Lotus Sutra's parable of the burning house, a father lures his children out with promised carts. Why does the Buddha say the father told no lie?","o":["the children never believed the promise anyway","the fire was only a dream and the house was safe","it was skillful means that saved their lives","a promise to children is not held to the truth"],"a":2,"es":{"q":"En la parábola de la casa en llamas del Sutra del Loto, un padre atrae a sus hijos afuera prometiéndoles carros. ¿Por qué dice el Buda que el padre no mintió?","o":["los hijos nunca creyeron la promesa de todos modos","el fuego era solo un sueño y la casa estaba a salvo","fue un medio hábil que les salvó la vida","una promesa a los niños no se mide por la verdad"]}},{"id":"BUDDHISM-s13-06","day":1127,"d":3,"q":"According to the Platform Sutra of the Zen (Chan) patriarch Huineng, which line of the Diamond Sutra opened his mind?","o":["look on the world as a bubble, a dream, dew","form is emptiness, emptiness is form","a mind should arise that rests on nothing","all beings have Buddha-nature without exception"],"a":2,"es":{"q":"Según el Sutra de la Plataforma del patriarca zen (chan) Huineng, ¿qué línea del Sutra del Diamante le abrió la mente?","o":["mira el mundo como una burbuja, un sueño, rocío","la forma es vacío, el vacío es forma","que surja una mente que no se apoye en nada","todos los seres tienen naturaleza de Buda sin excepción"]}}],[{"id":"BUDDHISM-s14-01","day":1154,"d":2,"q":"In the Lotus Sutra's parable of the burning house (a Mahayana sutra), a father promises his children goat, deer and ox carts, then gives each of them one great cart. What do the three promised carts stand for?","o":["the three jewels: the Buddha, the Dharma and the Sangha","the three vehicles: disciple, solitary buddha, bodhisattva","the three poisons in the mind: greed, hatred and delusion","the three bodies of a Buddha: the truth, bliss and form body"],"a":1,"es":{"q":"En la parábola de la casa en llamas del Sutra del Loto (un sutra mahayana), un padre les promete a sus hijos carros de cabras, de ciervos y de bueyes, y luego les da a todos un mismo gran carro. ¿Qué representan los tres carros prometidos?","o":["las tres joyas: el Buda, el Dharma y la Sangha","los tres vehículos: discípulo, buda solitario, bodhisattva","los tres venenos de la mente: codicia, odio e ignorancia","los tres cuerpos de un Buda: el de verdad, de gozo y de forma"]}},{"id":"BUDDHISM-s14-02","day":1192,"d":3,"q":"In the Vimalakirti Sutra, the bodhisattvas each explain how to enter non-duality; then the layman Vimalakirti stays silent, and Manjushri praises that silence. Why does the sutra treat the silence as the true answer?","o":["he was too ill to speak, and Manjushri honored his effort","he was yielding to Manjushri, who had already answered it","the bodhisattvas had spoken falsely, and silence rebuked them","non-duality is beyond words, so silence enters it directly"],"a":3,"es":{"q":"En el Sutra de Vimalakirti, cada bodhisattva explica cómo entrar en la no dualidad; luego el laico Vimalakirti guarda silencio, y Manjushri elogia ese silencio. ¿Por qué el sutra toma el silencio como la verdadera respuesta?","o":["estaba demasiado enfermo para hablar, y Manjushri honró su esfuerzo","cedía ante Manjushri, que ya había dado la respuesta","los bodhisattvas habían hablado en falso, y el silencio los corrigió","la no dualidad no cabe en palabras, y el silencio entra en ella"]}},{"id":"BUDDHISM-s14-03","day":1218,"d":3,"q":"In the Chan Platform Sutra, Shenxiu's verse says to wipe the mirror of the mind often so no dust collects; Huineng answers that from the start there is not a single thing for dust to land on. What is Huineng's verse pointing to?","o":["the mind's nature is already pure and is seen all at once","the mind must be polished steadily until no dust remains","the mirror must be broken so that no mind is left at all","dust is past karma that long years of sitting slowly burn away"],"a":0,"es":{"q":"En el Sutra de la Plataforma, del chan, el verso de Shenxiu dice que hay que limpiar a menudo el espejo de la mente para que no se junte polvo; Huineng responde que desde el principio no hay ni una sola cosa donde caiga el polvo. ¿A qué apunta el verso de Huineng?","o":["la naturaleza de la mente ya es pura y se ve de una vez","la mente debe pulirse con constancia hasta que no quede polvo","el espejo debe romperse para que no quede ninguna mente","el polvo es el karma pasado que años de sentarse van quemando"]}},{"id":"BUDDHISM-s14-04","day":1197,"d":2,"q":"The Lankavatara Sutra says that when someone points at the moon, a foolish person looks at the fingertip and not at the moon. What does the sutra warn against with this image?","o":["trusting a teacher's pointing instead of one's own insight","throwing away all scripture as useless for awakening","clinging to a teaching's words instead of what they mean","gazing at the sky instead of looking into one's own mind"],"a":2,"es":{"q":"El Sutra Lankavatara dice que, cuando alguien señala la luna, el necio mira la punta del dedo y no la luna. ¿Contra qué advierte el sutra con esta imagen?","o":["confiar en lo que señala un maestro en vez de en la propia visión","desechar toda escritura como inútil para el despertar","aferrarse a las palabras de una enseñanza en vez de a su sentido","mirar el cielo en vez de mirar dentro de la propia mente"]}},{"id":"BUDDHISM-s14-05","day":1231,"d":3,"q":"A student in Japan spends most retreats working on the koan \"What is the sound of one hand?\", presenting answers in private meetings with the teacher and hoping for kensho, seeing one's nature. Which Japanese Buddhist school does this emphasis most reflect?","o":["Soto Zen, the line Dogen brought from China","Tendai, the line Saicho brought from China","Rinzai Zen, the line Eisai brought from China","Shingon, the line Kukai brought from China"],"a":2,"es":{"q":"Un estudiante en Japón pasa la mayoría de sus retiros trabajando con el koan \"¿Cuál es el sonido de una sola mano?\", presentando respuestas en entrevistas privadas con el maestro y buscando kensho, ver la propia naturaleza. ¿Qué escuela budista japonesa refleja más este énfasis?","o":["el zen soto, el linaje que Dogen trajo de China","el tendai, el linaje que Saicho trajo de China","el zen rinzai, el linaje que Eisai trajo de China","el shingon, el linaje que Kukai trajo de China"]}},{"id":"BUDDHISM-s14-06","day":1200,"d":2,"q":"In Mahayana Buddhism, which bodhisattva is known for the vow not to become a Buddha until the hell realms are empty, and is honored in Japan as Jizo?","o":["Ksitigarbha","Akashagarbha","Samantabhadra","Manjushri"],"a":0,"es":{"q":"En el budismo mahayana, ¿qué bodhisattva es conocido por el voto de no hacerse Buda hasta que los infiernos queden vacíos, y en Japón se venera como Jizo?","o":["Ksitigarbha","Akashagarbha","Samantabhadra","Manjushri"]}}],[{"id":"BUDDHISM-s15-01","day":1257,"d":3,"q":"In the Larger Sukhavativyuha Sutra, the monk Dharmakara (later Amitabha) makes forty-eight vows. According to the eighteenth vow, the \"primal vow\" of Pure Land Buddhism, who will be born in his Pure Land?","o":["monks who keep the whole monastic code","those who trust him and call his name","scholars who master the Pure Land sutras","donors who build temples for the sangha"],"a":1,"es":{"q":"En el Sutra Sukhavativyuha mayor, el monje Dharmakara (luego Amitabha) hace cuarenta y ocho votos. Según el decimoctavo voto, el \"voto primordial\" del budismo de la Tierra Pura, ¿quiénes nacerán en su Tierra Pura?","o":["monjes que cumplen todo el código monástico","quienes se confían a él y dicen su nombre","eruditos que dominan los sutras de la Tierra Pura","donantes que construyen templos para la sangha"]}},{"id":"BUDDHISM-s15-02","day":1265,"d":3,"q":"In Shinran's Jodo Shinshu (True Pure Land) school, what is meant by tariki, \"other power\"?","o":["awakening is built by one's own discipline and merit","a living teacher grants awakening to worthy students","saying the name many times stores up merit for birth","rebirth in the Pure Land is the work of Amida's vow"],"a":3,"es":{"q":"En la escuela Jodo Shinshu (Verdadera Tierra Pura) de Shinran, ¿qué significa tariki, el \"otro poder\"?","o":["el despertar se construye con la disciplina y el mérito propios","un maestro vivo concede el despertar a los alumnos dignos","decir el nombre muchas veces acumula mérito para nacer allí","el nacimiento en la Tierra Pura es obra del voto de Amida"]}},{"id":"BUDDHISM-s15-03","day":1279,"d":3,"q":"In the Nyingma school of Tibetan Buddhism, what is a terma?","o":["a teaching Padmasambhava hid, later found by a terton","a vow a monk takes at full ordination, kept for life","a sand mandala made for one initiation, then swept away","a prayer wheel filled with mantras on rolled-up paper"],"a":0,"es":{"q":"En la escuela Nyingma del budismo tibetano, ¿qué es un terma?","o":["una enseñanza ocultada por Padmasambhava y hallada luego por un terton","un voto que un monje toma en la ordenación plena y guarda de por vida","un mandala de arena hecho para una iniciación y luego barrido","una rueda de oración llena de mantras en papel enrollado"]}},{"id":"BUDDHISM-s15-04","day":1288,"d":3,"q":"In Atisha's Lamp for the Path to Enlightenment, the basis of the Tibetan lamrim (\"stages of the path\"), practitioners are sorted into three kinds of person. What marks the person of the highest scope?","o":["seeks a good rebirth within the round of lives","seeks personal freedom from the round of rebirth","seeks awakening so all beings can be freed too","seeks long life and wealth in this present life"],"a":2,"es":{"q":"En la Lámpara para el camino a la iluminación de Atisha, base del lamrim tibetano (\"etapas del camino\"), los practicantes se ordenan en tres tipos de persona. ¿Qué distingue a la persona de alcance superior?","o":["busca un buen renacimiento dentro de la rueda de vidas","busca su propia liberación de la rueda del renacimiento","busca el despertar para que todos los seres se liberen","busca larga vida y riqueza en esta vida presente"]}},{"id":"BUDDHISM-s15-05","day":1309,"d":4,"q":"In Vajrayana deity yoga, the practitioner visualizes themselves as an awakened figure such as Tara. Why do Tibetan teachers insist that this figure be understood as empty, like a rainbow?","o":["so the deity is pleased by offerings made from afar","so the practice loosens the ego instead of feeding it","because the figure is mere art with no tie to awakening","because a solid figure is kept for initiated monks"],"a":1,"es":{"q":"En el yoga de la deidad del Vajrayana, el practicante se visualiza como una figura despierta, como Tara. ¿Por qué los maestros tibetanos insisten en entender esa figura como vacía, como un arcoíris?","o":["para que la deidad se agrade con ofrendas hechas de lejos","para que la práctica afloje el ego en vez de alimentarlo","porque la figura es solo arte, sin relación con el despertar","porque una figura sólida se reserva a monjes iniciados"]}},{"id":"BUDDHISM-s15-06","day":1298,"d":3,"q":"A student of the Tibetan Seven Points of Mind Training practices tonglen for a friend who is grieving. As the practice is taught, how does the student use the breath?","o":["breathes in the friend's peace, breathes out own sorrow","breathes in the deity's light, breathes out the grief","holds the breath and silently repeats the friend's name","breathes in the friend's pain, breathes out ease"],"a":3,"es":{"q":"Un estudiante de los Siete puntos del entrenamiento mental tibetano practica tonglen por un amigo que está en duelo. Tal como se enseña la práctica, ¿cómo usa la respiración?","o":["inhala la paz del amigo y exhala su propia tristeza","inhala la luz de la deidad y exhala el duelo del amigo","contiene el aliento y repite en silencio el nombre del amigo","inhala el dolor del amigo y le exhala bienestar"]}}],[{"id":"BUDDHISM-s16-01","day":1333,"d":4,"q":"in Zhiyi's Tiantai school, in its highest ('round') teaching, how are the three truths of emptiness, the provisional and the middle related?","o":["fused as one, each truth containing the other two","separate stages, climbed one after the other in order","only the middle is true; the other two are false views","emptiness is ultimate; the other two are conventional"],"a":0,"es":{"q":"en la escuela Tiantai de Zhiyi, en su enseñanza más alta (la 'redonda'), ¿cómo se relacionan las tres verdades: la vacuidad, lo provisional y el medio?","o":["unidas en una, cada verdad contiene a las otras dos","etapas separadas, que se suben una tras otra en orden","solo el medio es verdad; las otras dos son vistas falsas","la vacuidad es lo último; las otras dos son convencionales"]}},{"id":"BUDDHISM-s16-02","day":1336,"d":4,"q":"in the Huayan (Flower Garland) school, what does the teaching of the non-obstruction of event and event (shishi wu'ai) say about particular things?","o":["all of them dissolve into one undivided substance","they are illusions that hide the true principle","each holds all others, yet stays fully itself","they meet only in principle, never as events"],"a":2,"es":{"q":"en la escuela Huayan (Guirnalda de Flores), ¿qué dice la enseñanza de la no obstrucción entre evento y evento (shishi wu'ai) sobre las cosas particulares?","o":["todas se disuelven en una sola sustancia indivisa","son ilusiones que esconden el verdadero principio","cada una contiene a todas y sigue siendo ella misma","solo se encuentran en el principio, nunca como eventos"]}},{"id":"BUDDHISM-s16-03","day":1343,"d":2,"q":"in Nichiren Buddhism, what is inscribed in large letters down the center of the gohonzon, the scroll practitioners chant before?","o":["the nembutsu, Namu Amida Butsu","the daimoku, Namu-myoho-renge-kyo","the mani mantra, om mani padme hum","the Heart Sutra's mantra, gate gate"],"a":1,"es":{"q":"en el budismo de Nichiren, ¿qué está escrito en letras grandes en el centro del gohonzon, el pergamino ante el cual se recita?","o":["el nembutsu, Namu Amida Butsu","el daimoku, Namu-myoho-renge-kyo","el mantra mani, om mani padme hum","el mantra del Sutra del Corazón"]}},{"id":"BUDDHISM-s16-04","day":1394,"d":3,"q":"in the Dhammacakkappavattana Sutta, the Buddha's first sermon at the Deer Park, what is to be done with the second noble truth, the origin of suffering?","o":["it is to be understood","it is to be abandoned","it is to be realized","it is to be developed"],"a":1,"es":{"q":"en el Dhammacakkappavattana Sutta, el primer sermón del Buda en el Parque de los Ciervos, ¿qué hay que hacer con la segunda noble verdad, el origen del sufrimiento?","o":["hay que comprenderla","hay que abandonarla","hay que realizarla","hay que desarrollarla"]}},{"id":"BUDDHISM-s16-05","day":1406,"d":4,"q":"the Brahma's Net Sutra (Fanwang jing) sets out the bodhisattva precepts widely taken in East Asian Buddhism. If someone who wronged a precept-holder sincerely apologizes, what do those precepts require of the precept-holder?","o":["take it only once the harm has been repaid","bring it to the sangha for a ruling first","accept the apology and let the anger go","keep silent, neither accepting nor refusing"],"a":2,"es":{"q":"el Sutra de la Red de Brahma (Fanwang jing) expone los preceptos del bodhisattva que se toman mucho en el budismo de Asia oriental. Si alguien que ofendió a quien guarda los preceptos se disculpa con sinceridad, ¿qué le piden esos preceptos?","o":["aceptarla solo cuando el daño esté reparado","llevarlo primero a la sangha para que decida","aceptar la disculpa y soltar el enojo","callar, sin aceptar ni rechazar la disculpa"]}},{"id":"BUDDHISM-s16-06","day":1417,"d":2,"q":"in the Ullambana Sutra, the Chinese scripture behind the ghost festival, which disciple of the Buddha finds his dead mother among the hungry ghosts?","o":["Ananda, the attendant who heard the most","Mahakashyapa, foremost in ascetic practice","Upali, the master of monastic discipline","Maudgalyayana, foremost in psychic powers"],"a":3,"es":{"q":"en el Sutra Ullambana, la escritura china detrás del festival de los fantasmas, ¿qué discípulo del Buda encuentra a su madre muerta entre los fantasmas hambrientos?","o":["Ananda, el asistente que más escuchó","Mahakashyapa, el primero en la vida austera","Upali, el maestro de la disciplina monástica","Maudgalyayana, el primero en poderes psíquicos"]}}]],"CATHOLIC":[[{"id":"CATHOLIC-s00-01","day":1,"d":1,"q":"At the end of Matthew's Gospel (28:19, Douay-Rheims), Jesus sends the apostles out to baptize. In whose name, the same words Catholics say with the sign of the cross?","o":["the God of Abraham, and of Isaac, and of Jacob","the Lord Jesus Christ, and of his twelve apostles","the Father, and of the Son, and of the Holy Ghost","the Father, and of Moses, and of all the holy prophets"],"a":2,"es":{"q":"Al final del Evangelio de Mateo (28,19), Jesús envía a los apóstoles a bautizar. ¿En el nombre de quién, con las mismas palabras que dicen los católicos al hacer la señal de la cruz?","o":["el Dios de Abraham, de Isaac y de Jacob","el Señor Jesucristo y sus doce apóstoles","el Padre, y del Hijo, y del Espíritu Santo","el Padre, y de Moisés, y de todos los santos profetas"]}},{"id":"CATHOLIC-s00-02","day":2,"d":3,"q":"The Council of Trent taught transubstantiation (Catechism 1376). What does the Church mean by it for the bread and wine at Mass?","o":["their whole substance becomes Christ's body and blood, while they still look like bread and wine","Christ becomes present beside them, while they stay bread and wine in their substance as well","their look and taste turn into flesh and blood, while underneath they remain bread and wine","they stay just as they were and serve as a holy reminder of the meal Jesus shared at the Last Supper"],"a":0,"es":{"q":"El Concilio de Trento enseñó la transubstanciación (Catecismo 1376). ¿Qué quiere decir la Iglesia con eso sobre el pan y el vino en la misa?","o":["toda su sustancia se vuelve el cuerpo y la sangre de Cristo, aunque sigan pareciendo pan y vino","Cristo se hace presente junto a ellos, mientras siguen siendo pan y vino también en su sustancia","su aspecto y su sabor se vuelven carne y sangre, mientras por debajo siguen siendo pan y vino","quedan tal como estaban y sirven como un recuerdo santo de la cena que Jesús compartió la última noche"]}},{"id":"CATHOLIC-s00-03","day":4,"d":1,"q":"On the rosary as Catholics commonly pray it, which prayer is said on each of the ten small beads of a decade?","o":["the Our Father","the Hail Mary","the Glory Be","the Memorare"],"a":1,"es":{"q":"En el rosario tal como lo rezan comúnmente los católicos, ¿qué oración se dice en cada una de las diez cuentas pequeñas de una decena (un misterio)?","o":["el Padre Nuestro","el Ave María","el Gloria","el Acordaos"]}},{"id":"CATHOLIC-s00-04","day":7,"d":3,"q":"How does the Catechism (1667–1670) set sacramentals, such as holy water or a blessed medal, apart from the seven sacraments?","o":["they are signs the Church instituted, which prepare people to receive grace","they are signs Christ instituted, which give grace by the rite performed","they are objects that protect whoever carries them, with or without faith","they are local customs that the Church only puts up with and has never blessed"],"a":0,"es":{"q":"¿Cómo distingue el Catecismo (1667–1670) los sacramentales, como el agua bendita o una medalla bendecida, de los siete sacramentos?","o":["son signos instituidos por la Iglesia, que preparan para recibir la gracia","son signos instituidos por Cristo, que dan la gracia por el rito realizado","son objetos que protegen a quien los lleva, tenga fe o no la tenga","son costumbres locales que la Iglesia tolera pero nunca ha bendecido"]}},{"id":"CATHOLIC-s00-05","day":9,"d":2,"q":"In Luke 1:38 (Douay-Rheims), Mary answers the angel Gabriel: \"be it done to me according to thy word\" (in Latin, fiat). What does the Church see in this answer (Catechism 494)?","o":["her doubt, for which the angel left her unable to speak","a command she had no real freedom to turn down","her wish to wait for Joseph's word before agreeing","her free consent, in faith, to what God asked of her"],"a":3,"es":{"q":"En Lucas 1,38, María le responde al ángel Gabriel: \"hágase en mí según tu palabra\" (en latín, fiat). ¿Qué ve la Iglesia en esta respuesta (Catecismo 494)?","o":["su duda, por la que el ángel la dejó sin poder hablar","una orden que ella no tenía libertad real de rechazar","su deseo de esperar la palabra de José antes de aceptar","su libre consentimiento, en la fe, a lo que Dios le pedía"]}},{"id":"CATHOLIC-s00-06","day":19,"d":3,"q":"A family in Lebanon belongs to the Maronite Church, with its own liturgy partly in Syriac. According to the Second Vatican Council (Orientalium Ecclesiarum 2–3), how is that Church related to the Catholic Church?","o":["an Orthodox church outside communion with the pope","a Latin-rite diocese that has a translated Mass","an Eastern Catholic Church in full communion with Rome","a separate church Rome plans to merge into the Latin rite"],"a":2,"es":{"q":"Una familia en el Líbano pertenece a la Iglesia maronita, con su propia liturgia en parte en siríaco. Según el Concilio Vaticano II (Orientalium Ecclesiarum 2–3), ¿cómo se relaciona esa Iglesia con la Iglesia católica?","o":["una iglesia ortodoxa fuera de la comunión con el papa","una diócesis de rito latino que tiene la misa traducida","una Iglesia católica oriental en plena comunión con Roma","una iglesia aparte que Roma piensa fusionar con el rito latino"]}}],[{"id":"CATHOLIC-s01-01","day":27,"d":2,"q":"In Luke 2:29–32, the old man Simeon takes the infant Jesus in his arms in the Temple and prays \"Now thou dost dismiss thy servant, O Lord.\" By what Latin name is this canticle known?","o":["the Benedictus","the Magnificat","the Nunc Dimittis","the Gloria in excelsis"],"a":2,"es":{"q":"En Lucas 2,29–32, el anciano Simeón toma en brazos al niño Jesús en el Templo y reza: \"Ahora, Señor, despides a tu siervo\". ¿Con qué nombre latino se conoce este cántico?","o":["el Benedictus","el Magníficat","el Nunc Dimittis","el Gloria in excelsis"]}},{"id":"CATHOLIC-s01-02","day":35,"d":3,"q":"John's Gospel ends the story of the water made wine at Cana (John 2:11) by saying what this \"beginning of miracles\" did. What does it say?","o":["it won the crowds of Galilee over to follow him at once","it manifested his glory, and his disciples believed in him","it proved to the Pharisees that he had power to forgive sins","it showed that the wedding laws of Moses no longer applied"],"a":1,"es":{"q":"El Evangelio de Juan termina el relato del agua convertida en vino en Caná (Juan 2,11) diciendo qué logró este \"principio de los signos\". ¿Qué dice?","o":["ganó de inmediato a las multitudes de Galilea para seguirlo","manifestó su gloria, y sus discípulos creyeron en él","probó a los fariseos que tenía poder para perdonar pecados","mostró que las leyes de Moisés sobre las bodas ya no valían"]}},{"id":"CATHOLIC-s01-03","day":46,"d":3,"q":"Luke 15 opens by saying what led Jesus to tell the parables of the lost sheep, the lost coin and the prodigal son. What prompted them?","o":["his disciples asked him to teach them how they ought to pray","a rich young man asked what he must do to gain eternal life","the crowd demanded a sign after he fed the five thousand","Pharisees and scribes murmured that he received sinners"],"a":3,"es":{"q":"Lucas 15 comienza diciendo qué llevó a Jesús a contar las parábolas de la oveja perdida, la moneda perdida y el hijo pródigo. ¿Qué las motivó?","o":["sus discípulos le pidieron que les enseñara cómo debían orar","un joven rico preguntó qué debía hacer para ganar la vida eterna","la multitud exigió un signo después de alimentar a los cinco mil","los fariseos y escribas murmuraban porque recibía a pecadores"]}},{"id":"CATHOLIC-s01-04","day":45,"d":3,"q":"Someone reads Leviticus 19:18, \"love thy neighbour as thyself,\" and says a neighbor means a fellow member of one's own people. By Jesus's closing question in the good Samaritan parable (Luke 10:36–37), who is a neighbor?","o":["whoever shows mercy to the one in need, as the Samaritan did","any fellow Israelite who faithfully keeps the Law of Moses","the priest or the Levite, whose duty it was to give help","anyone who lives in the same town as the one in need"],"a":0,"es":{"q":"Alguien lee Levítico 19,18, \"amarás a tu prójimo como a ti mismo\", y dice que el prójimo es alguien del propio pueblo. Según la pregunta final de Jesús en la parábola del buen samaritano (Lucas 10,36–37), ¿quién es el prójimo?","o":["quien tiene misericordia del necesitado, como el samaritano","cualquier israelita que cumple fielmente la Ley de Moisés","el sacerdote o el levita, que tenían el deber de ayudar","cualquiera que vive en el mismo pueblo que el necesitado"]}},{"id":"CATHOLIC-s01-05","day":79,"d":3,"q":"Pope Pius IX defined the dogma of the Immaculate Conception in 1854 (Ineffabilis Deus). What does that dogma teach?","o":["Mary was kept free from original sin from her conception","Jesus was conceived in Mary's womb without a human father","Mary was taken up body and soul into heavenly glory","Mary remained a virgin before, during and after the birth"],"a":0,"es":{"q":"El papa Pío IX definió el dogma de la Inmaculada Concepción en 1854 (Ineffabilis Deus). ¿Qué enseña ese dogma?","o":["María fue preservada del pecado original al ser concebida","Jesús fue concebido en el seno de María sin un padre humano","María fue llevada en cuerpo y alma a la gloria del cielo","María siguió siendo virgen antes, durante y después del parto"]}},{"id":"CATHOLIC-s01-06","day":80,"d":2,"q":"The Council of Ephesus in 431 sided with Cyril of Alexandria against Nestorius and upheld which title for Mary?","o":["Christotokos, Christ-bearer","Anthropotokos, man-bearer","Theodochos, God-receiver","Theotokos, God-bearer"],"a":3,"es":{"q":"El Concilio de Éfeso, en el año 431, dio la razón a Cirilo de Alejandría frente a Nestorio y sostuvo ¿qué título para María?","o":["Christotokos, Madre de Cristo","Anthropotokos, madre del hombre","Theodochos, receptora de Dios","Theotokos, Madre de Dios"]}}],[{"id":"CATHOLIC-s02-01","day":103,"d":2,"q":"The Angelus, prayed traditionally at morning, noon and evening, begins \"The angel of the Lord declared unto Mary.\" Which Gospel event does it recall?","o":["the angel's message to Joseph in a dream","the angel Gabriel's announcement to Mary","the angel's news to the shepherds at night","the angel's word to the women at the tomb"],"a":1,"es":{"q":"El Ángelus, que tradicionalmente se reza por la mañana, al mediodía y por la tarde, empieza \"El ángel del Señor anunció a María\". ¿Qué hecho del Evangelio recuerda?","o":["el mensaje del ángel a José en un sueño","el anuncio del ángel Gabriel a María","la noticia del ángel a los pastores de noche","la palabra del ángel a las mujeres en el sepulcro"]}},{"id":"CATHOLIC-s02-02","day":120,"d":3,"q":"In 2002 Pope John Paul II added the luminous mysteries (the mysteries of light) to the rosary. Which event is one of them?","o":["the Finding in the Temple","the Agony in the Garden","the Wedding at Cana","the Descent of the Spirit"],"a":2,"es":{"q":"En 2002 el papa Juan Pablo II añadió al rosario los misterios luminosos (los misterios de luz). ¿Cuál de estos es uno de ellos?","o":["el Niño hallado en el Templo","la Oración en el Huerto","las Bodas de Caná","la Venida del Espíritu"]}},{"id":"CATHOLIC-s02-03","day":114,"d":3,"q":"In the Catholic teaching called transubstantiation (Council of Trent; Catechism 1376), what changes at the consecration of the bread and wine?","o":["their appearances become flesh and blood, while their substance stays the same","their substance becomes Christ's body and blood, while the appearances remain","they are blessed as holy signs and remain bread and wine in their substance","the bread becomes Christ's body, while the wine remains a sign of his blood"],"a":1,"es":{"q":"En la enseñanza católica llamada transustanciación (Concilio de Trento; Catecismo 1376), ¿qué cambia en la consagración del pan y el vino?","o":["sus apariencias se vuelven carne y sangre, y su sustancia sigue igual","su sustancia se vuelve el cuerpo y la sangre de Cristo, y quedan las apariencias","se bendicen como signos santos y siguen siendo pan y vino en su sustancia","el pan se vuelve el cuerpo de Cristo, y el vino sigue siendo signo de su sangre"]}},{"id":"CATHOLIC-s02-04","day":130,"d":3,"q":"According to the Catechism (1514), who may receive the sacrament of the anointing of the sick?","o":["a person in the last hours before death","anyone who has gone to confession that year","anyone beginning to be in danger from illness or age","priests and religious who are seriously ill"],"a":2,"es":{"q":"Según el Catecismo (1514), ¿quién puede recibir el sacramento de la unción de los enfermos?","o":["una persona en sus últimas horas antes de morir","cualquiera que se haya confesado ese año","quien empieza a estar en peligro por enfermedad o vejez","sacerdotes y religiosos que están gravemente enfermos"]}},{"id":"CATHOLIC-s02-05","day":137,"d":3,"q":"Under the seal of confession (Catechism 1467; Code of Canon Law 983), what may a priest reveal about the sins he hears?","o":["serious crimes, once the police ask him","whatever his bishop asks him to report","the sins, as long as he hides the name","nothing, to anyone, for any reason"],"a":3,"es":{"q":"Bajo el sigilo de la confesión (Catecismo 1467; Código de Derecho Canónico 983), ¿qué puede revelar un sacerdote de los pecados que escucha?","o":["los delitos graves, si la policía se lo pide","lo que su obispo le pida informar","los pecados, si oculta el nombre","nada, a nadie, por ningún motivo"]}},{"id":"CATHOLIC-s02-06","day":126,"d":3,"q":"A woman was validly baptized as a baby. Years later her family joins a new parish and asks to have her baptized again. What does Catholic teaching say (Catechism 1272)?","o":["it can't be repeated: it marks the soul for good","it may be repeated once she is old enough to choose","it is repeated in each new parish she joins","it may be repeated if she has sinned seriously"],"a":0,"es":{"q":"Una mujer fue bautizada válidamente de bebé. Años después, su familia se une a una nueva parroquia y pide que la bauticen otra vez. ¿Qué dice la enseñanza católica (Catecismo 1272)?","o":["no se repite: marca el alma para siempre","puede repetirse cuando tenga edad para elegir","se repite en cada nueva parroquia a la que va","puede repetirse si ella ha pecado gravemente"]}}],[{"id":"CATHOLIC-s03-01","day":157,"d":2,"q":"Why is the shepherd psalm (\"The Lord ruleth me\") numbered 22 in the Douay-Rheims Bible but 23 in most modern Bibles?","o":["it lists the psalms in the order they were written","it follows the old Greek and Latin psalm numbering","it leaves out one early psalm found in the Hebrew","it counts the title of each psalm as a psalm itself"],"a":1,"es":{"q":"¿Por qué el salmo del pastor (\"El Señor me gobierna\") lleva el número 22 en la Biblia Douay-Rheims y el 23 en la mayoría de las Biblias modernas?","o":["ordena los salmos según cuándo fueron escritos","sigue la antigua numeración griega y latina","omite un salmo antiguo que está en el hebreo","cuenta el título de cada salmo como otro salmo"]}},{"id":"CATHOLIC-s03-02","day":171,"d":2,"q":"The heading of Psalm 50 [51], the Miserere (\"Have mercy on me, O God\"), ties it to which moment in the life of King David?","o":["his flight from the revolt of his son Absalom","his bringing of the ark of God into Jerusalem","his anointing by Samuel while still a shepherd","Nathan's rebuke after his sin with Bathsheba"],"a":3,"es":{"q":"El encabezado del Salmo 50 [51], el Miserere (\"Ten piedad de mí, oh Dios\"), lo une a ¿qué momento de la vida del rey David?","o":["su huida ante la rebelión de su hijo Absalón","su traslado del arca de Dios a Jerusalén","su unción por Samuel cuando aún era pastor","el reproche de Natán por su pecado con Betsabé"]}},{"id":"CATHOLIC-s03-03","day":162,"d":3,"q":"On the cross, Jesus cries, \"My God, my God, why hast thou forsaken me?\" (Mark 15:34). Why do many readers, following the Church Fathers, hear more than despair in this cry?","o":["it opens a psalm that ends in praise and trust in God","in Aramaic the words are a blessing, not a question","Mark says he spoke the words to the crowd, not to God","the line is a later addition missing from early copies"],"a":0,"es":{"q":"En la cruz, Jesús grita: \"Dios mío, Dios mío, ¿por qué me has abandonado?\" (Marcos 15,34). ¿Por qué muchos lectores, siguiendo a los Padres de la Iglesia, oyen en ese grito algo más que desesperación?","o":["abre un salmo que termina en alabanza y confianza","en arameo esas palabras son una bendición, no una pregunta","Marcos dice que se las dirigió a la gente, no a Dios","la frase es un añadido tardío ausente en copias antiguas"]}},{"id":"CATHOLIC-s03-04","day":205,"d":3,"q":"In Mark 5:21–43, the healing of a woman who had bled for twelve years is told inside the story of Jairus's dying daughter. Which details tie the two stories together?","o":["both are healed in the synagogue on a sabbath","both are healed by a word spoken from far away","each is a \"daughter,\" and twelve years mark both","both are foreigners who at first argue with Jesus"],"a":2,"es":{"q":"En Marcos 5,21–43, la curación de una mujer que llevaba doce años con hemorragias se cuenta dentro del relato de la hija moribunda de Jairo. ¿Qué detalles unen los dos relatos?","o":["las dos son sanadas en la sinagoga en sábado","las dos son sanadas con una palabra a distancia","ambas son \"hija\" y doce años marcan a las dos","ambas son extranjeras y primero discuten con Jesús"]}},{"id":"CATHOLIC-s03-05","day":213,"d":4,"q":"At Bethsaida (Mark 8:22–26) a blind man first sees \"men as it were trees, walking\" and sees clearly only after a second touch. Mark sets this between the disciples' failure to understand (8:14–21) and Peter's confession (8:27–33). What do many commentators take the healing to picture?","o":["the crowds, who stay unconvinced after many signs","the Pharisees, whose blindness can never be healed","the gospel spreading slowly from Galilee to Rome","the disciples, who see partly and need more"],"a":3,"es":{"q":"En Betsaida (Marcos 8,22–26), un ciego primero ve \"hombres como árboles que andan\" y solo ve con claridad después de un segundo toque. Marcos lo coloca entre la falta de comprensión de los discípulos (8,14–21) y la confesión de Pedro (8,27–33). ¿Qué ven muchos comentaristas representado en esta curación?","o":["a la gente, que no se convence tras muchos signos","a los fariseos, cuya ceguera nunca puede sanar","al evangelio, que avanza despacio de Galilea a Roma","a los discípulos, que ven en parte y necesitan más"]}},{"id":"CATHOLIC-s03-06","day":222,"d":3,"q":"A new citizen asks how a Catholic should regard paying taxes to a secular state. In light of \"Render to Caesar\" (Mark 12:17), what does the Catechism teach?","o":["taxes are a civic matter outside morality; faith is silent on them","paying just taxes is a moral duty, while God keeps the first claim","taxes bind in conscience only when the state shares the faith","paying taxes is a counsel of perfection, praised but not required"],"a":1,"es":{"q":"Un ciudadano nuevo pregunta cómo debe ver un católico el pago de impuestos a un Estado laico. A la luz de \"Dad al César\" (Marcos 12,17), ¿qué enseña el Catecismo?","o":["los impuestos son asunto cívico ajeno a la moral; la fe calla","pagar impuestos justos es un deber moral; Dios conserva el primer lugar","los impuestos obligan en conciencia solo si el Estado comparte la fe","pagar impuestos es un consejo de perfección, alabado pero no exigido"]}}],[{"id":"CATHOLIC-s04-01","day":233,"d":2,"q":"in the Ladder of Monks by Guigo II, the classic outline of lectio divina (\"holy reading\"), which rung comes right after meditatio, meditation?","o":["lectio (reading)","collatio (discussion)","oratio (prayer)","contemplatio (gazing)"],"a":2,"es":{"q":"en la Escala de los monjes de Guigo II, el esquema clásico de la lectio divina (\"lectura santa\"), ¿qué peldaño viene justo después de la meditatio, la meditación?","o":["lectio (lectura)","collatio (conversación)","oratio (oración)","contemplatio (mirada)"]}},{"id":"CATHOLIC-s04-02","day":241,"d":2,"q":"in the Liturgy of the Hours, the canticle of Simeon, the Nunc Dimittis (\"now thou dost dismiss thy servant, O Lord\", Luke 2:29), is sung at which hour?","o":["Compline, night prayer","Lauds, morning prayer","Vespers, evening prayer","Terce, mid-morning prayer"],"a":0,"es":{"q":"en la Liturgia de las Horas, el cántico de Simeón, el Nunc Dimittis (\"ahora, Señor, despides a tu siervo\", Lucas 2:29), ¿en qué hora se canta?","o":["Completas, oración de la noche","Laudes, oración de la mañana","Vísperas, oración de la tarde","Tercia, oración de media mañana"]}},{"id":"CATHOLIC-s04-03","day":262,"d":3,"q":"in The Dark Night (book 1, chapter 9), St. John of the Cross gives signs that dryness in prayer is the night of the senses and not lukewarmness. which is one of his signs?","o":["the soul finds fresh comfort in created things","the soul keeps a painful care to serve God","the soul gains vivid images in its meditation","the soul stops caring whether it serves God"],"a":1,"es":{"q":"en La noche oscura (libro 1, capítulo 9), san Juan de la Cruz da señales de que la sequedad en la oración es la noche del sentido y no tibieza. ¿cuál es una de sus señales?","o":["el alma halla nuevo gusto en las cosas creadas","el alma teme con pena no servir bien a Dios","el alma recibe imágenes vivas en su meditación","el alma deja de preocuparse por servir a Dios"]}},{"id":"CATHOLIC-s04-04","day":265,"d":3,"q":"in the Ascent of Mount Carmel (1.11), St. John of the Cross says a bird tied by a thin thread cannot fly any more than one tied by a cord. what is his point?","o":["natural appetites must be fully removed before prayer begins","a thin thread matters less, since it can be broken at any time","grave sins hold back the soul, while small faults do no harm","a small attachment kept on purpose still holds the soul back"],"a":3,"es":{"q":"en la Subida del Monte Carmelo (1.11), san Juan de la Cruz dice que un ave atada con un hilo delgado no puede volar más que una atada con un cordel. ¿qué quiere decir?","o":["los apetitos naturales deben quitarse del todo antes de orar","un hilo delgado importa menos, pues se rompe en cualquier momento","los pecados graves frenan al alma, y las faltas pequeñas no dañan","un pequeño apego querido a propósito aparta al alma de Dios"]}},{"id":"CATHOLIC-s04-05","day":304,"d":3,"q":"what did the Council of Chalcedon (451) define about Jesus Christ?","o":["one person in two natures, divine and human, without confusion","two persons, one divine and one human, joined by a moral union","one nature in which divinity and humanity are blended together","a human person adopted as God's Son at his baptism in the Jordan"],"a":0,"es":{"q":"¿qué definió el Concilio de Calcedonia (451) sobre Jesucristo?","o":["una persona en dos naturalezas, divina y humana, sin confusión","dos personas, una divina y otra humana, unidas por un lazo moral","una sola naturaleza en la que se mezclan lo divino y lo humano","un hombre adoptado como Hijo de Dios en su bautismo en el Jordán"]}},{"id":"CATHOLIC-s04-06","day":311,"d":3,"q":"a man does something gravely wrong, freely and on purpose, but through no fault of his own he never knew it was wrong. under the Catechism's three conditions for mortal sin (CCC 1857), which one is missing?","o":["grave matter in the act","full knowledge of wrong","deliberate, free consent","a warning from a priest"],"a":1,"es":{"q":"un hombre hace algo gravemente malo, libremente y a propósito, pero sin culpa suya nunca supo que era malo. según las tres condiciones del Catecismo para el pecado mortal (CIC 1857), ¿cuál falta?","o":["materia grave en el acto","plena conciencia del mal","consentimiento deliberado","un aviso de un sacerdote"]}}],[{"id":"CATHOLIC-s05-01","day":334,"d":3,"q":"the Catechism (CCC 337) speaks of the six days of creation in Genesis 1. how does it say Scripture presents God's work there?","o":["as a scientific record of how long each age of the earth lasted","as a literal timetable every Catholic is bound to hold as fact","as symbols of God's ordered work, crowned by the day of rest","as a borrowed myth that tells the reader nothing about God at all"],"a":2,"es":{"q":"el Catecismo (CIC 337) habla de los seis días de la creación en Génesis 1. ¿cómo dice que la Escritura presenta allí la obra de Dios?","o":["como un registro científico de cuánto duró cada era de la tierra","como un horario literal que todo católico debe tener por hecho","como símbolos de la obra ordenada de Dios, que culmina en el descanso","como un mito prestado que no le dice nada al lector sobre Dios"]}},{"id":"CATHOLIC-s05-02","day":384,"d":2,"q":"in Numbers 6:22–27, God gives the blessing \"the Lord bless thee, and keep thee.\" whom does God tell to bless the children of Israel with these words?","o":["Moses and the seventy elders of Israel","Aaron and his sons, the priests","Joshua and the leaders of the tribes","David and the Levites who sing"],"a":1,"es":{"q":"en Números 6:22–27, Dios da la bendición \"el Señor te bendiga y te guarde\". ¿a quién le dice Dios que bendiga a los hijos de Israel con estas palabras?","o":["a Moisés y a los setenta ancianos de Israel","a Aarón y a sus hijos, los sacerdotes","a Josué y a los jefes de las tribus","a David y a los levitas cantores"]}},{"id":"CATHOLIC-s05-03","day":411,"d":3,"q":"a retreat leader wants an Old Testament scene showing that God may come to a prophet not in a mighty sign but in quiet. which scene fits best?","o":["Elijah at Horeb, hearing a gentle whisper after the fire","Elijah on Carmel, calling fire down on the altar","Moses at Sinai, amid the thunder, smoke and a loud trumpet","Isaiah in the Temple, as the seraphim cry holy"],"a":0,"es":{"q":"un guía de retiro busca una escena del Antiguo Testamento que muestre que Dios puede venir a un profeta no en una gran señal sino en el silencio. ¿qué escena encaja mejor?","o":["Elías en el Horeb, oyendo un susurro suave tras el fuego","Elías en el Carmelo, haciendo bajar fuego sobre el altar","Moisés en el Sinaí, entre truenos, humo y trompeta","Isaías en el Templo, mientras los serafines claman santo"]}},{"id":"CATHOLIC-s05-04","day":418,"d":3,"q":"the Church's list of the seven gifts of the Holy Spirit (wisdom, understanding, counsel, fortitude, knowledge, piety, fear of the Lord) is drawn from which Old Testament book?","o":["the Book of Proverbs","the Book of Wisdom","the Book of Sirach","the Book of Isaiah"],"a":3,"es":{"q":"la lista de la Iglesia de los siete dones del Espíritu Santo (sabiduría, entendimiento, consejo, fortaleza, ciencia, piedad, temor de Dios) viene de ¿qué libro del Antiguo Testamento?","o":["el libro de los Proverbios","el libro de la Sabiduría","el libro del Eclesiástico","el libro de Isaías"]}},{"id":"CATHOLIC-s05-05","day":423,"d":3,"q":"in Jeremiah 31:31–34, God promises a new covenant with the house of Israel. how does it differ from the covenant made when he led their fathers out of Egypt?","o":["its law will be carved again on new stone tablets","its law will be written by God in their hearts","its sacrifices will be offered by a new tribe of priests","its promise will pass from Israel to Babylon"],"a":1,"es":{"q":"en Jeremías 31:31–34, Dios promete una nueva alianza con la casa de Israel. ¿en qué se distingue de la alianza que hizo cuando sacó a sus padres de Egipto?","o":["su ley será tallada otra vez en nuevas tablas de piedra","su ley será escrita por Dios en sus corazones","sus sacrificios los ofrecerá una nueva tribu de sacerdotes","su promesa pasará de Israel a Babilonia"]}},{"id":"CATHOLIC-s05-06","day":441,"d":3,"q":"in 2 Maccabees 12:43–46, after a battle, Judas Maccabeus sends silver to Jerusalem for a sacrifice. why, according to the text?","o":["so the fallen might be loosed from their sins","so the priests would give thanks for the victory won","so the bodies of the fallen could be bought back","so the camp would be cleansed of the idols' charms"],"a":0,"es":{"q":"en 2 Macabeos 12:43–46, después de una batalla, Judas Macabeo envía plata a Jerusalén para un sacrificio. ¿por qué, según el texto?","o":["para que los caídos fueran librados de sus pecados","para que los sacerdotes dieran gracias por la victoria","para que se pudieran rescatar los cuerpos de los caídos","para que el campamento quedara limpio de amuletos de ídolos"]}}],[{"id":"CATHOLIC-s06-01","day":447,"d":2,"q":"Simeon's song when he takes the child Jesus in the Temple (Luke 2:29–32, the Nunc Dimittis: \"Now thou dost dismiss thy servant, O Lord\") is said every day in which hour of the Liturgy of the Hours?","o":["Morning Prayer (Lauds)","Evening Prayer (Vespers)","Midday Prayer (Sext)","Night Prayer (Compline)"],"a":3,"es":{"q":"El cántico de Simeón cuando toma en brazos al niño Jesús en el Templo (Lucas 2,29–32, el Nunc Dimittis: \"Ahora, Señor, puedes dejar ir a tu siervo\") se reza cada día en ¿cuál hora de la Liturgia de las Horas?","o":["Oración de la mañana (Laudes)","Oración de la tarde (Vísperas)","Oración de mediodía (Sexta)","Oración de la noche (Completas)"]}},{"id":"CATHOLIC-s06-02","day":488,"d":2,"q":"On the road to Emmaus (Luke 24:13–35), two disciples walk for miles with the risen Jesus without knowing him. At what moment, Luke says, were their eyes opened so that they knew him?","o":["in the breaking of the bread","when they saw the empty tomb","when he called them each by name","when he said, peace be to you"],"a":0,"es":{"q":"En el camino de Emaús (Lucas 24,13–35), dos discípulos caminan kilómetros con Jesús resucitado sin reconocerlo. ¿En qué momento, según Lucas, se les abrieron los ojos y lo reconocieron?","o":["en el momento de partir el pan","cuando vieron el sepulcro vacío","cuando los llamó por su nombre","al decirles: la paz con ustedes"]}},{"id":"CATHOLIC-s06-03","day":475,"d":2,"q":"In Jesus' parable of the Pharisee and the publican, the tax collector (Luke 18:9–14), which man \"went down into his house justified,\" and on what ground?","o":["the Pharisee, who fasted and tithed","the publican, who humbled himself","both, since each had gone to pray","neither, since both judged others"],"a":1,"es":{"q":"En la parábola de Jesús sobre el fariseo y el publicano, el cobrador de impuestos (Lucas 18,9–14), ¿cuál de los dos \"bajó a su casa justificado\", y por qué razón?","o":["el fariseo, que ayunaba y daba el diezmo","el publicano, que se humilló ante Dios","los dos, porque los dos fueron a orar","ninguno, porque los dos juzgaban a otros"]}},{"id":"CATHOLIC-s06-04","day":496,"d":3,"q":"The Gospel of John calls Jesus' miracles \"signs\" (Greek semeia), beginning with water made wine at Cana, where he \"manifested his glory\" (John 2:11). Why does John use that word for them?","o":["they were proofs given to satisfy the Pharisees","they foretold the Temple's coming destruction","they reveal his glory and lead to faith in him","they were acts he kept hidden from the crowds"],"a":2,"es":{"q":"El Evangelio de Juan llama \"signos\" (en griego semeia) a los milagros de Jesús, empezando por el agua convertida en vino en Caná, donde \"manifestó su gloria\" (Juan 2,11). ¿Por qué Juan usa esa palabra para ellos?","o":["eran pruebas para dejar contentos a los fariseos","anunciaban la próxima destrucción del Templo","revelan su gloria y llevan a creer en él","eran actos que ocultaba a la multitud"]}},{"id":"CATHOLIC-s06-05","day":533,"d":3,"q":"After the Resurrection, by the Sea of Galilee, Jesus asks Peter three times, \"lovest thou me?\" and each time gives him a charge: feed my lambs, feed my sheep (John 21:15–17). Since St. Augustine, why has the threefold question been explained?","o":["to undo his three denials, one by one","to match the three days in the tomb","to echo the three tents Peter offered","to recall the three years of his ministry"],"a":0,"es":{"q":"Después de la Resurrección, junto al mar de Galilea, Jesús le pregunta tres veces a Pedro \"¿me amas?\" y cada vez le da un encargo: apacienta mis corderos, apacienta mis ovejas (Juan 21,15–17). Desde san Agustín, ¿cómo se ha explicado la triple pregunta?","o":["para reparar sus tres negaciones, una por una","para evocar los tres días en el sepulcro","para recordar las tres tiendas que Pedro ofreció","para recordar los tres años de su ministerio"]}},{"id":"CATHOLIC-s06-06","day":468,"d":3,"q":"A family plans a dinner and, instead of the rich friends and relatives who would invite them back, asks people who could never host them in return. Which teaching of Jesus in Luke 14 are they following?","o":["sit down in the lowest place at table","first count the cost before you build","be not anxious for what you shall eat","when you make a feast, call the poor"],"a":3,"es":{"q":"Una familia organiza una cena y, en lugar de invitar a los amigos y parientes ricos que luego los invitarían a ellos, invita a personas que nunca podrían devolverles la invitación. ¿Qué enseñanza de Jesús en Lucas 14 están siguiendo?","o":["siéntate en el último lugar de la mesa","calcula primero el costo antes de construir","no te inquietes por lo que vas a comer","cuando des un banquete, invita a los pobres"]}}],[{"id":"CATHOLIC-s07-01","day":545,"d":2,"q":"according to the Acts of the Apostles (11:26), in which city were the disciples first called Christians?","o":["in Jerusalem, on the day of Pentecost","in Damascus, after Saul's baptism","in Antioch, a city of Roman Syria","in Rome, under Paul's house arrest"],"a":2,"es":{"q":"según los Hechos de los Apóstoles (11:26), ¿en qué ciudad se llamó por primera vez cristianos a los discípulos?","o":["en Jerusalén, el día de Pentecostés","en Damasco, tras el bautismo de Saulo","en Antioquía, una ciudad de la Siria romana","en Roma, durante el arresto de Pablo"]}},{"id":"CATHOLIC-s07-02","day":548,"d":3,"q":"at the Council of Jerusalem (Acts 15), what did the apostles and elders decide about Gentiles who came to believe in Christ?","o":["they need not be circumcised or keep the whole Law of Moses","they must be circumcised before they could be baptized","they must keep the Sabbath and all of the food laws","they should form churches apart from Jewish believers"],"a":0,"es":{"q":"en el Concilio de Jerusalén (Hechos 15), ¿qué decidieron los apóstoles y los ancianos sobre los gentiles que llegaban a creer en Cristo?","o":["no tenían que circuncidarse ni guardar toda la Ley de Moisés","tenían que circuncidarse antes de poder ser bautizados","tenían que guardar el sábado y todas las leyes de comida","debían formar iglesias aparte de los creyentes judíos"]}},{"id":"CATHOLIC-s07-03","day":563,"d":3,"q":"in Romans 6:3–4, Paul says that all who are baptized in Christ Jesus are baptized into what?","o":["his baptism by John the Baptist in the Jordan","his death, buried with him to rise to new life","his Transfiguration, to share his shining glory","his ministry, to preach and to heal as he did"],"a":1,"es":{"q":"en Romanos 6:3–4, Pablo dice que todos los bautizados en Cristo Jesús son bautizados en ¿qué?","o":["su bautismo por Juan el Bautista en el Jordán","su muerte, sepultados con él para una vida nueva","su Transfiguración, para compartir su gloria","su ministerio, para predicar y sanar como él"]}},{"id":"CATHOLIC-s07-04","day":573,"d":3,"q":"a parishioner who reads at Mass says the parish has no real need of the volunteers who clean the church. which line from Paul's image of the body of Christ in 1 Corinthians 12 answers him most directly?","o":["the eye cannot say to the hand: I need not thy help","in one Spirit were we all baptized into one body","there are diversities of graces, but the same Spirit","if one member suffer, all the members suffer with it"],"a":0,"es":{"q":"un feligrés que lee en la Misa dice que la parroquia no necesita de verdad a los voluntarios que limpian la iglesia. ¿qué frase de la imagen del cuerpo de Cristo en 1 Corintios 12 le responde más directamente?","o":["el ojo no puede decir a la mano: no necesito de ti","en un solo Espíritu fuimos bautizados en un cuerpo","hay diversidad de dones, pero el Espíritu es el mismo","si un miembro sufre, todos los miembros sufren con él"]}},{"id":"CATHOLIC-s07-05","day":587,"d":4,"q":"in the hymn of Philippians 2:6–8, Christ \"emptied himself\" (in Greek, kenosis). how does Catholic teaching, following the Council of Chalcedon, understand that self-emptying?","o":["he set aside being God for a time while he lived as a man","he poured out his Spirit on the apostles at Pentecost","he emptied the Temple of its sellers and money changers","he took a servant's form and our nature, still fully God"],"a":3,"es":{"q":"en el himno de Filipenses 2:6–8, Cristo \"se anonadó a sí mismo\" (en griego, kénosis). ¿cómo entiende la enseñanza católica, siguiendo el Concilio de Calcedonia, ese vaciarse?","o":["dejó de ser Dios por un tiempo mientras vivió como hombre","derramó su Espíritu sobre los apóstoles en Pentecostés","vació el Templo de sus vendedores y de los cambistas","tomó la forma de siervo y nuestra naturaleza, siendo aún Dios"]}},{"id":"CATHOLIC-s07-06","day":607,"d":2,"q":"the Council of Trent and the Catechism (CCC 1510) point to James 5:14–15, \"let him bring in the priests of the church… anointing him with oil,\" as a root of which sacrament?","o":["the sacrament of Confirmation","the sacrament of Holy Orders","the sacrament of Matrimony","the Anointing of the Sick"],"a":3,"es":{"q":"el Concilio de Trento y el Catecismo (CIC 1510) señalan Santiago 5:14–15, \"llame a los presbíteros de la Iglesia… ungiéndolo con óleo\", como raíz de ¿qué sacramento?","o":["el sacramento de la Confirmación","el sacramento del Orden","el sacramento del Matrimonio","la Unción de los Enfermos"]}}],[{"id":"CATHOLIC-s08-01","day":638,"d":2,"q":"The O Antiphons (\"O Wisdom,\" \"O Root of Jesse,\" \"O Emmanuel\") are sung at Evening Prayer from December 17 to 23. Which Gospel canticle do they frame?","o":["the Benedictus, the Song of Zechariah","the Nunc Dimittis, the Song of Simeon","the Magnificat, the Song of Mary","the Te Deum, the old hymn of praise"],"a":2,"es":{"q":"Las antífonas de la O (\"Oh Sabiduría\", \"Oh Raíz de Jesé\", \"Oh Emmanuel\") se cantan en las Vísperas del 17 al 23 de diciembre. ¿Qué cántico del Evangelio enmarcan?","o":["el Benedictus, el cántico de Zacarías","el Nunc Dimittis, el cántico de Simeón","el Magníficat, el cántico de María","el Te Deum, el antiguo himno de alabanza"]}},{"id":"CATHOLIC-s08-02","day":663,"d":3,"q":"The Roman Missal gives seven Old Testament readings for the Easter Vigil and lets parishes shorten the list. Which reading does it say may never be left out?","o":["the Red Sea crossing (Exodus 14)","the creation of the world (Genesis 1)","the sacrifice of Isaac (Genesis 22)","the new heart and spirit (Ezekiel 36)"],"a":0,"es":{"q":"El Misal Romano propone siete lecturas del Antiguo Testamento para la Vigilia Pascual y permite que las parroquias reduzcan la lista. ¿Qué lectura dice que nunca se puede omitir?","o":["el paso del mar Rojo (Éxodo 14)","la creación del mundo (Génesis 1)","el sacrificio de Isaac (Génesis 22)","el corazón y espíritu nuevos (Ezequiel 36)"]}},{"id":"CATHOLIC-s08-03","day":640,"d":3,"q":"The Christmas Day Gospel is the prologue of John. In Catholic teaching, what does its line \"the Word was made flesh\" (John 1:14) affirm?","o":["the Word only seemed to take on a human body","the eternal Word truly became a human being","a holy man was adopted as God's Son at baptism","the Word first came to exist at Jesus' birth"],"a":1,"es":{"q":"El Evangelio del día de Navidad es el prólogo de Juan. En la enseñanza católica, ¿qué afirma su frase \"el Verbo se hizo carne\" (Juan 1:14)?","o":["el Verbo solo aparentó tener un cuerpo humano","el Verbo eterno se hizo de verdad un ser humano","un hombre santo fue adoptado como Hijo en su bautismo","el Verbo empezó a existir al nacer Jesús"]}},{"id":"CATHOLIC-s08-04","day":652,"d":2,"q":"According to the Catechism (540), the Church's forty days of Lent unite her each year to which event?","o":["the forty days from Easter to the Ascension","Noah's forty days of rain upon the earth","Israel's forty years of exile in Babylon","Jesus' forty days of fasting in the desert"],"a":3,"es":{"q":"Según el Catecismo (540), ¿a qué acontecimiento une cada año a la Iglesia la cuaresma con sus cuarenta días?","o":["los cuarenta días de la Pascua a la Ascensión","los cuarenta días de lluvia del diluvio de Noé","los cuarenta años de Israel exiliado en Babilonia","los cuarenta días de ayuno de Jesús en el desierto"]}},{"id":"CATHOLIC-s08-05","day":688,"d":3,"q":"Pope Pius XI created the feast of Christ the King in his 1925 encyclical Quas Primas. What reason did he give for the new feast?","o":["the world's troubles came from shutting Christ out of public life","Europe's kings needed honor for defending the Church in the war","the Church had just settled its long dispute with the Italian state","the Epiphany needed a later feast to take over its royal theme"],"a":0,"es":{"q":"El papa Pío XI creó la fiesta de Cristo Rey en su encíclica Quas Primas, de 1925. ¿Qué razón dio para la nueva fiesta?","o":["los males del mundo venían de excluir a Cristo de la vida pública","los reyes de Europa merecían honor por defender a la Iglesia en la guerra","la Iglesia acababa de resolver su larga disputa con el Estado italiano","la Epifanía necesitaba una fiesta posterior que tomara su tema real"]}},{"id":"CATHOLIC-s08-06","day":696,"d":4,"q":"A parish reads Isaiah 7:14 (\"a virgin shall conceive\") in Advent and Matthew 1:23 at Christmas, treating them as one promise and its keeping. Which principle, from Saint Augustine and quoted in Dei Verbum 16, does this follow?","o":["read it within the living Tradition of the whole Church","seek what the sacred writers truly meant to affirm","the New hidden in the Old, the Old made plain in the New","attend to the content and unity of the whole of Scripture"],"a":2,"es":{"q":"Una parroquia lee Isaías 7:14 (\"una virgen concebirá\") en Adviento y Mateo 1:23 en Navidad, como una sola promesa y su cumplimiento. ¿Qué principio, de san Agustín y citado en Dei Verbum 16, está siguiendo?","o":["leerla dentro de la Tradición viva de toda la Iglesia","buscar lo que los autores sagrados quisieron afirmar","el Nuevo, oculto en el Antiguo; el Antiguo, claro en el Nuevo","atender al contenido y la unidad de toda la Escritura"]}}],[{"id":"CATHOLIC-s09-01","day":703,"d":2,"q":"Writing to the Christians of Smyrna on his way to martyrdom in Rome (c. 107), which bishop gives the earliest surviving use of the phrase \"the catholic church\"?","o":["Clement of Alexandria","Ignatius of Antioch","Polycarp of Smyrna","Irenaeus of Lyons"],"a":1,"es":{"q":"Al escribir a los cristianos de Esmirna camino a su martirio en Roma (c. 107), ¿qué obispo usa por primera vez, en lo que se conserva, la expresión \"la Iglesia católica\"?","o":["Clemente de Alejandría","Ignacio de Antioquía","Policarpo de Esmirna","Ireneo de Lyon"]}},{"id":"CATHOLIC-s09-02","day":769,"d":2,"q":"At the Council of Nicaea (325), which Greek word did the bishops use to say the Son shares the very being of the Father?","o":["homoousios","homoiousios","Theotokos","hypostasis"],"a":0,"es":{"q":"En el Concilio de Nicea (325), ¿qué palabra griega usaron los obispos para decir que el Hijo comparte el ser mismo del Padre?","o":["homoousios","homoiousios","Theotokos","hypostasis"]}},{"id":"CATHOLIC-s09-03","day":775,"d":3,"q":"The Second Council of Nicaea (787) approved the veneration of icons. According to the reasoning the Catechism quotes from it and from Saint Basil, why is this not idolatry?","o":["a priest's blessing makes the image fit for the worship due God","icons show only Christ, so all the honor goes to God alone","the honor shown to an image passes on to the one it portrays","the wood and paint are offered up to God as a sacrifice of thanks"],"a":2,"es":{"q":"El Segundo Concilio de Nicea (787) aprobó la veneración de los íconos. Según el razonamiento que el Catecismo cita de ese concilio y de san Basilio, ¿por qué esto no es idolatría?","o":["la bendición de un sacerdote hace la imagen digna del culto debido a Dios","los íconos muestran solo a Cristo, así que todo el honor va a Dios","el honor que se da a una imagen pasa a quien ella representa","la madera y la pintura se ofrecen a Dios como sacrificio de gracias"]}},{"id":"CATHOLIC-s09-04","day":788,"d":3,"q":"According to the First Vatican Council's constitution Pastor Aeternus (1870), when is the pope kept from error?","o":["whenever he preaches or gives a public interview as pope","when he issues any decree on Church discipline or law","when he acts together with the cardinals gathered in a consistory","when he solemnly defines faith or morals for the whole Church"],"a":3,"es":{"q":"Según la constitución Pastor Aeternus del Concilio Vaticano I (1870), ¿cuándo es preservado el papa del error?","o":["cada vez que predica o da una entrevista pública como papa","cuando emite cualquier decreto sobre disciplina o ley de la Iglesia","cuando actúa con los cardenales reunidos en un consistorio","cuando define solemnemente fe o moral para toda la Iglesia"]}},{"id":"CATHOLIC-s09-05","day":712,"d":4,"q":"After the persecution under Decius (c. 250), Cyprian of Carthage had to decide about the lapsed, Christians who had sacrificed to the gods. What did he hold, in On the Lapsed and his letters?","o":["they could return after real penance, with bishops deciding together","they could never again be received into the Church's communion","a note of peace from a confessor was enough to readmit them at once","only the bishop of Rome, acting on his own, could decide on their return"],"a":0,"es":{"q":"Tras la persecución de Decio (c. 250), Cipriano de Cartago tuvo que decidir sobre los lapsos, cristianos que habían sacrificado a los dioses. ¿Qué sostuvo en Sobre los lapsos y en sus cartas?","o":["podían volver tras una penitencia real, con los obispos decidiendo juntos","nunca más podían ser recibidos en la comunión de la Iglesia","bastaba una nota de paz de un confesor para readmitirlos enseguida","solo el obispo de Roma, actuando por su cuenta, podía decidir su regreso"]}},{"id":"CATHOLIC-s09-06","day":723,"d":3,"q":"A speaker argues that the Son is the first and greatest creature, made by God before time, through whom God then made everything else. Which early teacher's view does this match, and where was it rejected?","o":["Nestorius's view, rejected at Ephesus in 431","Arius's view, rejected at Nicaea in 325","Pelagius's view, rejected at Carthage in 418","Eutyches's view, rejected at Chalcedon in 451"],"a":1,"es":{"q":"Alguien sostiene que el Hijo es la primera y mayor criatura, hecha por Dios antes del tiempo, por medio de la cual Dios hizo luego todo lo demás. ¿Con qué maestro antiguo coincide esta idea, y dónde fue rechazada?","o":["la idea de Nestorio, rechazada en Éfeso en 431","la idea de Arrio, rechazada en Nicea en 325","la idea de Pelagio, rechazada en Cartago en 418","la idea de Eutiques, rechazada en Calcedonia en 451"]}}],[{"id":"CATHOLIC-s10-01","day":798,"d":3,"q":"Duke William of Aquitaine founded the abbey of Cluny in 910. what did his founding charter do that made the abbey unusual?","o":["placed it under the pope's protection, free of any lord's control","made the duke's own heirs the abbey's hereditary abbots for all time","put the abbey under the direct rule of the local bishop of Mâcon","replaced the Rule of Saint Benedict with a new, stricter rule"],"a":0,"es":{"q":"el duque Guillermo de Aquitania fundó la abadía de Cluny en el año 910. ¿qué hizo su carta de fundación que volvió inusual a la abadía?","o":["la puso bajo la protección del papa, libre del control de cualquier señor","hizo de los herederos del duque los abades hereditarios para siempre","puso la abadía bajo el gobierno directo del obispo de Mâcon","cambió la Regla de san Benito por una regla nueva y más estricta"]}},{"id":"CATHOLIC-s10-02","day":800,"d":3,"q":"in the Proslogion, Saint Anselm of Canterbury builds his single argument for God's existence on one description of God. which is it?","o":["the unmoved mover behind all things that move","that than which nothing greater can be thought","the first cause behind every chain of causes","the necessary being on whom all other things depend"],"a":1,"es":{"q":"en el Proslogion, san Anselmo de Canterbury construye su único argumento sobre la existencia de Dios a partir de una descripción de Dios. ¿cuál es?","o":["el motor inmóvil de todo lo que se mueve","aquello mayor que lo cual nada puede pensarse","la primera causa de toda cadena de causas","el ser necesario del que todo lo demás depende"]}},{"id":"CATHOLIC-s10-03","day":826,"d":3,"q":"how did the Western Schism (1378–1417), with rival claimants to the papacy in Rome and Avignon, finally come to an end?","o":["the Council of Pisa deposed both claimants, and all accepted its pope","the Avignon claimant died, and his cardinals simply went over to Rome","at Constance, one claimant resigned, two were deposed, Martin V chosen","the Holy Roman Emperor chose one claimant and exiled all the others"],"a":2,"es":{"q":"¿cómo terminó por fin el Cisma de Occidente (1378–1417), con papas rivales en Roma y en Aviñón?","o":["el Concilio de Pisa depuso a ambos, y todos aceptaron a su papa","murió el papa de Aviñón, y sus cardenales se pasaron a Roma","en Constanza, uno renunció, dos fueron depuestos y se eligió a Martín V","el emperador del Sacro Imperio eligió a uno y desterró a los otros"]}},{"id":"CATHOLIC-s10-04","day":839,"d":3,"q":"what did Pope Paul III's letter Sublimis Deus (1537) teach about the native peoples of the Americas?","o":["they keep their liberty and property only once they accept baptism","they are human, but must stay under Spanish guardianship until baptized","they must first be gathered into mission towns so they can be taught","they may not lose liberty or property, even while outside the faith"],"a":3,"es":{"q":"¿qué enseñó la carta Sublimis Deus (1537) del papa Pablo III sobre los pueblos nativos de América?","o":["conservan su libertad y sus bienes solo cuando aceptan el bautismo","son humanos, pero deben quedar bajo tutela española hasta bautizarse","primero deben reunirse en pueblos de misión para poder ser enseñados","no pueden perder libertad ni bienes, aunque estén fuera de la fe"]}},{"id":"CATHOLIC-s10-05","day":872,"d":4,"q":"why did Pope Clement XIV dissolve the Society of Jesus (the Jesuits) in 1773 with the brief Dominus ac Redemptor?","o":["under pressure from Catholic kings, for the sake of the Church's peace","because a general council had condemned the Jesuits' teaching as heresy","because the Jesuit superior general had asked for the order to end","because Ignatius's own rule had forbidden the Jesuits to run schools"],"a":0,"es":{"q":"¿por qué el papa Clemente XIV disolvió la Compañía de Jesús (los jesuitas) en 1773 con el breve Dominus ac Redemptor?","o":["por presión de reyes católicos, por el bien de la paz de la Iglesia","porque un concilio general había condenado como herejía su enseñanza","porque el superior general jesuita había pedido que la orden terminara","porque la regla del mismo Ignacio prohibía a los jesuitas tener escuelas"]}},{"id":"CATHOLIC-s10-06","day":863,"d":3,"q":"a shopkeeper with a family asks how to live a devout life. following Saint Francis de Sales's Introduction to the Devout Life, what is the core of his answer?","o":["leave the shop and enter an enclosed religious house","keep the full night prayers of monks along with the shop","practice devotion fitted to her own state and duties","put devotion aside until her children are grown and gone"],"a":2,"es":{"q":"una tendera con familia pregunta cómo vivir una vida devota. según la Introducción a la vida devota de san Francisco de Sales, ¿cuál es el centro de la respuesta?","o":["dejar la tienda y entrar en una casa religiosa de clausura","rezar las oraciones nocturnas de los monjes además de la tienda","vivir la devoción ajustada a su propio estado y sus deberes","dejar de lado la devoción hasta que sus hijos ya hayan crecido"]}}],[{"id":"CATHOLIC-s11-01","day":890,"d":4,"q":"in his Essay on the Development of Christian Doctrine (1845), John Henry Newman asks how a true development of doctrine differs from a corruption. what is his main test?","o":["it is accepted by most believers living at the time","it keeps the same type and principles as what came before","it uses only words already found in the four Gospels","it replaces the older teachings that later ages have outgrown"],"a":1,"es":{"q":"en su Ensayo sobre el desarrollo de la doctrina cristiana (1845), John Henry Newman se pregunta en qué se distingue un verdadero desarrollo de la doctrina de una corrupción. ¿cuál es su prueba principal?","o":["que la acepten la mayoría de los creyentes de su tiempo","que conserve el mismo tipo y los principios de lo anterior","que use solo palabras que ya están en los cuatro Evangelios","que reemplace las enseñanzas antiguas que ya quedaron atrás"]}},{"id":"CATHOLIC-s11-02","day":895,"d":2,"q":"Pope Leo XIII's encyclical Rerum Novarum (1891), often called the start of modern Catholic social teaching, was written mainly about what?","o":["papal infallibility as Vatican I defined it","the Mass celebrated in the people's languages","the Immaculate Conception of the Blessed Virgin Mary","the rights and condition of industrial workers"],"a":3,"es":{"q":"la encíclica Rerum Novarum (1891) del papa León XIII, a menudo vista como el inicio de la doctrina social católica moderna, ¿sobre qué trata principalmente?","o":["la infalibilidad papal definida en el Vaticano I","la misa celebrada en la lengua de cada pueblo","la Inmaculada Concepción de la Virgen María","los derechos y la situación de los obreros"]}},{"id":"CATHOLIC-s11-03","day":901,"d":3,"q":"the decree Quam singulari (1910), issued under Pope Pius X, set the age for a Latin-rite child's first communion. when did it say a child may receive?","o":["on reaching the age of reason, about seven","after being confirmed, at about the age of twelve","once able to explain the whole catechism","at fourteen, after two years of classes"],"a":0,"es":{"q":"el decreto Quam singulari (1910), publicado bajo el papa Pío X, fijó la edad de la primera comunión de un niño de rito latino. ¿cuándo dijo que un niño puede recibirla?","o":["al llegar al uso de razón, hacia los siete años","después de la confirmación, hacia los doce años","cuando pueda explicar todo el catecismo","a los catorce, tras dos años de catequesis"]}},{"id":"CATHOLIC-s11-04","day":918,"d":3,"q":"what does Vatican II's constitution on the liturgy, Sacrosanctum Concilium (1963), say about Latin in the Roman rite?","o":["Latin must be used for every single spoken part of the Mass","Latin is abolished and replaced by local languages","Latin is kept, while local languages may be used more","Latin may be kept only for the Gregorian chant"],"a":2,"es":{"q":"¿qué dice la constitución del Vaticano II sobre la liturgia, Sacrosanctum Concilium (1963), acerca del latín en el rito romano?","o":["el latín debe usarse en todas las partes habladas de la misa","el latín queda abolido y lo reemplazan las lenguas locales","el latín se conserva, y las lenguas locales pueden usarse más","el latín puede conservarse solo para el canto gregoriano"]}},{"id":"CATHOLIC-s11-05","day":948,"d":3,"q":"in Catholic teaching, what does the pope do when he canonizes someone?","o":["he raises a holy person into heaven by his decree","he makes the person holy through the decree","he grants the person worship due only to God","he declares a holiness that was already there"],"a":3,"es":{"q":"en la enseñanza católica, ¿qué hace el papa cuando canoniza a alguien?","o":["eleva por su decreto al cielo a una persona santa","vuelve santa a la persona mediante el decreto","le concede un culto que solo se le debe a Dios","declara una santidad que ya estaba presente"]}},{"id":"CATHOLIC-s11-06","day":949,"d":4,"q":"a nun from a small town has been beatified (declared Blessed) but not yet canonized. under the Church's usual rules, where may her feast be kept in public liturgy?","o":["across the whole Church on the general calendar","in a set place, such as her diocese or her order","nowhere in public, only in private family prayer","in Rome alone, at the tomb of the Apostle Peter"],"a":1,"es":{"q":"una religiosa de un pueblo pequeño fue beatificada (declarada beata) pero aún no canonizada. según las normas habituales de la Iglesia, ¿dónde puede celebrarse su fiesta en la liturgia pública?","o":["en toda la Iglesia, en el calendario general","en un lugar fijo, como su diócesis o su orden","en ningún lugar público, solo en oración privada","solo en Roma, ante la tumba del apóstol Pedro"]}}],[{"id":"CATHOLIC-s12-01","day":1052,"d":2,"q":"in the Guadalupe account, the Nican Mopohua, Juan Diego brings the Lady's sign to Bishop Zumárraga. where does her image appear?","o":["on a stone of the hill of Tepeyac","on Juan Diego's tilma, his cloak","on the wall of the bishop's chapel","on an altar cloth used at the Mass"],"a":1,"es":{"q":"en el relato de Guadalupe, el Nican Mopohua, Juan Diego le lleva al obispo Zumárraga la señal de la Señora. ¿dónde aparece su imagen?","o":["en una piedra del cerro del Tepeyac","en la tilma de Juan Diego, su manta","en la pared de la capilla del obispo","en un mantel del altar usado en misa"]}},{"id":"CATHOLIC-s12-02","day":993,"d":3,"q":"Bernardine of Siena held up a board bearing the letters IHS to honor the Holy Name. where do those three letters come from?","o":["the Latin title Pilate set over the cross","the initials of the Franciscan vows in Latin","the first letters of Jesus' name in Greek","the opening words of the Hail Mary in Latin"],"a":2,"es":{"q":"Bernardino de Siena mostraba una tabla con las letras IHS para honrar el Santo Nombre. ¿de dónde vienen esas tres letras?","o":["del título en latín que Pilato puso en la cruz","de las iniciales de los votos franciscanos en latín","de las primeras letras del nombre de Jesús en griego","de las primeras palabras del avemaría en latín"]}},{"id":"CATHOLIC-s12-03","day":999,"d":3,"q":"in Acts 9:26–27, when Saul comes to Jerusalem after his conversion, Barnabas has to bring him to the apostles and speak for him. why was that needed?","o":["they feared him and doubted he was a disciple","he had not yet been baptized by anyone in Damascus","he spoke only Greek and needed someone to translate","he arrived without a letter from the church at Antioch"],"a":0,"es":{"q":"en Hechos 9,26–27, cuando Saulo llega a Jerusalén después de su conversión, Bernabé tiene que llevarlo a los apóstoles y hablar por él. ¿por qué hacía falta?","o":["le temían y dudaban que fuera discípulo","todavía nadie lo había bautizado en Damasco","solo hablaba griego y necesitaba que alguien tradujera","llegó sin una carta de la iglesia de Antioquía"]}},{"id":"CATHOLIC-s12-04","day":1027,"d":3,"q":"after Matthew the publican is called, Jesus eats with publicans and sinners, and the Pharisees object. he answers with a saying about a physician (Matthew 9:12–13). what does it mean?","o":["illness is a sign of sin, so the sick need forgiving","sinners must be made well before he can eat with them","the publicans were more righteous than the Pharisees","he came for sinners, as a doctor goes to the sick"],"a":3,"es":{"q":"después del llamado de Mateo el publicano, Jesús come con publicanos y pecadores, y los fariseos protestan. él responde con un dicho sobre el médico (Mateo 9,12–13). ¿qué quiere decir?","o":["la enfermedad es señal de pecado, y el enfermo necesita perdón","los pecadores deben sanar antes de que él coma con ellos","los publicanos eran más justos que los fariseos","vino por los pecadores, como el médico va al enfermo"]}},{"id":"CATHOLIC-s12-05","day":1031,"d":4,"q":"in the letter of Jude (verse 9), the archangel Michael, disputing with the devil over the body of Moses, does not curse him but says \"The Lord command thee.\" what does his answer show?","o":["the devil holds rightful power over the body of Moses","he leaves judgment to God instead of claiming it","angels are forbidden to speak to the devil at all","he is weaker than the devil until the end of time"],"a":1,"es":{"q":"en la carta de Judas (versículo 9), el arcángel Miguel, en disputa con el diablo por el cuerpo de Moisés, no lo maldice sino que dice \"El Señor te reprenda\". ¿qué muestra su respuesta?","o":["el diablo tiene un poder legítimo sobre el cuerpo de Moisés","deja el juicio a Dios en lugar de tomarlo para sí","los ángeles tienen prohibido hablarle al diablo","es más débil que el diablo hasta el fin de los tiempos"]}},{"id":"CATHOLIC-s12-06","day":989,"d":3,"q":"in Acts 1:21–22, Peter sets the test for the one who will take Judas's place among the Twelve. by that test, which of these men would qualify?","o":["a man with them from John's baptism to the ascension","a believer who met the risen Lord years later on a road","a Temple priest who came to believe soon after Pentecost","a Pharisee who once heard Jesus teach in Jerusalem"],"a":0,"es":{"q":"en Hechos 1,21–22, Pedro pone la condición para quien ocupará el lugar de Judas entre los Doce. según esa condición, ¿cuál de estos hombres podría ser elegido?","o":["uno que estuvo con ellos del bautismo de Juan a la ascensión","un creyente que vio al Señor resucitado años después en un camino","un sacerdote del Templo que creyó poco después de Pentecostés","un fariseo que una vez oyó a Jesús enseñar en Jerusalén"]}}],[{"id":"CATHOLIC-s13-01","day":1066,"d":3,"q":"the Catechism (CCC 115–118) divides the senses of Scripture into the literal and three spiritual senses. which sense reads a text for what it shows of our final destiny, eternal life with God?","o":["the moral sense","the anagogical sense","the allegorical sense","the literal sense"],"a":1,"es":{"q":"el Catecismo (CIC 115–118) divide los sentidos de la Escritura en el literal y tres sentidos espirituales. ¿qué sentido lee un texto por lo que muestra de nuestro destino final, la vida eterna con Dios?","o":["el sentido moral","el sentido anagógico","el sentido alegórico","el sentido literal"]}},{"id":"CATHOLIC-s13-02","day":1148,"d":3,"q":"which early Christian writer called the Lord's Prayer \"breviarium totius evangelii,\" a summary of the whole gospel, as the Catechism quotes in CCC 2761?","o":["Saint Ambrose","Thomas Aquinas","Tertullian","Saint Augustine"],"a":2,"es":{"q":"¿qué escritor cristiano antiguo llamó al Padrenuestro \"breviarium totius evangelii\", un resumen de todo el Evangelio, como cita el Catecismo en CIC 2761?","o":["San Ambrosio","Tomás de Aquino","Tertuliano","San Agustín"]}},{"id":"CATHOLIC-s13-03","day":1113,"d":3,"q":"the Catechism (CCC 1750–1756) names three sources of the morality of an act: the object chosen, the intention and the circumstances. why can a good intention not make a lie told to help a neighbor into a good act?","o":["an act whose object is evil stays evil, whatever its purpose","intentions count only once the circumstances are all known","only an act's results decide whether it is good or bad","intentions are hidden, so no one can judge them at all"],"a":0,"es":{"q":"el Catecismo (CIC 1750–1756) nombra tres fuentes de la moralidad de un acto: el objeto elegido, la intención y las circunstancias. ¿por qué una buena intención no puede convertir en bueno un acto como mentir para ayudar a un vecino?","o":["un acto cuyo objeto es malo sigue siendo malo, sea cual sea su fin","las intenciones cuentan solo cuando se conocen las circunstancias","solo los resultados de un acto deciden si es bueno o malo","las intenciones están ocultas, así que nadie puede juzgarlas"]}},{"id":"CATHOLIC-s13-04","day":1098,"d":4,"q":"according to the Catechism (CCC 1366–1367), how is the sacrifice of the Mass related to Christ's sacrifice on the cross?","o":["it is a new sacrifice that adds to what the cross achieved","it is only a reminder of the cross, with no sacrifice in it at all","it is the one sacrifice of the cross, made present without blood","it is the Church's own sacrifice, offered apart from Christ"],"a":2,"es":{"q":"según el Catecismo (CIC 1366–1367), ¿cómo se relaciona el sacrificio de la Misa con el sacrificio de Cristo en la cruz?","o":["es un sacrificio nuevo que se suma a lo que logró la cruz","es un recuerdo de la cruz sin ningún sacrificio en él","es el único sacrificio de la cruz, hecho presente sin sangre","es un sacrificio propio de la Iglesia, ofrecido aparte de Cristo"]}},{"id":"CATHOLIC-s13-05","day":1095,"d":4,"q":"the Catechism (CCC 1257) says that God has bound salvation to the sacrament of Baptism, \"but he himself is not bound by his sacraments.\" what does it draw from this?","o":["Baptism is optional for those who have already heard the Gospel","the Church may stop baptizing people who already seek God","a sacrament works only when a person feels its grace","God can save some who die unbaptized, as by blood or desire"],"a":3,"es":{"q":"el Catecismo (CIC 1257) dice que Dios ha vinculado la salvación al sacramento del Bautismo, \"pero él no queda sometido a sus sacramentos\". ¿qué concluye de esto?","o":["el Bautismo es opcional para quien ya ha escuchado el Evangelio","la Iglesia puede dejar de bautizar a quienes ya buscan a Dios","un sacramento actúa solo cuando la persona siente su gracia","Dios puede salvar a algunos sin bautismo, por sangre o por deseo"]}},{"id":"CATHOLIC-s13-06","day":1120,"d":3,"q":"a town's parents run an after-school program that works well. the national government proposes to take it over and run it from the capital. what does the principle of subsidiarity (CCC 1883) advise?","o":["the state takes it over, as it serves the common good best","leave it with the parents, and help them if they need it","hand it to the parish, which should run every social service","leave it alone, and refuse it any help whatever happens"],"a":1,"es":{"q":"los padres de un pueblo dirigen un programa extraescolar que funciona bien. el gobierno nacional propone quedarse con él y dirigirlo desde la capital. ¿qué aconseja el principio de subsidiariedad (CIC 1883)?","o":["que el Estado se quede con él, pues sirve mejor al bien común","dejarlo en manos de los padres, y ayudarlos si lo necesitan","pasarlo a la parroquia, que debería llevar todo servicio social","dejarlo solo y negarle cualquier ayuda, pase lo que pase"]}}],[{"id":"CATHOLIC-s14-01","day":1152,"d":2,"q":"As a young man, Thomas Aquinas was held for many months in his family's castle at Roccasecca. Which religious order were his noble family trying to keep him from joining?","o":["the Benedictines, monks of Monte Cassino","the Dominicans, the Order of Preachers","the Franciscans, the Friars Minor","the Cistercians, the monks of Citeaux"],"a":1,"es":{"q":"De joven, Tomás de Aquino estuvo retenido muchos meses en el castillo de su familia en Roccasecca. ¿A qué orden religiosa intentaba su noble familia impedirle entrar?","o":["los benedictinos, monjes de Montecassino","los dominicos, la Orden de Predicadores","los franciscanos, los Frailes Menores","los cistercienses, los monjes del Císter"]}},{"id":"CATHOLIC-s14-02","day":1202,"d":3,"q":"In chapter 58 of the Rule of Saint Benedict, what three things does the novice promise before the whole community in the oratory?","o":["poverty, chastity and obedience to the abbot","silence, humility and obedience to the Rule","prayer, manual work and lifelong enclosure","stability, conversion of life and obedience"],"a":3,"es":{"q":"En el capítulo 58 de la Regla de san Benito, ¿qué tres cosas promete el novicio ante toda la comunidad en el oratorio?","o":["pobreza, castidad y obediencia al abad","silencio, humildad y obediencia a la Regla","oración, trabajo manual y clausura de por vida","estabilidad, conversión de vida y obediencia"]}},{"id":"CATHOLIC-s14-03","day":1162,"d":3,"q":"In the Summa Theologiae (I, q. 104), Thomas Aquinas compares creatures to air lit by the sun. What is the comparison meant to show?","o":["creatures run on their own, as a clock does once it is wound","creatures are parts of God's own substance, flowing from him","creatures need God to keep them in being at every moment","the world began in time, so it must end at a set time too"],"a":2,"es":{"q":"En la Suma Teológica (I, q. 104), Tomás de Aquino compara a las criaturas con el aire iluminado por el sol. ¿Qué busca mostrar la comparación?","o":["las criaturas funcionan solas, como un reloj al que se le dio cuerda","las criaturas son partes de la sustancia de Dios, que fluyen de él","las criaturas necesitan que Dios las mantenga en el ser a cada momento","el mundo empezó en el tiempo, así que debe terminar en un tiempo fijo"]}},{"id":"CATHOLIC-s14-04","day":1163,"d":3,"q":"Following Saint Augustine, how does Thomas Aquinas define evil in the Summa Theologiae (I, q. 48)?","o":["the lack of a good that ought to be there","a real substance God created to test us","an illusion of the mind with no real effect","a quality built into bodily matter itself"],"a":0,"es":{"q":"Siguiendo a san Agustín, ¿cómo define Tomás de Aquino el mal en la Suma Teológica (I, q. 48)?","o":["la falta de un bien que debería estar ahí","una sustancia real creada por Dios para probarnos","una ilusión de la mente sin ningún efecto real","una cualidad propia de la materia corporal"]}},{"id":"CATHOLIC-s14-05","day":1182,"d":4,"q":"In the Summa Theologiae (II-II, q. 188, a. 6), Thomas Aquinas ranks kinds of religious life. Which does he place highest?","o":["contemplation alone, kept in silence and enclosure","active works alone, like nursing and feeding the poor","contemplating, then handing on its fruit to others","study pursued for its own sake, apart from preaching"],"a":2,"es":{"q":"En la Suma Teológica (II-II, q. 188, a. 6), Tomás de Aquino ordena las formas de vida religiosa. ¿Cuál pone en el lugar más alto?","o":["la sola contemplación, en silencio y clausura","las solas obras activas, como cuidar enfermos","contemplar y luego entregar a otros su fruto","el estudio buscado por sí mismo, sin predicar"]}},{"id":"CATHOLIC-s14-06","day":1192,"d":3,"q":"A monk carries out every task the abbot gives him, but grumbles in his heart the whole time. By the standard of chapter 5 of the Rule of Saint Benedict, what is wrong with his obedience?","o":["nothing: the Rule judges obedience by the finished deed alone","it earns no reward: God sees the grumbling in his heart","he should first have told the abbot the task was too hard","it is still fine, as long as he never grumbles out loud"],"a":1,"es":{"q":"Un monje cumple cada tarea que le da el abad, pero refunfuña en su corazón todo el tiempo. Según el capítulo 5 de la Regla de san Benito, ¿qué falla en su obediencia?","o":["nada: la Regla juzga la obediencia solo por la obra terminada","no gana premio: Dios ve la murmuración en su corazón","debió decir antes al abad que la tarea era demasiado dura","sigue bien, mientras nunca murmure en voz alta"]}}],[{"id":"CATHOLIC-s15-01","day":1255,"d":3,"q":"In Ignatius of Loyola's Spiritual Exercises, the meditation on the Two Standards describes the enemy's plan. Through which three steps does he lead people on to every other vice?","o":["sloth, then envy, then despair","riches, then honor, then pride","fear, then doubt, then anger","pleasures, then lust, then rage"],"a":1,"es":{"q":"En los Ejercicios Espirituales de Ignacio de Loyola, la meditación de las Dos Banderas describe el plan del enemigo. ¿Por qué tres escalones lleva a las personas a todos los demás vicios?","o":["pereza, luego envidia, luego desesperación","riquezas, luego honor, luego soberbia","miedo, luego duda, luego ira","placer, luego lujuria, luego furia"]}},{"id":"CATHOLIC-s15-02","day":1257,"d":3,"q":"A retreatant chose a way of life during a peaceful season of prayer. Now he feels dark, restless and far from God, and wants to drop the choice. Following Ignatius's Rules for the Discernment of Spirits, what should he do?","o":["keep the choice made in the time of peace","drop it, since the darkness shows God's will","make a new choice while the feeling lasts","stop praying until the peace comes back"],"a":0,"es":{"q":"Un ejercitante eligió una forma de vida durante una temporada de oración en paz. Ahora se siente a oscuras, inquieto y lejos de Dios, y quiere dejar esa elección. Según las Reglas de discernimiento de espíritus de Ignacio, ¿qué debe hacer?","o":["mantener la elección hecha en el tiempo de paz","dejarla, ya que la oscuridad muestra la voluntad de Dios","hacer una nueva elección mientras dura el sentimiento","dejar de orar hasta que vuelva la paz"]}},{"id":"CATHOLIC-s15-03","day":1272,"d":3,"q":"The hermits living near the spring on Mount Carmel asked for a written way of life in the early 1200s. Who wrote the Rule of Carmel for them?","o":["Simon Stock, an English prior","John of the Cross, the friar","Albert, patriarch of Jerusalem","Teresa of Ávila, the great reformer"],"a":2,"es":{"q":"Los ermitaños que vivían junto a la fuente del monte Carmelo pidieron una forma de vida por escrito a comienzos del siglo XIII. ¿Quién les escribió la Regla del Carmelo?","o":["Simón Stock, un prior inglés","Juan de la Cruz, el fraile","Alberto, patriarca de Jerusalén","Teresa de Ávila, la gran reformadora"]}},{"id":"CATHOLIC-s15-04","day":1281,"d":3,"q":"In Story of a Soul, Thérèse of Lisieux reads 1 Corinthians 12–13 and concludes that her vocation is love, in the heart of the Church. Why does love answer her longing for every calling?","o":["the Carmelite Rule forbade every other calling","Paul names love as the gift proper to cloistered nuns","her prioress assigned her the work of charity","love moves every member, so it holds every calling"],"a":3,"es":{"q":"En Historia de un alma, Teresa de Lisieux lee 1 Corintios 12–13 y concluye que su vocación es el amor, en el corazón de la Iglesia. ¿Por qué el amor responde a su deseo de tener todas las vocaciones?","o":["la Regla del Carmelo le prohibía toda otra vocación","Pablo presenta el amor como el don propio de las monjas de clausura","su priora le asignó la tarea de la caridad","el amor mueve a cada miembro, así que abarca todas"]}},{"id":"CATHOLIC-s15-05","day":1308,"d":4,"q":"John Paul II wrote of \"structures of sin\" in Sollicitudo Rei Socialis (1987). How does the Catechism describe these structures?","o":["sins committed by institutions, not by persons","the expression and effect of personal sins","the original sin passed down through society","social evils that free persons from all blame"],"a":1,"es":{"q":"Juan Pablo II habló de \"estructuras de pecado\" en Sollicitudo Rei Socialis (1987). ¿Cómo describe el Catecismo estas estructuras?","o":["pecados cometidos por instituciones, no por personas","la expresión y el efecto de pecados personales","el pecado original transmitido por la sociedad","males sociales que libran a las personas de toda culpa"]}},{"id":"CATHOLIC-s15-06","day":1307,"d":4,"q":"In Laborem Exercens (1981), John Paul II teaches the priority of labor over capital. What reason does the letter give?","o":["capital is only things that work has made","workers outnumber those who own the capital","the state should own all means of production","labor is older than money in human history"],"a":0,"es":{"q":"En Laborem Exercens (1981), Juan Pablo II enseña la prioridad del trabajo sobre el capital. ¿Qué razón da la carta?","o":["el capital es un conjunto de cosas hechas por el trabajo","los trabajadores son más que los dueños del capital","el Estado debe poseer todos los medios de producción","el trabajo es más antiguo que el dinero en la historia"]}}],[{"id":"CATHOLIC-s16-01","day":1337,"d":2,"q":"the Marian antiphon Regina Caeli (\"Queen of heaven, rejoice, alleluia\") takes the place of the Angelus during which season of the Church's year?","o":["the Easter season","the Lenten season","the Advent season","the Christmas season"],"a":0,"es":{"q":"la antífona mariana Regina Caeli (\"Reina del cielo, alégrate, aleluya\") reemplaza al Ángelus durante ¿qué tiempo del año litúrgico?","o":["el tiempo de Pascua","el tiempo de Cuaresma","el tiempo de Adviento","el tiempo de Navidad"]}},{"id":"CATHOLIC-s16-02","day":1416,"d":3,"q":"the last canon of the Latin Church's 1983 Code of Canon Law (canon 1752) names what as \"the supreme law in the Church\"?","o":["the authority of the pope","the letter of the canons","the unity of the bishops","the salvation of souls"],"a":3,"es":{"q":"el último canon del Código de Derecho Canónico de 1983 de la Iglesia latina (canon 1752), ¿qué nombra como \"la ley suprema en la Iglesia\"?","o":["la autoridad del papa","la letra de los cánones","la unidad de los obispos","la salvación de las almas"]}},{"id":"CATHOLIC-s16-03","day":1343,"d":3,"q":"according to the Catechism (CCC 67), what is the role of a private revelation, such as an apparition the Church has recognized?","o":["to complete what Christ left unfinished in his revelation","to help people live more fully by Christ's revelation","to add new doctrines that every Catholic must believe","to replace Scripture for those who receive the vision"],"a":1,"es":{"q":"según el Catecismo (CIC 67), ¿cuál es el papel de una revelación privada, como una aparición que la Iglesia ha reconocido?","o":["completar lo que Cristo dejó sin terminar en la revelación","ayudar a vivir más plenamente la revelación de Cristo","añadir doctrinas nuevas que todo católico debe creer","reemplazar la Escritura para quienes reciben la visión"]}},{"id":"CATHOLIC-s16-04","day":1361,"d":4,"q":"in the Eastern rites an infant is baptized, chrismated (confirmed) and given the Eucharist in one celebration. according to the Catechism (CCC 1292), what does this practice bring out?","o":["the bond with the bishop who confirms the infant","the child's arrival at the age of reason","the unity of the three sacraments of initiation","the way chrismation takes the place of baptism"],"a":2,"es":{"q":"en los ritos orientales, a un bebé se le bautiza, se le crisma (confirma) y se le da la Eucaristía en una sola celebración. según el Catecismo (CIC 1292), ¿qué resalta esta práctica?","o":["el vínculo con el obispo que confirma al niño","la llegada del niño a la edad de la razón","la unidad de los tres sacramentos de iniciación","que la crismación ocupa el lugar del bautismo"]}},{"id":"CATHOLIC-s16-05","day":1368,"d":4,"q":"the Catechism (CCC 460) quotes Saint Athanasius: the Son of God \"was made man so that we might be made God.\" what does the Church mean by this, which the East calls theosis?","o":["people become a second God, equal to the Father in nature","people lose their own selves and dissolve into God's being","people earn divine status through their own ascetic effort","people share God's life by grace while staying creatures"],"a":3,"es":{"q":"el Catecismo (CIC 460) cita a san Atanasio: el Hijo de Dios \"se hizo hombre para que nosotros nos hiciéramos Dios\". ¿qué quiere decir la Iglesia con esto, que Oriente llama theosis?","o":["las personas se vuelven otro Dios, igual al Padre en naturaleza","las personas pierden su propio ser y se disuelven en el ser de Dios","las personas ganan un rango divino por su propio esfuerzo ascético","las personas participan de la vida de Dios por gracia sin dejar de ser criaturas"]}},{"id":"CATHOLIC-s16-06","day":1395,"d":3,"q":"a healthy adult planning to receive communion swallows a prescribed pill with a glass of water twenty minutes before Mass. under canon 919 on the Eucharistic fast, what follows?","o":["it breaks the fast, so she should wait to receive at a later Mass","she keeps the fast, since water and medicine do not break it","the water breaks it, though the pill taken on its own would not","it breaks the fast unless a priest first gives her a dispensation"],"a":1,"es":{"q":"una adulta sana que piensa comulgar se toma una pastilla recetada con un vaso de agua veinte minutos antes de misa. según el canon 919 sobre el ayuno eucarístico, ¿qué pasa?","o":["rompe el ayuno, así que debería esperar a comulgar en una misa posterior","mantiene el ayuno, porque el agua y las medicinas no lo rompen","el agua lo rompe, aunque la pastilla tomada sola no lo rompería","rompe el ayuno, a menos que un sacerdote antes le dé una dispensa"]}}]],"CHRISTIANITY":[[{"id":"CHRISTIANITY-s00-01","day":3,"d":1,"q":"in the Gospel of John (chapter 3), which man comes to Jesus by night and is told he must be \"born again,\" or \"born from above\"?","o":["Nicodemus","Zacchaeus","Bartimaeus","Nathanael"],"a":0,"es":{"q":"en el Evangelio de Juan (capítulo 3), ¿qué hombre va a ver a Jesús de noche y oye que debe \"nacer de nuevo\", o \"nacer de lo alto\"?","o":["Nicodemo","Zaqueo","Bartimeo","Natanael"]}},{"id":"CHRISTIANITY-s00-02","day":1,"d":2,"q":"the word Eucharist, which many churches use for the Lord's Supper, comes from a Greek word. what does that Greek word mean?","o":["breaking bread","sharing a meal","remembrance","giving thanks"],"a":3,"es":{"q":"la palabra Eucaristía, que muchas iglesias usan para la Cena del Señor, viene de una palabra griega. ¿qué significa esa palabra griega?","o":["partir el pan","compartir la mesa","el recuerdo","dar gracias"]}},{"id":"CHRISTIANITY-s00-03","day":12,"d":2,"q":"in Luke's parable of the Good Samaritan, why would a Samaritan as the hero have surprised Jesus' first listeners?","o":["Samaritans were Roman soldiers posted along that road","Samaritans and Judeans were related but long at odds","Samaritans were Temple priests from Jerusalem itself","Samaritans were known as robbers on the Jericho road"],"a":1,"es":{"q":"en la parábola del buen samaritano, en Lucas, ¿por qué un samaritano como héroe habría sorprendido a quienes oyeron primero a Jesús?","o":["los samaritanos eran soldados romanos de ese camino","samaritanos y judíos eran parientes, pero enemistados","los samaritanos eran sacerdotes del Templo de Jerusalén","los samaritanos eran famosos asaltantes de ese camino"]}},{"id":"CHRISTIANITY-s00-04","day":9,"d":2,"q":"in 2 Corinthians 12, Paul begs the Lord three times to take away his \"thorn in the flesh.\" what does the answer he receives, \"My grace is sufficient for thee,\" tell him?","o":["the thorn goes away once his faith grows strong enough","the thorn is a test to overcome by his own strength","the thorn stays, but God's gift is enough to bear it","the thorn will be healed later, once his work is done"],"a":2,"es":{"q":"en 2 Corintios 12, Pablo le ruega al Señor tres veces que le quite su \"aguijón en la carne\". ¿qué le dice la respuesta que recibe, \"Bástate mi gracia\"?","o":["el aguijón se irá cuando su fe sea bastante fuerte","el aguijón es una prueba que vencer con su propia fuerza","el aguijón se queda, pero el don de Dios basta para llevarlo","el aguijón sanará más tarde, cuando termine su obra"]}},{"id":"CHRISTIANITY-s00-05","day":15,"d":2,"q":"Paul's words \"love is patient, love is kind\" (1 Corinthians 13) are often read at weddings. who was he writing to when he first wrote them?","o":["a young couple he married in Corinth","the Roman officials who held him in prison","the elders of the Temple in Jerusalem","a church in Corinth split by rivalries"],"a":3,"es":{"q":"las palabras de Pablo \"el amor es paciente, es bondadoso\" (1 Corintios 13) se leen mucho en las bodas. ¿a quién le escribía cuando las escribió por primera vez?","o":["a una pareja joven que casó en Corinto","a los oficiales romanos que lo tenían preso","a los ancianos del Templo de Jerusalén","a una iglesia de Corinto dividida en bandos"]}},{"id":"CHRISTIANITY-s00-06","day":13,"d":2,"q":"a woman thinks it is unfair that her sister, who left the family and wasted her inheritance, is welcomed home with a party. in Luke's parable of the Prodigal Son, whose reaction is most like hers?","o":["the younger son","the older brother","the hired servants","the father himself"],"a":1,"es":{"q":"una mujer piensa que es injusto que a su hermana, que dejó a la familia y malgastó su herencia, la reciban en casa con una fiesta. en la parábola del hijo pródigo, en Lucas, ¿la reacción de quién se parece más a la de ella?","o":["el hijo menor","el hermano mayor","los jornaleros","el padre mismo"]}}],[{"id":"CHRISTIANITY-s01-01","day":23,"d":2,"q":"In Matthew 13:18–23, Jesus explains his parable of the sower to the disciples. What does the seed stand for?","o":["the prophets sent to Israel","the prayers offered to God","the word of the kingdom","the miracles done in Galilee"],"a":2,"es":{"q":"En Mateo 13:18–23, Jesús les explica a los discípulos su parábola del sembrador. ¿Qué representa la semilla?","o":["los profetas enviados a Israel","las oraciones ofrecidas a Dios","la palabra del reino","los milagros hechos en Galilea"]}},{"id":"CHRISTIANITY-s01-02","day":43,"d":2,"q":"In Luke 2, which devout old man takes the infant Jesus in his arms in the temple and prays, \"Lord, now lettest thou thy servant depart in peace\" (the Nunc dimittis)?","o":["Simeon","Zacharias","Nicodemus","Barnabas"],"a":0,"es":{"q":"En Lucas 2, ¿qué anciano piadoso toma en brazos al niño Jesús en el templo y ora: \"Ahora, Señor, despides a tu siervo en paz\" (el Nunc dimittis)?","o":["Simeón","Zacarías","Nicodemo","Bernabé"]}},{"id":"CHRISTIANITY-s01-03","day":28,"d":3,"q":"A volunteer who joins a project in its last week receives the same thank-you gift as those who served all year, and the long-serving volunteers grumble. Which parable of Jesus in Matthew's Gospel has the same shape?","o":["the ten bridesmaids and their lamps","the servant who would not forgive","the servants and their talents","the workers in the vineyard"],"a":3,"es":{"q":"Un voluntario que se suma a un proyecto en su última semana recibe el mismo regalo de agradecimiento que quienes sirvieron todo el año, y los voluntarios de siempre se quejan. ¿Qué parábola de Jesús en el Evangelio de Mateo tiene la misma forma?","o":["las diez vírgenes y sus lámparas","el siervo que no quiso perdonar","los siervos y sus talentos","los obreros de la viña"]}},{"id":"CHRISTIANITY-s01-04","day":32,"d":2,"q":"In Jesus's parable of the Pharisee and the tax collector (Luke 18:9–14), which man goes home justified, and why?","o":["the Pharisee, because his fasting and tithing were real","the tax collector, who asks God's mercy as a sinner","the Pharisee, because he opens his prayer with thanks","the tax collector, who vows to repay all he has taken"],"a":1,"es":{"q":"En la parábola de Jesús del fariseo y el publicano (Lucas 18:9–14), ¿cuál de los dos vuelve a casa justificado, y por qué?","o":["el fariseo, porque su ayuno y su diezmo eran reales","el publicano, que pide a Dios compasión como pecador","el fariseo, porque comienza su oración dando gracias","el publicano, que promete devolver todo lo que tomó"]}},{"id":"CHRISTIANITY-s01-05","day":57,"d":2,"q":"In Matthew 16, after Peter says, \"Thou art the Christ, the Son of the living God,\" what does Jesus say he will give Peter?","o":["a seat at his right hand in his kingdom","a sword to defend the coming kingdom","the keys of the kingdom of heaven","a double portion of his own spirit"],"a":2,"es":{"q":"En Mateo 16, después de que Pedro dice: \"Tú eres el Cristo, el Hijo del Dios viviente\", ¿qué dice Jesús que le dará a Pedro?","o":["un lugar a su derecha en su reino","una espada para defender el reino","las llaves del reino de los cielos","una doble porción de su propio espíritu"]}},{"id":"CHRISTIANITY-s01-06","day":82,"d":3,"q":"In Acts 10, after his vision of a sheet full of unclean animals and his visit to the Roman centurion Cornelius, what does Peter conclude?","o":["that God shows no favoritism between peoples","that Cornelius must be circumcised before baptism","that only the apostles may share meals with Gentiles","that he must leave Judea and go to preach in Rome"],"a":0,"es":{"q":"En Hechos 10, después de su visión de un lienzo lleno de animales impuros y de su visita al centurión romano Cornelio, ¿a qué conclusión llega Pedro?","o":["que Dios no hace distinción entre los pueblos","que Cornelio debe circuncidarse antes del bautismo","que solo los apóstoles pueden comer con gentiles","que debe dejar Judea e ir a predicar a Roma"]}}],[{"id":"CHRISTIANITY-s02-01","day":99,"d":2,"q":"the Jesus Prayer, treasured in the Orthodox churches and repeated on a prayer rope, is usually said in which words?","o":["Lord Jesus Christ, Son of God, have mercy on me","Holy God, Holy Mighty, Holy Immortal, have mercy on us","Glory to the Father, and to the Son, and to the Spirit","Our Father, who art in heaven, hallowed be thy name"],"a":0,"es":{"q":"la Oración de Jesús, muy querida en las iglesias ortodoxas y repetida con un cordón de oración, ¿con qué palabras se dice por lo general?","o":["Señor Jesucristo, Hijo de Dios, ten piedad de mí","Santo Dios, Santo Fuerte, Santo Inmortal, ten piedad de nosotros","Gloria al Padre, y al Hijo, y al Espíritu Santo","Padre nuestro, que estás en el cielo, santificado sea tu nombre"]}},{"id":"CHRISTIANITY-s02-02","day":112,"d":3,"q":"in the Orthodox churches, the feast of January 6 is called Theophany (\"God shown\"). which event stands at its center?","o":["the visit of the magi to the child","the wedding feast at Cana in Galilee","the baptism of Jesus in the Jordan","the presentation of Jesus in the Temple"],"a":2,"es":{"q":"en las iglesias ortodoxas, la fiesta del 6 de enero se llama Teofanía (\"Dios manifestado\"). ¿qué acontecimiento está en su centro?","o":["la visita de los magos al niño","las bodas de Caná de Galilea","el bautismo de Jesús en el Jordán","la presentación de Jesús en el Templo"]}},{"id":"CHRISTIANITY-s02-03","day":101,"d":3,"q":"in Guigo II's Ladder of Monks, the classic account of lectio divina (\"sacred reading\"), what is the fourth and highest rung, contemplatio?","o":["reading the passage slowly, often aloud","turning a phrase over in the mind to ponder it","answering God in one's own words of prayer","resting quietly in God, beyond words"],"a":3,"es":{"q":"en la Escala de los monjes de Guigo II, el relato clásico de la lectio divina (\"lectura sagrada\"), ¿cuál es el cuarto y más alto peldaño, la contemplatio?","o":["leer el pasaje despacio, a menudo en voz alta","dar vueltas a una frase en la mente para meditarla","responder a Dios con palabras propias de oración","descansar en silencio en Dios, sin más palabras"]}},{"id":"CHRISTIANITY-s02-04","day":120,"d":3,"q":"in the Western church calendar, why is the long season after Pentecost called \"ordinary time\"?","o":["it recalls the hidden life of Jesus at Nazareth","its Sundays are simply numbered, one after another","it was once the season for ordaining new priests","it recalls the apostles being ordained at Pentecost"],"a":1,"es":{"q":"en el calendario de la iglesia occidental, ¿por qué el largo tiempo después de Pentecostés se llama \"tiempo ordinario\"?","o":["recuerda la vida oculta de Jesús en Nazaret","sus domingos simplemente se numeran, uno tras otro","antes era el tiempo de ordenar a nuevos sacerdotes","recuerda la ordenación de los apóstoles en Pentecostés"]}},{"id":"CHRISTIANITY-s02-05","day":125,"d":3,"q":"why does a Catholic Bible have more Old Testament books than most Protestant Bibles?","o":["Catholics split Samuel, Kings and Chronicles into more books","Catholics add the book of Enoch and a Psalm 151","Catholics count each of the twelve minor prophets as a book","Catholics also accept Tobit, Judith, Maccabees and others"],"a":3,"es":{"q":"¿por qué una Biblia católica tiene más libros en el Antiguo Testamento que la mayoría de las Biblias protestantes?","o":["los católicos dividen Samuel, Reyes y Crónicas en más libros","los católicos añaden el libro de Enoc y un Salmo 151","los católicos cuentan cada uno de los doce profetas menores aparte","los católicos aceptan también Tobías, Judit, Macabeos y otros"]}},{"id":"CHRISTIANITY-s02-06","day":147,"d":3,"q":"an Orthodox Christian is keeping a strict fast day in Great Lent, the fast before Pascha (Easter). by the traditional Orthodox rule, which meal fits that day?","o":["a cheese omelet with buttered toast and fruit","lentil soup and bread, with no meat or dairy","roast chicken with rice and steamed vegetables","baked fish in butter sauce with a glass of wine"],"a":1,"es":{"q":"un cristiano ortodoxo guarda un día de ayuno estricto en la Gran Cuaresma, el ayuno antes de la Pascua. según la regla ortodoxa tradicional, ¿qué comida corresponde a ese día?","o":["una tortilla de queso con pan con mantequilla y fruta","sopa de lentejas y pan, sin carne ni lácteos","pollo asado con arroz y verduras al vapor","pescado al horno en salsa de mantequilla con vino"]}}],[{"id":"CHRISTIANITY-s03-01","day":180,"d":3,"q":"In the Gospel of Mark (6:3), when Jesus teaches in the synagogue at Nazareth, what trade do the people of his hometown name when they ask, \"Is not this the ___, the son of Mary?\"","o":["a fisherman","a carpenter","a shepherd","a tax collector"],"a":1,"es":{"q":"En el Evangelio de Marcos (6:3), cuando Jesús enseña en la sinagoga de Nazaret, ¿qué oficio nombra la gente de su pueblo al preguntar: \"¿No es este el ___, el hijo de María?\"","o":["el pescador","el carpintero","el pastor","el publicano"]}},{"id":"CHRISTIANITY-s03-02","day":221,"d":3,"q":"In the Gospel of Mark (14:36), praying in Gethsemane, Jesus addresses God with the Aramaic word \"Abba.\" What does it mean?","o":["father","master","teacher","brother"],"a":0,"es":{"q":"En el Evangelio de Marcos (14:36), orando en Getsemaní, Jesús se dirige a Dios con la palabra aramea \"Abba\". ¿Qué significa?","o":["padre","señor","maestro","hermano"]}},{"id":"CHRISTIANITY-s03-03","day":165,"d":3,"q":"In the Gospel of Mark (2:18–20), people ask why Jesus's disciples do not fast while John's disciples and the Pharisees do. How does Jesus answer?","o":["the law of Moses had never commanded any days of fasting","only the priests serving in the temple were bound to keep fasts","wedding guests don't fast while the bridegroom is with them","his disciples were too poor to set aside food on fast days"],"a":2,"es":{"q":"En el Evangelio de Marcos (2:18–20), le preguntan a Jesús por qué sus discípulos no ayunan, mientras que los de Juan y los fariseos sí. ¿Qué responde Jesús?","o":["la ley de Moisés nunca había mandado ningún día de ayuno","solo los sacerdotes que servían en el templo debían ayunar","los invitados no ayunan mientras el novio está con ellos","sus discípulos eran muy pobres para guardar comida en días de ayuno"]}},{"id":"CHRISTIANITY-s03-04","day":210,"d":3,"q":"In the Gospel of Mark (12:1–12), Jesus tells the parable of the tenants who kill the vineyard owner's beloved son. Whom do the chief priests, scribes and elders realize the story was told against?","o":["the Roman governor and his soldiers","the crowds who had shouted hosanna","the disciples who would soon desert him","themselves, the leaders in the temple"],"a":3,"es":{"q":"En el Evangelio de Marcos (12:1–12), Jesús cuenta la parábola de los labradores que matan al hijo amado del dueño de la viña. ¿Contra quién entienden los principales sacerdotes, los escribas y los ancianos que iba la historia?","o":["el gobernador romano y sus soldados","la multitud que había gritado hosanna","los discípulos que pronto lo abandonarían","ellos mismos, los líderes del templo"]}},{"id":"CHRISTIANITY-s03-05","day":214,"d":3,"q":"In the Gospel of Mark (12:41–44), why does Jesus say the poor widow who put two small coins in the temple treasury gave more than all the others?","o":["her coins were silver, while the rich gave only copper","she gave all she had to live on; they gave from surplus","she gave on the sabbath, when a gift was counted double","she was a widow, and the law set widows' gifts above all"],"a":1,"es":{"q":"En el Evangelio de Marcos (12:41–44), ¿por qué dice Jesús que la viuda pobre que echó dos moneditas en el tesoro del templo dio más que todos los demás?","o":["sus monedas eran de plata y las de los ricos, de cobre","dio todo su sustento; ellos dieron de lo que les sobraba","dio en sábado, cuando una ofrenda contaba el doble","era viuda, y la ley ponía las ofrendas de viudas sobre todas"]}},{"id":"CHRISTIANITY-s03-06","day":172,"d":3,"q":"In Jesus's explanation of the parable of the sower (Mark 4:14–20), the seed is the word. A man hears the teaching gladly, but worry about money and his business slowly crowd it out until it bears nothing. Which ground is he?","o":["the seed sown by the wayside","the seed sown on stony ground","the seed sown among thorns","the seed sown on good ground"],"a":2,"es":{"q":"En la explicación que da Jesús de la parábola del sembrador (Marcos 4:14–20), la semilla es la palabra. Un hombre escucha la enseñanza con gusto, pero las preocupaciones por el dinero y su negocio la van ahogando hasta que no da fruto. ¿Qué terreno es?","o":["la semilla sembrada junto al camino","la semilla sembrada en pedregales","la semilla sembrada entre espinos","la semilla sembrada en buena tierra"]}}],[{"id":"CHRISTIANITY-s04-01","day":260,"d":2,"q":"in the Gospel of Matthew, how does Jesus close the Sermon on the Mount: whoever hears his sayings and does them is like whom?","o":["a sower whose seed fell on good ground","a virgin who kept oil ready for her lamp","a wise man who built his house on a rock","a merchant who sold all he had for one pearl"],"a":2,"es":{"q":"en el Evangelio de Mateo, ¿cómo cierra Jesús el Sermón del Monte: a quién se parece el que oye sus palabras y las pone en práctica?","o":["a un sembrador cuya semilla cayó en buena tierra","a una virgen que tuvo aceite listo para su lámpara","a un hombre sabio que construyó su casa sobre la roca","a un comerciante que vendió todo por una sola perla"]}},{"id":"CHRISTIANITY-s04-02","day":272,"d":3,"q":"in Julian of Norwich's Revelations of Divine Love, she is shown a little thing the size of a hazelnut in the palm of her hand. what is she told it is?","o":["all that God has made","her own soul before God","the whole church on earth","the bread of the Eucharist"],"a":0,"es":{"q":"en las Revelaciones del amor divino de Juliana de Norwich, a ella se le muestra una cosa pequeña, del tamaño de una avellana, en la palma de la mano. ¿qué se le dice que es?","o":["todo lo que Dios ha hecho","su propia alma ante Dios","toda la Iglesia en la tierra","el pan de la Eucaristía"]}},{"id":"CHRISTIANITY-s04-03","day":286,"d":3,"q":"in the split between the Eastern and Western churches usually dated to 1054, one sore point was the Latin word filioque, added in the West to the Nicene Creed. what does the added word say?","o":["the Son is begotten of the Father before all ages","the Spirit proceeds from the Father and the Son","the bishop of Rome is the head of the whole church","Mary, the Mother of God, was conceived without sin"],"a":1,"es":{"q":"en la división entre las Iglesias de Oriente y Occidente, que suele fecharse en 1054, un punto de conflicto fue la palabra latina filioque, añadida en Occidente al Credo niceno. ¿qué dice la palabra añadida?","o":["que el Hijo es engendrado antes de todos los siglos","que el Espíritu procede del Padre y del Hijo","que el obispo de Roma es la cabeza de toda la Iglesia","que María, Madre de Dios, fue concebida sin pecado"]}},{"id":"CHRISTIANITY-s04-04","day":301,"d":3,"q":"how did the Council of Chalcedon (451) describe Jesus Christ?","o":["a man adopted as God's Son at his baptism","God in a human body without a human mind","two persons, one divine and one human, joined","one person in two natures, divine and human"],"a":3,"es":{"q":"¿cómo describió a Jesucristo el Concilio de Calcedonia (451)?","o":["un hombre adoptado como Hijo de Dios en su bautismo","Dios en un cuerpo humano, sin mente humana","dos personas, una divina y una humana, unidas","una sola persona en dos naturalezas, divina y humana"]}},{"id":"CHRISTIANITY-s04-05","day":315,"d":4,"q":"in Romans 4, Paul notes that Abraham's faith was \"counted unto him for righteousness\" at a certain point in Genesis. why does that timing matter to his argument?","o":["it came before his circumcision, so it reaches the uncircumcised too","it came after his circumcision, so the sign is what made it count","it came after the law at Sinai, so keeping the law made it count","it came after he tithed to Melchizedek, so his gift made it count"],"a":0,"es":{"q":"en Romanos 4, Pablo señala que la fe de Abraham \"le fue contada por justicia\" en cierto momento del Génesis. ¿por qué importa ese momento para su argumento?","o":["fue antes de su circuncisión, así que alcanza también a los incircuncisos","fue después de su circuncisión, así que la señal es lo que la hizo valer","fue después de la ley del Sinaí, así que cumplir la ley la hizo valer","fue después de dar el diezmo a Melquisedec, así que su ofrenda la hizo valer"]}},{"id":"CHRISTIANITY-s04-06","day":308,"d":3,"q":"a man sees that he has been living wrongly, changes his whole way of thinking and turns his life around. which New Testament Greek word, usually translated \"repentance,\" names this?","o":["koinonia","metanoia","anamnesis","kenosis"],"a":1,"es":{"q":"un hombre se da cuenta de que ha vivido mal, cambia toda su manera de pensar y le da un giro a su vida. ¿qué palabra griega del Nuevo Testamento, que suele traducirse \"arrepentimiento\", nombra esto?","o":["koinonia","metanoia","anamnesis","kenosis"]}}],[{"id":"CHRISTIANITY-s05-01","day":350,"d":3,"q":"in Genesis 14, when Abram returns from rescuing Lot, Melchizedek, king of Salem and priest of God Most High, comes out to bless him. what does Melchizedek bring out?","o":["oil and incense","bread and wine","milk and honey","salt and water"],"a":1,"es":{"q":"en Génesis 14, cuando Abram vuelve de rescatar a Lot, Melquisedec, rey de Salem y sacerdote del Dios Altísimo, sale a bendecirlo. ¿qué saca Melquisedec?","o":["aceite e incienso","pan y vino","leche y miel","sal y agua"]}},{"id":"CHRISTIANITY-s05-02","day":364,"d":3,"q":"in Genesis 32, Jacob wrestles all night with a mysterious man by the ford of the Jabbok and will not let go until he is blessed. what new name is Jacob given?","o":["Peniel","Judah","Edom","Israel"],"a":3,"es":{"q":"en Génesis 32, Jacob lucha toda la noche con un hombre misterioso junto al vado del Jaboc y no lo suelta hasta recibir una bendición. ¿qué nombre nuevo recibe Jacob?","o":["Peniel","Judá","Edom","Israel"]}},{"id":"CHRISTIANITY-s05-03","day":357,"d":3,"q":"in Genesis 22, Abraham is told to offer his son Isaac on Mount Moriah, and at the last moment God provides a ram in his place. since the early church, which event in the life of Christ have Christians most often seen foreshadowed in this story?","o":["his crucifixion on Calvary","his baptism by John in the Jordan","his birth to Mary in Bethlehem","his feeding of the five thousand"],"a":0,"es":{"q":"en Génesis 22, Dios le pide a Abraham ofrecer a su hijo Isaac en el monte Moriah, y en el último momento provee un carnero en su lugar. desde la iglesia antigua, ¿qué momento de la vida de Cristo han visto anunciado los cristianos sobre todo en este relato?","o":["su crucifixión en el Calvario","su bautismo por Juan en el Jordán","su nacimiento de María en Belén","su multiplicación de los panes"]}},{"id":"CHRISTIANITY-s05-04","day":375,"d":3,"q":"at the end of Genesis, Joseph tells the brothers who sold him: \"ye thought evil against me; but God meant it unto good\" (Genesis 50:20). what is he saying?","o":["the brothers had secretly meant well when they sold him to traders","the pit and the prison were good things in and of themselves","the harm was real, yet God worked through it to save many lives","God would punish the brothers later, so Joseph need not do it"],"a":2,"es":{"q":"al final del Génesis, José les dice a los hermanos que lo vendieron: \"ustedes pensaron mal contra mí, mas Dios lo encaminó a bien\" (Génesis 50:20). ¿qué está diciendo?","o":["los hermanos en secreto tenían buena intención al venderlo","el pozo y la cárcel fueron cosas buenas en sí mismas","el daño fue real, pero Dios obró a través de él para salvar vidas","Dios castigaría a los hermanos más tarde, así que José no lo haría"]}},{"id":"CHRISTIANITY-s05-05","day":386,"d":3,"q":"in many languages the Christian name for Easter (Greek Pascha, Spanish Pascua, French Pâques) comes from Pesach, the Hebrew name for Passover. why?","o":["Pesach means \"new life,\" the main theme of the spring feast","Pesach was the old Hebrew word for rising from the dead","Pascha is the Greek word for the empty tomb in the Gospels","the Gospels set Jesus's death and rising at Passover time"],"a":3,"es":{"q":"en muchos idiomas el nombre cristiano de la fiesta de Resurrección (en griego Pascha, en español Pascua, en francés Pâques) viene de Pésaj, el nombre hebreo de la Pascua judía. ¿por qué?","o":["Pésaj significa \"vida nueva\", el tema principal de la fiesta","Pésaj era la antigua palabra hebrea para la resurrección","Pascha es la palabra griega para la tumba vacía en los Evangelios","los Evangelios sitúan la muerte y resurrección de Jesús en Pascua"]}},{"id":"CHRISTIANITY-s05-06","day":392,"d":3,"q":"a pastor is worn out from settling every dispute in her large church by herself. following Jethro's advice to Moses in Exodus 18:17–22, what should change?","o":["she should step aside and let the church elders choose a new leader","she should hear every case herself, but only on one set day a week","she should let able helpers handle small cases, keep the hard ones","she should send the two sides away until they make peace on their own"],"a":2,"es":{"q":"una pastora está agotada de resolver ella sola cada disputa en su iglesia grande. según el consejo de Jetro a Moisés en Éxodo 18:17–22, ¿qué debería cambiar?","o":["debería hacerse a un lado y dejar que los ancianos elijan a otro líder","debería oír cada caso ella misma, pero solo un día fijo a la semana","debería dejar los casos pequeños a ayudantes capaces y tomar los difíciles","debería despedir a las dos partes hasta que hagan las paces solas"]}}],[{"id":"CHRISTIANITY-s06-01","day":416,"d":2,"q":"in the Gospels of Matthew and Mark, Jesus on the cross cries out \"my God, my God, why hast thou forsaken me?\" which psalm opens with these words?","o":["Psalm 23","Psalm 22","Psalm 51","Psalm 130"],"a":1,"es":{"q":"en los Evangelios de Mateo y Marcos, Jesús en la cruz exclama: \"Dios mío, Dios mío, ¿por qué me has abandonado?\". ¿qué salmo comienza con estas palabras?","o":["el Salmo 23","el Salmo 22","el Salmo 51","el Salmo 130"]}},{"id":"CHRISTIANITY-s06-02","day":454,"d":2,"q":"in the book of Ecclesiastes, the Hebrew word hevel, rendered \"vanity\" in the King James Bible (\"vanity of vanities\"), literally means what?","o":["pride or conceit","dust and ashes","chasing the wind","breath or vapor"],"a":3,"es":{"q":"en el libro del Eclesiastés, la palabra hebrea hével, traducida \"vanidad\" (\"vanidad de vanidades\"), ¿qué significa literalmente?","o":["orgullo o soberbia","polvo y ceniza","correr tras el viento","aliento o vapor"]}},{"id":"CHRISTIANITY-s06-03","day":460,"d":3,"q":"why do Catholic Bibles have more books in the Old Testament than most Protestant Bibles?","o":["they follow the longer Hebrew canon; Protestants, the shorter Greek one","they follow the longer Greek Septuagint canon; Protestants, the Hebrew one","Luther dropped books that the Hebrew Bible had always counted","the Council of Trent wrote new books to answer the Reformers"],"a":1,"es":{"q":"¿por qué las Biblias católicas tienen más libros en el Antiguo Testamento que la mayoría de las Biblias protestantes?","o":["siguen el canon hebreo, más largo; los protestantes, el griego, más corto","siguen el canon griego de la Septuaginta, más largo; los protestantes, el hebreo","Lutero quitó libros que la Biblia hebrea siempre había contado","el Concilio de Trento escribió libros nuevos para responder a los reformadores"]}},{"id":"CHRISTIANITY-s06-04","day":476,"d":3,"q":"in Jeremiah 31:31–34, God promises a \"new covenant\" with the house of Israel and the house of Judah. what does the passage say will be new about it?","o":["the covenant will be sealed with a sign in the sky, like Noah's rainbow","the covenant will be made with the nations in place of Israel and Judah","God's law will be written on their hearts, not on tablets of stone","the covenant will depend on a new temple being built in Jerusalem"],"a":2,"es":{"q":"en Jeremías 31:31–34, Dios promete un \"nuevo pacto\" con la casa de Israel y la casa de Judá. ¿qué dice el pasaje que tendrá de nuevo?","o":["el pacto se sellará con una señal en el cielo, como el arcoíris de Noé","el pacto se hará con las naciones en lugar de Israel y Judá","la ley de Dios estará escrita en el corazón, no en tablas de piedra","el pacto dependerá de que se construya un templo nuevo en Jerusalén"]}},{"id":"CHRISTIANITY-s06-05","day":488,"d":3,"q":"at the end of the book of Jonah, God sets Jonah's grief over a withered plant beside God's own pity for the city of Nineveh. what point is God making?","o":["Nineveh will wither later, like the plant, because it is so wicked","if Jonah can pity a plant, God may surely pity a great city","Jonah is being punished with the heat for having fled to Tarshish","plants and animals matter to God more than the people of Nineveh"],"a":1,"es":{"q":"al final del libro de Jonás, Dios pone la pena de Jonás por una planta seca al lado de su propia compasión por la ciudad de Nínive. ¿qué quiere mostrar Dios?","o":["Nínive se secará más tarde, como la planta, por ser tan malvada","si Jonás se apiada de una planta, Dios bien puede apiadarse de una gran ciudad","Jonás está siendo castigado con el calor por haber huido a Tarsis","a Dios le importan más las plantas y los animales que la gente de Nínive"]}},{"id":"CHRISTIANITY-s06-06","day":449,"d":3,"q":"a woman falls gravely ill, and three friends insist it must be punishment for some hidden sin. at the end of the book of Job, what does God say about Job's friends, who argued the same way?","o":["he praises them for defending his justice against Job's complaints","he says they were right, but should have spoken more gently to Job","he rewards them with double what Job lost, for their loyal counsel","he says they did not speak of him rightly, as his servant Job had"],"a":3,"es":{"q":"una mujer enferma gravemente, y tres amigos insisten en que debe ser castigo por algún pecado oculto. al final del libro de Job, ¿qué dice Dios de los amigos de Job, que razonaban igual?","o":["los elogia por defender su justicia frente a las quejas de Job","dice que tenían razón, pero que debieron hablarle a Job con más dulzura","los premia con el doble de lo que Job perdió, por su consejo leal","dice que no hablaron de él con rectitud, como sí lo hizo su siervo Job"]}}],[{"id":"CHRISTIANITY-s07-01","day":516,"d":2,"q":"In the Gospel of Luke (4:16–21), Jesus stands up in the synagogue at Nazareth, reads \"The Spirit of the Lord is upon me,\" and says, \"This day is this scripture fulfilled in your ears.\" Which prophet's book is he handed?","o":["the book of Isaiah","the book of Jeremiah","the book of Ezekiel","the book of Malachi"],"a":0,"es":{"q":"En el Evangelio de Lucas (4:16–21), Jesús se pone de pie en la sinagoga de Nazaret, lee \"El Espíritu del Señor está sobre mí\" y dice: \"Hoy se ha cumplido esta Escritura delante de ustedes\". ¿Qué libro profético le entregan?","o":["el libro de Isaías","el libro de Jeremías","el libro de Ezequiel","el libro de Malaquías"]}},{"id":"CHRISTIANITY-s07-02","day":563,"d":2,"q":"In the Gospel of Luke (17:11–19), Jesus heals ten men with leprosy on his way to Jerusalem. Only one of them turns back to give thanks. Who does Luke say that man was?","o":["a Roman centurion's servant","a Samaritan, a foreigner","a priest from the temple","a tax collector of Jericho"],"a":1,"es":{"q":"En el Evangelio de Lucas (17:11–19), Jesús sana a diez hombres con lepra camino a Jerusalén. Solo uno vuelve para dar las gracias. ¿Quién dice Lucas que era ese hombre?","o":["el siervo de un centurión romano","un samaritano, un extranjero","un sacerdote del templo","un cobrador de impuestos de Jericó"]}},{"id":"CHRISTIANITY-s07-03","day":541,"d":3,"q":"In the Gospel of Luke (10:25–37), a lawyer asks Jesus, \"Who is my neighbour?\" Jesus answers with the parable of the Good Samaritan. What question does Jesus put to the lawyer at the end?","o":["which of the three men kept the law of purity best","whether the wounded man deserved the help he got","whether the innkeeper should be repaid his costs","which of the three proved a neighbour to the man"],"a":3,"es":{"q":"En el Evangelio de Lucas (10:25–37), un experto en la ley le pregunta a Jesús: \"¿Quién es mi prójimo?\". Jesús responde con la parábola del buen samaritano. ¿Qué le pregunta Jesús al final?","o":["cuál de los tres cumplió mejor la ley de pureza","si el herido merecía la ayuda que recibió","si al posadero había que pagarle sus gastos","cuál de los tres fue el prójimo de aquel hombre"]}},{"id":"CHRISTIANITY-s07-04","day":557,"d":3,"q":"In the Gospel of Luke (15), Jesus tells three parables in a row: the lost sheep, the lost coin and the lost son. According to Luke 15:1–2, what is he answering?","o":["disciples arguing among themselves over who was the greatest","a rich ruler asking how to inherit eternal life","Pharisees and scribes grumbling that he eats with sinners","a crowd demanding a sign from heaven to prove him"],"a":2,"es":{"q":"En el Evangelio de Lucas (15), Jesús cuenta tres parábolas seguidas: la oveja perdida, la moneda perdida y el hijo perdido. Según Lucas 15:1–2, ¿a qué está respondiendo?","o":["a los discípulos que discuten entre sí quién de ellos es el mayor","a un hombre rico que pregunta cómo heredar la vida eterna","a fariseos y escribas que murmuran porque come con pecadores","a una multitud que le exige una señal del cielo como prueba"]}},{"id":"CHRISTIANITY-s07-05","day":560,"d":4,"q":"In the Gospel of Luke (16:1–8), a manager about to lose his post cuts the debts owed to his master so the debtors will welcome him later. Why does Luke say the master commends him?","o":["because he acted shrewdly to provide for his future","because he had repaid in full the goods he had wasted","because he had been honest about the true debts","because he gave the money he saved to the poor"],"a":0,"es":{"q":"En el Evangelio de Lucas (16:1–8), un administrador a punto de perder su puesto rebaja las deudas que otros tienen con su amo para que después lo reciban. ¿Por qué dice Lucas que el amo lo elogia?","o":["porque actuó con astucia para asegurar su futuro","porque devolvió por completo todo lo que había malgastado","porque fue honesto sobre las deudas reales","porque dio a los pobres el dinero que ahorró"]}},{"id":"CHRISTIANITY-s07-06","day":554,"d":3,"q":"A family hosting a holiday dinner skips the usual round of relatives and well-off neighbours and instead seats people from the shelter down the street. Which teaching of Jesus in Luke 14 are they following?","o":["choose the lowest seat at a feast rather than the place of honour","count the cost first, as a builder does before raising a tower","heal and do good on the Sabbath, as you'd pull an ox from a well","call the poor to your table, not those who can repay the favour"],"a":3,"es":{"q":"Una familia que organiza una cena de fiesta deja de lado a los parientes y vecinos acomodados de siempre y, en cambio, sienta a su mesa a personas del albergue de la calle. ¿Qué enseñanza de Jesús en Lucas 14 está siguiendo?","o":["elige el último lugar en un banquete y no el puesto de honor","calcula primero el costo, como quien va a levantar una torre","sana y haz el bien en sábado, como sacarías a un buey de un pozo","invita a tu mesa a los pobres, no a quienes te pueden devolver el favor"]}}],[{"id":"CHRISTIANITY-s08-01","day":597,"d":2,"q":"In the Gospel of John (2:1–11), what does Jesus do at a wedding in Cana of Galilee, which John calls \"the beginning of miracles\" (his first sign)?","o":["he heals a royal official's dying son","he turns water in stone jars into wine","he feeds a great crowd with five loaves","he gives sight to a man born blind"],"a":1,"es":{"q":"En el Evangelio de Juan (2:1–11), ¿qué hace Jesús en una boda en Caná de Galilea, que Juan llama \"el principio de las señales\" (su primera señal)?","o":["sana al hijo moribundo de un funcionario real","convierte en vino el agua de unas tinajas","alimenta a una gran multitud con cinco panes","le da la vista a un hombre ciego de nacimiento"]}},{"id":"CHRISTIANITY-s08-02","day":651,"d":2,"q":"In the Gospel of John (20:11–18), who is weeping outside the empty tomb, mistakes the risen Jesus for the gardener, and knows him when he says her name, answering \"Rabboni\"?","o":["Mary Magdalene","Mary of Bethany","Martha of Bethany","Mary, his mother"],"a":0,"es":{"q":"En el Evangelio de Juan (20:11–18), ¿quién llora afuera del sepulcro vacío, confunde a Jesús resucitado con el jardinero y lo reconoce cuando él dice su nombre, respondiendo \"Rabboni\"?","o":["María Magdalena","María de Betania","Marta de Betania","María, su madre"]}},{"id":"CHRISTIANITY-s08-03","day":647,"d":3,"q":"In the Gospel of John (19:30), Jesus's last words from the cross, \"It is finished,\" are one Greek word, tetelestai, from telos (end, goal). What sense does the word carry?","o":["my strength is gone, and I can do no more","the prophecy is not yet fulfilled, but will be","the work is accomplished, brought to its goal","the crowd's mockery has finally come to an end"],"a":2,"es":{"q":"En el Evangelio de Juan (19:30), las últimas palabras de Jesús en la cruz, \"Consumado es\", son una sola palabra griega, tetelestai, de telos (fin, meta). ¿Qué sentido tiene esa palabra?","o":["mis fuerzas se acabaron y ya no puedo más","la profecía aún no se cumple, pero se cumplirá","la obra está cumplida, llevada a su meta","las burlas de la gente por fin se terminaron"]}},{"id":"CHRISTIANITY-s08-04","day":630,"d":3,"q":"In the Gospel of John (13:34), Jesus calls \"love one another\" a new commandment, though Leviticus 19:18 already commands love of neighbor. What measure does the verse itself give for this love?","o":["love as you love yourselves","love as Moses' law commands","love as you love your family","love as I have loved you"],"a":3,"es":{"q":"En el Evangelio de Juan (13:34), Jesús llama \"ámense unos a otros\" un mandamiento nuevo, aunque Levítico 19:18 ya manda amar al prójimo. ¿Qué medida da el versículo mismo para ese amor?","o":["amar como se aman a sí mismos","amar como manda la ley de Moisés","amar como aman a su familia","amar como yo los he amado"]}},{"id":"CHRISTIANITY-s08-05","day":622,"d":3,"q":"In the Gospel of John (11:23–26), Martha says she knows her brother Lazarus will rise \"in the resurrection at the last day.\" What does Jesus's answer, \"I am the resurrection, and the life,\" add to her belief?","o":["the resurrection is present in him, not only at the last day","there is no rising at the last day, only a spiritual one","only those who saw him in the flesh would rise to new life","Lazarus would rise again, but only when this age ended"],"a":0,"es":{"q":"En el Evangelio de Juan (11:23–26), Marta dice que sabe que su hermano Lázaro resucitará \"en la resurrección, en el día final\". ¿Qué agrega a su fe la respuesta de Jesús, \"Yo soy la resurrección y la vida\"?","o":["la resurrección está presente en él, no solo en el día final","no hay resurrección en el día final, solo una espiritual","solo los que lo vieron en persona resucitarían a nueva vida","Lázaro resucitaría, pero solo cuando terminara esta era"]}},{"id":"CHRISTIANITY-s08-06","day":617,"d":3,"q":"After a fire, someone says a family's loss must be punishment for sin. In the Gospel of John (9:1–3), the disciples ask the same kind of question about a man blind from birth. How does Jesus answer it?","o":["the man himself sinned, before he was even born","his parents sinned, and their child bears the cost","neither this man nor his parents sinned to cause it","the cause is hidden, and it is wrong to ask about it"],"a":2,"es":{"q":"Después de un incendio, alguien dice que la pérdida de una familia debe ser castigo por algún pecado. En el Evangelio de Juan (9:1–3), los discípulos hacen esa misma pregunta sobre un hombre ciego de nacimiento. ¿Cómo responde Jesús?","o":["el hombre mismo pecó, antes incluso de nacer","pecaron sus padres, y el hijo carga con eso","ni él ni sus padres pecaron para causarlo","la causa es oculta, y está mal preguntar por ella"]}}],[{"id":"CHRISTIANITY-s09-01","day":724,"d":2,"q":"In 2 Samuel 12, how does the prophet Nathan bring King David to see his own wrong?","o":["he reads him the lost book of the law from the temple","he tells of a rich man who took a poor man's lamb","he tears a new cloak into twelve pieces before him","he writes the king's sin upon the palace wall"],"a":1,"es":{"q":"En 2 Samuel 12, ¿cómo hace el profeta Natán que el rey David vea su propia falta?","o":["le lee el libro perdido de la ley hallado en el templo","le cuenta de un rico que le quitó al pobre su oveja","rompe un manto nuevo en doce pedazos frente a él","escribe el pecado del rey en el muro del palacio"]}},{"id":"CHRISTIANITY-s09-02","day":755,"d":3,"q":"In his letter to the Romans, written on his way to martyrdom, what does Ignatius of Antioch call himself?","o":["a voice crying out in the wilderness of Rome","a lamp lit for Rome, set high upon its stand","a servant of the servants of God in Rome","God's wheat, ground by the teeth of beasts"],"a":3,"es":{"q":"En su carta a los romanos, escrita camino al martirio, ¿cómo se llama a sí mismo Ignacio de Antioquía?","o":["una voz que clama en el desierto de Roma","una lámpara encendida en lo alto para Roma","un siervo de los siervos de Dios en Roma","trigo de Dios, molido por dientes de fieras"]}},{"id":"CHRISTIANITY-s09-03","day":748,"d":3,"q":"At the council in Jerusalem described in Acts 15, what did the apostles and elders decide about Gentile believers?","o":["they need not be circumcised to join the church","they must be circumcised before they are baptized","they must keep every food law found in Leviticus","they should gather apart from the Jewish believers"],"a":0,"es":{"q":"En el concilio de Jerusalén que narra Hechos 15, ¿qué decidieron los apóstoles y ancianos sobre los creyentes gentiles?","o":["no necesitan circuncidarse para pertenecer","deben circuncidarse antes de ser bautizados","deben guardar cada ley de comida del Levítico","deben reunirse aparte de los creyentes judíos"]}},{"id":"CHRISTIANITY-s09-04","day":768,"d":3,"q":"Against the teaching of Arius, what did the Council of Nicaea (325) affirm with the Greek word homoousios?","o":["the Son is of like substance to the Father","the Son was the first and highest of creatures","the Son is of one substance with the Father","the Father and Son are one person in two modes"],"a":2,"es":{"q":"Frente a la enseñanza de Arrio, ¿qué afirmó el Concilio de Nicea (325) con la palabra griega homoousios?","o":["el Hijo es de sustancia semejante al Padre","el Hijo fue la primera y más alta criatura","el Hijo es de una sustancia con el Padre","Padre e Hijo son una persona en dos modos"]}},{"id":"CHRISTIANITY-s09-05","day":801,"d":4,"q":"During the iconoclast controversy, on what main ground did John of Damascus defend the making of icons?","o":["an icon holds the very soul of the saint it shows","the emperor alone may rule on how the church worships","icons are older than the written gospels themselves","God became visible in Christ, so he can be pictured"],"a":3,"es":{"q":"Durante la controversia iconoclasta, ¿con qué argumento principal defendió Juan Damasceno la creación de íconos?","o":["un ícono contiene el alma misma del santo que muestra","solo el emperador puede decidir cómo adora la iglesia","los íconos son más antiguos que los evangelios escritos","Dios se hizo visible en Cristo, y puede ser pintado"]}},{"id":"CHRISTIANITY-s09-06","day":783,"d":4,"q":"A friend says that in Christ the divine nature swallowed up the human, like a drop of vinegar lost in the sea. According to the Definition of the Council of Chalcedon (451), what is wrong with that picture?","o":["he is two persons who share one will between them","his two natures remain, unconfused and unchanged","his human nature began only when he was baptized","his divine nature left him before he died on the cross"],"a":1,"es":{"q":"Un amigo dice que en Cristo la naturaleza divina absorbió a la humana, como una gota de vinagre perdida en el mar. Según la Definición del Concilio de Calcedonia (451), ¿qué falla en esa imagen?","o":["él es dos personas que comparten una sola voluntad","sus dos naturalezas siguen, sin confusión ni cambio","su naturaleza humana empezó solo cuando fue bautizado","su naturaleza divina lo dejó antes de morir en la cruz"]}}],[{"id":"CHRISTIANITY-s10-01","day":808,"d":2,"q":"In 1054, Cardinal Humbert, the pope's envoy, laid a bull excommunicating Patriarch Michael Cerularius on the altar of which church?","o":["the Church of the Holy Sepulchre","the basilica of St John Lateran","Hagia Sophia in Constantinople","the Church of the Holy Apostles"],"a":2,"es":{"q":"En 1054, el cardenal Humberto, enviado del papa, puso una bula que excomulgaba al patriarca Miguel Cerulario sobre el altar de ¿qué iglesia?","o":["la iglesia del Santo Sepulcro","la basílica de San Juan de Letrán","Santa Sofía de Constantinopla","la iglesia de los Santos Apóstoles"]}},{"id":"CHRISTIANITY-s10-02","day":809,"d":3,"q":"Anselm of Canterbury described his theology as \"faith seeking understanding\" (fides quaerens intellectum). What does the phrase mean?","o":["faith comes first, then seeks to grasp what it holds","reason must prove each doctrine before it is believed","understanding replaces faith once a person is learned","faith and reason study separate truths that never meet"],"a":0,"es":{"q":"Anselmo de Canterbury describió su teología como \"la fe que busca entender\" (fides quaerens intellectum). ¿Qué significa la frase?","o":["la fe va primero y luego busca entender lo que cree","la razón debe probar cada doctrina antes de creerla","entender reemplaza a la fe cuando uno ya es instruido","la fe y la razón estudian verdades que nunca se tocan"]}},{"id":"CHRISTIANITY-s10-03","day":826,"d":3,"q":"Gregory Palamas defended the hesychast monks of Mount Athos, who said that in prayer they could see God's uncreated light. With which New Testament event did they identify that light?","o":["the star that led the Magi to Bethlehem","the Transfiguration on Mount Tabor","the tongues of fire at Pentecost","the light at Paul's conversion"],"a":1,"es":{"q":"Gregorio Palamás defendió a los monjes hesicastas del monte Athos, que decían ver en la oración la luz increada de Dios. ¿Con qué hecho del Nuevo Testamento identificaban esa luz?","o":["la estrella que guió a los magos a Belén","la Transfiguración en el monte Tabor","las lenguas de fuego en Pentecostés","la luz en la conversión de Pablo"]}},{"id":"CHRISTIANITY-s10-04","day":846,"d":3,"q":"A poor pilgrim arrives unannounced at a Benedictine monastery late in the day. According to chapter 53 of the Rule of Saint Benedict, how are the monks to receive him?","o":["at the gate only, so the monks' silence is kept","only once he can pay for his food and lodging","after three days of fasting outside the walls","as Christ, with special care since he is poor"],"a":3,"es":{"q":"Un peregrino pobre llega sin aviso a un monasterio benedictino al final del día. Según el capítulo 53 de la Regla de san Benito, ¿cómo deben recibirlo los monjes?","o":["solo en la puerta, para no romper el silencio","solo cuando pueda pagar su comida y alojamiento","después de tres días de ayuno fuera de los muros","como a Cristo, con más cuidado por ser pobre"]}},{"id":"CHRISTIANITY-s10-05","day":852,"d":3,"q":"Martin Luther later wrote that his breakthrough came over \"the righteousness of God\" in Romans 1:17. How did he come to read that phrase?","o":["as the justice by which God punishes the unrighteous","as the merit earned by keeping a religious rule","as the holiness reached through frequent confession","as the righteousness God gives freely through faith"],"a":3,"es":{"q":"Martín Lutero escribió después que su gran descubrimiento fue sobre \"la justicia de Dios\" en Romanos 1:17. ¿Cómo llegó a leer esa frase?","o":["como la justicia con que Dios castiga a los injustos","como el mérito ganado al cumplir una regla religiosa","como la santidad alcanzada con la confesión frecuente","como la justicia que Dios da gratis por medio de la fe"]}},{"id":"CHRISTIANITY-s10-06","day":860,"d":3,"q":"In Zurich in 1525, Conrad Grebel, Felix Manz and their circle began baptizing one another as adults. Why, in their reading of the New Testament?","o":["baptism must be given again after every grave sin","baptism should follow one's own confession of faith","baptism is valid only when done in a flowing river","baptism counts only when a worthy priest performs it"],"a":1,"es":{"q":"En Zúrich, en 1525, Conrad Grebel, Félix Manz y su círculo empezaron a bautizarse unos a otros siendo adultos. ¿Por qué, según su lectura del Nuevo Testamento?","o":["el bautismo debe repetirse después de cada pecado grave","el bautismo debe seguir a la propia confesión de fe","el bautismo solo vale si se hace en un río que corre","el bautismo solo cuenta si lo da un sacerdote digno"]}}],[{"id":"CHRISTIANITY-s11-01","day":894,"d":3,"q":"in John Wesley's journal for 24 May 1738, at a society meeting in Aldersgate Street, London, he felt his heart \"strangely warmed.\" what was being read aloud at that moment?","o":["Calvin's Institutes of the Christian Religion","Thomas à Kempis's The Imitation of Christ","Luther's preface to the letter to the Romans","Bunyan's The Pilgrim's Progress, part one"],"a":2,"es":{"q":"en el diario de John Wesley del 24 de mayo de 1738, en una reunión de una sociedad en la calle Aldersgate, en Londres, sintió su corazón \"extrañamente reconfortado\". ¿qué se estaba leyendo en voz alta en ese momento?","o":["la Institución de la religión cristiana de Calvino","La imitación de Cristo de Tomás de Kempis","el prefacio de Lutero a la carta a los Romanos","El progreso del peregrino de Bunyan, primera parte"]}},{"id":"CHRISTIANITY-s11-02","day":901,"d":3,"q":"the Philokalia, the anthology compiled by Nikodemos of the Holy Mountain and Makarios of Corinth and printed in 1782, gathers Orthodox writings mainly on which subject?","o":["the lives of the saints for each day of the year","inner prayer and watchfulness of the heart","the canons of the seven ecumenical councils","the rubrics for celebrating the Divine Liturgy"],"a":1,"es":{"q":"la Filocalia, la antología que reunieron Nicodemo el Hagiorita y Macario de Corinto y que se imprimió en 1782, recoge escritos ortodoxos sobre todo acerca de ¿qué tema?","o":["las vidas de los santos para cada día del año","la oración interior y la vigilancia del corazón","los cánones de los siete concilios ecuménicos","las rúbricas para celebrar la Divina Liturgia"]}},{"id":"CHRISTIANITY-s11-03","day":890,"d":3,"q":"Blaise Pascal's \"Memorial\" of his night of 23 November 1654 begins \"Fire. God of Abraham, God of Isaac, God of Jacob, not of the philosophers and scholars.\" what is he saying by that contrast?","o":["reason is sinful, so a believer should give up philosophy","the God of Israel is a different God from the God of Jesus Christ","God can be proven step by step, as a theorem in geometry","he met a living, personal God, not a God reached by argument"],"a":3,"es":{"q":"el \"Memorial\" de Blaise Pascal sobre su noche del 23 de noviembre de 1654 empieza: \"Fuego. Dios de Abraham, Dios de Isaac, Dios de Jacob, no de los filósofos y de los sabios\". ¿qué quiere decir con ese contraste?","o":["la razón es pecado, y el creyente debe dejar la filosofía","el Dios de Israel es otro Dios distinto del Dios de Cristo","a Dios se lo demuestra paso a paso, como un teorema de geometría","encontró a un Dios vivo y personal, no a un Dios de argumentos"]}},{"id":"CHRISTIANITY-s11-04","day":963,"d":2,"q":"what did the Second Vatican Council's constitution on the liturgy, Sacrosanctum Concilium (1963), do for the Catholic Mass?","o":["allowed local languages and called for the people's full, active part","abolished Latin and removed it from every Catholic Mass in the world","required Latin alone, so that the Mass would sound the same in every land","kept the prayers for the clergy and asked the laity to pray silently"],"a":0,"es":{"q":"¿qué hizo por la misa católica la constitución del Concilio Vaticano II sobre la liturgia, Sacrosanctum Concilium (1963)?","o":["permitió lenguas locales y pidió la participación plena y activa","abolió el latín y lo quitó de todas las misas católicas del mundo","exigió solo el latín, para que la misa sonara igual en todas partes","dejó las oraciones al clero y pidió a los laicos rezar en silencio"]}},{"id":"CHRISTIANITY-s11-05","day":964,"d":3,"q":"on 7 December 1965, Pope Paul VI and Ecumenical Patriarch Athenagoras issued a joint Catholic-Orthodox declaration. what did it do?","o":["restored full communion between the Catholic and Orthodox churches","lifted the 1054 excommunications; full unity still lay ahead","settled the filioque quarrel with a new creed that both churches signed","placed the patriarch of Constantinople under the authority of Rome"],"a":1,"es":{"q":"el 7 de diciembre de 1965, el papa Pablo VI y el patriarca ecuménico Atenágoras publicaron una declaración conjunta católico-ortodoxa. ¿qué hizo?","o":["restableció la comunión plena entre la Iglesia católica y la ortodoxa","levantó las excomuniones de 1054; la unidad plena seguía pendiente","resolvió la disputa del filioque con un nuevo credo firmado por ambas","puso al patriarca de Constantinopla bajo la autoridad de Roma"]}},{"id":"CHRISTIANITY-s11-06","day":948,"d":4,"q":"a church body announces that its nation's founding story is a second revelation of God, to be preached beside the Bible. how would the first article of the Barmen Declaration (1934) judge this?","o":["acceptable, as long as the nation's leaders also honor the Bible","a question for the state to settle, outside the church's concern","false teaching, since Christ is the one Word of God the church hears","acceptable, if the church's synods vote to approve it by a clear majority"],"a":2,"es":{"q":"una iglesia anuncia que la historia de la fundación de su país es una segunda revelación de Dios, que debe predicarse junto a la Biblia. ¿cómo juzgaría esto el primer artículo de la Declaración de Barmen (1934)?","o":["aceptable, siempre que los líderes del país también honren la Biblia","un asunto que debe resolver el Estado, fuera de lo que toca a la iglesia","falsa doctrina: Cristo es la única Palabra de Dios que la iglesia escucha","aceptable, si los sínodos de la iglesia lo aprueban por una clara mayoría"]}}],[{"id":"CHRISTIANITY-s12-01","day":972,"d":3,"q":"In autumn 1989, weekly Monday prayers for peace in Leipzig, East Germany, led into the candlelit marches that helped bring down the Berlin Wall. In which church were those Monday prayers held?","o":["St. Thomas Church (Thomaskirche)","St. Nicholas Church (Nikolaikirche)","Church of Our Lady (Frauenkirche)","St. Michael's Church (Michaeliskirche)"],"a":1,"es":{"q":"En el otoño de 1989, las oraciones por la paz de cada lunes en Leipzig, Alemania Oriental, dieron paso a las marchas con velas que ayudaron a derribar el Muro de Berlín. ¿En qué iglesia se hacían esas oraciones de los lunes?","o":["la iglesia de Santo Tomás (Thomaskirche)","la iglesia de San Nicolás (Nikolaikirche)","la iglesia de Nuestra Señora (Frauenkirche)","la iglesia de San Miguel (Michaeliskirche)"]}},{"id":"CHRISTIANITY-s12-02","day":988,"d":3,"q":"Georges Lemaître, a Belgian Catholic priest and physicist, proposed the \"primeval atom,\" the idea later called the Big Bang. When church voices hailed it as scientific proof of creation, he objected. What was his reason, as it is usually reported?","o":["physics and scripture ask different questions","his theory showed the universe had no beginning","the Church had already condemned his theory","he held that physics had already disproved God"],"a":0,"es":{"q":"Georges Lemaître, sacerdote católico y físico belga, propuso el \"átomo primitivo\", la idea que después se llamó Big Bang. Cuando algunas voces de la Iglesia la celebraron como prueba científica de la creación, él se opuso. ¿Cuál era su razón, según se suele contar?","o":["la física y la Escritura hacen preguntas distintas","su teoría mostraba que el universo no tuvo comienzo","la Iglesia ya había condenado su teoría","pensaba que la física ya había refutado a Dios"]}},{"id":"CHRISTIANITY-s12-03","day":1005,"d":2,"q":"In the Catholic and other Western churches, the third Sunday of Advent is Gaudete Sunday, named for its opening chant \"Rejoice in the Lord always\" (Philippians 4:4). Why are rose vestments and a rose candle used that day?","o":["to mark the end of Advent and the start of Christmas","to honor the martyrs kept in the days after Christmas","to mark joy midway through the waiting: the Lord is near","to mark a stricter fast in the last week before Christmas"],"a":2,"es":{"q":"En la Iglesia católica y otras iglesias occidentales, el tercer domingo de Adviento es el domingo Gaudete, llamado así por su canto de entrada \"Alégrense siempre en el Señor\" (Filipenses 4:4). ¿Por qué ese día se usan ornamentos y una vela de color rosa?","o":["para marcar el fin del Adviento y el inicio de la Navidad","para honrar a los mártires que se recuerdan tras la Navidad","para marcar alegría en plena espera: el Señor está cerca","para marcar un ayuno más estricto antes de la Navidad"]}},{"id":"CHRISTIANITY-s12-04","day":1016,"d":3,"q":"Eastern Orthodox churches keep 6 January as Theophany (\"God appearing\"), the feast of Jesus's baptism in the river Jordan. According to the feast's own hymn, what is made manifest at the Jordan?","o":["Jesus becoming God's Son by adoption at that moment","the worship of the Trinity: Father, Son and Holy Spirit","Christ as king to the Gentiles, through the Magi's visit","Christ's glory through his first miracle, water into wine"],"a":1,"es":{"q":"Las iglesias ortodoxas orientales celebran el 6 de enero la Teofanía (\"Dios que se manifiesta\"), la fiesta del bautismo de Jesús en el río Jordán. Según el himno propio de la fiesta, ¿qué se manifiesta en el Jordán?","o":["que Jesús se vuelve Hijo de Dios por adopción en ese momento","la adoración de la Trinidad: Padre, Hijo y Espíritu Santo","Cristo como rey de los gentiles, por la visita de los magos","la gloria de Cristo en su primer milagro, el agua en vino"]}},{"id":"CHRISTIANITY-s12-05","day":1025,"d":2,"q":"On 25 March, the feast of the Annunciation (Luke 1:26–38), a preacher says: \"Today the Word became flesh\" (John 1:14). What does that claim hold about this feast?","o":["Mary herself was conceived free from original sin on this day","Jesus was adopted as God's Son when the angel spoke to Mary","Christ's incarnation began at his conception in Mary's womb","the Word first took flesh at the birth in Bethlehem, months on"],"a":2,"es":{"q":"El 25 de marzo, fiesta de la Anunciación (Lucas 1:26–38), un predicador dice: \"Hoy el Verbo se hizo carne\" (Juan 1:14). ¿Qué sostiene esa afirmación sobre esta fiesta?","o":["que María misma fue concebida sin pecado original este día","que Jesús fue adoptado como Hijo de Dios al hablar el ángel","que la encarnación de Cristo empezó en su concepción en María","que el Verbo tomó carne recién al nacer en Belén, meses después"]}},{"id":"CHRISTIANITY-s12-06","day":1047,"d":1,"q":"In the Gospels of Matthew, Mark and Luke, Jesus is transfigured on a high mountain before Peter, James and John, his face shining like the sun. Which two figures appear there talking with him?","o":["Abraham and Isaac","Elijah and Elisha","Moses and Aaron","Moses and Elijah"],"a":3,"es":{"q":"En los Evangelios de Mateo, Marcos y Lucas, Jesús se transfigura en un monte alto delante de Pedro, Santiago y Juan, con el rostro brillando como el sol. ¿Qué dos figuras aparecen allí hablando con él?","o":["Abraham e Isaac","Elías y Eliseo","Moisés y Aarón","Moisés y Elías"]}}],[{"id":"CHRISTIANITY-s13-01","day":1071,"d":2,"q":"Western churches such as the Catholic and Anglican churches say the Latin word filioque in the Nicene Creed's line about the Holy Spirit. what does filioque mean?","o":["of one being","from the Father","and the Son","and the Word"],"a":2,"es":{"q":"iglesias occidentales como la católica y la anglicana dicen la palabra latina filioque en la línea del Credo niceno sobre el Espíritu Santo. ¿qué significa filioque?","o":["de una sola esencia","desde el Padre","y del Hijo","y del Verbo"]}},{"id":"CHRISTIANITY-s13-02","day":1077,"d":3,"q":"in the fifth-century dispute between Augustine of Hippo and the monk Pelagius, what did Augustine hold about a person's ability to do good?","o":["the will itself is wounded and needs God's grace first to choose good","free will and God's commandments are enough for a person to obey God","good efforts made on one's own earn the grace that God then gives","grace means the good example Jesus set, which anyone can copy"],"a":0,"es":{"q":"en la disputa del siglo V entre Agustín de Hipona y el monje Pelagio, ¿qué sostenía Agustín sobre la capacidad de una persona para hacer el bien?","o":["la voluntad misma está herida y necesita primero la gracia de Dios para elegir el bien","el libre albedrío y los mandamientos de Dios bastan para que una persona obedezca a Dios","los buenos esfuerzos hechos por cuenta propia ganan la gracia que Dios da después","la gracia es el buen ejemplo que dio Jesús, que cualquiera puede imitar"]}},{"id":"CHRISTIANITY-s13-03","day":1083,"d":4,"q":"in Anselm of Canterbury's Why God Became Human (Cur Deus Homo), why must the one who makes satisfaction for sin be both God and human?","o":["the devil holds rights over humankind that only God can buy back","God's anger must fall as punishment on someone who is sinless","people need a perfect human example of love to move them to repent","humankind owes the debt, but only God is able to pay it in full"],"a":3,"es":{"q":"en Por qué Dios se hizo hombre (Cur Deus Homo), de Anselmo de Canterbury, ¿por qué quien da satisfacción por el pecado tiene que ser a la vez Dios y humano?","o":["el diablo tiene derechos sobre la humanidad que solo Dios puede rescatar","la ira de Dios debe caer como castigo sobre alguien sin pecado","la gente necesita un ejemplo humano perfecto de amor que la mueva a arrepentirse","la humanidad debe la deuda, pero solo Dios puede pagarla por completo"]}},{"id":"CHRISTIANITY-s13-04","day":1116,"d":2,"q":"in chapter 7 of the Rule of Saint Benedict, what biblical picture does Benedict use for the twelve steps of humility?","o":["the stairs of Solomon's temple","the ladder in Jacob's dream","the mountain Moses climbed","the tower built at Babel"],"a":1,"es":{"q":"en el capítulo 7 de la Regla de san Benito, ¿qué imagen bíblica usa Benito para los doce grados de la humildad?","o":["las gradas del templo de Salomón","la escalera del sueño de Jacob","el monte que subió Moisés","la torre construida en Babel"]}},{"id":"CHRISTIANITY-s13-05","day":1144,"d":3,"q":"a man first wants more possessions, then wants to be admired for them, and ends up looking down on everyone. in Ignatius of Loyola's meditation on the Two Standards, whose steps, in what order, has he followed?","o":["the enemy's: pride, then honor, then riches","Christ's: poverty, then insults, then humility","the enemy's: pleasure, then envy, then despair","the enemy's: riches, then honor, then pride"],"a":3,"es":{"q":"un hombre primero quiere más posesiones, después quiere que lo admiren por ellas y termina mirando a todos por encima del hombro. en la meditación de las Dos Banderas de Ignacio de Loyola, ¿qué pasos ha seguido, y en qué orden?","o":["los del enemigo: soberbia, luego honor, luego riquezas","los de Cristo: pobreza, luego oprobios, luego humildad","los del enemigo: placer, luego envidia, luego desesperación","los del enemigo: riquezas, luego honor, luego soberbia"]}},{"id":"CHRISTIANITY-s13-06","day":1135,"d":3,"q":"in Teresa of Ávila's The Interior Castle, the soul is a castle with seven dwelling places (moradas). what is in the innermost one?","o":["the door of prayer through which the soul first enters","a dark night where God seems to have gone far away","God, the King, dwelling at the very center of the soul","a store of merits the soul has earned by its good works"],"a":2,"es":{"q":"en Las moradas del castillo interior, de Teresa de Ávila, el alma es un castillo con siete moradas. ¿qué hay en la más interior?","o":["la puerta de la oración por la que el alma entra primero","una noche oscura en la que Dios parece haberse ido lejos","Dios, el Rey, que habita en el centro mismo del alma","un depósito de méritos que el alma ganó con sus buenas obras"]}}],[{"id":"CHRISTIANITY-s14-01","day":1158,"d":3,"q":"the Heidelberg Catechism, a Reformed book of questions and answers, opens by asking \"What is your only comfort in life and in death?\" how does its answer begin?","o":["that my good works will be weighed fairly at the judgment","that I am not my own, but belong to Jesus Christ","that the church holds the keys to the kingdom of heaven","that God's law is set down clearly in holy Scripture"],"a":1,"es":{"q":"el Catecismo de Heidelberg, un libro reformado de preguntas y respuestas, empieza preguntando \"¿Cuál es tu único consuelo en la vida y en la muerte?\". ¿cómo comienza su respuesta?","o":["que mis buenas obras serán pesadas con justicia en el juicio","que no me pertenezco a mí mismo, sino a Jesucristo","que la iglesia tiene las llaves del reino de los cielos","que la ley de Dios está escrita con claridad en la Escritura"]}},{"id":"CHRISTIANITY-s14-02","day":1165,"d":2,"q":"in an unprogrammed Quaker meeting for worship, with no pastor and no set order of service, how does the hour usually go?","o":["an elder reads set prayers aloud, and the people answer","members take turns leading psalms in a fixed rotation","the clerk gives a short sermon, then everyone sings","Friends sit in silence until someone is moved to speak"],"a":3,"es":{"q":"en una reunión de culto cuáquera no programada, sin pastor ni orden de culto fijo, ¿cómo suele transcurrir la hora?","o":["un anciano lee oraciones fijas, y el pueblo responde","los miembros se turnan para dirigir salmos en un orden fijo","el secretario da un sermón breve y luego todos cantan","los Amigos callan hasta que alguien se siente movido a hablar"]}},{"id":"CHRISTIANITY-s14-03","day":1183,"d":4,"q":"Catholics and Lutherans, following Augustine, treat the ban on carved images as part of the first commandment. how do they still count ten commandments?","o":["they divide the command against coveting into two","they divide the sabbath command into rest and worship","they add Jesus' new command to love one another","they count honoring mother and father as two"],"a":0,"es":{"q":"los católicos y los luteranos, siguiendo a Agustín, toman la prohibición de imágenes talladas como parte del primer mandamiento. ¿cómo llegan aun así a diez mandamientos?","o":["dividen en dos el mandamiento contra la codicia","dividen el mandamiento del sábado en descanso y culto","añaden el mandamiento nuevo de Jesús de amarse","cuentan honrar al padre y a la madre como dos"]}},{"id":"CHRISTIANITY-s14-04","day":1204,"d":4,"q":"the desert monk Evagrius called acedia, the old name behind the sin of sloth, \"the noonday demon.\" what did he mean by acedia?","o":["a burning anger at the brothers who disturb one's prayer","a hunger for praise from the visitors who come to the cell","a heavy, restless boredom with prayer and the life chosen","a love of rich food that breaks the monk's daily fast"],"a":2,"es":{"q":"el monje del desierto Evagrio llamó a la acedia, el nombre antiguo detrás del pecado de la pereza, \"el demonio del mediodía\". ¿qué quería decir con acedia?","o":["un enojo ardiente contra los hermanos que estorban la oración","un hambre de elogios de las visitas que llegan a la celda","un tedio pesado e inquieto ante la oración y la vida elegida","un gusto por la comida rica que rompe el ayuno diario del monje"]}},{"id":"CHRISTIANITY-s14-05","day":1214,"d":3,"q":"Martin Luther taught that a milkmaid's work, done in faith, pleases God as much as a monk's. what was his point about vocation?","o":["only those who take holy vows receive a real calling","God calls ordinary people to serve others in daily work","hard physical labor earns more grace from God than prayer","good work earns salvation, whatever a person's station"],"a":1,"es":{"q":"Martín Lutero enseñó que el trabajo de una lechera, hecho con fe, agrada a Dios tanto como el de un monje. ¿qué quería decir sobre la vocación?","o":["solo quienes hacen votos santos reciben un llamado real","Dios llama a la gente común a servir al prójimo en su trabajo","el trabajo físico duro gana más gracia ante Dios que la oración","las buenas obras ganan la salvación, sea cual sea tu oficio"]}},{"id":"CHRISTIANITY-s14-06","day":1229,"d":3,"q":"a woman feels wronged by a close friend in her congregation. following Jesus' steps in Matthew 18:15–17, what should come first?","o":["going to the friend and naming the fault, just the two of them","asking the pastor to settle it before saying anything at all","writing a complaint to the elders and then waiting for their ruling","waiting quietly until the friend comes to her to apologize"],"a":0,"es":{"q":"una mujer se siente ofendida por una amiga cercana de su congregación. según los pasos de Jesús en Mateo 18:15–17, ¿qué debe venir primero?","o":["ir con la amiga y decirle su falta, solo entre las dos","pedirle al pastor que lo resuelva antes de decir nada","escribir una queja a los ancianos y esperar su decisión","esperar en silencio hasta que la amiga venga a disculparse"]}}],[{"id":"CHRISTIANITY-s15-01","day":1238,"d":3,"q":"Irenaeus of Lyon, in Against Heresies, answered teachers (later called Gnostics) who said matter was a trap made by a lesser power. On what grounds did he reject that view?","o":["the soul is spirit alone, so matter can never truly touch it","the body is a prison, but one God built to purify the soul","salvation comes by secret knowledge kept by the apostles","God made the material world good, and the Word became flesh"],"a":3,"es":{"q":"Ireneo de Lyon, en Contra las herejías, respondió a maestros (más tarde llamados gnósticos) que decían que la materia era una trampa hecha por un poder inferior. ¿Con qué fundamento rechazó esa idea?","o":["el alma es solo espíritu, así que la materia nunca la toca de verdad","el cuerpo es una cárcel, pero una que Dios hizo para purificar el alma","la salvación viene por un saber secreto que guardaron los apóstoles","Dios hizo bueno el mundo material, y el Verbo se hizo carne"]}},{"id":"CHRISTIANITY-s15-02","day":1250,"d":2,"q":"In the Summa Theologiae, Thomas Aquinas sets out five ways to show that God exists. From what does the first way begin?","o":["from a moral law written in every human conscience","from motion: whatever is moved is moved by another","from the idea of a being than which none is greater","from the miracles recorded in the four Gospels"],"a":1,"es":{"q":"En la Suma teológica, Tomás de Aquino presenta cinco vías para mostrar que Dios existe. ¿De qué parte la primera vía?","o":["de una ley moral escrita en toda conciencia humana","del movimiento: todo lo que se mueve es movido por otro","de la idea de un ser mayor que el cual no hay nada","de los milagros que narran los cuatro Evangelios"]}},{"id":"CHRISTIANITY-s15-03","day":1253,"d":3,"q":"Two explanations fit the same symptoms equally well: one needs three separate rare illnesses, the other a single common one. Which would William of Ockham's \"razor\" favor, and why?","o":["the three illnesses, since more causes explain more","the single illness, since causes need not be multiplied","neither, since only revelation can explain illness","both at once, since each fits the symptoms equally"],"a":1,"es":{"q":"Dos explicaciones encajan igual de bien con los mismos síntomas: una necesita tres enfermedades raras distintas; la otra, una sola enfermedad común. ¿Cuál preferiría la \"navaja\" de Guillermo de Ockham, y por qué?","o":["las tres enfermedades, porque más causas explican más","la sola enfermedad, porque no hay que multiplicar causas","ninguna, porque solo la revelación explica la enfermedad","las dos a la vez, porque las dos encajan con los síntomas"]}},{"id":"CHRISTIANITY-s15-04","day":1255,"d":3,"q":"Martin Luther's The Freedom of a Christian (1520) opens with two theses: a Christian is a free lord of all, subject to none, and a dutiful servant of all, subject to all. How does the treatise hold them together?","o":["lord over others in this life, servant only in the age to come","lord by good works done well, servant by obeying the old law","lord once baptized, servant until every penance is complete","lord through faith in God's promise, servant through love"],"a":3,"es":{"q":"La libertad cristiana (1520), de Martín Lutero, abre con dos tesis: el cristiano es señor libre de todo, sujeto a nadie, y siervo obediente de todos, sujeto a todos. ¿Cómo une el tratado las dos?","o":["señor de otros en esta vida, siervo solo en la vida futura","señor por obras bien hechas, siervo por cumplir la ley antigua","señor desde el bautismo, siervo hasta cumplir cada penitencia","señor por la fe en la promesa de Dios, siervo por el amor"]}},{"id":"CHRISTIANITY-s15-05","day":1298,"d":2,"q":"In Revelation 5, an elder tells the weeping John that the Lion of the tribe of Judah has prevailed to open the sealed scroll. What does John see when he looks?","o":["a Lamb standing, as though it had been slain","a lion standing with seven horns and seven eyes","a rider on a white horse, wearing a crown","a mighty angel holding a little open scroll"],"a":0,"es":{"q":"En Apocalipsis 5, un anciano le dice a Juan, que está llorando, que el León de la tribu de Judá ha vencido para abrir el rollo sellado. ¿Qué ve Juan cuando mira?","o":["un Cordero de pie, como si lo hubieran degollado","un león de pie, con siete cuernos y siete ojos","un jinete en un caballo blanco, con corona","un ángel poderoso con un rollo pequeño ya abierto"]}},{"id":"CHRISTIANITY-s15-06","day":1325,"d":3,"q":"In 1 Corinthians 15, Paul answers the question \"with what body do they come?\" by pointing to a seed sown in the ground. What does the image teach about the resurrection body?","o":["the body is planted again and grows back exactly as it was","the soul rises free and leaves every kind of body behind","what is sown and what is raised are one life, yet changed","the dead return to the earth and are born again as infants"],"a":2,"es":{"q":"En 1 Corintios 15, Pablo responde a la pregunta \"¿con qué cuerpo vendrán?\" señalando una semilla sembrada en la tierra. ¿Qué enseña la imagen sobre el cuerpo resucitado?","o":["el cuerpo se siembra otra vez y vuelve a crecer tal como era","el alma se levanta libre y deja atrás todo tipo de cuerpo","lo que se siembra y lo que resucita es una vida, pero cambiada","los muertos vuelven a la tierra y renacen como recién nacidos"]}}],[{"id":"CHRISTIANITY-s16-01","day":1336,"d":3,"q":"In the Orthodox Divine Liturgy of Saint John Chrysostom, what is the procession called in which the clergy carry the bread and wine to the altar?","o":["the Little Entrance","the Great Entrance","the Proskomedia","the Kiss of Peace"],"a":1,"es":{"q":"En la Divina Liturgia ortodoxa de san Juan Crisóstomo, ¿cómo se llama la procesión en la que el clero lleva el pan y el vino al altar?","o":["la Pequeña Entrada","la Gran Entrada","la Proscomidia","el beso de la paz"]}},{"id":"CHRISTIANITY-s16-02","day":1379,"d":3,"q":"Which lament psalm in the Bible is known for ending in darkness, with no closing turn to trust or praise?","o":["Psalm 13","Psalm 22","Psalm 42","Psalm 88"],"a":3,"es":{"q":"¿Qué salmo de lamento de la Biblia es conocido por terminar en la oscuridad, sin un giro final hacia la confianza o la alabanza?","o":["Salmo 13","Salmo 22","Salmo 42","Salmo 88"]}},{"id":"CHRISTIANITY-s16-03","day":1378,"d":3,"q":"At the end of the Book of Job, why does God tell Eliphaz that his anger burns against him and his two friends?","o":["they had not spoken what was right of God, as Job had","they had left Job alone in his grief on the ash heap","they had questioned God's justice alongside Job","they had failed to offer sacrifices for Job's children"],"a":0,"es":{"q":"Al final del libro de Job, ¿por qué le dice Dios a Elifaz que su enojo arde contra él y sus dos amigos?","o":["no habían hablado de Dios lo que era recto, como Job","habían dejado a Job solo en su dolor sobre la ceniza","habían cuestionado la justicia de Dios junto con Job","no habían ofrecido sacrificios por los hijos de Job"]}},{"id":"CHRISTIANITY-s16-04","day":1389,"d":3,"q":"In 2 Corinthians 12, Paul asks the Lord three times to take away his \"thorn in the flesh.\" What answer does he report?","o":["the thorn would be taken away once his work was done","he would be healed if he prayed with greater faith","my grace is enough; power is made perfect in weakness","the thorn was a just punishment he must bear in silence"],"a":2,"es":{"q":"En 2 Corintios 12, Pablo le pide al Señor tres veces que le quite su \"aguijón en la carne\". ¿Qué respuesta dice haber recibido?","o":["le quitaría el aguijón una vez que terminara toda su obra","sanaría por completo si oraba con una fe más grande","bástate mi gracia; el poder se perfecciona en la debilidad","el aguijón era un justo castigo que debía llevar en silencio"]}},{"id":"CHRISTIANITY-s16-05","day":1415,"d":3,"q":"In 2 Corinthians 4:7, why does Paul say the treasure of the gospel is held in \"earthen vessels,\" that is, clay jars?","o":["so the apostles are honored as craftsmen of the church","so the surpassing power is seen to be God's, not ours","so believers keep their faith as a private matter","so the gospel will fade when Christ comes again in glory"],"a":1,"es":{"q":"En 2 Corintios 4:7, ¿por qué dice Pablo que el tesoro del evangelio está en \"vasos de barro\", es decir, en vasijas de arcilla?","o":["para que se honre a los apóstoles como artesanos de la iglesia","para que se vea que el gran poder es de Dios y no nuestro","para que los creyentes guarden su fe como asunto privado","para que el evangelio se apague cuando Cristo vuelva en gloria"]}},{"id":"CHRISTIANITY-s16-06","day":1412,"d":4,"q":"A friend in the hospital reads 1 Thessalonians 5:18 and asks whether Paul is telling her to thank God for her illness itself. What do Paul's words in that verse ask?","o":["to give thanks in all circumstances, even in this one","to give thanks once the illness has passed and she is well","to give thanks instead of asking God for her healing","to give thanks when the church gathers on the Lord's Day"],"a":0,"es":{"q":"Una amiga en el hospital lee 1 Tesalonicenses 5:18 y pregunta si Pablo le pide dar gracias a Dios por la enfermedad misma. ¿Qué piden las palabras de Pablo en ese versículo?","o":["dar gracias en toda circunstancia, también en esta","dar gracias cuando la enfermedad pase y ella esté bien","dar gracias en lugar de pedirle a Dios su sanación","dar gracias cuando la iglesia se reúne el día del Señor"]}}]],"HINDUISM":[[{"id":"HINDUISM-s00-01","day":2,"d":1,"q":"In the Mandukya Upanishad, which state of consciousness does the sound M of om (a-u-m) stand for?","o":["the state of waking","the state of dreaming","deep dreamless sleep","the soundless fourth"],"a":2,"es":{"q":"En la Mandukya Upanishad, ¿qué estado de conciencia representa el sonido M de om (a-u-m)?","o":["el estado de vigilia","el estado de soñar","el sueño profundo","el cuarto, sin sonido"]}},{"id":"HINDUISM-s00-02","day":3,"d":1,"q":"The Sanskrit word dharma comes from the verbal root dhṛ. What does that root mean?","o":["to act, to perform","to hold, to uphold","to see, to perceive","to bow, to give way"],"a":1,"es":{"q":"La palabra sánscrita dharma viene de la raíz verbal dhṛ. ¿Qué significa esa raíz?","o":["actuar, llevar a cabo","sostener, sustentar","ver, darse cuenta","inclinarse, ceder"]}},{"id":"HINDUISM-s00-03","day":11,"d":2,"q":"In the Chandogya Upanishad, Uddalaka has his son Shvetaketu dissolve salt in water and then taste it. What is the teaching?","o":["Brahman pervades all, though it cannot be seen","the body must be purified before the self is known","the senses deceive us, so taste cannot be trusted","all things arise from water, the first element"],"a":0,"es":{"q":"En la Chandogya Upanishad, Uddalaka le pide a su hijo Shvetaketu que disuelva sal en agua y luego la pruebe. ¿Cuál es la enseñanza?","o":["Brahman lo impregna todo, aunque no se vea","hay que purificar el cuerpo para conocer el ser","los sentidos engañan; no hay que fiarse del gusto","todo nace del agua, el primero de los elementos"]}},{"id":"HINDUISM-s00-04","day":19,"d":2,"q":"In the Katha Upanishad, Yama offers Nachiketa wealth, long life and kingdoms in place of his third wish. How does Nachiketa respond?","o":["he accepts a kingdom so that he can rule with justice","he asks Yama for a lasting place among the gods","he takes the wealth and gives it away to the poor","he refuses them as fleeting and keeps his question"],"a":3,"es":{"q":"En la Katha Upanishad, Yama le ofrece a Nachiketa riquezas, larga vida y reinos en lugar de su tercer deseo. ¿Cómo responde Nachiketa?","o":["acepta un reino para poder gobernar con justicia","le pide a Yama un lugar eterno entre los dioses","toma las riquezas y las reparte entre los pobres","los rechaza por efímeros y sigue en su pregunta"]}},{"id":"HINDUISM-s00-05","day":16,"d":2,"q":"In Bhagavad Gita 9.26, Krishna says he accepts even a leaf, a flower, a fruit or water. What makes such an offering acceptable to him?","o":["the purity of the priest who presents it","the devotion with which it is given","the rarity and cost of what is brought","the correct Vedic verse recited with it"],"a":1,"es":{"q":"En el Bhagavad Gita 9.26, Krishna dice que acepta incluso una hoja, una flor, una fruta o agua. ¿Qué hace que esa ofrenda le sea aceptable?","o":["la pureza del sacerdote que la da","la devoción con la que se ofrece","lo raro y costoso de lo que se trae","el verso védico correcto que se recita"]}},{"id":"HINDUISM-s00-06","day":10,"d":2,"q":"A student says, 'My true self is my thoughts.' Following Yajnavalkya in the Brihadaranyaka Upanishad ('you cannot think the thinker of thinking'), what is the reply?","o":["thoughts are known, so they are not the knower","thoughts are pure, so they reveal the true self","thoughts are of the mind, so the mind is the self","thoughts see the world, so they are the seer"],"a":0,"es":{"q":"Un estudiante dice: «Mi verdadero ser son mis pensamientos». Siguiendo a Yajnavalkya en la Brihadaranyaka Upanishad («no puedes pensar al pensador del pensar»), ¿cuál es la respuesta?","o":["los pensamientos se conocen; no son quien conoce","los pensamientos son puros y así revelan el ser","los pensamientos son de la mente, y la mente es el ser","los pensamientos ven el mundo; ellos son quien ve"]}}],[{"id":"HINDUISM-s01-01","day":29,"d":1,"q":"In the Ramayana tradition, what does 'hanu' in the name Hanuman refer to?","o":["his tail, set alight in the city of Lanka","his father, Vayu, the god of the wind","his leap across the ocean to find Sita","his jaw, struck by Indra's thunderbolt"],"a":3,"es":{"q":"En la tradición del Ramayana, ¿a qué se refiere «hanu» en el nombre Hanuman?","o":["a su cola, incendiada en la ciudad de Lanka","a su padre, Vayu, el dios del viento","a su salto sobre el océano para hallar a Sita","a su mandíbula, golpeada por el rayo de Indra"]}},{"id":"HINDUISM-s01-02","day":26,"d":1,"q":"Ganesha is often shown holding his own broken tusk. In the best-known popular telling, what did he use it for?","o":["as a pen to write down Vyasa's dictation","as an offering laid down at his father's feet","as a parting gift for his brother Kartikeya","as a stylus to carve the Vedas in stone"],"a":0,"es":{"q":"A Ganesha se le muestra a menudo con su propio colmillo roto en la mano. En el relato popular más conocido, ¿para qué lo usó?","o":["como pluma para escribir lo que dictaba Vyasa","como ofrenda depositada a los pies de su padre","como regalo de despedida para su hermano Kartikeya","como punzón para grabar los Vedas en piedra"]}},{"id":"HINDUISM-s01-03","day":39,"d":2,"q":"In the Valmiki Ramayana, why does King Dasharatha send Rama into fourteen years of exile?","o":["Rama has broken a law and has to be punished","the priests rule that Bharata is the elder son","he is bound by two boons he once promised Kaikeyi","a sage warns that Rama will bring the kingdom harm"],"a":2,"es":{"q":"En el Ramayana de Valmiki, ¿por qué el rey Dasharatha envía a Rama a catorce años de exilio?","o":["Rama violó una ley y tiene que ser castigado","los sacerdotes deciden que Bharata es el mayor","está atado a dos deseos que le prometió a Kaikeyi","un sabio advierte que Rama dañará al reino"]}},{"id":"HINDUISM-s01-04","day":44,"d":2,"q":"In the Ramayana, after Rama refuses to come back from the forest, how does Bharata govern Ayodhya?","o":["as crowned king, as his mother Kaikeyi wished","as regent, with Rama's sandals on the throne","as heir, until his own son could take the throne","as co-ruler, sharing power with Lakshmana"],"a":1,"es":{"q":"En el Ramayana, después de que Rama se niega a volver del bosque, ¿cómo gobierna Bharata Ayodhya?","o":["como rey coronado, como quería su madre Kaikeyi","como regente, con las sandalias de Rama en el trono","como heredero, hasta que su hijo pudiera reinar","como cogobernante, compartiendo el poder con Lakshmana"]}},{"id":"HINDUISM-s01-05","day":82,"d":2,"q":"Holika Dahan, the bonfire lit on the night before Holi, recalls which story?","o":["Sita passing through fire after the war in Lanka","Hanuman setting Lanka ablaze with his burning tail","Krishna swallowing a forest fire to save the herders","Prahlad surviving the fire that burned his aunt"],"a":3,"es":{"q":"Holika Dahan, la hoguera que se enciende la noche antes de Holi, ¿qué historia recuerda?","o":["Sita atraviesa el fuego después de la guerra en Lanka","Hanuman incendia Lanka con su cola en llamas","Krishna se traga un incendio para salvar a los pastores","Prahlad sobrevive al fuego que quemó a su tía"]}},{"id":"HINDUISM-s01-06","day":83,"d":2,"q":"A temple stays open all night on the fourteenth night of the waning moon in late winter. Devotees fast, pour water and milk over a lingam and offer bilva leaves. Which festival is being kept?","o":["Makar Sankranti","Ganesh Chaturthi","Maha Shivaratri","Vasant Panchami"],"a":2,"es":{"q":"Un templo queda abierto toda la noche en la decimocuarta noche de la luna menguante, a fines del invierno. Los devotos ayunan, vierten agua y leche sobre un lingam y ofrecen hojas de bilva. ¿Qué festividad se celebra?","o":["Makar Sankranti","Ganesh Chaturthi","Maha Shivaratri","Vasant Panchami"]}}],[{"id":"HINDUISM-s02-01","day":108,"d":2,"q":"Which sage does tradition name as the seer of the Gayatri mantra (Rig Veda 3.62.10)?","o":["the sage Vasishtha","the sage Vishvamitra","the sage Bharadvaja","the sage Markandeya"],"a":1,"es":{"q":"¿A qué sabio nombra la tradición como el vidente del mantra Gayatri (Rig Veda 3.62.10)?","o":["el sabio Vasishtha","el sabio Vishvamitra","el sabio Bharadvaja","el sabio Markandeya"]}},{"id":"HINDUISM-s02-02","day":130,"d":2,"q":"When in the Hindu calendar is Ekadashi, a common fast day for devotees of Vishnu, kept?","o":["on the full-moon day of every lunar month","on the eleventh day of every solar month","on the new-moon day of each lunar month","on each fortnight's eleventh lunar day"],"a":3,"es":{"q":"¿Cuándo se guarda en el calendario hindú Ekadashi, un día de ayuno común entre los devotos de Vishnu?","o":["el día de luna llena de cada mes lunar","el día once de cada mes del calendario solar","el día de luna nueva de cada mes lunar","el undécimo día lunar de cada quincena"]}},{"id":"HINDUISM-s02-03","day":133,"d":2,"q":"In Hindu temple worship, what does it mean to 'take darshan' of a deity?","o":["to see the deity's image and be seen by it","to walk clockwise around the inner shrine","to receive food that was offered to the deity","to hear the priest recite the deity's names"],"a":0,"es":{"q":"En el culto del templo hindú, ¿qué significa «tomar darshan» de una deidad?","o":["ver la imagen de la deidad y ser visto por ella","caminar en sentido horario alrededor del santuario","recibir comida que se le ofreció a la deidad","escuchar al sacerdote recitar los nombres de la deidad"]}},{"id":"HINDUISM-s02-04","day":128,"d":2,"q":"Bhagavad Gita 17.8–10 sorts food by the three gunas. Which food does it call sattvic?","o":["very pungent, sour, salty, dry food that burns and stings","stale, tasteless food, left over and kept overnight","savory, rich, lasting food that adds life and health","plain, raw, unseasoned food prepared without oil"],"a":2,"es":{"q":"El Bhagavad Gita 17.8–10 clasifica los alimentos según los tres gunas. ¿Qué comida llama sáttvica?","o":["comida muy picante, agria, salada y seca, que quema","comida rancia, insípida, sobrante, de la víspera","comida sabrosa, untuosa y firme, que da vida y salud","comida simple, cruda, sin sazón y preparada sin aceite"]}},{"id":"HINDUISM-s02-05","day":134,"d":2,"q":"Why is pradakshina, walking around a shrine or sacred place, done clockwise?","o":["so that the holy center stays on one's right","so that one's shadow does not fall on the shrine","so that the walker mirrors the waning moon","so that the shrine's guardians are greeted first"],"a":0,"es":{"q":"¿Por qué la pradakshina, caminar alrededor de un santuario o lugar sagrado, se hace en sentido horario?","o":["para que el centro sagrado quede a la derecha","para que la sombra no caiga sobre el santuario","para que quien camina imite a la luna menguante","para saludar primero a los guardianes del santuario"]}},{"id":"HINDUISM-s02-06","day":151,"d":3,"q":"A family checks the panchang every year for the date of Diwali, but always plans Makar Sankranti for mid-January. What makes this possible?","o":["Sankranti is lunar; Diwali is set by the sun","Diwali is moved each year to match the harvest","priests pick a fresh date for Diwali each year","Sankranti is solar; Diwali is set by the moon"],"a":3,"es":{"q":"Una familia consulta cada año el panchang para saber la fecha de Diwali, pero siempre planea Makar Sankranti para mediados de enero. ¿Qué lo hace posible?","o":["Sankranti es lunar; Diwali depende del sol","Diwali se mueve cada año según la cosecha","cada año los sacerdotes fijan otra fecha","Sankranti es solar; Diwali depende de la luna"]}}],[{"id":"HINDUISM-s03-01","day":157,"d":2,"q":"In the Bhagavad Gita, who reports the battlefield dialogue between Krishna and Arjuna to the blind king Dhritarashtra?","o":["Sanjaya, the king's charioteer and aide","Vidura, the king's wise younger half-brother","Bhishma, the grand elder of the Kuru house","Yudhishthira, the eldest of the Pandavas"],"a":0,"es":{"q":"En el Bhagavad Gita, ¿quién le cuenta al rey ciego Dhritarashtra el diálogo entre Krishna y Arjuna en el campo de batalla?","o":["Sanjaya, auriga y consejero del rey","Vidura, el sabio medio hermano del rey","Bhishma, el gran anciano de la casa Kuru","Yudhishthira, el mayor de los Pandava"]}},{"id":"HINDUISM-s03-02","day":171,"d":2,"q":"In Bhagavad Gita 4.7–8, Krishna says he brings himself forth age after age. When does he say this happens?","o":["whenever the Vedas are recited without faith","whenever a world-age ends in fire and flood","whenever dharma declines and adharma rises","whenever a king breaks his oath to a sage"],"a":2,"es":{"q":"En el Bhagavad Gita 4.7–8, Krishna dice que se manifiesta era tras era. ¿Cuándo dice que esto ocurre?","o":["cuando los Vedas se recitan sin ninguna fe","cuando una era termina en fuego y diluvio","cuando el dharma decae y crece el adharma","cuando un rey rompe su juramento a un sabio"]}},{"id":"HINDUISM-s03-03","day":180,"d":2,"q":"Which image does Bhagavad Gita 6.19 use for the steady mind of a yogi in meditation?","o":["a lotus leaf water cannot wet","a lamp in a place with no wind","a tortoise drawing in its limbs","an ocean unmoved by inflowing rivers"],"a":1,"es":{"q":"¿Qué imagen usa el Bhagavad Gita 6.19 para la mente firme de un yogui en meditación?","o":["una hoja de loto que el agua no moja","una lámpara donde no sopla el viento","una tortuga que recoge sus miembros","un océano que los ríos no agitan"]}},{"id":"HINDUISM-s03-04","day":219,"d":3,"q":"In Bhagavad Gita 18.2, what do the wise call tyaga, relinquishment?","o":["giving up actions done out of desire","giving up home to wander as a monk","giving up food and sleep as austerity","giving up the fruits of all actions"],"a":3,"es":{"q":"En el Bhagavad Gita 18.2, ¿a qué llaman los sabios tyaga, el desprendimiento?","o":["a dejar las acciones hechas por deseo","a dejar el hogar y vagar como monje","a dejar comida y sueño como austeridad","a renunciar a los frutos de toda acción"]}},{"id":"HINDUISM-s03-05","day":207,"d":3,"q":"According to Bhagavad Gita 14.6–8, how does tamas bind the embodied self?","o":["by attachment to happiness and knowledge","by heedlessness, laziness and sleep","by attachment to action and its fruits","by fear of death and grief for the dead"],"a":1,"es":{"q":"Según el Bhagavad Gita 14.6–8, ¿cómo ata tamas al ser encarnado?","o":["con apego a la felicidad y al saber","con la negligencia, la pereza y el sueño","con apego a la acción y sus frutos","con miedo a morir y pena por los muertos"]}},{"id":"HINDUISM-s03-06","day":222,"d":3,"q":"A talented musician envies a friend's legal career and wants to copy it, though it suits neither his gifts nor his nature. Which Bhagavad Gita teaching speaks most directly to this?","o":["the self is unborn and undying, so do not grieve","the wise see the same in a priest and in a dog","better one's own dharma, flawed, than another's","work done as an offering (yajna) does not bind"],"a":2,"es":{"q":"Un músico talentoso envidia la carrera de abogado de un amigo y quiere copiarla, aunque no va con sus dones ni con su naturaleza. ¿Qué enseñanza del Bhagavad Gita habla más directamente de esto?","o":["el ser no nace ni muere, así que no te aflijas","el sabio ve lo mismo en un sacerdote y en un perro","mejor el dharma propio, imperfecto, que el ajeno","el trabajo hecho como ofrenda (yajna) no ata"]}}],[{"id":"HINDUISM-s04-01","day":233,"d":3,"q":"the Isha Upanishad's first verse says \"tena tyaktena bhunjitha.\" in its common reading, which takes bhunjitha as \"enjoy,\" what does that phrase tell the reader to do?","o":["renounce the world in order to reach heaven","enjoy the world while gathering more wealth","enjoy the world through renunciation","give up all action and live in the forest"],"a":2,"es":{"q":"el primer verso de la Isha Upanishad dice \"tena tyaktena bhunjitha\". en su lectura común, que entiende bhunjitha como \"disfruta\", ¿qué le pide esa frase al lector?","o":["renunciar al mundo para llegar al cielo","disfrutar del mundo mientras junta más riqueza","disfrutar del mundo a través de la renuncia","dejar toda acción e irse a vivir al bosque"]}},{"id":"HINDUISM-s04-02","day":243,"d":3,"q":"in the Kena Upanishad's story, the gods boast of a victory, and Agni, the fire god, cannot burn a single blade of grass set before him by a mysterious being (a yaksha). what is the story teaching?","o":["the gods' powers come from Brahman, not from the gods themselves","fire is the weakest of the gods, so it was tested first","the gods won their victory by the power of their own sacrifices","Brahman is seen by the eye once the gods have given up their pride"],"a":0,"es":{"q":"en el relato de la Kena Upanishad, los dioses presumen de una victoria, y Agni, el dios del fuego, no logra quemar una sola brizna de hierba que le pone delante un ser misterioso (un yaksha). ¿qué enseña el relato?","o":["los poderes de los dioses vienen de Brahman, no de los dioses mismos","el fuego es el más débil de los dioses, por eso lo probaron primero","los dioses ganaron la victoria por la fuerza de sus propios sacrificios","Brahman se ve con los ojos cuando los dioses dejan de lado su orgullo"]}},{"id":"HINDUISM-s04-03","day":248,"d":3,"q":"a merchant turns down a profitable but dishonest deal so as to keep his word. in the terms of the Katha Upanishad's two paths (1.2.1–2), what has he chosen?","o":["preyas, the pleasant, over shreyas, the good","shreyas, the good, over preyas, the pleasant","artha, prosperity, over dharma, right conduct","kama, desire, over moksha, liberation"],"a":1,"es":{"q":"un comerciante rechaza un negocio rentable pero deshonesto para cumplir su palabra. en los términos de los dos caminos de la Katha Upanishad (1.2.1–2), ¿qué eligió?","o":["preyas, lo agradable, por encima de shreyas, lo bueno","shreyas, lo bueno, por encima de preyas, lo agradable","artha, la prosperidad, por encima de dharma, la recta conducta","kama, el deseo, por encima de moksha, la liberación"]}},{"id":"HINDUISM-s04-04","day":256,"d":3,"q":"in the Mandukya Upanishad, the third quarter of the self, called prajna (\"the knowing one\"), is one mass of knowing, made of bliss. which state is its field?","o":["the state of waking","the state of dreaming","the fourth, turiya","dreamless deep sleep"],"a":3,"es":{"q":"en la Mandukya Upanishad, el tercer cuarto del ser, llamado prajna (\"el que conoce\"), es una sola masa de conocer, hecha de dicha. ¿cuál es su campo?","o":["el estado de estar despierto","el estado de sueño con sueños","el cuarto estado, turiya","el sueño profundo sin sueños"]}},{"id":"HINDUISM-s04-05","day":289,"d":3,"q":"according to Ramanuja's Vishishtadvaita (\"qualified non-dualism\"), how are the world and individual souls related to God?","o":["they are an illusion laid over Brahman, like a snake seen on a rope","they are fully real and exist entirely independent of God","they are a dream of God that ends when God wakes from it","they are real and form God's body, wholly dependent on God"],"a":3,"es":{"q":"según el Vishishtadvaita de Ramanuja (\"no dualismo calificado\"), ¿cómo se relacionan el mundo y las almas individuales con Dios?","o":["son una ilusión sobre Brahman, como la serpiente en la cuerda","son plenamente reales y existen del todo independientes de Dios","son solo un sueño de Dios, que se acaba cuando él despierta","son reales y forman el cuerpo de Dios, dependientes de él"]}},{"id":"HINDUISM-s04-06","day":320,"d":3,"q":"among the Bhagavad Gita's three kinds of gift (17.20–22), which kind is a gift given expecting something in return, or given grudgingly?","o":["sattvic, of clarity and goodness","rajasic, of restless passion","tamasic, of dullness and inertia","daivi, of the divine qualities"],"a":1,"es":{"q":"entre los tres tipos de regalo del Bhagavad Gita (17.20–22), ¿de qué tipo es un regalo dado esperando algo a cambio, o dado de mala gana?","o":["sáttvico, de claridad y bondad","rajásico, de pasión inquieta","tamásico, de torpeza e inercia","daivi, de las cualidades divinas"]}}],[{"id":"HINDUISM-s05-01","day":404,"d":3,"q":"which Upanishad contains the great saying (mahavakya) \"prajnanam brahma,\" \"consciousness is Brahman\"?","o":["the Aitareya Upanishad","the Chandogya Upanishad","the Taittiriya Upanishad","the Mandukya Upanishad"],"a":0,"es":{"q":"¿qué Upanishad contiene la gran sentencia (mahavakya) \"prajnanam brahma\", \"la conciencia es Brahman\"?","o":["la Aitareya Upanishad","la Chandogya Upanishad","la Taittiriya Upanishad","la Mandukya Upanishad"]}},{"id":"HINDUISM-s05-02","day":340,"d":3,"q":"in the Chandogya Upanishad (6.1.4), Uddalaka tells his son Shvetaketu that by knowing one lump of clay, everything made of clay is known. what point is he making?","o":["the world was shaped by the gods as a potter shapes clay","knowing many objects one at a time adds up to knowing all","pots differ only in name; the clay alone is what is real","the clay changes its true nature each time it is shaped"],"a":2,"es":{"q":"en la Chandogya Upanishad (6.1.4), Uddalaka le dice a su hijo Shvetaketu que al conocer un solo terrón de barro se conoce todo lo hecho de barro. ¿qué quiere mostrar?","o":["los dioses dieron forma al mundo como un alfarero al barro","conocer muchas cosas una por una suma hasta conocerlo todo","las vasijas difieren solo en el nombre; lo real es el barro","el barro cambia su verdadera naturaleza cada vez que se moldea"]}},{"id":"HINDUISM-s05-03","day":358,"d":4,"q":"in the Chandogya Upanishad (8.9), why does Indra turn back to Prajapati after being taught that the self is the body seen reflected in water?","o":["he forgot the teaching on his way home and had to hear it again","he saw that such a self would decay and die with the body","Virochana challenged him to a debate that he could not win","the gods refused to accept him as king until he learned more"],"a":1,"es":{"q":"en la Chandogya Upanishad (8.9), ¿por qué Indra vuelve con Prajapati después de que le enseñaron que el ser es el cuerpo reflejado en el agua?","o":["olvidó la enseñanza camino a casa y tuvo que oírla de nuevo","vio que ese ser se deterioraría y moriría junto con el cuerpo","Virochana lo desafió a un debate que él no podía ganar","los dioses no lo aceptaban como rey hasta que aprendiera más"]}},{"id":"HINDUISM-s05-04","day":377,"d":3,"q":"at King Janaka's court in the Brihadaranyaka Upanishad, which woman questions Yajnavalkya about what everything is \"woven\" on?","o":["Maitreyi, his wife","Katyayani, his wife","Apala, a Vedic seer","Gargi Vachaknavi"],"a":3,"es":{"q":"en la corte del rey Janaka, en la Brihadaranyaka Upanishad, ¿qué mujer le pregunta a Yajnavalkya sobre qué está \"tejido\" todo?","o":["Maitreyi, su esposa","Katyayani, su esposa","Apala, una rishika","Gargi Vachaknavi"]}},{"id":"HINDUISM-s05-05","day":393,"d":3,"q":"in the Taittiriya Upanishad (2.1–2.5), which is the innermost of the five sheaths (koshas) of the self?","o":["anandamaya, made of bliss","vijnanamaya, made of insight","manomaya, made of the mind","pranamaya, made of breath"],"a":0,"es":{"q":"en la Taittiriya Upanishad (2.1–2.5), ¿cuál es la más interior de las cinco envolturas (koshas) del ser?","o":["anandamaya, hecha de dicha","vijnanamaya, hecha de saber","manomaya, hecha de mente","pranamaya, hecha de aliento"]}},{"id":"HINDUISM-s05-06","day":411,"d":4,"q":"a scholar has mastered the four Vedas, phonetics, grammar and ritual, but has not come to know the imperishable. in the Mundaka Upanishad's terms (1.1.4–5), what kind of knowledge does he have?","o":["para vidya, the higher knowledge","apara vidya, the lower knowledge","brahma vidya, knowledge of Brahman","atma vidya, knowing the self"],"a":1,"es":{"q":"un erudito domina los cuatro Vedas, la fonética, la gramática y el ritual, pero no ha llegado a conocer lo imperecedero. en los términos de la Mundaka Upanishad (1.1.4–5), ¿qué clase de conocimiento tiene?","o":["para vidya, el conocimiento superior","apara vidya, el conocimiento inferior","brahma vidya, el conocimiento de Brahman","atma vidya, el conocimiento del ser"]}}],[{"id":"HINDUISM-s06-01","day":428,"d":3,"q":"the last verse of the Shvetashvatara Upanishad (6.23) says its teachings shine for one who has the highest devotion (bhakti) to God, and the same devotion to whom?","o":["to one's mother and father","to a guest at one's door","to one's teacher (guru)","to the king of one's land"],"a":2,"es":{"q":"el último verso de la Shvetashvatara Upanishad (6.23) dice que sus enseñanzas brillan para quien tiene la más alta devoción (bhakti) a Dios, y la misma devoción ¿a quién?","o":["a su madre y a su padre","a un huésped en su puerta","a su maestro, el guru","al rey de su propia tierra"]}},{"id":"HINDUISM-s06-02","day":430,"d":3,"q":"how does Patanjali define yoga in Yoga Sutra 1.2?","o":["the stilling of the turnings of the mind","the union of the individual self with God","a steady and comfortable posture of the body","the regulation of the breath's in and out flow"],"a":0,"es":{"q":"¿cómo define Patanjali el yoga en el Yoga Sutra 1.2?","o":["el aquietamiento de los giros de la mente","la unión del ser individual con Dios","una postura del cuerpo firme y cómoda","el manejo del aliento al entrar y salir"]}},{"id":"HINDUISM-s06-03","day":449,"d":4,"q":"Yoga Sutra 2.5 defines avidya, the ignorance Patanjali names as the field of the other afflictions. what kind of error is it?","o":["not having studied the Vedas and the rules of correct ritual","forgetting the knowledge one gained in earlier births","doubting the teacher's words and the scripture's authority","mistaking the passing and the non-self for the lasting self"],"a":3,"es":{"q":"el Yoga Sutra 2.5 define avidya, la ignorancia que Patanjali nombra como el campo de las demás aflicciones. ¿qué clase de error es?","o":["no haber estudiado los Vedas ni las reglas del ritual correcto","olvidar el conocimiento que uno ganó en nacimientos anteriores","dudar de las palabras del maestro y de la autoridad de la escritura","tomar lo pasajero y lo que no es el ser por el ser duradero"]}},{"id":"HINDUISM-s06-04","day":440,"d":3,"q":"a coworker has just been caught lying to cheat a client. Yoga Sutra 1.33 pairs four attitudes with four kinds of people. which attitude does it pair with someone like this?","o":["karuna, compassion","upeksha, equanimity","maitri, friendliness","mudita, gladness"],"a":1,"es":{"q":"a un compañero de trabajo lo acaban de descubrir mintiendo para estafar a un cliente. el Yoga Sutra 1.33 empareja cuatro actitudes con cuatro tipos de personas. ¿qué actitud empareja con alguien así?","o":["karuna, compasión","upeksha, ecuanimidad","maitri, amabilidad","mudita, regocijo"]}},{"id":"HINDUISM-s06-05","day":473,"d":4,"q":"in book three of Patanjali's Yoga Sutras, how are the extraordinary powers (siddhis) to be regarded?","o":["as illusions with no reality, which only mislead the yogi","as the proof of samadhi that every yogi should seek","as powers to the outward mind but obstacles to samadhi","as gifts from Ishvara granted only to the devoted"],"a":2,"es":{"q":"en el libro tercero de los Yoga Sutras de Patanjali, ¿cómo hay que ver los poderes extraordinarios (siddhis)?","o":["como ilusiones sin realidad que solo confunden al yogui","como la prueba del samadhi que todo yogui debe buscar","como poderes afuera, pero estorbos para el samadhi","como dones de Ishvara concedidos solo a los devotos"]}},{"id":"HINDUISM-s06-06","day":509,"d":3,"q":"in the Bala Kanda of Valmiki's Ramayana, what happens when Rama takes up Shiva's great bow at King Janaka's court in Mithila?","o":["he strings it, draws it, and it breaks in two","he strings it and shoots through a spinning target","he cannot lift it until Vishvamitra blesses him","he lifts it but chooses not to string it in court"],"a":0,"es":{"q":"en el Bala Kanda del Ramayana de Valmiki, ¿qué pasa cuando Rama toma el gran arco de Shiva en la corte del rey Janaka, en Mithila?","o":["lo encuerda, lo tensa y el arco se parte en dos","lo encuerda y dispara a través de un blanco giratorio","no puede levantarlo hasta que Vishvamitra lo bendice","lo levanta, pero decide no encordarlo en la corte"]}}],[{"id":"HINDUISM-s07-01","day":519,"d":3,"q":"In Valmiki's Ramayana, why does King Dasharatha owe Kaikeyi two boons?","o":["he lost a wager to her during the horse sacrifice","she cured him of a long fever with forest herbs","she saved his life in the war against Shambara","she brought a rich dowry from the Kekaya kingdom"],"a":2,"es":{"q":"En el Ramayana de Valmiki, ¿por qué el rey Dasharatha le debe dos dones a Kaikeyi?","o":["perdió una apuesta con ella en el rito del caballo","lo curó de una larga fiebre con hierbas del bosque","le salvó la vida en la guerra contra Shambara","trajo una rica dote desde el reino de Kekaya"]}},{"id":"HINDUISM-s07-02","day":543,"d":3,"q":"In Valmiki's Ramayana, Dasharatha tells Kausalya that his death from grief for a son was foretold long ago. Who foretold it?","o":["the blind father of a young ascetic he shot by mistake","the sage Vasishtha, angered by the hasty coronation plan","Kaikeyi's father, the king of Kekaya, at her wedding","the sage Vishvamitra, when he took Rama to the forest"],"a":0,"es":{"q":"En el Ramayana de Valmiki, Dasharatha le dice a Kausalya que su muerte por el dolor de perder a un hijo fue anunciada hace mucho. ¿Quién la anunció?","o":["el padre ciego de un joven asceta al que mató por error","el sabio Vasishtha, molesto por la coronación apresurada","el padre de Kaikeyi, el rey de Kekaya, en la boda de ella","el sabio Vishvamitra, cuando llevó a Rama al bosque"]}},{"id":"HINDUISM-s07-03","day":549,"d":3,"q":"In Valmiki's Ramayana, why does Bharata set Rama's sandals on the throne at Nandigrama?","o":["to show the people that the throne was cursed","to govern only in Rama's name until he returns","to keep Kaikeyi from claiming the throne herself","to mark the year of mourning for Dasharatha"],"a":1,"es":{"q":"En el Ramayana de Valmiki, ¿por qué Bharata pone las sandalias de Rama sobre el trono en Nandigrama?","o":["para mostrarle a todo el pueblo que el trono estaba maldito","para gobernar solo en nombre de Rama hasta su regreso","para impedir que Kaikeyi reclamara el trono para sí","para marcar el año de luto por el rey Dasharatha"]}},{"id":"HINDUISM-s07-04","day":583,"d":3,"q":"In Valmiki's Ramayana, what do Rama and Sugriva walk around together to seal their friendship?","o":["a shrine to Shiva on Rishyamuka hill","the shore of Lake Pampa at sunrise","a banyan tree planted by the sage Matanga","a fire that Hanuman kindles between them"],"a":3,"es":{"q":"En el Ramayana de Valmiki, ¿alrededor de qué caminan juntos Rama y Sugriva para sellar su amistad?","o":["un santuario de Shiva en el monte Rishyamuka","la orilla del lago Pampa al amanecer","un baniano plantado por el sabio Matanga","un fuego que Hanuman enciende entre ellos"]}},{"id":"HINDUISM-s07-05","day":571,"d":4,"q":"A friend describes Lakshmana drawing a protective line around Sita's hut as a scene from Valmiki's Ramayana. What is accurate to tell them?","o":["Valmiki has it, but Ravana breaks the line by force","Valmiki has no such line; later tellings added it","Valmiki has it, but Rama is the one who draws the line","Valmiki has it, but only later, in the Uttara Kanda"],"a":1,"es":{"q":"Un amigo describe a Lakshmana trazando una línea protectora alrededor de la choza de Sita como una escena del Ramayana de Valmiki. ¿Qué es correcto decirle?","o":["Valmiki la incluye, pero Ravana la rompe por la fuerza","Valmiki no tiene esa línea; se añadió después","Valmiki la incluye, pero es Rama quien traza la línea","Valmiki la incluye, pero más tarde, en el Uttara Kanda"]}},{"id":"HINDUISM-s07-06","day":603,"d":3,"q":"In Valmiki's Kishkindha Kanda, why does Jambavan tell Hanuman the story of his birth on the shore?","o":["to rouse him to the leap by recalling his own power","to prove that Hanuman outranks Angada in the army","to warn him of a curse that will defeat him in Lanka","to explain why he must first ask Sugriva's leave"],"a":0,"es":{"q":"En el Kishkindha Kanda de Valmiki, ¿por qué Jambavan le cuenta a Hanuman la historia de su nacimiento en la orilla?","o":["para animarlo al salto recordándole su propio poder","para probar que Hanuman tiene más rango que Angada","para advertirle de una maldición que lo vencerá en Lanka","para explicarle por qué debe pedir permiso a Sugriva"]}}],[{"id":"HINDUISM-s08-01","day":636,"d":3,"q":"In Valmiki's Ramayana, who leads the building of the bridge to Lanka?","o":["Angada, the young son of Vali","Nala, the son of Vishvakarma","Jambavan, the king of the bears","Sushena, the father of Tara"],"a":1,"es":{"q":"En el Ramayana de Valmiki, ¿quién dirige la construcción del puente hacia Lanka?","o":["Angada, el joven hijo de Vali","Nala, el hijo de Vishvakarma","Jambavan, el rey de los osos","Sushena, el padre de Tara"]}},{"id":"HINDUISM-s08-02","day":655,"d":3,"q":"In the traditional (vulgate) text of Valmiki's Ramayana, which hymn does the sage Agastya teach Rama just before his final battle with Ravana?","o":["the Shiva Tandava, on Shiva's cosmic dance","the Vishnu Sahasranama, a thousand names","the Gayatri mantra, a Vedic verse to Savitr","the Aditya Hridayam, in praise of the sun"],"a":3,"es":{"q":"En el texto tradicional (vulgata) del Ramayana de Valmiki, ¿qué himno le enseña el sabio Agastya a Rama justo antes de su batalla final con Ravana?","o":["el Shiva Tandava, sobre la danza cósmica de Shiva","el Vishnu Sahasranama, los mil nombres de Vishnu","el mantra Gayatri, un verso védico a Savitr","el Aditya Hridayam, un himno en alabanza del sol"]}},{"id":"HINDUISM-s08-03","day":625,"d":4,"q":"In Valmiki's Sundara Kanda, after finding Sita, why does Hanuman decide to wreck Ravana's ashoka grove?","o":["to test the enemy's strength and be brought to Ravana","to carry out Sugriva's order to ruin all Ravana's gardens","to light a signal the army across the sea could see","to answer Sita's request to frighten her guards away"],"a":0,"es":{"q":"En el Sundara Kanda de Valmiki, después de encontrar a Sita, ¿por qué decide Hanuman destrozar el bosque de ashokas de Ravana?","o":["para medir la fuerza del enemigo y ser llevado ante Ravana","para cumplir la orden de Sugriva de arruinar los jardines","para encender una señal visible para el ejército al otro lado","para atender el pedido de Sita de asustar a sus guardias"]}},{"id":"HINDUISM-s08-04","day":638,"d":3,"q":"In Valmiki's Ramayana, when Vibhishana asks Rama for refuge and the camp argues, what vow does Rama state?","o":["to judge Vibhishana only after the war has been won","to accept him once he has fought against Ravana","to protect all who come once and say 'I am yours'","to shelter only those who share his own royal line"],"a":2,"es":{"q":"En el Ramayana de Valmiki, cuando Vibhishana le pide refugio a Rama y el campamento discute, ¿qué voto declara Rama?","o":["juzgar a Vibhishana solo después de ganar la guerra","aceptarlo una vez que haya luchado contra Ravana","proteger a quien venga una vez y diga 'soy tuyo'","dar refugio solo a quienes sean de su linaje real"]}},{"id":"HINDUISM-s08-05","day":657,"d":4,"q":"Two rival clans have fought for years, and one clan's leader has just been killed. A storyteller cites what Rama tells Vibhishana in Valmiki's Ramayana: enmity ends at death. What does that principle call for?","o":["leave his body unburied as a warning to allies","allow quiet rites for him, without any honors","honor him only once his clan admits its wrongs","give his body full funeral rites with honor"],"a":3,"es":{"q":"Dos clanes rivales llevan años peleando, y el líder de uno acaba de morir. Un narrador cita lo que Rama le dice a Vibhishana en el Ramayana de Valmiki: la enemistad termina con la muerte. ¿Qué pide ese principio?","o":["dejar su cuerpo sin sepultar como aviso a sus aliados","permitir ritos discretos, sin ningún honor para él","honrarlo solo cuando su clan admita sus culpas","darle a su cuerpo todos los ritos fúnebres con honor"]}},{"id":"HINDUISM-s08-06","day":629,"d":3,"q":"In Valmiki's Sundara Kanda, why is Hanuman horrified just after setting Lanka on fire?","o":["he fears the fire may have burned Sita herself","he sees that Vibhishana's house has caught fire","he recalls that Rama had forbidden any burning","he finds that his own tail cannot be put out"],"a":0,"es":{"q":"En el Sundara Kanda de Valmiki, ¿por qué Hanuman se horroriza justo después de incendiar Lanka?","o":["teme que el fuego haya quemado a la propia Sita","ve que la casa de Vibhishana ha empezado a arder","recuerda que Rama había prohibido quemar nada","descubre que no puede apagar su propia cola"]}}],[{"id":"HINDUISM-s09-01","day":697,"d":3,"q":"In the Mahabharata's frame story, who recites the epic at King Janamejaya's snake sacrifice?","o":["Sanjaya, the blind king's charioteer","Shuka, the son of the sage Vyasa","Vaishampayana, a disciple of Vyasa","Narada, the wandering divine sage"],"a":2,"es":{"q":"En el relato marco del Mahabharata, ¿quién recita la épica en el sacrificio de serpientes del rey Janamejaya?","o":["Sanjaya, el auriga del rey ciego","Shuka, el hijo del gran sabio Vyasa","Vaishampayana, discípulo de Vyasa","Narada, el sabio divino errante"]}},{"id":"HINDUISM-s09-02","day":713,"d":3,"q":"In the Mahabharata's Adi Parva, why does Devavrata come to be called Bhishma?","o":["for his fearsome duel with his teacher Parashurama","for his terrible vow to give up throne and marriage","for slaying the gandharva who had killed his brother","for the dread curse he laid on the house of Drupada"],"a":1,"es":{"q":"En el Adi Parva del Mahabharata, ¿por qué a Devavrata se le llega a llamar Bhishma?","o":["por su temible duelo contra su propio maestro Parashurama","por su terrible voto de dejar el trono y el matrimonio","por matar al gandharva que había matado a su hermano","por la maldición que lanzó sobre la casa de Drupada"]}},{"id":"HINDUISM-s09-03","day":722,"d":3,"q":"In the Mahabharata's Adi Parva, why is Dhritarashtra born blind?","o":["Shantanu's grief fell upon the unborn child","a sage cursed the Kuru line for Bhishma's vow","Gandhari's father laid a curse on the house","Ambika shut her eyes in fear when Vyasa came"],"a":3,"es":{"q":"En el Adi Parva del Mahabharata, ¿por qué Dhritarashtra nace ciego?","o":["el dolor de Shantanu cayó sobre el niño por nacer","un sabio maldijo el linaje kuru por el voto de Bhishma","el padre de Gandhari lanzó una maldición sobre la casa","Ambika cerró los ojos por miedo cuando llegó Vyasa"]}},{"id":"HINDUISM-s09-04","day":761,"d":3,"q":"In the Mahabharata's Sabha Parva, Krishna had promised Shishupala's mother to pardon how many of her son's offenses?","o":["100 offenses","1,000 offenses","108 offenses","500 offenses"],"a":0,"es":{"q":"En el Sabha Parva del Mahabharata, Krishna le había prometido a la madre de Shishupala perdonar ¿cuántas ofensas de su hijo?","o":["100 ofensas","1000 ofensas","108 ofensas","500 ofensas"]}},{"id":"HINDUISM-s09-05","day":786,"d":4,"q":"In the Vana Parva, Shiva gives Arjuna the Pashupata weapon with a warning about its use. If Arjuna later faced a weak, ordinary human foe, what would that warning require?","o":["use it only after first warning the foe","use it if the foe had struck the first blow","use it once Indra had given his own consent","hold it back and not hurl it at such a foe"],"a":3,"es":{"q":"En el Vana Parva, Shiva le da a Arjuna el arma Pashupata con una advertencia sobre su uso. Si Arjuna se enfrentara más tarde a un enemigo humano común y débil, ¿qué exigiría esa advertencia?","o":["usarla solo después de avisar al enemigo","usarla si el enemigo dio el primer golpe","usarla cuando Indra haya dado su permiso","contenerse y no lanzarla contra él"]}},{"id":"HINDUISM-s09-06","day":755,"d":3,"q":"In the Mahabharata's Sabha Parva, why must Jarasandha be dealt with before Yudhishthira can perform the Rajasuya?","o":["he holds many kings captive and blocks the rite","he has seized the Kuru capital at Hastinapura","he has stolen the horse meant for the great sacrifice","he has sworn to kill Yudhishthira at the rite"],"a":0,"es":{"q":"En el Sabha Parva del Mahabharata, ¿por qué hay que enfrentar a Jarasandha antes de que Yudhishthira pueda celebrar el Rajasuya?","o":["tiene presos a muchos reyes y bloquea el rito","se ha apoderado de la capital kuru, Hastinapura","ha robado el caballo destinado al gran sacrificio","ha jurado matar a Yudhishthira durante el rito"]}}],[{"id":"HINDUISM-s10-01","day":807,"d":4,"q":"During the Pandavas' year in disguise at King Virata's court (Mahabharata, Virata Parva), what role did Arjuna take?","o":["a cook and wrestler called Vallava","a dice-playing courtier called Kanka","a eunuch dance teacher, Brihannala","a keeper of the horses, Granthika"],"a":2,"es":{"q":"durante el año en que los Pandavas vivieron disfrazados en la corte del rey Virata (Mahabharata, Virata Parva), ¿qué papel asumió Arjuna?","o":["un cocinero y luchador llamado Vallava","un cortesano jugador de dados, Kanka","un eunuco maestro de danza, Brihannala","un cuidador de caballos, Granthika"]}},{"id":"HINDUISM-s10-02","day":806,"d":4,"q":"In the Mahabharata's episode of the Yaksha's questions, why does Yudhishthira ask that Nakula be revived rather than Bhima or Arjuna?","o":["so that Madri, like Kunti, would still have a living son","because Nakula was the youngest and most helpless brother","because Nakula had not drunk from the yaksha's lake","because the yaksha had offered to revive the weakest one"],"a":0,"es":{"q":"en el episodio de las preguntas del yaksha en el Mahabharata, ¿por qué Yudhishthira pide que reviva Nakula y no Bhima ni Arjuna?","o":["para que Madri, como Kunti, tuviera todavía un hijo vivo","porque Nakula era el hermano más joven y más indefenso","porque Nakula no había bebido del lago del yaksha","porque el yaksha había ofrecido revivir al más débil"]}},{"id":"HINDUISM-s10-03","day":835,"d":5,"q":"In the Drona Parva, why does Karna's use of Indra's Shakti dart against Ghatotkacha matter so much for Arjuna?","o":["the dart passed to Ashvatthama, who later turned it on Arjuna","it was a weapon made for rakshasas, with no power over men","using it broke Karna's oath and kept him off the field a day","it could be thrown once, so it was spent before he met Arjuna"],"a":3,"es":{"q":"en el Drona Parva, ¿por qué importa tanto para Arjuna que Karna use contra Ghatotkacha el dardo Shakti de Indra?","o":["el dardo pasó a Ashvatthama, que luego lo lanzó contra Arjuna","era un arma hecha para rakshasas, sin poder contra los hombres","usarlo rompió el juramento de Karna y lo alejó un día del campo","se podía lanzar una vez, así que se gastó antes de enfrentar a Arjuna"]}},{"id":"HINDUISM-s10-04","day":840,"d":5,"q":"In the Karna Parva, Krishna tells of the ascetic Kaushika, who truthfully showed robbers where travelers were hiding. Applying that teaching to a new case, how should a villager who truthfully tells a mob where a hunted innocent is hiding be judged?","o":["as right, since a true statement carries no fault in itself","as wrong, since truth is weighed by its effect on living beings","as blameless, since the guilt falls on the mob that acts on it","as right, provided the villager had taken a solemn vow of truth"],"a":1,"es":{"q":"en el Karna Parva, Krishna cuenta la historia del asceta Kaushika, que con verdad les mostró a unos ladrones dónde se escondían unos viajeros. Aplicando esa enseñanza a un caso nuevo, ¿cómo se juzga a un aldeano que con verdad le dice a una turba dónde se esconde un inocente perseguido?","o":["como correcto, porque una afirmación verdadera no tiene falta en sí","como incorrecto, porque la verdad se mide por su efecto en los seres","como libre de culpa, porque la culpa es de la turba que actúa","como correcto, si el aldeano había hecho un voto solemne de verdad"]}},{"id":"HINDUISM-s10-05","day":859,"d":4,"q":"In the Stri Parva of the Mahabharata, what does Gandhari's curse on Krishna foretell?","o":["that his brother Balarama would one day turn on him in battle","that he would lose his sight, as she had given up her own","that his own clan, the Vrishnis, would destroy one another","that his name would be forgotten in the land of the Kurus"],"a":2,"es":{"q":"en el Stri Parva del Mahabharata, ¿qué anuncia la maldición de Gandhari contra Krishna?","o":["que su hermano Balarama un día se volvería contra él en batalla","que perdería la vista, como ella había renunciado a la suya","que su propio clan, los Vrishnis, se destruiría a sí mismo","que su nombre sería olvidado en la tierra de los Kurus"]}},{"id":"HINDUISM-s10-06","day":872,"d":4,"q":"In the Ashvamedhika Parva, what does the half-golden mongoose claim about Yudhishthira's horse sacrifice?","o":["it is worth less than a poor family's gift of flour to a guest","it is void, since the horse was seized from a defeated king","it is flawed, since Krishna stayed away from the whole rite","it cannot wash away the sin of Drona's death by a lie"],"a":0,"es":{"q":"en el Ashvamedhika Parva, ¿qué afirma la mangosta medio dorada sobre el sacrificio del caballo de Yudhishthira?","o":["vale menos que la harina que una familia pobre dio a un huésped","es nulo, porque el caballo fue tomado de un rey vencido","tiene un defecto, porque Krishna no asistió a todo el rito","no puede lavar el pecado de la muerte de Drona por una mentira"]}}],[{"id":"HINDUISM-s11-01","day":890,"d":4,"q":"In the Bhagavata Purana, when Yashoda looks into the mouth of the child Krishna after he is accused of eating earth, what does she see?","o":["the serpent Kaliya coiled in a poisoned pool of the Yamuna","the whole universe, with the village of Vraja and herself in it","the city of Mathura, with King Kamsa seated on his throne","a lotus rising from his navel, with Brahma seated upon it"],"a":1,"es":{"q":"en el Bhagavata Purana, cuando Yashoda mira dentro de la boca del niño Krishna después de que lo acusan de comer tierra, ¿qué ve?","o":["la serpiente Kaliya enroscada en un estanque envenenado del Yamuna","el universo entero, con la aldea de Vraja y ella misma dentro","la ciudad de Mathura, con el rey Kamsa sentado en su trono","un loto que brota de su ombligo, con Brahma sentado sobre él"]}},{"id":"HINDUISM-s11-02","day":895,"d":4,"q":"In the Bhagavata Purana, why does the boy Krishna persuade the cowherds of Vraja to give up their yearly sacrifice to Indra?","o":["Indra had cursed the village with a drought that same year","King Kamsa had forbidden all offerings to the gods of rain","the rite required them to slaughter cattle from their herds","they live by their cows and the hill, so should honor those"],"a":3,"es":{"q":"en el Bhagavata Purana, ¿por qué el niño Krishna convence a los pastores de Vraja de dejar su sacrificio anual a Indra?","o":["Indra había maldecido a la aldea con una sequía ese mismo año","el rey Kamsa había prohibido toda ofrenda a los dioses de la lluvia","el rito los obligaba a sacrificar reses de sus propios rebaños","viven de sus vacas y de la colina, y deben honrar a estas"]}},{"id":"HINDUISM-s11-03","day":900,"d":5,"q":"In Bhagavata Purana 10.29, King Parikshit asks how the gopis, who loved Krishna as a lover rather than as the Absolute, could be set free. How does the sage Shuka answer?","o":["as Shishupala reached Krishna through hatred, any mind fixed on him attains him","the gopis' husbands had given them leave, so no dharma was broken on that night","the gopis had studied the Upanishads and already knew him as Brahman","Krishna had first given them knowledge of the Self through the sage Narada"],"a":0,"es":{"q":"en el Bhagavata Purana 10.29, el rey Parikshit pregunta cómo pudieron liberarse las gopis, que amaban a Krishna como amante y no como el Absoluto. ¿Qué responde el sabio Shuka?","o":["así como Shishupala llegó a Krishna por el odio, toda mente fija en él lo alcanza","los esposos de las gopis les habían dado permiso, así que no se rompió el dharma","las gopis habían estudiado las Upanishads y ya lo conocían como Brahman","Krishna antes les había dado el conocimiento del Ser por medio del sabio Narada"]}},{"id":"HINDUISM-s11-04","day":910,"d":4,"q":"In Tamil devotional tradition, how do the Alvars differ from the Nayanars?","o":["the Alvars sang in Sanskrit; the Nayanars sang in Tamil","the Alvars sang to Shiva; the Nayanars sang to Vishnu","the Alvars sang to Vishnu; the Nayanars sang to Shiva","the Alvars wrote in prose; the Nayanars wrote in verse"],"a":2,"es":{"q":"en la tradición devocional tamil, ¿en qué se diferencian los Alvars de los Nayanars?","o":["los Alvars cantaban en sánscrito; los Nayanars, en tamil","los Alvars le cantaban a Shiva; los Nayanars, a Vishnu","los Alvars le cantaban a Vishnu; los Nayanars, a Shiva","los Alvars escribían en prosa; los Nayanars, en verso"]}},{"id":"HINDUISM-s11-05","day":939,"d":4,"q":"At the World's Parliament of Religions in Chicago (1893), Vivekananda quoted a hymn likening humanity's paths to rivers that all flow into the sea. What did he use it to show?","o":["that each faith must purify itself as a river cleans its waters","that different paths, crooked or straight, all lead to one God","that faiths shift their course over the centuries, as rivers do","that pilgrimage to the sacred rivers is the oldest of all paths"],"a":1,"es":{"q":"en el Parlamento Mundial de las Religiones de Chicago (1893), Vivekananda citó un himno que compara los caminos de la humanidad con ríos que desembocan en el mar. ¿Qué quiso mostrar con él?","o":["que cada fe debe purificarse como un río limpia sus aguas","que caminos distintos, rectos o torcidos, llevan al mismo Dios","que las fes cambian su curso con los siglos, como los ríos","que la peregrinación a los ríos sagrados es el camino más antiguo"]}},{"id":"HINDUISM-s11-06","day":950,"d":5,"q":"A practitioner of self-enquiry notices worry about tomorrow rising during a sitting. Following Ramana Maharshi's Who Am I? (Nan Yar), what should they do with the thought?","o":["follow the worry to its end so that it exhausts itself","write the worry down and examine its meaning afterward","push the worry away by force and keep the body still","ask to whom it has come, and turn back to that 'I'"],"a":3,"es":{"q":"alguien que practica la indagación del Ser nota que, durante la sesión, le surge preocupación por el día de mañana. Según ¿Quién soy yo? (Nan Yar) de Ramana Maharshi, ¿qué debe hacer con ese pensamiento?","o":["seguir la preocupación hasta el final para que se agote","anotar la preocupación y examinar su sentido después","apartar la preocupación a la fuerza y quedarse quieto","preguntar a quién le vino y volver a ese 'yo'"]}}],[{"id":"HINDUISM-s12-01","day":963,"d":4,"q":"In Bhagavad Gita chapter 3, why does Krishna tell Arjuna that simply giving up action is no real way out?","o":["laying down action is a right kept for the priestly class","action is a debt to the ancestors that each son must repay","no one stays inactive even a moment; nature makes all act","the Vedas forbid a prince to withdraw to the forest"],"a":2,"es":{"q":"en el capítulo 3 del Bhagavad Gita, ¿por qué Krishna le dice a Arjuna que dejar de actuar no es una salida real?","o":["dejar la acción es un derecho reservado a la clase sacerdotal","la acción es una deuda con los ancestros que cada hijo debe pagar","nadie queda inactivo ni un momento; la naturaleza hace actuar a todos","los Vedas prohíben a un príncipe retirarse a vivir al bosque"]}},{"id":"HINDUISM-s12-02","day":970,"d":4,"q":"Bhagavad Gita 3.35 says it is better to do one's own duty, even imperfectly, than another's duty well. What Sanskrit term names that 'own duty'?","o":["svadharma","paradharma","rajadharma","apaddharma"],"a":0,"es":{"q":"el Bhagavad Gita 3.35 dice que es mejor cumplir el propio deber, aunque sea imperfectamente, que cumplir bien el deber de otro. ¿Qué término sánscrito nombra ese 'deber propio'?","o":["svadharma","paradharma","rajadharma","apaddharma"]}},{"id":"HINDUISM-s12-03","day":975,"d":4,"q":"Who composed the Gita Govinda, the twelfth-century Sanskrit poem on the love of Radha and Krishna?","o":["Vidyapati","Chandidas","Kalidasa","Jayadeva"],"a":3,"es":{"q":"¿quién compuso el Gita Govinda, el poema sánscrito del siglo XII sobre el amor de Radha y Krishna?","o":["Vidyapati","Chandidas","Kalidasa","Jayadeva"]}},{"id":"HINDUISM-s12-04","day":996,"d":5,"q":"The Vivekachudamani, traditionally attributed to Shankara, names the deer, elephant, moth, fish and bee, each destroyed through a single sense. What conclusion does it draw?","o":["each sense belongs to a deity and must be offered back to it","if one sense can destroy them, a person bound by five is worse off","animals follow their own nature, so humans must follow theirs","the senses weaken with age, so the practice must begin in youth"],"a":1,"es":{"q":"el Vivekachudamani, atribuido por la tradición a Shankara, nombra al venado, el elefante, la polilla, el pez y la abeja, cada uno destruido por un solo sentido. ¿Qué conclusión saca?","o":["cada sentido pertenece a una deidad y debe devolvérsele","si un sentido los destruye, quien está atado a los cinco está peor","los animales siguen su naturaleza; los humanos deben seguir la suya","los sentidos se debilitan con la edad; hay que empezar de joven"]}},{"id":"HINDUISM-s12-05","day":1002,"d":5,"q":"In the Ashtavakra Gita (3.2), what does the image of someone mistaking mother-of-pearl for silver explain?","o":["wealth is acceptable so long as it is given to the needy","the world is real, but the value we give it is invented","craving for the world arises from not knowing the Self","the Self wears away through contact, as silver does"],"a":2,"es":{"q":"en el Ashtavakra Gita (3.2), ¿qué explica la imagen de alguien que confunde el nácar con plata?","o":["la riqueza es aceptable si se da a los necesitados","el mundo es real, pero el valor que le damos es inventado","el deseo por el mundo surge de no conocer el Ser","el Ser se desgasta con el contacto, como la plata"]}},{"id":"HINDUISM-s12-06","day":1043,"d":4,"q":"In standard Sanskrit transliteration (IAST), a reader meets the name Gaṇeśa. What does the dot under the n tell them to do?","o":["lengthen the vowel that comes just before the n","nasalize the vowel before it with no full n sound","touch the tongue to the back of the upper teeth","curl the tongue back toward the roof of the mouth"],"a":3,"es":{"q":"en la transliteración estándar del sánscrito (IAST), alguien lee el nombre Gaṇeśa. ¿Qué le indica el punto debajo de la n?","o":["alargar la vocal que va justo antes de la n","nasalizar la vocal anterior sin una n completa","tocar con la lengua la parte de atrás de los dientes","curvar la lengua hacia atrás, hacia el paladar"]}}],[{"id":"HINDUISM-s13-01","day":1062,"d":3,"q":"the Devi Mahatmya, also called the Chandi or the Durga Saptashati, is traditionally found inside which larger text?","o":["the Brahmanda Purana","the Markandeya Purana","the Bhagavata Purana","the Shiva Purana"],"a":1,"es":{"q":"el Devi Mahatmya, también llamado Chandi o Durga Saptashati, ¿dentro de qué texto más amplio se encuentra tradicionalmente?","o":["el Brahmanda Purana","el Markandeya Purana","el Bhagavata Purana","el Shiva Purana"]}},{"id":"HINDUISM-s13-02","day":1063,"d":3,"q":"in the first episode of the Devi Mahatmya, Brahma is threatened by the demons Madhu and Kaitabha and praises the goddess as Yoganidra. why does he turn to her?","o":["she created the two demons and alone can call them back","she is Brahma's own consort, sworn to protect the creator","Vishnu had asked her to keep watch over him while he slept","she is the sleep holding Vishnu, so only she can wake him"],"a":3,"es":{"q":"en el primer episodio del Devi Mahatmya, Brahma se ve amenazado por los demonios Madhu y Kaitabha y alaba a la diosa como Yoganidra. ¿por qué recurre a ella?","o":["ella creó a los dos demonios y solo ella puede hacerlos volver","ella es la consorte de Brahma y juró proteger al creador","Vishnu le había pedido que lo cuidara mientras dormía","ella es el sueño de Vishnu y solo ella puede despertarlo"]}},{"id":"HINDUISM-s13-03","day":1068,"d":3,"q":"in the Devi Mahatmya, Kali springs from the goddess's frowning brow and brings her the heads of the demons Chanda and Munda. what name does the goddess then give her?","o":["Chamunda","Kaushiki","Shakambhari","Bhramari"],"a":0,"es":{"q":"en el Devi Mahatmya, Kali brota de la frente fruncida de la diosa y le trae las cabezas de los demonios Chanda y Munda. ¿qué nombre le da entonces la diosa?","o":["Chamunda","Kaushiki","Shakambhari","Bhramari"]}},{"id":"HINDUISM-s13-04","day":1070,"d":3,"q":"in the Devi Mahatmya's last battle, the demon Shumbha taunts the goddess for fighting with the strength of others. what happens next in the text?","o":["the gods take back the powers they had lent to her","Kali alone stays beside her while the rest withdraw","the goddesses enter her body, being her own powers","she sends the other goddesses back to their own gods"],"a":2,"es":{"q":"en la última batalla del Devi Mahatmya, el demonio Shumbha se burla de la diosa por pelear con la fuerza de otros. ¿qué pasa después en el texto?","o":["los dioses recuperan los poderes que le habían prestado","solo Kali se queda a su lado y las demás se retiran","las diosas entran en ella, pues son sus propios poderes","ella devuelve las otras diosas a sus propios dioses"]}},{"id":"HINDUISM-s13-05","day":1124,"d":3,"q":"in Shaiva tradition, what does Ardhanarishvara, the form of Shiva whose body is half male and half female, chiefly express?","o":["that Shiva and his Shakti are inseparable, never two","that Shiva and Vishnu share a single body, half each","that the goddess rules the world while Shiva meditates","that Shiva gave Parvati half his realm at their wedding"],"a":0,"es":{"q":"en la tradición shivaíta, ¿qué expresa sobre todo Ardhanarishvara, la forma de Shiva cuyo cuerpo es mitad masculino y mitad femenino?","o":["que Shiva y su Shakti son inseparables, nunca dos","que Shiva y Vishnu comparten un solo cuerpo, mitad y mitad","que la diosa gobierna el mundo mientras Shiva medita","que Shiva le dio a Parvati la mitad de su reino al casarse"]}},{"id":"HINDUISM-s13-06","day":1104,"d":3,"q":"Shaiva and Shakta teachers speak of five acts of the divine (pancha-kritya), and the Lalita Sahasranama gives all five to the goddess. someone who for years saw only the ordinary world suddenly recognizes the divine within it. in this scheme, which act is at work?","o":["srishti, creating","tirodhana, concealing","samhara, withdrawing","anugraha, grace"],"a":3,"es":{"q":"maestros shivaítas y shaktas hablan de cinco actos de lo divino (pancha-kritya), y el Lalita Sahasranama le atribuye los cinco a la diosa. alguien que durante años vio solo el mundo ordinario de pronto reconoce lo divino en él. en este esquema, ¿qué acto está obrando?","o":["srishti, crear","tirodhana, ocultar","samhara, retirar","anugraha, gracia"]}}],[{"id":"HINDUISM-s14-01","day":1160,"d":2,"q":"How many pramanas, or means of valid knowing, does the Nyaya Sutra of Gautama accept?","o":["two pramanas","six pramanas","four pramanas","three pramanas"],"a":2,"es":{"q":"¿Cuántos pramanas, o medios de conocimiento válido, acepta el Nyaya Sutra de Gautama?","o":["dos pramanas","seis pramanas","cuatro pramanas","tres pramanas"]}},{"id":"HINDUISM-s14-02","day":1168,"d":3,"q":"In Vaisheshika's list of categories (padarthas), which one names the inseparable relation by which a quality such as color exists in its substance?","o":["samavaya, or inherence","samyoga, or conjunction","samanya, or the universal","vishesha, or particularity"],"a":0,"es":{"q":"En la lista de categorías (padarthas) del Vaisheshika, ¿cuál nombra la relación inseparable por la que una cualidad, como el color, existe en su sustancia?","o":["samavaya, o inherencia","samyoga, o conjunción","samanya, o lo universal","vishesha, o particularidad"]}},{"id":"HINDUISM-s14-03","day":1161,"d":3,"q":"In Nyaya's classic inference, smoke on a hill proves there is fire there. Why can't fire be used in the same way to prove smoke?","o":["fire is seen directly, so it is never inferred","inference cannot run from a cause to its effect","only testimony can establish smoke on a hill","fire occurs without smoke, as in red-hot iron"],"a":3,"es":{"q":"En la inferencia clásica del Nyaya, el humo en una colina prueba que allí hay fuego. ¿Por qué no se puede usar el fuego de la misma manera para probar el humo?","o":["el fuego se ve directamente, nunca se infiere","la inferencia no va de una causa a su efecto","solo el testimonio prueba el humo en la colina","hay fuego sin humo, como en el hierro al rojo"]}},{"id":"HINDUISM-s14-04","day":1173,"d":3,"q":"The Samkhya Karika compares the three gunas (sattva, rajas and tamas) to a lamp. What does the comparison teach about them?","o":["sattva gives the light, so the other two must go","though opposed, they work together for one end","they belong to purusha, as a flame to its lamp","each burns out in turn until prakriti is spent"],"a":1,"es":{"q":"La Samkhya Karika compara los tres gunas (sattva, rajas y tamas) con una lámpara. ¿Qué enseña esa comparación sobre ellos?","o":["sattva da la luz, así que los otros dos sobran","aunque opuestos, trabajan juntos para un fin","pertenecen a purusha, como la llama a la lámpara","cada uno se apaga hasta que prakriti se agota"]}},{"id":"HINDUISM-s14-05","day":1194,"d":3,"q":"In Ramanuja's Vishishtadvaita Vedanta, how is the individual self related to Brahman?","o":["as the space in a pot to the space outside it","as a wave that sinks back and merges in the sea","as a body to the self that dwells within it","as a dream figure to the mind that dreams it"],"a":2,"es":{"q":"En el Vedanta Vishishtadvaita de Ramanuja, ¿cómo se relaciona el ser individual con Brahman?","o":["como el espacio de una vasija con el de afuera","como una ola que vuelve y se funde en el mar","como un cuerpo con el ser que habita en él","como una figura soñada con quien la sueña"]}},{"id":"HINDUISM-s14-06","day":1236,"d":4,"q":"A student argues that moksha, liberation, can be produced by performing enough Vedic rites. In Shankara's Advaita commentary on the Brahma Sutras, what is the main objection?","o":["what action makes has a beginning, so it ends","rites are for householders, not for renunciates","one mistake in a rite cancels all of its merit","moksha needs many lifetimes, whatever one does"],"a":0,"es":{"q":"Un estudiante sostiene que moksha, la liberación, se puede producir haciendo suficientes ritos védicos. En el comentario advaita de Shankara a los Brahma Sutras, ¿cuál es la objeción principal?","o":["lo que la acción produce empieza, así que termina","los ritos son para casados, no para renunciantes","un solo error en el rito anula todo su mérito","moksha pide muchas vidas, se haga lo que se haga"]}}],[{"id":"HINDUISM-s15-01","day":1245,"d":2,"q":"Hindu tradition classes the four Vedas as shruti. what does that word mean, and what does it say about how the Vedas came to be?","o":["what is remembered: texts that human authors composed","what is heard: revelation received by ancient seers","what is written: scripture first set down by the sages","what is sung: hymns composed for the temple festivals"],"a":1,"es":{"q":"la tradición hindú clasifica los cuatro Vedas como shruti. ¿qué significa esa palabra y qué dice sobre el origen de los Vedas?","o":["lo recordado: textos compuestos por autores humanos","lo escuchado: revelación que recibieron los videntes","lo escrito: escritura fijada primero por los sabios","lo cantado: himnos compuestos para fiestas del templo"]}},{"id":"HINDUISM-s15-02","day":1255,"d":3,"q":"the Nasadiya Sukta, the Rig Veda's hymn of creation (10.129), ends by asking who knows where creation came from. what do its last two verses answer?","o":["the gods know, since they were there before the world began","the seers know, since they watched creation unfold in a vision","the one in highest heaven knows, or perhaps does not know","the waters know, since they held the first seed from the start"],"a":2,"es":{"q":"el Nasadiya Sukta, el himno de la creación del Rig Veda (10.129), termina preguntando quién sabe de dónde vino la creación. ¿qué responden sus dos últimos versos?","o":["lo saben los dioses, que estaban allí antes de que el mundo empezara","lo saben los videntes, que vieron la creación en una visión","lo sabe el que está en lo más alto del cielo, o quizás no","lo saben las aguas, que guardaron la primera semilla desde el inicio"]}},{"id":"HINDUISM-s15-03","day":1257,"d":3,"q":"the Purusha Sukta (Rig Veda 10.90.3) says that all beings are one quarter of the cosmic Person, the Purusha, and three quarters are immortal in heaven. what does this say about the Purusha and the world?","o":["the world truly is the Purusha's, yet he is far greater","the world is an illusion that keeps the Purusha out of sight","the world is a separate thing the Purusha made and then left","the Purusha is exactly as large as the world he turned into"],"a":0,"es":{"q":"el Purusha Sukta (Rig Veda 10.90.3) dice que todos los seres son una cuarta parte de la Persona cósmica, el Purusha, y que tres cuartas partes son inmortales en el cielo. ¿qué dice esto sobre el Purusha y el mundo?","o":["el mundo es de verdad del Purusha, pero él es mayor","el mundo es una ilusión que mantiene oculto al Purusha","el mundo es algo aparte que el Purusha hizo y luego dejó","el Purusha mide justo lo mismo que el mundo en que se convirtió"]}},{"id":"HINDUISM-s15-04","day":1263,"d":2,"q":"the Gayatri mantra (Rig Veda 3.62.10), recited at dawn and dusk, asks a Vedic god to stir our thoughts. which god is it addressed to?","o":["Agni, the fire that carries offerings","Indra, the storm god who frees waters","Varuna, guardian of the cosmic order","Savitr, the sun who sets all moving"],"a":3,"es":{"q":"el mantra Gayatri (Rig Veda 3.62.10), que se recita al amanecer y al atardecer, le pide a un dios védico que impulse nuestros pensamientos. ¿a qué dios está dirigido?","o":["Agni, el fuego que lleva las ofrendas","Indra, dios de la tormenta y las aguas","Varuna, guardián del orden cósmico","Savitr, el sol que todo lo impulsa"]}},{"id":"HINDUISM-s15-05","day":1301,"d":3,"q":"the Charaka Samhita divides the year into adana, the taking half (late winter to summer), and visarga, the giving half (the rains to early winter). why does it say people are weakest at the end of the taking half?","o":["the strong sun and wind have drawn moisture and strength out","the strong moon has cooled and smothered the digestive fire","the heavy foods of the cold months have dulled the whole body","the long rains have soaked the body and weighed down its tissues"],"a":0,"es":{"q":"el Charaka Samhita divide el año en adana, la mitad que toma (del final del invierno al verano), y visarga, la mitad que da (de las lluvias al comienzo del invierno). ¿por qué dice que la gente está más débil al final de la mitad que toma?","o":["el sol y el viento fuertes han sacado la humedad y la fuerza","la luna fuerte ha enfriado y apagado el fuego digestivo","las comidas pesadas de los meses fríos han embotado el cuerpo","las largas lluvias han empapado el cuerpo y cargado sus tejidos"]}},{"id":"HINDUISM-s15-06","day":1287,"d":3,"q":"in classical Ayurveda, a person whose vata dosha is out of balance would most likely be advised to favor which of these?","o":["cool, sweet drinks and long rests in the shade","fasting, light dry meals and brisk exercise","warm, oily, nourishing meals and a steady daily routine","raw salads, cold water and frequent travel"],"a":2,"es":{"q":"en el Ayurveda clásico, ¿qué se le aconsejaría preferir a una persona con el dosha vata desequilibrado?","o":["bebidas frescas y dulces y largos descansos a la sombra","ayuno, comidas ligeras y secas y ejercicio enérgico","comidas tibias, untuosas y nutritivas, y una rutina diaria estable","ensaladas crudas, agua fría y viajes frecuentes"]}}],[{"id":"HINDUISM-s16-01","day":1330,"d":3,"q":"In Valmiki's Ramayana, when Ravana courts the captive Sita in the Ashoka grove, what does she place between herself and him before answering?","o":["a small lit lamp of clay","a fold of her own sari","a single blade of grass","the jewel from her hair"],"a":2,"es":{"q":"En el Ramayana de Valmiki, cuando Ravana corteja a Sita, su cautiva, en el bosque de Ashoka, ¿qué pone ella entre los dos antes de responderle?","o":["una pequeña lámpara de barro","un pliegue de su propio sari","una sola brizna de hierba","la joya de su cabello"]}},{"id":"HINDUISM-s16-02","day":1346,"d":3,"q":"In the Mahabharata's tale of Nala and Damayanti, four gods take Nala's form at her svayamvara (bride's choice). How does Damayanti tell the real Nala apart?","o":["only he bears the marks of a mortal body","only he answers when she calls his name","only he wears the ring she sent to him","a swan lands right at his feet to show her"],"a":0,"es":{"q":"En el relato de Nala y Damayanti del Mahabharata, cuatro dioses toman la forma de Nala en su svayamvara (elección de esposo). ¿Cómo distingue Damayanti al verdadero Nala?","o":["solo él tiene las señales de un cuerpo mortal","solo él responde cuando ella dice su nombre","solo él lleva el anillo que ella le envió","un cisne se posa a sus pies para mostrárselo"]}},{"id":"HINDUISM-s16-03","day":1373,"d":3,"q":"According to the Periya Puranam, who feeds the child Sambandar milk from a golden cup beside the temple tank at Sirkazhi?","o":["the sage Agastya, first teacher of Tamil","the poet-saint Karaikkal Ammaiyar","the saint Appar, his elder companion","the Goddess Parvati, Shiva's consort"],"a":3,"es":{"q":"Según el Periya Puranam, ¿quién le da al niño Sambandar leche en una copa de oro junto al estanque del templo de Sirkazhi?","o":["el sabio Agastya, primer maestro del tamil","la poeta santa Karaikkal Ammaiyar","el santo Appar, su compañero mayor","la diosa Parvati, consorte de Shiva"]}},{"id":"HINDUISM-s16-04","day":1383,"d":3,"q":"In the Varkari tradition of Maharashtra, why does Vitthal at Pandharpur stand on a brick?","o":["Jnaneshwar laid it as the shrine's very first stone","Pundalik gave it to him while tending his parents","Namdev set it there so the god would never leave","Janabai offered it as a seat while grinding grain"],"a":1,"es":{"q":"En la tradición varkari de Maharashtra, ¿por qué Vitthal, en Pandharpur, está de pie sobre un ladrillo?","o":["Jnaneshwar lo puso como primera piedra del templo","Pundalik se lo lanzó mientras atendía a sus padres","Namdev lo colocó para que el dios nunca se fuera","Janabai se lo ofreció de asiento mientras molía grano"]}},{"id":"HINDUISM-s16-05","day":1395,"d":3,"q":"In the Bhagavata Purana, why does King Bali still grant the dwarf Vamana three steps of land after his teacher Shukra warns that the boy is Vishnu?","o":["he hopes to win Vishnu's help against Indra","he fears a curse from the young brahmin boy","he will not take back a promise once given","he doubts his teacher's word about the boy"],"a":2,"es":{"q":"En el Bhagavata Purana, ¿por qué el rey Bali le concede al enano Vamana tres pasos de tierra aun después de que su maestro Shukra le advierte que el niño es Vishnu?","o":["espera ganar la ayuda de Vishnu contra Indra","teme una maldición del joven brahmán","no retira una promesa una vez dada","duda de lo que su maestro dice del niño"]}},{"id":"HINDUISM-s16-06","day":1419,"d":4,"q":"Shankara's Advaita Vedanta explains bondage with a rope mistaken for a snake. At dusk a traveler takes a tree stump for a man and is afraid. On Shankara's reasoning, what makes the 'man' go away?","o":["the man walking off down the road by himself","a torch held up to drive the man off the road","the stump accepted as a real form of the man","the stump seen clearly as the stump it is"],"a":3,"es":{"q":"El Advaita Vedanta de Shankara explica la atadura con una cuerda que se confunde con una serpiente. Al anochecer, un viajero confunde un tocón con un hombre y siente miedo. Según el razonamiento de Shankara, ¿qué hace que el 'hombre' desaparezca?","o":["que el hombre se vaya solo por el camino","una antorcha alzada para echarlo del camino","aceptar el tocón como forma real del hombre","ver con claridad que el tocón es un tocón"]}}]],"ISLAM":[[{"id":"ISLAM-s00-01","day":3,"d":2,"q":"the Qur'an's verse on washing before prayer (wudu), Surah al-Ma'idah 5:6, names which parts of the body?","o":["the hands, the mouth, the nose and the ears","the face, the chest, the hands and the knees","the face, the arms, the head and the feet","the whole body, washed from the head down"],"a":2,"es":{"q":"el versículo del Corán sobre lavarse antes de la oración (wudu), sura al-Ma'ida 5:6, ¿qué partes del cuerpo nombra?","o":["las manos, la boca, la nariz y las orejas","la cara, el pecho, las manos y las rodillas","la cara, los brazos, la cabeza y los pies","todo el cuerpo, lavado de la cabeza para abajo"]}},{"id":"ISLAM-s00-02","day":7,"d":1,"q":"Eid al-Adha, the feast of sacrifice, remembers which prophet's readiness to sacrifice his son at God's command?","o":["Yaqub (Jacob)","Ibrahim (Abraham)","Sulayman (Solomon)","Dawud (David)"],"a":1,"es":{"q":"Eid al-Adha, la fiesta del sacrificio, ¿recuerda la disposición de qué profeta a sacrificar a su hijo por mandato de Dios?","o":["Yaqub (Jacob)","Ibrahim (Abraham)","Sulaimán (Salomón)","Daud (David)"]}},{"id":"ISLAM-s00-03","day":8,"d":2,"q":"the greeting as-salamu alaykum, the name Islam and the word Muslim all grow from one Arabic root, s-l-m. what does that root carry?","o":["peace and surrender to God","faith and trust placed in God","praise and thanks given to God","purity and growth by giving"],"a":0,"es":{"q":"el saludo as-salamu alaykum, el nombre Islam y la palabra musulmán nacen de una misma raíz árabe, s-l-m. ¿qué lleva esa raíz?","o":["paz y entrega a Dios","fe y confianza en Dios","alabanza y gracias a Dios","pureza y crecimiento al dar"]}},{"id":"ISLAM-s00-04","day":10,"d":2,"q":"Muslims speak of two kinds of prayer, salat and du'a. what is the difference between them?","o":["salat is said alone at home; du'a only in a mosque","salat is in one's own words; du'a has a set form","salat is the Friday prayer; du'a is the daily prayer","salat has set times and form; du'a is asking freely"],"a":3,"es":{"q":"los musulmanes hablan de dos tipos de oración, salat y du'a. ¿cuál es la diferencia entre ellas?","o":["la salat se hace solo en casa; la du'a, en la mezquita","la salat es con palabras propias; la du'a tiene forma fija","la salat es la oración del viernes; la du'a, la diaria","la salat tiene horas y forma fijas; la du'a es pedir libre"]}},{"id":"ISLAM-s00-05","day":11,"d":2,"q":"a woman hears she did not get a job she hoped for and answers, \"alhamdulillah.\" going by the words themselves, what is she saying?","o":["God willing, a better job will come later","what God has willed is good, as it is","praise belongs to God, whatever happens","I ask God to forgive me for my mistakes"],"a":2,"es":{"q":"una mujer se entera de que no obtuvo un trabajo que esperaba y responde: \"alhamdulillah\". según las palabras mismas, ¿qué está diciendo?","o":["si Dios quiere, vendrá un trabajo mejor","lo que Dios ha querido es bueno así","la alabanza es de Dios, pase lo que pase","le pido a Dios que perdone mis errores"]}},{"id":"ISLAM-s00-06","day":13,"d":2,"q":"al-Fatiha's third verse calls God ar-Rahman ar-Rahim. what quality do these two names describe?","o":["God's power and majesty","God's justice and judgment","God's oneness and uniqueness","God's mercy and compassion"],"a":3,"es":{"q":"el tercer versículo de al-Fatiha llama a Dios ar-Rahman ar-Rahim. ¿qué cualidad describen estos dos nombres?","o":["el poder y la majestad de Dios","la justicia y el juicio de Dios","la unicidad de Dios","la misericordia y compasión de Dios"]}}],[{"id":"ISLAM-s01-01","day":24,"d":1,"q":"in Surah Al-A'raf (7:11–12), God asks Iblis what kept him from bowing to Adam when commanded. what reason does Iblis give?","o":["Adam would shed blood and spread harm on earth","he was created of fire, and Adam only of clay","Adam had already eaten from the forbidden tree","he had been told to bow to God and none other"],"a":1,"es":{"q":"en la sura Al-A'raf (7:11–12), Dios le pregunta a Iblís qué le impidió inclinarse ante Adán cuando se le ordenó. ¿qué razón da Iblís?","o":["Adán derramaría sangre y sembraría daño en la tierra","él fue creado de fuego, y Adán solo de barro","Adán ya había comido del árbol prohibido","le habían dicho que se inclinara solo ante Dios"]}},{"id":"ISLAM-s01-02","day":27,"d":2,"q":"in Surah Al-A'raf, both Iblis and Adam fall into disobedience. how does Adam's response (7:23) differ from Iblis's (7:16)?","o":["Adam blames the whisperer; Iblis admits his own pride","Adam blames his wife; Iblis admits he has done wrong","Adam asks to stay in the garden; Iblis asks for pardon","Adam owns his wrong; Iblis says God sent him astray"],"a":3,"es":{"q":"en la sura Al-A'raf, tanto Iblís como Adán caen en la desobediencia. ¿en qué se diferencia la respuesta de Adán (7:23) de la de Iblís (7:16)?","o":["Adán culpa al que susurra; Iblís admite su propio orgullo","Adán culpa a su esposa; Iblís admite que hizo mal","Adán pide quedarse en el jardín; Iblís pide perdón","Adán reconoce su falta; Iblís dice que Dios lo extravió"]}},{"id":"ISLAM-s01-03","day":32,"d":3,"q":"in Surah Al-An'am (6:76–78), Ibrahim turns from the star, the moon and the sun, saying \"I love not things that set.\" by that same test, why would he refuse to take a great river as his lord?","o":["a river is shaped by the hands of the people","a river lies far lower than the stars and sun","a river can run dry and vanish like the rest","a river was not among his people's idols"],"a":2,"es":{"q":"en la sura Al-An'am (6:76–78), Ibrahim se aparta de la estrella, la luna y el sol, diciendo \"no amo lo que se pone\". con esa misma prueba, ¿por qué se negaría a tomar un gran río como su señor?","o":["un río lo moldean las manos de la gente","un río está mucho más abajo que el sol y los astros","un río puede secarse y desaparecer como los demás","un río no estaba entre los ídolos de su pueblo"]}},{"id":"ISLAM-s01-04","day":34,"d":2,"q":"in Surah Al-Anbiya (21:62–66), asked who smashed the town's idols, Ibrahim points to the largest and says \"question them, if they can speak.\" what is he leading the people to see?","o":["idols that cannot speak can neither help nor harm","the chief idol had turned in anger on the others","the idols must first be judged by the town elders","the largest idol alone deserved their worship"],"a":0,"es":{"q":"en la sura Al-Anbiya (21:62–66), cuando le preguntan quién destrozó los ídolos del pueblo, Ibrahim señala el más grande y dice \"pregúntenles, si es que pueden hablar\". ¿qué quiere que la gente vea?","o":["ídolos que no hablan no pueden ayudar ni dañar","el ídolo mayor se había enojado con los demás","los ancianos del pueblo debían juzgar a los ídolos","solo el ídolo más grande merecía su adoración"]}},{"id":"ISLAM-s01-05","day":68,"d":2,"q":"in Surah Yusuf (12:89–92), when his brothers finally recognize Yusuf in Egypt and admit they were wrong, how does he answer them?","o":["he tells them God will settle their account in the end","he forgives them once their father has pardoned them","he says no blame is on them today and prays for them","he keeps their grain until they repay what they took"],"a":2,"es":{"q":"en la sura Yusuf (12:89–92), cuando sus hermanos por fin reconocen a Yusuf en Egipto y admiten que obraron mal, ¿cómo les responde?","o":["les dice que Dios les pedirá cuentas al final","los perdona cuando su padre ya los haya perdonado","les dice que hoy no hay reproche y ruega por ellos","retiene su grano hasta que paguen lo que tomaron"]}},{"id":"ISLAM-s01-06","day":76,"d":2,"q":"in Surah Al-Anbiya (21:87), Yunus (Dhu'n-Nun, \"the man of the fish\") cries out from within the darkness. what does he say?","o":["Our Lord, we have wronged ourselves; have mercy on us","There is no god but You; glory to You; I was wrong","My Lord, I am in need of whatever good You send me","My Lord, open my breast for me and ease my task"],"a":1,"es":{"q":"en la sura Al-Anbiya (21:87), Yunus (Dhu'n-Nun, \"el del pez\") clama desde la oscuridad. ¿qué dice?","o":["Señor nuestro, fuimos injustos con nosotros; ten piedad","No hay dios sino Tú; gloria a Ti; yo obré mal","Señor mío, necesito el bien que me hagas descender","Señor mío, ensancha mi pecho y facilita mi tarea"]}}],[{"id":"ISLAM-s02-01","day":99,"d":2,"q":"for some sixteen or seventeen months after the hijra, before Qur'an 2:144 turned the prayer toward the Sacred Mosque in Mecca, which way did the Muslims in Medina face?","o":["toward the cave of Hira, near Mecca","toward Mount Uhud, north of Medina","toward Jerusalem, Bayt al-Maqdis","toward the sunrise, in the east"],"a":2,"es":{"q":"durante unos dieciséis o diecisiete meses después de la hégira, antes de que el Corán 2:144 dirigiera la oración hacia la Mezquita Sagrada de La Meca, ¿hacia dónde se orientaban los musulmanes de Medina?","o":["hacia la cueva de Hira, cerca de La Meca","hacia el monte Uhud, al norte de Medina","hacia Jerusalén, Bayt al-Maqdis","hacia el amanecer, en el este"]}},{"id":"ISLAM-s02-02","day":105,"d":2,"q":"the Arabic word masjid, behind the English \"mosque,\" comes from the same root as sujud. what does masjid literally mean?","o":["a place of recitation","a place of prostration","a place of gathering","a place of cleansing"],"a":1,"es":{"q":"la palabra árabe masjid, de donde viene \"mezquita\", sale de la misma raíz que sujud. ¿qué significa masjid literalmente?","o":["un lugar de recitación","un lugar de postración","un lugar de reunión","un lugar de purificación"]}},{"id":"ISLAM-s02-03","day":107,"d":3,"q":"Ibn Mas'ud reports in Sahih al-Bukhari that the companions once said \"peace be on Allah\" in the sitting of the prayer, and the Prophet ﷺ told them to stop. what reason did he give?","o":["peace may be wished upon the prophets alone","no greeting may be spoken inside the prayer","the angels alone may send greetings to Allah","Allah is Himself the Peace, as-Salam"],"a":3,"es":{"q":"Ibn Mas'ud relata en Sahih al-Bujari que los compañeros decían una vez \"la paz sea sobre Allah\" en la posición sentada de la oración, y el Profeta ﷺ les dijo que dejaran de hacerlo. ¿qué razón dio?","o":["la paz se desea solo sobre los profetas","no se dice ningún saludo dentro de la oración","solo los ángeles envían saludos a Allah","Allah mismo es la Paz, as-Salam"]}},{"id":"ISLAM-s02-04","day":124,"d":3,"q":"Surah al-Qadr (97:3) says the Night of Power is \"better than a thousand months.\" how do classical commentators such as Ibn Kathir read that line?","o":["deeds that night outweigh those of a thousand months","the Qur'an took a thousand months to be revealed after it","the night comes round once in every thousand months or so","its reward is kept for those who fasted a thousand months"],"a":0,"es":{"q":"la sura al-Qadr (97:3) dice que la Noche del Poder es \"mejor que mil meses\". ¿cómo leen esa línea comentaristas clásicos como Ibn Kazir?","o":["las obras de esa noche valen más que las de mil meses","el Corán tardó mil meses en revelarse después de ella","esa noche vuelve más o menos una vez cada mil meses","su recompensa es para quien haya ayunado mil meses"]}},{"id":"ISLAM-s02-05","day":153,"d":3,"q":"in the hadith of Sahih Muslim, a person's deeds end at death except for three, and the first is sadaqah jariyah. why would a public well or a planted tree count as sadaqah jariyah?","o":["it is given in secret, so that no one knows the giver","it is paid once a year from savings, like the zakat","it is given by the family on the day of the funeral","its benefit keeps flowing after the giver has died"],"a":3,"es":{"q":"en el hadiz de Sahih Muslim, las obras de una persona terminan con la muerte salvo tres, y la primera es la sadaqah jariyah. ¿por qué un pozo público o un árbol plantado cuentan como sadaqah jariyah?","o":["se da en secreto, para que nadie sepa quién la dio","se paga una vez al año de los ahorros, como el zakat","la entrega la familia el mismo día del funeral","su beneficio sigue fluyendo tras morir quien la dio"]}},{"id":"ISLAM-s02-06","day":126,"d":3,"q":"a baby is born to a Muslim family a few days before the end of Ramadan. according to Ibn Umar's report in Sahih al-Bukhari, does the family owe zakat al-fitr, the charity of breaking the fast, for the baby?","o":["no, it is owed by those who fasted the month","yes, it is owed for every member, young or old","no, a child owes it from the age of puberty","yes, but only once the baby has been weaned from milk"],"a":1,"es":{"q":"a una familia musulmana le nace un bebé unos días antes del final de Ramadán. según el relato de Ibn Umar en Sahih al-Bujari, ¿debe la familia el zakat al-fitr, la caridad de romper el ayuno, por el bebé?","o":["no, lo deben quienes ayunaron el mes","sí, se debe por cada miembro, pequeño o mayor","no, un niño lo debe desde la pubertad","sí, pero solo cuando el bebé ya haya dejado la leche materna"]}}],[{"id":"ISLAM-s03-01","day":169,"d":2,"q":"Surah al-Fil (105) recalls the army of the Elephant that marched on the Ka'bah in the year the Prophet Muhammad ﷺ was born. according to the commentators and the early biography, who led that army?","o":["Abu Lahab, the Prophet's uncle","Abraha, a ruler from Yemen","Abu Jahl, a chief of Quraysh","Abu Sufyan, a Meccan leader"],"a":1,"es":{"q":"la sura al-Fil (105) recuerda al ejército del Elefante que marchó contra la Kaaba el año en que nació el Profeta Muhammad ﷺ. según los comentaristas y la biografía temprana, ¿quién dirigía ese ejército?","o":["Abu Lahab, el tío del Profeta","Abraha, un gobernante de Yemen","Abu Jahl, un jefe de Quraysh","Abu Sufyan, un líder de La Meca"]}},{"id":"ISLAM-s03-02","day":224,"d":2,"q":"which verse of the Qur'an says of Allah, in Pickthall's words, \"Neither slumber nor sleep overtaketh Him\"?","o":["the Light Verse, an-Nur 24:35","the opening of al-Hadid, 57:3","the closing of al-Baqarah, 2:286","Ayat al-Kursi, al-Baqarah 2:255"],"a":3,"es":{"q":"¿qué verso del Corán dice de Allah, en palabras de Pickthall, \"ni la somnolencia ni el sueño lo alcanzan\"?","o":["el Verso de la Luz, an-Nur 24:35","el comienzo de al-Hadid, 57:3","el cierre de al-Baqarah, 2:286","Ayat al-Kursi, al-Baqarah 2:255"]}},{"id":"ISLAM-s03-03","day":162,"d":3,"q":"the Prophet Muhammad ﷺ said that Surah al-Ikhlas (112) equals a third of the Qur'an (Sahih al-Bukhari). what is a well-known explanation of this among the scholars?","o":["it came down after a third of the Qur'an had been revealed","its four short verses hold a third of all the words in the Qur'an","it holds Allah's oneness, one of the Qur'an's three great themes","the Prophet recited it in a third of all the prayers he led"],"a":2,"es":{"q":"el Profeta Muhammad ﷺ dijo que la sura al-Ijlas (112) equivale a un tercio del Corán (Sahih al-Bujari). ¿cuál es una explicación conocida de esto entre los sabios?","o":["fue revelada cuando ya había bajado un tercio del Corán","sus cuatro versos cortos contienen un tercio de las palabras del Corán","trata la unicidad de Allah, uno de los tres grandes temas del Corán","el Profeta la recitó en un tercio de las oraciones que dirigió"]}},{"id":"ISLAM-s03-04","day":185,"d":3,"q":"Surah ash-Sharh (94:5–6) says twice, \"with hardship goeth ease.\" in Arabic, hardship carries the article both times (al-'usr) and ease does not (yusr). what do classical commentators draw from this?","o":["one and the same hardship is met by two different eases","two separate hardships are each met by one and the same ease","ease comes after the hardship has entirely ended","the hardship is long lasting while the ease is short"],"a":0,"es":{"q":"la sura ash-Sharh (94:5–6) dice dos veces: \"con la dificultad viene la facilidad\". en árabe, la dificultad lleva artículo las dos veces (al-'usr) y la facilidad no (yusr). ¿qué deducen de esto los comentaristas clásicos?","o":["una misma dificultad se encuentra con dos facilidades distintas","dos dificultades distintas se encuentran con una misma facilidad","la facilidad llega cuando la dificultad ya terminó del todo","la dificultad dura mucho y la facilidad dura muy poco"]}},{"id":"ISLAM-s03-05","day":213,"d":3,"q":"Surah 'Abasa (80:1–10) opens with a blind man, 'Abdullah ibn Umm Maktum, coming to ask to be taught while leaders of Quraysh were being spoken to. what is the passage's main lesson?","o":["a sincere seeker deserves attention, even over the powerful","blind people were excused from coming to the Prophet's gatherings","the leaders of Quraysh accepted Islam once they heard this surah","teaching should go first to those whose standing helps it spread"],"a":0,"es":{"q":"la sura 'Abasa (80:1–10) empieza con un hombre ciego, 'Abdullah ibn Umm Maktum, que llega a pedir que le enseñen mientras se hablaba con líderes de Quraysh. ¿cuál es la enseñanza principal del pasaje?","o":["quien busca de verdad merece atención, aun antes que los poderosos","los ciegos estaban dispensados de ir a las reuniones del Profeta","los líderes de Quraysh aceptaron el islam al oír esta sura","la enseñanza debe ir primero a quienes por su posición la difunden"]}},{"id":"ISLAM-s03-06","day":193,"d":3,"q":"a woman pays to set free a man held in bondage, and on a day of hunger she feeds an orphan from her own family. Surah al-Balad (90:11–16) gives deeds like these a name. what is it?","o":["an-najdayn, the two highways","al-kawthar, the great abundance","al-'aqabah, the steep ascent","as-sirat, the straight path"],"a":2,"es":{"q":"una mujer paga para liberar a un hombre que está en servidumbre y, en un día de hambre, da de comer a un huérfano de su propia familia. la sura al-Balad (90:11–16) da un nombre a obras como estas. ¿cuál es?","o":["an-najdayn, los dos caminos","al-kawthar, la gran abundancia","al-'aqabah, la cuesta empinada","as-sirat, el camino recto"]}}],[{"id":"ISLAM-s04-01","day":294,"d":2,"q":"In the Hadith of Jibril (Sahih Muslim), the Prophet ﷺ defines one term as worshipping Allah as though you see Him, for though you do not see Him, He sees you. Which term is it?","o":["ihsan","iman","islam","tawhid"],"a":0,"es":{"q":"En el hadiz de Yibril (Sahih Muslim), el Profeta ﷺ define un término como adorar a Allah como si lo vieras, porque aunque tú no lo veas, Él te ve. ¿Qué término es?","o":["ihsan","iman","islam","tawhid"]}},{"id":"ISLAM-s04-02","day":316,"d":3,"q":"According to Sahih al-Bukhari, after many who had memorized the Qur'an were killed at the battle of Yamamah, the caliph Abu Bakr gave which companion the task of gathering it into one collection?","o":["Ubayy ibn Ka'b","Mu'adh ibn Jabal","Zayd ibn Thabit","Abdullah ibn Mas'ud"],"a":2,"es":{"q":"Según Sahih al-Bujari, después de que murieran en la batalla de Yamama muchos que se sabían el Corán de memoria, ¿a qué compañero le encargó el califa Abu Bakr reunirlo en una sola colección?","o":["Ubayy ibn Ka'b","Mu'adh ibn Yabal","Zayd ibn Thabit","Abdullah ibn Mas'ud"]}},{"id":"ISLAM-s04-03","day":291,"d":3,"q":"When the Prophet ﷺ died, Abu Bakr told the people: whoever worshipped Muhammad, Muhammad has died; whoever worships Allah, Allah is living and does not die. Then he recited Qur'an 3:144. What was he making clear?","o":["the Qur'an's revelation would continue through the companions","mourning the Prophet ﷺ was forbidden to the believers","the Prophet's grave should become the community's place of prayer","the Prophet ﷺ was a mortal; Allah alone is worshipped"],"a":3,"es":{"q":"Cuando murió el Profeta ﷺ, Abu Bakr dijo a la gente: quien adoraba a Muhammad, Muhammad ha muerto; quien adora a Allah, Allah está vivo y no muere. Luego recitó el Corán 3:144. ¿Qué estaba dejando claro?","o":["la revelación del Corán seguiría a través de los compañeros","a los creyentes se les prohibía guardar luto por el Profeta ﷺ","la tumba del Profeta debía ser el lugar de oración de la comunidad","el Profeta ﷺ era mortal; solo Allah es adorado"]}},{"id":"ISLAM-s04-04","day":313,"d":3,"q":"Scholars of the Qur'an label each surah as Meccan (makki) or Medinan (madani). In the most widely used definition, what does the label mark?","o":["where the surah is placed in the order of the mushaf","whether it was revealed before or after the Hijra","which city's scribes first wrote the surah down","whether it addresses the Arabs or all of humankind"],"a":1,"es":{"q":"Los estudiosos del Corán clasifican cada sura como mecana (makki) o medinense (madani). Según la definición más usada, ¿qué indica esa etiqueta?","o":["el lugar que ocupa la sura en el orden del mushaf","si fue revelada antes o después de la Hégira","qué escribas de qué ciudad la pusieron primero por escrito","si se dirige a los árabes o a toda la humanidad"]}},{"id":"ISLAM-s04-05","day":278,"d":3,"q":"In Ibn Ishaq's biography, when the Prophet ﷺ entered Mecca in triumph, he told Quraysh he would speak to them as Yusuf spoke to his brothers: \"no blame on you this day\" (Qur'an 12:92). What did those words signal?","o":["a demand that they repay what the migrants had lost","a sentence of exile for the chiefs who led Quraysh","a warning that their judgment was delayed until later","forgiveness for the people who had long opposed him"],"a":3,"es":{"q":"En la biografía de Ibn Ishaq, cuando el Profeta ﷺ entró triunfante en La Meca, les dijo a los Quraysh que les hablaría como Yusuf habló a sus hermanos: \"hoy no hay reproche contra ustedes\" (Corán 12:92). ¿Qué indicaban esas palabras?","o":["una exigencia de devolver lo que perdieron los emigrantes","una sentencia de destierro para los jefes de los Quraysh","un aviso de que su juicio solo quedaba aplazado","el perdón para la gente que se le había opuesto por años"]}},{"id":"ISLAM-s04-06","day":306,"d":4,"q":"Classical scholars draw three stages of the self (nafs) from the Qur'an (12:53, 75:2, 89:27). A man cheats a partner, then cannot rest, reproaching himself until he makes it right. Which term fits his self at that moment?","o":["an-nafs al-lawwamah, the self that blames","an-nafs al-ammarah, the self that urges evil","an-nafs al-mutma'innah, the self at peace","al-qalb as-salim, the heart that is sound"],"a":0,"es":{"q":"Los estudiosos clásicos sacan del Corán tres etapas del ser (nafs) (12:53, 75:2, 89:27). Un hombre engaña a un socio y luego no puede descansar, reprochándose hasta que lo repara. ¿Qué término describe su ser en ese momento?","o":["an-nafs al-lawwamah, el ser que se reprocha","an-nafs al-ammarah, el ser que incita al mal","an-nafs al-mutma'innah, el ser en paz","al-qalb as-salim, el corazón que está sano"]}}],[{"id":"ISLAM-s05-01","day":341,"d":2,"q":"in Surah al-Baqarah (2:67–73), Musa tells his people to sacrifice a cow. according to verses 72–73, what were they then told to do with a part of it?","o":["feed it to the needy among the Children of Israel","use it to seal the covenant made with them at the mountain","strike the slain man with it to bring out his killer","burn it whole on the altar as an offering to Allah"],"a":2,"es":{"q":"en la sura al-Baqarah (2:67–73), Moisés (Musa) le dice a su pueblo que sacrifique una vaca. según los versículos 72–73, ¿qué se les dijo que hicieran luego con una parte de ella?","o":["dársela de comer a los necesitados de los hijos de Israel","usarla para sellar la alianza hecha con ellos en el monte","golpear con ella al muerto para descubrir al culpable","quemarla entera en el altar como una ofrenda a Alá"]}},{"id":"ISLAM-s05-02","day":356,"d":1,"q":"which verse of the Qur'an is known as Ayat al-Kursi, the Throne Verse, which says of Allah that neither slumber nor sleep overtakes Him?","o":["Surah al-Baqarah, verse 255","Surah al-Baqarah, verse 286","Surah al-Mu'minun, verse 116","Surah al-Hashr, verse 22"],"a":0,"es":{"q":"¿qué versículo del Corán se conoce como Ayat al-Kursi, el versículo del Trono, que dice de Alá que no lo toman ni la somnolencia ni el sueño?","o":["sura al-Baqarah, versículo 255","sura al-Baqarah, versículo 286","sura al-Mu'minun, versículo 116","sura al-Hashr, versículo 22"]}},{"id":"ISLAM-s05-03","day":357,"d":2,"q":"Surah al-Baqarah 2:256 opens, \"There is no compulsion in religion.\" what reason does the verse itself give right after?","o":["forced belief would earn no reward on the Last Day","the right direction is now made distinct from error","each community was given its own law and its own way","faith lies hidden in the heart, where no one can see"],"a":1,"es":{"q":"la sura al-Baqarah 2:256 empieza: \"No hay coacción en la religión\". ¿qué razón da el propio versículo justo después?","o":["la fe forzada no tendría recompensa en el Último Día","el buen camino ya se distingue claramente del error","a cada comunidad se le dio su propia ley y su propio camino","la fe está escondida en el corazón, donde nadie la ve"]}},{"id":"ISLAM-s05-04","day":360,"d":3,"q":"a man pays a struggling neighbor's rent, then brings it up at every family gathering. in the terms of Surah al-Baqarah 2:261–265, what happens to his gift?","o":["it is spoiled, like soil washed off a smooth rock","it is doubled, like a garden on a hill in heavy rain","it grows seven ears of grain, each with a hundred","it is purer, since giving openly sets an example"],"a":0,"es":{"q":"un hombre le paga el alquiler a un vecino en apuros y luego lo menciona en cada reunión familiar. en los términos de la sura al-Baqarah 2:261–265, ¿qué le pasa a su regalo?","o":["se pierde, como tierra que la lluvia quita de una roca","se duplica, como un jardín en una colina con lluvia","crece en siete espigas, cada una con cien granos","es más puro, porque dar en público da buen ejemplo"]}},{"id":"ISLAM-s05-05","day":373,"d":2,"q":"in Surah Al 'Imran 3:159, revealed after the battle of Uhud, the Prophet's gentleness with his companions is called a mercy from Allah. what does the verse say would have happened had he been stern and harsh of heart?","o":["the hypocrites would have turned the believers back","Quraysh would have returned to attack Medina","the angels would no longer have aided his army","the people would have dispersed from about him"],"a":3,"es":{"q":"en la sura Al 'Imran 3:159, revelada después de la batalla de Uhud, la bondad del Profeta con sus compañeros se llama una misericordia de Alá. ¿qué dice el versículo que habría pasado si él hubiera sido duro y áspero de corazón?","o":["los hipócritas habrían hecho retroceder a los fieles","Quraysh habría vuelto para atacar a Medina","los ángeles ya no habrían ayudado a su ejército","la gente se habría dispersado de su alrededor"]}},{"id":"ISLAM-s05-06","day":417,"d":3,"q":"about the battle of Badr, Surah al-Anfal 8:17 tells the Prophet ﷺ, \"thou threwest not when thou didst throw, but Allah threw.\" what is the verse saying?","o":["the Prophet ﷺ never really threw anything that day","the throw was his, yet its effect was Allah's","angels threw the dust there in the Prophet's place","the believers won at Badr by their own strength"],"a":1,"es":{"q":"sobre la batalla de Badr, la sura al-Anfal 8:17 le dice al Profeta ﷺ: \"no fuiste tú quien arrojó cuando arrojaste, sino que Alá arrojó\". ¿qué está diciendo el versículo?","o":["el Profeta ﷺ en realidad no arrojó nada ese día","el lanzamiento fue suyo, pero su efecto fue de Alá","los ángeles arrojaron el polvo en lugar del Profeta","los creyentes ganaron en Badr por su propia fuerza"]}}],[{"id":"ISLAM-s06-01","day":421,"d":2,"q":"of the 114 surahs of the Qur'an, which one is the only surah that does not open with the bismillah (\"in the name of Allah, the Beneficent, the Merciful\")?","o":["Surah Al-Anfal, the eighth","Surah At-Tawbah, the ninth","Surah Yunus, the tenth","Surah Al-Ikhlas, number 112"],"a":1,"es":{"q":"de las 114 suras del Corán, ¿cuál es la única que no empieza con la basmala (\"en el nombre de Allah, el Clemente, el Misericordioso\")?","o":["la sura Al-Anfal, la octava","la sura At-Tawbah, la novena","la sura Yunus, la décima","la sura Al-Ijlas, la número 112"]}},{"id":"ISLAM-s06-02","day":469,"d":3,"q":"in Surah Al-Kahf (18:71–79), al-Khidr makes a hole in the boat that has carried him and Musa. what reason does he later give for it?","o":["a king ahead was seizing every sound boat by force","its crew had planned to rob the two travelers at sea","the boat was carrying stolen goods to a wicked town","its owners had refused to let Musa ride for free"],"a":0,"es":{"q":"en la sura Al-Kahf (18:71–79), al-Jidr le hace un agujero a la barca que lo llevaba a él y a Musa. ¿qué razón da después?","o":["un rey más adelante se apoderaba de toda barca en buen estado","la tripulación pensaba robar a los dos viajeros en el mar","la barca llevaba mercancía robada a una ciudad malvada","sus dueños se habían negado a llevar gratis a Musa"]}},{"id":"ISLAM-s06-03","day":443,"d":3,"q":"Surah Ar-Ra'd 13:11 says, in Pickthall's words, \"Allah changeth not the condition of a folk until they (first) change that which is in their hearts.\" what does the verse teach?","o":["God rewards a people's hard work with worldly success","a people's state follows the change within them","a people's fate is fixed and can never be changed","a people must replace their rulers before God helps"],"a":1,"es":{"q":"la sura Ar-Ra'd 13:11 dice: \"Allah no cambia la condición de un pueblo hasta que ellos (primero) cambien lo que hay en sus corazones\". ¿qué enseña el versículo?","o":["Dios premia el trabajo duro de un pueblo con éxito mundano","el estado de un pueblo sigue al cambio dentro de sí mismo","el destino de un pueblo está fijado y nunca puede cambiar","un pueblo debe cambiar a sus gobernantes antes de que Dios ayude"]}},{"id":"ISLAM-s06-04","day":486,"d":3,"q":"Surah Al-Hajj 22:37 says of the animals offered in sacrifice, \"their flesh and their blood reach not Allah, but the devotion from you reacheth Him.\" what does this teach about the sacrifice?","o":["its blood must be placed on the Ka'ba for it to be accepted","its meat must be burned whole so that none of it is eaten","its worth lies in the giver's taqwa, not in meat or blood","its offering takes the place of the prayers missed that year"],"a":2,"es":{"q":"la sura Al-Hajj 22:37 dice de los animales ofrecidos en sacrificio: \"ni su carne ni su sangre llegan a Allah, pero sí le llega la devoción de ustedes\". ¿qué enseña esto sobre el sacrificio?","o":["su sangre debe ponerse en la Kaaba para que sea aceptado","su carne debe quemarse entera para que nadie la coma","su valor está en la taqwa, no en la carne ni la sangre","su ofrenda reemplaza las oraciones que faltaron ese año"]}},{"id":"ISLAM-s06-05","day":515,"d":2,"q":"why does the month of Ramadan move through all the seasons, coming round to the same season roughly every 33 years?","o":["a council sets its dates anew each year by the harvest","an extra month is added to the year every third year","the Hijri year counts from the hijra, not the solstice","the lunar Hijri year runs about 11 days shorter"],"a":3,"es":{"q":"¿por qué el mes de Ramadán pasa por todas las estaciones y vuelve a la misma más o menos cada 33 años?","o":["un consejo fija sus fechas cada año según la cosecha","se añade un mes extra al año cada tercer año","el año hiyri se cuenta desde la hégira, no el solsticio","el año hiyri lunar es unos 11 días más corto"]}},{"id":"ISLAM-s06-06","day":454,"d":3,"q":"a carpenter is paid for a plain shelf and gives the customer exactly what was agreed, then sands and finishes it with great care, working as though God sees her. Qur'an 16:90 commands 'adl and a further quality; which term names what she adds?","o":["'adl, justice, giving each what is due","ihsan, doing what is good and beautiful","zakat, the alms owed on wealth each year","sabr, steady patience under hardship"],"a":1,"es":{"q":"a una carpintera le pagan una repisa sencilla; le da al cliente justo lo acordado y luego la lija y la termina con mucho cuidado, trabajando como si Dios la viera. el Corán 16:90 ordena el 'adl y otra cualidad más; ¿qué término nombra lo que ella añade?","o":["'adl, la justicia, dar a cada uno lo debido","ihsan, hacer lo que es bueno y hermoso","zakat, la limosna anual debida sobre los bienes","sabr, la paciencia firme en la dificultad"]}}],[{"id":"ISLAM-s07-01","day":520,"d":2,"q":"in Surah An-Naml (27:18–19), an ant warns the other ants to enter their dwellings so that Sulayman and his armies don't crush them unawares. how does Sulayman respond when he hears her?","o":["he halts his army and orders the valley cleared","he rebukes the ant for doubting his army's care","he smiles and prays that he be made thankful","he sends the hoopoe to lead the ants to safety"],"a":2,"es":{"q":"en la sura An-Naml (27:18–19), una hormiga advierte a las demás que entren en sus moradas para que Salomón (Sulayman) y sus ejércitos no las aplasten sin darse cuenta. ¿cómo responde Sulayman al oírla?","o":["detiene a su ejército y ordena despejar el valle","reprende a la hormiga por dudar de su ejército","sonríe y le pide a su Señor que lo haga agradecido","envía a la abubilla a llevar a las hormigas a salvo"]}},{"id":"ISLAM-s07-02","day":544,"d":3,"q":"in Surah Saba' (34:14), Sulayman dies while the jinn are still at work building for him. what first shows them that he has died?","o":["the wind he commanded stops blowing for him","a creature of the earth gnaws away his staff","the hoopoe brings word that the king is gone","his throne is found empty at the hour of court"],"a":1,"es":{"q":"en la sura Saba' (34:14), Salomón (Sulayman) muere mientras los genios (yinn) siguen trabajando en sus obras. ¿qué les muestra primero que él ha muerto?","o":["el viento que él dominaba deja de soplar para él","una criatura de la tierra le roe el bastón","la abubilla trae la noticia de que el rey ya no está","su trono aparece vacío a la hora de la audiencia"]}},{"id":"ISLAM-s07-03","day":580,"d":3,"q":"Surah Al-Fath came to the Prophet Muhammad ﷺ on the way home from Hudaybiyyah, after a treaty that many companions felt was a setback. how does its first verse (48:1) describe what had happened?","o":["a trial sent to test the believers' patience","a punishment for the companions' many doubts","a defeat to be repaid in battle the next year","a clear opening, given by God to the Prophet"],"a":3,"es":{"q":"la sura Al-Fath le llegó al Profeta Muhammad ﷺ en el camino de regreso de Hudaybiyyah, tras un tratado que muchos compañeros sintieron como un revés. ¿cómo describe su primer verso (48:1) lo que había pasado?","o":["una prueba para la paciencia de los creyentes","un castigo por las muchas dudas de los compañeros","una derrota que se cobraría en batalla al año siguiente","una apertura clara, dada por Dios al Profeta"]}},{"id":"ISLAM-s07-04","day":587,"d":3,"q":"Surah Al-Hujurat (49:12) forbids ghibah, backbiting, and a hadith in Sahih Muslim (2589) defines it. according to that hadith, what is ghibah?","o":["making up a false story about someone who is absent","rebuking a brother harshly to his face before others","praising someone absent more highly than he deserves","mentioning a brother with a true thing he'd dislike"],"a":3,"es":{"q":"la sura Al-Hujurat (49:12) prohíbe la ghibah, la murmuración, y un hadiz de Sahih Muslim (2589) la define. según ese hadiz, ¿qué es la ghibah?","o":["inventar una historia falsa sobre alguien que no está","reprender con dureza a un hermano en su cara ante otros","elogiar a alguien ausente más de lo que se merece","mencionar de un hermano algo cierto que le disgustaría"]}},{"id":"ISLAM-s07-05","day":588,"d":2,"q":"in Surah Al-Hujurat (49:13), God says He created humankind male and female and made them nations and tribes. what purpose does the verse give for those nations and tribes?","o":["so that the noblest tribe might lead the rest","so that they may come to know one another","so that they might be tested by their wars","so that each might guard its own land apart"],"a":1,"es":{"q":"en la sura Al-Hujurat (49:13), Dios dice que creó a la humanidad varón y mujer y la hizo naciones y tribus. ¿qué propósito da el verso para esas naciones y tribus?","o":["para que la tribu más noble guíe a las demás","para que lleguen a conocerse unos a otros","para que sean puestas a prueba por sus guerras","para que cada una guarde su propia tierra aparte"]}},{"id":"ISLAM-s07-06","day":584,"d":3,"q":"a story reaches a town that a neighboring family has done something terrible, and the one who brought it is known for crossing the line. by Surah Al-Hujurat (49:6), what should the townspeople do first?","o":["find out if it's true before acting on it","warn everyone at once so no one else is hurt","take it to a judge so the family is punished","drop it, as such a man's word has no weight"],"a":0,"es":{"q":"a un pueblo llega la historia de que una familia vecina hizo algo terrible, y quien la trajo es conocido por pasarse de la raya. según la sura Al-Hujurat (49:6), ¿qué debe hacer primero la gente del pueblo?","o":["averiguar primero si es cierto, antes de actuar","avisar a todos enseguida para que nadie salga herido","llevarlo ante un juez para que castigue a la familia","descartarlo, porque la palabra de ese hombre no vale"]}}],[{"id":"ISLAM-s08-01","day":616,"d":3,"q":"Surah al-Mujadila (58), \"she who pleads,\" opens: \"Allah hath heard the saying of her that disputeth with thee (Muhammad) concerning her husband.\" What had her husband done?","o":["declared her to be like his mother's back (zihar)","refused to pay her the dowry (mahr) he had promised","divorced her three times in a single sitting","taken a second wife without telling her first"],"a":0,"es":{"q":"La sura al-Mujadila (58), \"la que discute\", comienza: \"Alá ha oído las palabras de la que discutía contigo (Muhámmad) acerca de su esposo\". ¿Qué había hecho su esposo?","o":["declararla como la espalda de su madre (zihar)","negarse a pagarle la dote (mahr) que había prometido","divorciarse de ella tres veces en una sola sesión","tomar una segunda esposa sin avisarle a la primera"]}},{"id":"ISLAM-s08-02","day":657,"d":3,"q":"In Surah al-Qiyamah (75:2), Allah swears by \"an-nafs al-lawwamah\" (Pickthall: \"the accusing soul\"). In the classical reading, what kind of self is this?","o":["the self that urges a person on toward wrong","the self that reproaches itself for its faults","the self at rest, well pleased with its Lord","the self that boasts of its good deeds to others"],"a":1,"es":{"q":"En la sura al-Qiyamah (75:2), Alá jura por \"an-nafs al-lawwamah\" (Pickthall: \"el alma que acusa\"). En la lectura clásica, ¿qué clase de yo es este?","o":["el yo que empuja a la persona hacia el mal","el yo que se reprocha a sí mismo sus faltas","el yo en reposo, satisfecho con su Señor","el yo que presume ante otros de sus buenas obras"]}},{"id":"ISLAM-s08-03","day":618,"d":3,"q":"Qur'an 59:9 praises the Ansar of Medina, who \"prefer (the fugitives) above themselves though poverty become their lot.\" What quality, called ithar, is the verse praising?","o":["giving the emigrants what was left after their own needs","hosting the emigrants for the three days custom required","putting the emigrants' needs first even when in need","welcoming the emigrants if they joined the Ansar's clans"],"a":2,"es":{"q":"Corán 59:9 elogia a los ansar de Medina, que \"prefieren (a los emigrados) antes que a sí mismos, aunque pasen necesidad\". ¿Qué cualidad, llamada ithar, elogia el versículo?","o":["dar a los emigrados lo que sobraba tras sus propias necesidades","hospedar a los emigrados los tres días que pedía la costumbre","poner primero las necesidades de los emigrados aun en necesidad","acoger a los emigrados si se unían a los clanes de los ansar"]}},{"id":"ISLAM-s08-04","day":642,"d":3,"q":"In Surah al-Qalam (68:17–33), the owners of a garden find it destroyed overnight. According to the passage, what had they planned to do?","o":["sell the whole harvest to a merchant from a far-off town","harvest on a sacred day when work was forbidden","cut down their late father's trees to sell the wood","harvest at dawn so no needy person could get a share"],"a":3,"es":{"q":"En la sura al-Qalam (68:17–33), los dueños de un huerto lo encuentran destruido de la noche a la mañana. Según el pasaje, ¿qué habían planeado hacer?","o":["vender toda la cosecha a un comerciante de un pueblo lejano","cosechar en un día sagrado en el que se prohibía trabajar","talar los árboles de su difunto padre para vender la madera","cosechar al alba para que ningún necesitado recibiera parte"]}},{"id":"ISLAM-s08-05","day":674,"d":3,"q":"In Surah an-Naml (27:29–35), the Queen of Sheba receives Sulayman's letter and consults her chiefs. What does she decide to do first?","o":["send her army to his border to show its great might","hide her great throne in a fortress far away","send him a gift and see what her envoys report","have the hoopoe that brought the letter caged"],"a":2,"es":{"q":"En la sura an-Naml (27:29–35), la reina de Saba recibe la carta de Sulaimán y consulta a sus jefes. ¿Qué decide hacer primero?","o":["enviar su ejército a la frontera para mostrar su poder","esconder su gran trono en una fortaleza muy lejana","enviarle un regalo y ver qué informan sus enviados","mandar encerrar a la abubilla que trajo la carta"]}},{"id":"ISLAM-s08-06","day":680,"d":3,"q":"A ruler orders a conquered people to accept Islam by force. Which verse of the Qur'an speaks most directly against that order?","o":["\"Lo! Allah loveth not aggressors\" (2:190)","\"There is no compulsion in religion\" (2:256)","\"If they incline to peace, incline thou to it\" (8:61)","\"If ye judge between mankind, judge justly\" (4:58)"],"a":1,"es":{"q":"Un gobernante ordena a un pueblo conquistado aceptar el islam por la fuerza. ¿Qué versículo del Corán habla más directamente contra esa orden?","o":["\"Alá no ama a los agresores\" (2:190)","\"No hay coacción en la religión\" (2:256)","\"Si se inclinan a la paz, inclínate tú a ella\" (8:61)","\"Si juzgáis entre la gente, juzgad con justicia\" (4:58)"]}}],[{"id":"ISLAM-s09-01","day":736,"d":2,"q":"In Ibn Ishaq's sirah, what word does Bilal ibn Rabah repeat in Mecca while his master Umayyah has a great rock laid on his chest?","o":["haqq, haqq: 'Truth, Truth'","ahad, ahad: 'One, One'","salam, salam: 'Peace, Peace'","nur, nur: 'Light, Light'"],"a":1,"es":{"q":"En la sira de Ibn Ishaq, ¿qué palabra repite Bilal ibn Rabah en La Meca mientras su amo Umayyah le pone una gran roca sobre el pecho?","o":["haqq, haqq: 'Verdad, Verdad'","ahad, ahad: 'Uno, Uno'","salam, salam: 'Paz, Paz'","nur, nur: 'Luz, Luz'"]}},{"id":"ISLAM-s09-02","day":767,"d":2,"q":"Which companion earned the name dhat al-nitaqayn, 'she of the two belts', on the night of the hijrah to Medina?","o":["Umm Ayman, the Prophet's nurse","Fatimah, the Prophet's daughter","Asma, the daughter of Abu Bakr","Aisha, the daughter of Abu Bakr"],"a":2,"es":{"q":"¿Qué compañera recibió el nombre de dhat al-nitaqayn, 'la de los dos cinturones', la noche de la hégira a Medina?","o":["Umm Ayman, la nodriza del Profeta","Fátima, la hija del Profeta","Asma, la hija de Abu Bakr","Aisha, la hija de Abu Bakr"]}},{"id":"ISLAM-s09-03","day":725,"d":3,"q":"In Sahih al-Bukhari, after the first revelation at Hira, on what grounds does Khadijah tell the Prophet ﷺ that Allah will never disgrace him?","o":["his descent from Ibrahim through Banu Hashim","his long seclusion and prayer on Mount Hira","a dream of light she had seen before their marriage","his care for kin, the weak, the poor and guests"],"a":3,"es":{"q":"En Sahih al-Bujari, después de la primera revelación en Hira, ¿en qué se basa Jadiya para decirle al Profeta ﷺ que Allah nunca lo deshonrará?","o":["su linaje desde Ibrahim por el clan de Banu Hashim","su largo retiro y oración en el monte Hira","un sueño de luz que tuvo antes de casarse con él","su cuidado de parientes, débiles, pobres y huéspedes"]}},{"id":"ISLAM-s09-04","day":756,"d":3,"q":"In the hadith of the Mi'raj in Sahih al-Bukhari, why are the fifty daily prayers first given reduced to five?","o":["Musa urges him to go back and ask for less","Jibril pleads that his people are too weak","Ibrahim counsels him to seek a lighter load","Isa warns the burden will be too heavy"],"a":0,"es":{"q":"En el hadiz del Miraj en Sahih al-Bujari, ¿por qué las cincuenta oraciones diarias que se dieron al principio se reducen a cinco?","o":["Musa le insiste en volver y pedir menos","Yibril ruega porque su pueblo es muy débil","Ibrahim le aconseja buscar una carga más ligera","Isa le advierte que la carga será muy pesada"]}},{"id":"ISLAM-s09-05","day":779,"d":3,"q":"At the Battle of Uhud, why does the fighting turn against the Muslims after their strong start?","o":["a sandstorm blinds the Muslim ranks at noon","the Meccans seize the wells behind their lines","the archers leave their hill to gather spoils","fresh troops from Ta'if reach the Meccan side"],"a":2,"es":{"q":"En la batalla de Uhud, ¿por qué el combate se vuelve contra los musulmanes después de su buen comienzo?","o":["una tormenta de arena ciega a las filas musulmanas","los mecanos toman los pozos detrás de sus líneas","los arqueros dejan su colina para tomar el botín","llegan tropas frescas de Taif al lado mecano"]}},{"id":"ISLAM-s09-06","day":786,"d":3,"q":"Under the Treaty of Hudaybiyyah as Sahih al-Bukhari records its terms, a young man of Mecca becomes Muslim and flees to Medina without his guardian's leave. What does the treaty require?","o":["Medina may keep him, since he is now a Muslim","Medina may keep him if it pays Quraysh a ransom","Medina must let him choose the city he lives in","Medina must send him back to Quraysh in Mecca"],"a":3,"es":{"q":"Según el Tratado de Hudaybiyya tal como Sahih al-Bujari registra sus términos, un joven de La Meca se hace musulmán y huye a Medina sin permiso de su tutor. ¿Qué exige el tratado?","o":["Medina puede quedárselo, porque ya es musulmán","Medina puede quedárselo si paga un rescate a Quraysh","Medina debe dejarle elegir la ciudad donde vivir","Medina debe devolverlo a Quraysh en La Meca"]}}],[{"id":"ISLAM-s10-01","day":805,"d":2,"q":"Sahih al-Bukhari tells that the Prophet ﷺ found Ali ibn Abi Talib asleep in the mosque, his side covered in dust, and woke him with a nickname that Ali loved best of all his names. what was it?","o":["Abu Hurayrah","Abu Dharr","Abu Turab","Abu Hafs"],"a":2,"es":{"q":"Sahih al-Bukhari cuenta que el Profeta ﷺ encontró a Ali ibn Abi Talib dormido en la mezquita, con el costado cubierto de polvo, y lo despertó con un apodo que Ali amaba más que todos sus nombres. ¿cuál era?","o":["Abu Hurayrah","Abu Dharr","Abu Turab","Abu Hafs"]}},{"id":"ISLAM-s10-02","day":828,"d":2,"q":"tradition holds that only one companion of the Prophet ﷺ is named in the Qur'an, in Surah Al-Ahzab (33:37). who is he?","o":["Zayd ibn Harithah","Usamah ibn Zayd","Bilal ibn Rabah","Mus'ab ibn Umayr"],"a":0,"es":{"q":"la tradición sostiene que solo un compañero del Profeta ﷺ aparece con su nombre en el Corán, en la sura Al-Ahzab (33:37). ¿quién es?","o":["Zayd ibn Harithah","Usamah ibn Zayd","Bilal ibn Rabah","Mus'ab ibn Umayr"]}},{"id":"ISLAM-s10-03","day":812,"d":3,"q":"in Sahih Muslim, Aisha reports that the Prophet ﷺ told his wives the one with the \"longest hand\" would be the first to join him after his death. what did the \"longest hand\" turn out to mean?","o":["the arm that was longest when they measured","the wife who was the eldest among them","the wife married to him the longest","the hand that gave most in charity"],"a":3,"es":{"q":"en Sahih Muslim, Aisha relata que el Profeta ﷺ les dijo a sus esposas que la de la \"mano más larga\" sería la primera en reunirse con él después de su muerte. ¿qué resultó significar la \"mano más larga\"?","o":["el brazo más largo cuando se midieron","la esposa de mayor edad entre ellas","la esposa casada con él por más tiempo","la mano que más daba en caridad"]}},{"id":"ISLAM-s10-04","day":820,"d":3,"q":"in Sahih al-Bukhari, the Prophet ﷺ says of his grandson al-Hasan: \"perhaps God will make peace through him between two great groups of Muslims.\" what event is this report linked to?","o":["his win over Mu'awiyah's army in open battle","his settlement with Mu'awiyah, giving up rule","his ending of the fighting at Siffin by arbitration","his reconciling of the Aws and Khazraj tribes"],"a":1,"es":{"q":"en Sahih al-Bukhari, el Profeta ﷺ dice de su nieto al-Hasan: \"quizá Dios haga la paz por medio de él entre dos grandes grupos de musulmanes\". ¿con qué hecho se relaciona este relato?","o":["su victoria sobre el ejército de Mu'awiyah en batalla","su acuerdo con Mu'awiyah, dejando el gobierno","su fin de la lucha en Siffin mediante un arbitraje","su reconciliación de las tribus de Aws y Jazrach"]}},{"id":"ISLAM-s10-05","day":852,"d":3,"q":"after the Tabuk expedition, Ka'b ibn Malik admitted to the Prophet ﷺ that he had no excuse for staying behind. how, according to his own account in Sahih al-Bukhari, was his case finally settled?","o":["he was forgiven that same day, like the others","he freed a slave as expiation and was pardoned","after fifty nights, a verse accepted his repentance","he rode after the army to Tabuk late and made up for it"],"a":2,"es":{"q":"después de la expedición de Tabuk, Ka'b ibn Malik le admitió al Profeta ﷺ que no tenía excusa por haberse quedado atrás. según su propio relato en Sahih al-Bukhari, ¿cómo se resolvió al final su caso?","o":["fue perdonado ese mismo día, como los demás","liberó a un esclavo como expiación y fue perdonado","tras cincuenta noches, un verso aceptó su arrepentimiento","salió tarde tras el ejército hacia Tabuk y así lo compensó"]}},{"id":"ISLAM-s10-06","day":875,"d":3,"q":"plague breaks out in the city where a merchant lives, and he wants to flee to a healthy town. by the hadith Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf quoted to Umar on the road to Syria (Sahih al-Bukhari), what should he do?","o":["stay where he is and not flee the land","leave quickly, from God's decree to God's decree","leave, as long as he goes to a land without it","go wherever he likes, since all is already decreed"],"a":0,"es":{"q":"estalla la peste en la ciudad donde vive un comerciante, y él quiere huir a un pueblo sano. según el hadiz que Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf le citó a Umar en el camino a Siria (Sahih al-Bukhari), ¿qué debe hacer?","o":["quedarse donde está y no huir de esa tierra","irse rápido, del decreto de Dios al decreto de Dios","irse, siempre que vaya a una tierra sin peste","ir adonde quiera, pues todo ya está decretado"]}}],[{"id":"ISLAM-s11-01","day":884,"d":3,"q":"after the Battle of Siffin, the Kharijites (khawarij, \"those who went out\") left Ali's camp crying \"no judgment but God's\" (la hukma illa lillah). what were they protesting?","o":["his march on Basra against Aisha, Talhah and Zubayr","his agreement to let men arbitrate with Mu'awiyah","his move of the seat of rule from Medina to Kufa","his refusal to hand over the killers of Uthman"],"a":1,"es":{"q":"después de la batalla de Siffin, los jariyíes (khawarij, \"los que salieron\") dejaron el campamento de Ali gritando \"no hay juicio sino el de Dios\" (la hukma illa lillah). ¿contra qué protestaban?","o":["su marcha a Basora contra Aisha, Talhah y Zubayr","su acuerdo de dejar que hombres arbitraran con Muawiya","su traslado de la sede del gobierno de Medina a Kufa","su negativa a entregar a los asesinos de Uthman"]}},{"id":"ISLAM-s11-02","day":891,"d":2,"q":"Husayn ibn Ali was killed at Karbala on a day already kept with a fast since the Prophet ﷺ came to Medina. which day of the Islamic calendar was it?","o":["the first day of Shawwal","the twelfth of Rabi al-Awwal","the tenth day of Muharram","the fifteenth of Sha'ban"],"a":2,"es":{"q":"Husayn ibn Ali murió en Karbala en un día que ya se guardaba con ayuno desde que el Profeta ﷺ llegó a Medina. ¿qué día del calendario islámico era?","o":["el primer día de Shawwal","el doce de Rabi al-Awwal","el décimo día de Muharram","el decimoquinto de Shaabán"]}},{"id":"ISLAM-s11-03","day":885,"d":3,"q":"a ruler claims a coat of armour (dir') that another man holds; his witnesses are his son and his freed servant. in the well-known report of Caliph Ali before the judge Shurayh, how was the case decided?","o":["for the other man, since the son's word for his father was refused","for the caliph, since a ruler's own word needs no further witness","by sending it up to the caliph's council for a final verdict","by splitting the disputed armour between the two men equally"],"a":0,"es":{"q":"un gobernante reclama una cota de malla (dir') que tiene otro hombre; sus testigos son su hijo y su sirviente liberto. en el conocido relato del califa Ali ante el juez Shurayh, ¿cómo se resolvió el caso?","o":["a favor del otro hombre: no se aceptó al hijo por su padre","a favor del califa, pues su palabra no necesita otro testigo","enviándolo al consejo del califa para un veredicto final","repartiendo la cota de malla en disputa entre los dos hombres"]}},{"id":"ISLAM-s11-04","day":925,"d":3,"q":"in his Book of Optics (Kitab al-Manazir), what did Ibn al-Haytham (Alhazen) of Cairo argue is how we come to see things?","o":["rays sent out from the eye reach the things it sees","thin copies shed by things travel into the eye","the eye's rays meet sunlight halfway to the thing","light from each point of a thing enters the eye"],"a":3,"es":{"q":"en su Libro de óptica (Kitab al-Manazir), ¿cómo dijo Ibn al-Haytham (Alhacén) de El Cairo que llegamos a ver las cosas?","o":["el ojo envía rayos que alcanzan las cosas que ve","copias finas que sueltan las cosas entran al ojo","los rayos del ojo se juntan con la luz del sol","la luz de cada punto de una cosa entra en el ojo"]}},{"id":"ISLAM-s11-05","day":940,"d":4,"q":"in his Decisive Treatise (Fasl al-Maqal), what does Ibn Rushd (Averroes) argue the religious law says about studying philosophy?","o":["it forbids it, as reasoning leads believers from faith","it permits it only to rulers and their court doctors","it commands it for those able to reason with rigor","it ignores it, as a matter wholly outside religion"],"a":2,"es":{"q":"en su Tratado decisivo (Fasl al-Maqal), ¿qué dice Ibn Rushd (Averroes) que manda la ley religiosa sobre el estudio de la filosofía?","o":["lo prohíbe, pues razonar aleja a los creyentes de la fe","lo permite solo a gobernantes y a sus médicos de corte","lo ordena a quienes son capaces de razonar con rigor","lo ignora, por ser un asunto del todo ajeno a la religión"]}},{"id":"ISLAM-s11-06","day":954,"d":2,"q":"which Sunni school of law, carried west from Medina and Kairouan, became the main legal tradition of North Africa and West Africa?","o":["the Hanafi school","the Maliki school","the Shafi'i school","the Hanbali school"],"a":1,"es":{"q":"¿qué escuela sunita de derecho, llevada al oeste desde Medina y Kairuán, se volvió la principal tradición legal del norte y el oeste de África?","o":["la escuela hanafí","la escuela malikí","la escuela shafií","la escuela hanbalí"]}}],[{"id":"ISLAM-s12-01","day":965,"d":3,"q":"Sahih al-Bukhari reports that Umar told Asma bint Umays, back from Abyssinia, that his emigration gave him more right to the Prophet ﷺ. what did the Prophet ﷺ answer about the people of the ship?","o":["they should go back to the Negus and settle in Abyssinia for good","they were to lead the first army sent across the sea into Africa","they had made two hijrahs, one to Abyssinia and one to Medina","they had lost their reward by leaving Mecca without his leave"],"a":2,"es":{"q":"Sahih al-Bujari relata que Umar le dijo a Asma bint Umais, recién llegada de Abisinia, que su emigración le daba más derecho al Profeta ﷺ. ¿qué respondió el Profeta ﷺ sobre la gente del barco?","o":["que debían volver con el Negus y quedarse en Abisinia para siempre","que iban a encabezar el primer ejército enviado por mar a África","que habían hecho dos hiyras, una a Abisinia y otra a Medina","que habían perdido su recompensa al salir de La Meca sin su permiso"]}},{"id":"ISLAM-s12-02","day":969,"d":2,"q":"Mansa Musa, king of Mali, passed through Cairo on his pilgrimage to Mecca in 1324. according to the historian al-Umari, what did his visit do to the city?","o":["the price of gold fell, since he spent and gave so freely","the grain ran short, since his caravan bought up the harvest","a plague broke out, brought in by his caravan's camels","a revolt broke out, since he refused the sultan's taxes"],"a":0,"es":{"q":"Mansa Musa, rey de Malí, pasó por El Cairo en su peregrinación a La Meca en 1324. según el historiador al-Umari, ¿qué le causó su visita a la ciudad?","o":["bajó el precio del oro, porque gastó y regaló con mucha generosidad","escaseó el grano, porque su caravana compró toda la cosecha","estalló una peste, traída por los camellos de su caravana","estalló una revuelta, porque se negó a pagar los impuestos del sultán"]}},{"id":"ISLAM-s12-03","day":978,"d":3,"q":"at the end of Farid al-Din Attar's Persian poem The Conference of the Birds (Mantiq al-Tayr), thirty birds reach their king, the Simorgh. what wordplay gives the ending its meaning?","o":["\"Simorgh\" is Persian for hoopoe, so their guide was the king all along","\"thirty birds\" in Persian is si morgh, so they see the Simorgh in themselves","\"thirty\" in Persian also means valley, so each bird had crossed its own valley","\"Simorgh\" is Persian for Solomon, so the king they find is the prophet"],"a":1,"es":{"q":"al final del poema persa de Farid al-Din Attar, La conferencia de los pájaros (Mantiq al-Tayr), treinta pájaros llegan ante su rey, el Simurg. ¿qué juego de palabras le da sentido al final?","o":["\"Simurg\" significa abubilla en persa, así que su guía era el rey","\"treinta pájaros\" en persa es si morgh, así que ven al Simurg en sí mismos","\"treinta\" también significa valle en persa, así que cada pájaro cruzó su valle","\"Simurg\" significa Salomón en persa, así que el rey que hallan es el profeta"]}},{"id":"ISLAM-s12-04","day":987,"d":3,"q":"why is the rise of the Safavid dynasty under Shah Isma'il I, from 1501, a turning point in the religious history of Iran?","o":["it brought Iran under Ottoman rule as a province of the sultan","it made Persian the language of the prayer in place of Arabic","it made Hanafi law the law of the state, just as in the Ottoman lands","it made Twelver Shi'ism the state faith, so Iran grew mostly Shia"],"a":3,"es":{"q":"¿por qué el ascenso de la dinastía safávida con el sha Ismail I, desde 1501, es un punto de giro en la historia religiosa de Irán?","o":["puso a Irán bajo el dominio otomano como provincia del sultán","hizo del persa el idioma de la oración en lugar del árabe","hizo de la escuela hanafí la ley del Estado, como en tierras otomanas","hizo del chiismo duodecimano la fe oficial, e Irán se volvió chiita"]}},{"id":"ISLAM-s12-05","day":1004,"d":2,"q":"which Arabic script, named after a city in Iraq, is angular, with straight strokes and sharp corners, and was used for early copies of the Qur'an and for carved inscriptions?","o":["the Naskh script","the Kufic script","the Thuluth script","the Diwani script"],"a":1,"es":{"q":"¿qué escritura árabe, que lleva el nombre de una ciudad de Irak, es angulosa, de trazos rectos y esquinas marcadas, y se usó en las primeras copias del Corán y en inscripciones talladas?","o":["la escritura naskh","la escritura cúfica","la escritura thuluth","la escritura diwani"]}},{"id":"ISLAM-s12-06","day":1013,"d":3,"q":"a woman in Cairo sets aside a row of shops so they can never be sold, and their rent pays a Qur'an teacher long after her death. in Islamic law, what is this arrangement called?","o":["a waqf, a property endowed for good","zakat, the obligatory alms paid each year","a hiba, a gift between living persons","a kaffarah, alms paid to atone for a fault"],"a":0,"es":{"q":"una mujer en El Cairo destina una fila de tiendas para que nunca puedan venderse, y su renta paga a un maestro de Corán mucho después de su muerte. en la ley islámica, ¿cómo se llama este arreglo?","o":["un waqf, un bien donado para el bien","el zakat, la limosna obligatoria anual","una hiba, un regalo entre personas vivas","una kaffarah, limosna para expiar una falta"]}}],[{"id":"ISLAM-s13-01","day":1078,"d":2,"q":"in the dawn call to prayer as recorded in Sunan Abu Dawud (500), which line is added after \"come to success\" (hayya ala al-falah)?","o":["glory be to my Lord, the Most High","there is no power except with God","prayer is better than sleep","the prayer has now been established"],"a":2,"es":{"q":"en el llamado a la oración del alba, tal como lo recoge el Sunan de Abu Dawud (500), ¿qué frase se añade después de \"vengan al éxito\" (hayya ala al-falah)?","o":["gloria a mi Señor, el Altísimo","no hay poder sino en Dios","la oración es mejor que el sueño","la oración ya se ha establecido"]}},{"id":"ISLAM-s13-02","day":1132,"d":3,"q":"in Jabir ibn Abdullah's account of the Prophet's ﷺ Hajj in Sahih Muslim, how does he pray maghrib and isha on reaching Muzdalifah?","o":["together, one call, nothing prayed between","each at its own time, with a full call for each","isha alone, since maghrib was prayed at Arafah","maghrib alone, with isha delayed until Mina"],"a":0,"es":{"q":"en el relato de Jabir ibn Abdullah sobre el Hajj del Profeta ﷺ, en Sahih Muslim, ¿cómo reza el maghrib y el isha al llegar a Muzdalifa?","o":["juntos, un solo llamado, nada rezado entre ellos","cada uno a su hora, con un llamado completo para cada uno","solo el isha, porque el maghrib se rezó en Arafat","solo el maghrib, y el isha se deja para Mina"]}},{"id":"ISLAM-s13-03","day":1126,"d":3,"q":"in Sahih al-Bukhari, Umar ibn al-Khattab kisses the Black Stone and says: \"I know you are a stone; you can neither harm nor help. If I had not seen the Prophet kiss you, I would not have kissed you.\" what is he making clear?","o":["the stone holds a blessing that heals whoever touches it","kissing the stone is a duty without which Hajj is void","the stone marks the place where Ibrahim first prayed","the kiss follows the Prophet ﷺ; the stone has no power"],"a":3,"es":{"q":"en Sahih al-Bujari, Umar ibn al-Jattab besa la Piedra Negra y dice: \"Sé que eres una piedra; no puedes dañar ni ayudar. Si no hubiera visto al Profeta besarte, no te habría besado\". ¿qué deja claro?","o":["la piedra tiene una bendición que sana a quien la toca","besar la piedra es un deber sin el cual el Hajj no vale","la piedra marca el lugar donde Ibrahim rezó por primera vez","el beso sigue al Profeta ﷺ; la piedra no tiene poder"]}},{"id":"ISLAM-s13-04","day":1120,"d":2,"q":"Qur'an 2:196 (Pickthall) says: \"Perform the pilgrimage and the visit (to Mecca) for Allah.\" what is the main difference in timing between the pilgrimage (Hajj) and the visit (umrah)?","o":["umrah is kept for Ramadan; Hajj may be made in any month","Hajj has set days in Dhul Hijjah; umrah may be made any time","umrah is for people of Mecca; Hajj is for those from afar","Hajj is made by night; umrah is made during the daylight hours"],"a":1,"es":{"q":"el Corán 2:196 dice: \"Realicen la peregrinación y la visita (a La Meca) por Dios\". ¿cuál es la principal diferencia de calendario entre la peregrinación (Hajj) y la visita (umrah)?","o":["la umrah se guarda para Ramadán; el Hajj puede hacerse en cualquier mes","el Hajj tiene días fijos en Dhul Hiyya; la umrah, cualquier día del año","la umrah es para la gente de La Meca; el Hajj para quienes vienen de lejos","el Hajj se hace de noche; la umrah, en cambio, durante las horas del día"]}},{"id":"ISLAM-s13-05","day":1134,"d":3,"q":"about the animals sacrificed at Hajj, Surah Al-Hajj (22:37, Pickthall) says: \"Their flesh and their blood reach not Allah, but the devotion from you reacheth Him.\" what does the verse teach?","o":["God accepts the offering by its devotion, not its meat","the meat must be burned whole so that its smoke rises to God","the blood must be poured out at the Ka'ba to count","only the pilgrims at Mina may offer such an animal"],"a":0,"es":{"q":"sobre los animales sacrificados en el Hajj, la sura Al-Hajj (22:37) dice: \"Ni su carne ni su sangre llegan a Dios, pero sí le llega la devoción de ustedes\". ¿qué enseña el verso?","o":["Dios acepta la ofrenda por su devoción, no por su carne","la carne debe quemarse entera para que su humo suba hasta Dios","la sangre debe derramarse en la Kaaba para que cuente","solo los peregrinos en Mina pueden ofrecer un animal así"]}},{"id":"ISLAM-s13-06","day":1110,"d":3,"q":"a Muslim who is fasting in Ramadan is insulted by a stranger in a long line. according to the hadith in Sahih al-Bukhari that calls the fast a shield, what should the person say?","o":["\"God forgive you\"","\"Allah is enough\"","\"Allah is greatest\"","\"I am fasting\""],"a":3,"es":{"q":"una persona musulmana que ayuna en Ramadán recibe un insulto de un desconocido en una fila larga. según el hadiz de Sahih al-Bujari que llama al ayuno un escudo, ¿qué debe decir?","o":["\"Dios te perdone\"","\"Dios me basta\"","\"Dios es el más grande\"","\"estoy ayunando\""]}}],[{"id":"ISLAM-s14-01","day":1145,"d":2,"q":"In the science of hadith, what is the isnad of a report?","o":["the grade a scholar gives the report","the chain of narrators who passed it on","the wording of what the Prophet ﷺ said","the book in which the report is recorded"],"a":1,"es":{"q":"En la ciencia del hadiz, ¿qué es el isnad de un relato?","o":["la calificación que un sabio le da al relato","la cadena de narradores que lo transmitieron","la redacción de lo que dijo el Profeta ﷺ","el libro en el que está registrado el relato"]}},{"id":"ISLAM-s14-02","day":1147,"d":4,"q":"In classical hadith science, what usually separates a hasan (good) hadith from a sahih (sound) one?","o":["its narrators' memory is a little less precise","its chain has one missing link along the way","it reaches us through only a single chain","its wording goes against a more reliable report"],"a":0,"es":{"q":"En la ciencia clásica del hadiz, ¿qué suele distinguir a un hadiz hasan (bueno) de uno sahih (sólido)?","o":["sus narradores tienen memoria algo menos precisa","a su cadena le falta un eslabón en el camino","nos llega por una sola cadena de narradores","su texto contradice un relato más confiable"]}},{"id":"ISLAM-s14-03","day":1157,"d":3,"q":"What is a hadith qudsi, a 'sacred report'?","o":["a Companion's own saying about the Prophet ﷺ","a report both Bukhari and Muslim graded sound","Allah's words as related by the Prophet ﷺ","a report traced to an imam of Ahl al-Bayt"],"a":2,"es":{"q":"¿Qué es un hadiz qudsi, un 'relato sagrado'?","o":["un dicho de un Compañero sobre el Profeta ﷺ","un relato que Bujari y Muslim calificaron sólido","palabras de Allah transmitidas por el Profeta ﷺ","un relato atribuido a un imán de Ahl al-Bayt"]}},{"id":"ISLAM-s14-04","day":1172,"d":4,"q":"The Qur'an (5:90) forbids khamr, wine. A Sunni jurist rules that a newly made drink is forbidden too, because it shares wine's effective cause: it intoxicates. Which source of law is he using?","o":["ijma', the agreement of the scholars","'urf, the custom of the local people","istihsan, a jurist's equitable choice","qiyas, analogy from a shared cause"],"a":3,"es":{"q":"El Corán (5:90) prohíbe el jamr, el vino. Un jurista sunita dictamina que una bebida nueva también está prohibida, porque comparte la causa efectiva del vino: embriaga. ¿Qué fuente del derecho está usando?","o":["el iyma', el acuerdo de los sabios","el 'urf, la costumbre de la gente local","el istihsan, una elección por equidad","el qiyas, la analogía por causa común"]}},{"id":"ISLAM-s14-05","day":1176,"d":3,"q":"In Sahih al-Bukhari, the Prophet ﷺ says he would have ordered the siwak (tooth-stick) at every prayer if it were not hard on his community. In which of the five rulings do jurists place the siwak?","o":["wajib, obligatory","mustahabb, recommended","mubah, simply permitted","makruh, disliked"],"a":1,"es":{"q":"En Sahih al-Bujari, el Profeta ﷺ dice que habría ordenado el siwak (palito para los dientes) en cada oración si no fuera difícil para su comunidad. ¿En cuál de los cinco dictámenes colocan los juristas el siwak?","o":["wayib, obligatorio","mustahabb, recomendado","mubah, solo permitido","makruh, desaconsejado"]}},{"id":"ISLAM-s14-06","day":1188,"d":4,"q":"In the Muwatta, why does Imam Malik sometimes leave aside a sound hadith that he himself records?","o":["its chain passed through narrators from Iraq","his teacher Abu Hanifa had ruled against it","the caliph in Baghdad had forbidden its use","Medina's inherited practice ran the other way"],"a":3,"es":{"q":"En el Muwatta, ¿por qué el imán Malik a veces deja de lado un hadiz sólido que él mismo registra?","o":["su cadena pasaba por narradores de Irak","su maestro Abu Hanifa había dictaminado en contra","el califa en Bagdad había prohibido aplicarlo","la práctica heredada de Medina iba al revés"]}}],[{"id":"ISLAM-s15-01","day":1243,"d":2,"q":"During the mihna, the Abbasid inquisition begun by the caliph al-Ma'mun, which scholar is remembered for refusing to declare that the Qur'an is created?","o":["Ahmad ibn Hanbal of Baghdad","Malik ibn Anas of Medina","Abu Hanifa al-Nu'man of Kufa","al-Layth ibn Sa'd of Egypt"],"a":0,"es":{"q":"Durante la mihna, la inquisición abasí iniciada por el califa al-Ma'mun, ¿qué erudito es recordado por negarse a declarar que el Corán es creado?","o":["Ahmad ibn Hanbal de Bagdad","Malik ibn Anas de Medina","Abu Hanifa al-Nu'man de Kufa","al-Layth ibn Sa'd de Egipto"]}},{"id":"ISLAM-s15-02","day":1244,"d":3,"q":"After Abu al-Hasan al-Ash'ari broke with his Mu'tazili teacher al-Jubba'i, what approach to theology did he take?","o":["he held that reason alone decides what is good or evil","he used kalam to defend the creed of the hadith folk","he kept their view that the Qur'an is created speech","he left theology to found a school of law in Basra"],"a":1,"es":{"q":"Después de que Abu al-Hasan al-Ash'ari rompió con su maestro mutazilí al-Jubba'i, ¿qué enfoque tomó en teología?","o":["sostuvo que solo la razón decide qué es bueno o malo","usó el kalam para defender el credo de la gente del hadiz","mantuvo la idea de ellos de que el Corán es palabra creada","dejó la teología para fundar una escuela de ley en Basora"]}},{"id":"ISLAM-s15-03","day":1260,"d":2,"q":"In the hadith of Sahih al-Bukhari about the Day of Resurrection, what is the sirat?","o":["a scale on which every person's deeds are weighed","a record of deeds placed in each person's hand","a bridge laid over the fire that all must cross","a pool where the Prophet gives his community drink"],"a":2,"es":{"q":"En el hadiz de Sahih al-Bukhari sobre el Día de la Resurrección, ¿qué es el sirat?","o":["una balanza donde se pesan las obras de cada persona","un registro de obras puesto en la mano de cada uno","un puente tendido sobre el fuego que todos deben cruzar","un estanque donde el Profeta da de beber a su comunidad"]}},{"id":"ISLAM-s15-04","day":1266,"d":2,"q":"A hadith in Sahih al-Bukhari says Allah made mercy in a hundred parts and sent one part down to the earth. What does it say comes from that one part?","o":["the help He gives the believers on the Last Day","the gifts given to the prophets alone to pass on","the pardon granted to those who repent in life","the mercy all creatures show to one another"],"a":3,"es":{"q":"Un hadiz de Sahih al-Bukhari dice que Allah hizo la misericordia en cien partes y envió una parte a la tierra. ¿Qué dice que viene de esa única parte?","o":["la ayuda que Él da a los creyentes en el Último Día","los dones dados solo a los profetas para repartir","el perdón concedido a quienes se arrepienten en vida","la misericordia que todas las criaturas se muestran"]}},{"id":"ISLAM-s15-05","day":1269,"d":3,"q":"Al-Ghazali's Ihya Ulum al-Din (Revival of the Religious Sciences) is arranged in four quarters of ten books each. What do its third and fourth quarters cover?","o":["the law of trade, then the law of inheritance","the history of prophets, then the lives of saints","what destroys the soul, then what saves it","proofs of the creed, then replies to philosophers"],"a":2,"es":{"q":"El Ihya Ulum al-Din (Revivificación de las ciencias religiosas) de al-Ghazali se divide en cuatro cuartos de diez libros cada uno. ¿Qué tratan su tercer y cuarto cuarto?","o":["la ley del comercio, luego la ley de herencias","la historia de los profetas, luego vidas de santos","lo que destruye el alma, luego lo que la salva","pruebas del credo, luego respuestas a los filósofos"]}},{"id":"ISLAM-s15-06","day":1294,"d":3,"q":"In Jami' al-Tirmidhi, al-Miqdam ibn Ma'dikarib reports the Prophet ﷺ on how much to eat. If someone at an ordinary meal must eat more than a few mouthfuls, what measure does the hadith give?","o":["eat until full, so long as no food is left to waste","a third food, a third drink, a third left for breath","eat a single meal a day, between noon and the afternoon","leave out drink so the whole stomach holds the food"],"a":1,"es":{"q":"En el Jami' de al-Tirmidhi, al-Miqdam ibn Ma'dikarib transmite lo que dijo el Profeta ﷺ sobre cuánto comer. Si en una comida común alguien debe comer más de unos bocados, ¿qué medida da el hadiz?","o":["comer hasta llenarse, sin dejar comida que se desperdicie","un tercio comida, un tercio bebida, un tercio para respirar","comer una sola vez al día, entre el mediodía y la tarde","no beber para que todo el estómago quede para la comida"]}}],[{"id":"ISLAM-s16-01","day":1341,"d":2,"q":"salat al-janazah, the Islamic funeral prayer, is prayed entirely standing. what does it leave out that the five daily prayers include?","o":["bowing (ruku') and prostration (sujud)","the opening takbir, \"Allahu akbar\"","standing in rows facing the qiblah","the closing greeting of peace, the taslim"],"a":0,"es":{"q":"salat al-janazah, la oración fúnebre islámica, se reza toda de pie. ¿qué deja fuera que sí tienen las cinco oraciones diarias?","o":["la inclinación (ruku') y la postración (suyud)","el takbir inicial, \"Allahu akbar\"","estar de pie en filas hacia la qibla","el saludo de paz que cierra la oración (taslim)"]}},{"id":"ISLAM-s16-02","day":1345,"d":2,"q":"in Sahih al-Bukhari, Anas tells that the Prophet ﷺ wept as his infant son Ibrahim was dying, and Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf asked, \"even you?\" what did the Prophet ﷺ answer?","o":["that tears show weak faith, so he asked God to forgive him for them","that tears are mercy, and the tongue says only what pleases God","that weeping is allowed for a small child but never for an adult","that loud wailing together is the proper way to honor the dead"],"a":1,"es":{"q":"en Sahih al-Bujari, Anas cuenta que el Profeta ﷺ lloró mientras su hijo pequeño Ibrahim moría, y Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf le preguntó: \"¿incluso tú?\". ¿qué respondió el Profeta ﷺ?","o":["que las lágrimas muestran poca fe, y le pidió a Dios que lo perdonara por ellas","que las lágrimas son misericordia, y la lengua dice solo lo que agrada a Dios","que llorar se permite por un niño, pero nunca por un adulto","que lamentarse a gritos en grupo es la forma correcta de honrar a los muertos"]}},{"id":"ISLAM-s16-03","day":1375,"d":3,"q":"the Isma'ilis, a branch of Shia Islam, take their name from Isma'il, through whom they trace their line of Imams. whose son was this Isma'il?","o":["Imam Musa al-Kazim","Imam Ali Zayn al-Abidin","Imam Ja'far al-Sadiq","Imam Muhammad al-Baqir"],"a":2,"es":{"q":"los ismailíes, una rama del islam chiita, toman su nombre de Ismail, por quien trazan su línea de imanes. ¿de quién era hijo este Ismail?","o":["el imán Musa al-Kazim","el imán Ali Zayn al-Abidin","el imán Yafar al-Sadiq","el imán Muhammad al-Baqir"]}},{"id":"ISLAM-s16-04","day":1388,"d":2,"q":"Surah al-Ma'idah 5:32 comes right after the story of Adam's two sons. what does it say about killing one human being unjustly?","o":["it is a grave sin only when the one killed is a believer","it weighs no more than any other sin a person commits","it is excused when done to defend one's own tribe or clan","it is as if the killer had slain all of mankind"],"a":3,"es":{"q":"la sura al-Maida 5:32 viene justo después del relato de los dos hijos de Adán. ¿qué dice sobre matar injustamente a un ser humano?","o":["es un pecado grave solo cuando el que muere es un creyente","no pesa más que cualquier otro pecado que alguien comete","se excusa cuando se hace para defender a la propia tribu","es como si el asesino hubiera matado a toda la humanidad"]}},{"id":"ISLAM-s16-05","day":1395,"d":4,"q":"in Sahih Muslim, the Prophet ﷺ speaks of a coming day \"as long as a year,\" and his companions ask whether one day's prayers will be enough for it. what does he answer?","o":["yes, the five prayers of one ordinary day are enough","no, they should stop praying until the sun sets again","no, they should estimate its measure and pray by that","yes, one prayer at noon is enough for that whole long day"],"a":2,"es":{"q":"en Sahih Muslim, el Profeta ﷺ habla de un día por venir \"tan largo como un año\", y sus compañeros preguntan si les bastarán las oraciones de un día. ¿qué responde?","o":["sí, bastan las cinco oraciones de un día normal","no, deben dejar de orar hasta que el sol se ponga otra vez","no, deben calcular su medida y orar según ella","sí, una oración al mediodía cubre todo ese día largo"]}},{"id":"ISLAM-s16-06","day":1397,"d":3,"q":"a Muslim worker fell into debt paying a hospital bill and cannot repay it. by the list of zakat recipients in Surah al-Tawbah (9:60), may zakat be given to him?","o":["no, zakat goes only to the poor who own nothing at all","yes, those in debt are among the groups the verse names","no, debtors may be helped only through voluntary charity","yes, but only if he is also a traveler far from home"],"a":1,"es":{"q":"un trabajador musulmán se endeudó para pagar una cuenta de hospital y no puede saldarla. según la lista de quienes reciben el zakat en la sura al-Tawba (9:60), ¿se le puede dar zakat?","o":["no, el zakat es solo para los pobres que no tienen nada","sí, los endeudados están entre los grupos que nombra el verso","no, a los endeudados solo se les ayuda con caridad voluntaria","sí, pero solo si además es un viajero que está lejos de su casa"]}}]],"JUDAISM":[[{"id":"JUDAISM-s00-01","day":1,"d":1,"q":"a mezuzah is the small case fixed to the doorpost of a Jewish home. what is written on the parchment scroll inside it?","o":["the names of the family who live in the house","Torah verses that begin with the Shema prayer","the priestly blessing from the book of Numbers","the mourner's Kaddish, written out in Aramaic"],"a":1,"es":{"q":"una mezuzá es el pequeño estuche fijado en el marco de la puerta de un hogar judío. ¿qué está escrito en el pergamino que lleva dentro?","o":["los nombres de la familia que vive en la casa","versículos de la Torá que comienzan con el Shemá","la bendición sacerdotal del libro de Números","el Kadish de los dolientes, escrito en arameo"]}},{"id":"JUDAISM-s00-02","day":2,"d":1,"q":"Shabbat, like every day in the Jewish calendar, begins at sundown rather than at midnight or dawn. what reason does the tradition give for this?","o":["the manna stopped falling each Friday at sunset","the Temple priests lit the menorah each evening","Genesis 1 counts days as evening, then morning","Israel left Egypt at night on the first Passover"],"a":2,"es":{"q":"el Shabat, como cada día del calendario judío, empieza al ponerse el sol, no a medianoche ni al amanecer. ¿qué razón da la tradición?","o":["el maná dejaba de caer cada viernes al atardecer","los sacerdotes del Templo encendían la menorá de noche","Génesis 1 cuenta cada día como tarde y luego mañana","Israel salió de Egipto de noche en la primera Pésaj"]}},{"id":"JUDAISM-s00-03","day":7,"d":2,"q":"in the Talmud (Eruvin 13b), a heavenly voice declares that the teachings of both the school of Hillel and the school of Shammai are \"the words of the living God.\" why, then, does the law follow Hillel?","o":["Hillel was the older teacher and reached Jerusalem first","Shammai's rulings were all later shown to be in error","a prophet of that generation ruled that Shammai had erred","Hillel's school was humble and taught Shammai's too"],"a":3,"es":{"q":"en el Talmud (Eruvín 13b), una voz del cielo declara que las enseñanzas de la escuela de Hilel y de la escuela de Shamai son \"palabras del Dios vivo\". entonces, ¿por qué la ley sigue a Hilel?","o":["Hilel era el maestro mayor y llegó primero a Jerusalén","las decisiones de Shamai se mostraron todas erradas","un profeta de esa generación dijo que Shamai se equivocaba","la escuela de Hilel era humilde y enseñaba también a Shamai"]}},{"id":"JUDAISM-s00-04","day":9,"d":2,"q":"in Genesis 32, after Jacob wrestles through the night with a mysterious figure and will not let go without a blessing, what new name is he given?","o":["Israel","Peniel","Edom","Ishmael"],"a":0,"es":{"q":"en Génesis 32, después de que Jacob lucha toda la noche con una figura misteriosa y no la suelta sin una bendición, ¿qué nombre nuevo recibe?","o":["Israel","Peniel","Edom","Ismael"]}},{"id":"JUDAISM-s00-05","day":10,"d":2,"q":"at Sinai the people answer \"na'aseh v'nishma,\" \"we will do and we will hear\" (Exodus 24:7). what does the Talmud (Shabbat 88a) praise in this answer?","o":["they asked to hear every law before agreeing to it","they pledged to do it before hearing it explained","the elders alone answered on behalf of the people","they promised obedience only for that generation"],"a":1,"es":{"q":"en el Sinaí el pueblo responde \"naasé venishmá\", \"haremos y escucharemos\" (Éxodo 24:7). ¿qué elogia el Talmud (Shabat 88a) en esa respuesta?","o":["pidieron escuchar cada ley antes de aceptarla","se comprometieron a hacer antes de oír la explicación","solo los ancianos respondieron en nombre del pueblo","prometieron obedecer solo durante esa generación"]}},{"id":"JUDAISM-s00-06","day":16,"d":2,"q":"a shop owner gives a struggling neighbor a steady job so that he no longer needs to ask anyone for help. on Maimonides' eight levels of tzedakah (Mishneh Torah, Gifts to the Poor 10:7), where does this stand?","o":["the lowest level, since the giver is known to him","the middle, below a gift given without names","the top level, as it makes him self-reliant","outside tzedakah, since the neighbor earns the pay"],"a":2,"es":{"q":"el dueño de una tienda le da a un vecino en apuros un trabajo estable, para que ya no tenga que pedir ayuda a nadie. en los ocho niveles de tzedaká de Maimónides (Mishné Torá, Dones a los pobres 10:7), ¿dónde se ubica esto?","o":["el nivel más bajo, porque él conoce a quien da","el medio, por debajo de un regalo sin nombres","el nivel más alto, porque lo vuelve autosuficiente","fuera de la tzedaká, porque el vecino gana su paga"]}}],[{"id":"JUDAISM-s01-01","day":24,"d":2,"q":"In Mishnah Sanhedrin 4:5, a human king stamps many coins with one seal and they all come out alike. What does the Mishnah say happens when God stamps every person with the seal of the first human, Adam?","o":["each person bears Adam's very face and form","the seal grows fainter with every generation","no single person is exactly like another","only the righteous keep the seal's likeness"],"a":2,"es":{"q":"En la Mishná Sanedrín 4:5, un rey humano acuña muchas monedas con un solo sello y todas salen iguales. ¿Qué dice la Mishná que pasa cuando Dios sella a cada persona con el sello del primer ser humano, Adán?","o":["cada persona lleva el mismo rostro y forma de Adán","el sello se va borrando con cada generación","ninguna persona es exactamente igual a otra","solo los justos conservan la imagen del sello"]}},{"id":"JUDAISM-s01-02","day":38,"d":2,"q":"In the midrash in Genesis Rabbah 38, young Abram smashes the idols in his father Terah's shop. When Terah asks what happened, what does Abram claim?","o":["a thief broke in and smashed them in the night","the biggest idol took a stick to the rest","a buyer knocked them down while choosing one","the ground shook and threw them off the shelf"],"a":1,"es":{"q":"En el midrash de Génesis Rabá 38, el joven Abram rompe los ídolos de la tienda de su padre Téraj. Cuando Téraj pregunta qué pasó, ¿qué afirma Abram?","o":["un ladrón entró y los rompió durante la noche","el ídolo mayor rompió a los demás con un palo","un comprador los tiró mientras escogía uno","la tierra tembló y los tiró del estante"]}},{"id":"JUDAISM-s01-03","day":58,"d":2,"q":"In Genesis 29, Leah names her fourth son with the words \"This time will I praise the LORD.\" Which son is it?","o":["Reuben","Simeon","Levi","Judah"],"a":3,"es":{"q":"En Génesis 29, Lea nombra a su cuarto hijo con las palabras \"Esta vez alabaré al SEÑOR\". ¿Qué hijo es?","o":["Rubén","Simeón","Leví","Judá"]}},{"id":"JUDAISM-s01-04","day":86,"d":4,"q":"The Torah says God hardened Pharaoh's heart during the plagues. How does Maimonides, in his Laws of Repentance (6:3), explain this?","o":["Pharaoh sinned freely so much that the way to repent was closed to him","Pharaoh never chose at all, since his part was fixed before his birth","the hardening tested the trust of Moses and was no judgment on Pharaoh","Pharaoh's own advisers hardened him against what he truly wanted"],"a":0,"es":{"q":"La Torá dice que Dios endureció el corazón del faraón durante las plagas. ¿Cómo lo explica Maimónides en sus Leyes del Arrepentimiento (6:3)?","o":["el faraón pecó libremente tanto que se le cerró el camino del arrepentimiento","el faraón nunca eligió nada, pues su papel estaba fijado antes de nacer","el endurecimiento probaba la confianza de Moisés y no juzgaba al faraón","los propios consejeros del faraón lo endurecieron contra lo que él quería"]}},{"id":"JUDAISM-s01-05","day":90,"d":3,"q":"According to the Talmud (Megillah 10b), God stops the ministering angels from singing as the Egyptians drown in the sea. What reason does God give?","o":["heaven's songs are kept for the Sabbath and festivals","the drowning Egyptians are the work of God's hands","the angels had played no part in parting the sea","only a prophet may sing of a rescue God has worked"],"a":1,"es":{"q":"Según el Talmud (Meguilá 10b), Dios impide que los ángeles servidores canten mientras los egipcios se ahogan en el mar. ¿Qué razón da Dios?","o":["los cantos del cielo se guardan para el Shabat y las fiestas","los egipcios que se ahogan son obra de las manos de Dios","los ángeles no tuvieron parte en la división del mar","solo un profeta puede cantar un rescate obrado por Dios"]}},{"id":"JUDAISM-s01-06","day":93,"d":3,"q":"A community leader hears every dispute personally, from morning to evening, and is worn out. Following Jethro's advice to Moses in Exodus 18, what should the leader do?","o":["set able, honest people over smaller groups and keep the hard cases","hand the whole task to the priests and stop hearing any cases at all","hear disputes only on fixed days and send everyone else away unheard","let each side in a dispute pick its own judge from its own family"],"a":0,"es":{"q":"Un líder de una comunidad escucha él mismo cada disputa, de la mañana a la noche, y está agotado. Siguiendo el consejo de Jetró a Moisés en Éxodo 18, ¿qué debería hacer ese líder?","o":["poner a gente capaz y honesta sobre grupos menores y quedarse con lo difícil","pasarles toda la tarea a los sacerdotes y dejar de escuchar casos por completo","escuchar disputas solo en días fijos y despedir a los demás sin oírlos","dejar que cada parte de una disputa elija a su propio juez entre su familia"]}}],[{"id":"JUDAISM-s02-01","day":108,"d":2,"q":"Havdalah, said on Saturday night as Shabbat ends, has a blessing over wine and blessings over two other things before the closing blessing of separation. what are those two things?","o":["two braided loaves and a dish of salt","fragrant spices and a candle's flame","bitter herbs and a roasted shank bone","a ram's horn and a cup of fresh water"],"a":1,"es":{"q":"la Havdalá, que se dice el sábado en la noche cuando termina el Shabat, tiene una bendición sobre el vino y bendiciones sobre otras dos cosas antes de la bendición final de separación. ¿cuáles son esas dos cosas?","o":["dos panes trenzados y un plato de sal","especias aromáticas y la llama de una vela","hierbas amargas y un hueso asado de cordero","un cuerno de carnero y un vaso de agua fresca"]}},{"id":"JUDAISM-s02-02","day":131,"d":2,"q":"the Talmud (Shabbat 21b) records a dispute about lighting the Hanukkah lights over eight nights. what did the House of Hillel say, the view Jewish practice follows?","o":["one light the first night, one more each night","eight lights the first night, one fewer each night","eight lights on every one of the eight nights","seven lights each night, as on the Temple lamp"],"a":0,"es":{"q":"el Talmud (Shabat 21b) recoge una discusión sobre cómo encender las luces de Janucá durante ocho noches. ¿qué dijo la escuela de Hillel, la opinión que sigue la práctica judía?","o":["una luz la primera noche, una más cada noche","ocho luces la primera noche, una menos cada noche","ocho luces en cada una de las ocho noches","siete luces cada noche, como en la lámpara del Templo"]}},{"id":"JUDAISM-s02-03","day":105,"d":2,"q":"Mishnah Shabbat 7:2 lists thirty-nine main kinds of work (melachot) not done on Shabbat. in the Talmud's best-known explanation (Shabbat 49b), what do these categories correspond to?","o":["the tasks the Israelites did as slaves in Egypt","the labors placed on Adam after leaving Eden","the work of building the Tabernacle (mishkan)","the farm work set aside in the sabbatical year"],"a":2,"es":{"q":"la Mishná Shabat 7:2 enumera treinta y nueve tipos principales de trabajo (melajot) que no se hacen en Shabat. según la explicación más conocida del Talmud (Shabat 49b), ¿a qué corresponden esas categorías?","o":["a las tareas de los israelitas como esclavos en Egipto","a los trabajos impuestos a Adán al salir del Edén","al trabajo de construir el Tabernáculo (mishkán)","a las labores del campo suspendidas en el año sabático"]}},{"id":"JUDAISM-s02-04","day":115,"d":2,"q":"among the Jewish blessings over food, why does Birkat Hamazon, the blessing after a meal with bread, hold a special place in Jewish law?","o":["it is said only on Shabbat and on festivals","it takes the place of the blessing before eating","it may be said only with a quorum of ten people","its duty comes from the Torah, not the rabbis"],"a":3,"es":{"q":"entre las bendiciones judías sobre la comida, ¿por qué Birkat Hamazón, la bendición después de una comida con pan, tiene un lugar especial en la ley judía?","o":["se dice solo en Shabat y en las festividades","reemplaza a la bendición de antes de comer","solo se puede decir con un quórum de diez","su deber viene de la Torá, no de los rabinos"]}},{"id":"JUDAISM-s02-05","day":146,"d":2,"q":"the Torah says \"you shall not boil a kid in its mother's milk\" three times (Exodus 23:19 and 34:26; Deuteronomy 14:21). how does the Talmud (Chullin 115b) read the three mentions?","o":["as three bans: on cooking, eating and benefiting","as one ban each for goats, sheep and cattle","as a ban for each of the three pilgrim festivals","as one ban each for weekdays, Shabbat and feasts"],"a":0,"es":{"q":"la Torá dice \"no cocerás el cabrito en la leche de su madre\" tres veces (Éxodo 23:19 y 34:26; Deuteronomio 14:21). ¿cómo lee el Talmud (Julín 115b) las tres menciones?","o":["como tres prohibiciones: cocinar, comer y beneficiarse","como una prohibición para cabras, ovejas y vacas","como una prohibición por cada fiesta de peregrinación","como una para días comunes, Shabat y fiestas"]}},{"id":"JUDAISM-s02-06","day":113,"d":2,"q":"someone is about to eat a fresh pear. by the categories of Mishnah Berakhot 6:1, which blessing is set for it?","o":["borei pri ha'adamah, who creates fruit of the ground","borei pri hagafen, who creates the fruit of the vine","borei pri ha'etz, who creates the fruit of the tree","hamotzi lechem, who brings forth bread from the earth"],"a":2,"es":{"q":"alguien está por comer una pera fresca. según las categorías de la Mishná Berajot 6:1, ¿qué bendición le corresponde?","o":["boré pri haadamá, que crea el fruto de la tierra","boré pri haguefen, que crea el fruto de la vid","boré pri haetz, que crea el fruto del árbol","hamotzí léjem, que saca el pan de la tierra"]}}],[{"id":"JUDAISM-s03-01","day":158,"d":2,"q":"Jewish communities read the Torah aloud in weekly portions through the year. on which festival do they finish Deuteronomy and begin Genesis again?","o":["Shavuot, the feast of weeks","Rosh Hashanah, the new year","Simchat Torah, after Sukkot","Passover, the spring festival"],"a":2,"es":{"q":"las comunidades judías leen la Torá en voz alta en porciones semanales a lo largo del año. ¿en qué festividad terminan el Deuteronomio y vuelven a empezar el Génesis?","o":["Shavuot, la fiesta de las semanas","Rosh Hashaná, el año nuevo","Simjat Torá, al final de Sucot","Pésaj, la fiesta de primavera"]}},{"id":"JUDAISM-s03-02","day":163,"d":2,"q":"the Mishnah (Sanhedrin 4:5) explains why God first created a single human being. what does it teach about one life?","o":["a single life matters less than the welfare of the many","a life is worth what its deeds earn in the world to come","the life of a firstborn outweighs that of later children","to destroy one life is like destroying a whole world"],"a":3,"es":{"q":"la Mishná (Sanedrín 4:5) explica por qué Dios creó primero a un solo ser humano. ¿qué enseña sobre una sola vida?","o":["una sola vida importa menos que el bienestar de muchos","una vida vale lo que sus actos ganan en el mundo venidero","la vida del primogénito pesa más que la de los demás hijos","destruir una vida es como destruir un mundo entero"]}},{"id":"JUDAISM-s03-03","day":176,"d":3,"q":"the Talmud (Sotah 14a) teaches people to walk in God's ways by copying God's deeds in the Torah. by that teaching, someone who comforts a family sitting shiva is imitating which deed?","o":["God visiting Abraham after his circumcision","God clothing Adam and Eve in garments of skin","God burying Moses in a valley in Moab","God blessing Isaac after Abraham died"],"a":3,"es":{"q":"el Talmud (Sotá 14a) enseña a andar en los caminos de Dios imitando lo que Dios hace en la Torá. según esa enseñanza, quien consuela a una familia que guarda shivá imita ¿cuál de estos actos?","o":["Dios visita a Abraham tras su circuncisión","Dios viste a Adán y Eva con túnicas de piel","Dios entierra a Moisés en un valle de Moab","Dios bendice a Isaac tras morir Abraham"]}},{"id":"JUDAISM-s03-04","day":192,"d":2,"q":"in Genesis, Jacob says \"Surely the LORD is in this place; and I knew it not.\" when does he say it?","o":["on waking from a dream of a ladder to heaven","after wrestling with a stranger by the Jabbok","on meeting a camp of angels at Mahanaim","at the well where he first met Rachel"],"a":0,"es":{"q":"en el Génesis, Jacob dice: \"Ciertamente el Señor está en este lugar, y yo no lo sabía\". ¿cuándo lo dice?","o":["al despertar de un sueño con una escalera al cielo","tras luchar con un desconocido junto al Jaboc","al ver un campamento de ángeles en Majanáyim","en el pozo donde conoció por primera vez a Raquel"]}},{"id":"JUDAISM-s03-05","day":220,"d":2,"q":"after Jacob dies, Joseph's brothers fear he will take revenge. what is Joseph's answer in Genesis 50:19–21?","o":["he will judge them once their father is buried","he will forgive them if they serve as his slaves","he is not in God's place; God meant it for good","he leaves their punishment to Pharaoh's courts"],"a":2,"es":{"q":"cuando muere Jacob, los hermanos de José temen que él se vengue. ¿qué les responde José en Génesis 50:19–21?","o":["los juzgará cuando hayan enterrado a su padre","los perdonará si se quedan como sus esclavos","no está en lugar de Dios, que lo encaminó al bien","deja su castigo en manos de las cortes del faraón"]}},{"id":"JUDAISM-s03-06","day":228,"d":3,"q":"according to Rashi on Exodus 7:19, why does Aaron, not Moses, strike the Nile to start the plague of blood?","o":["Moses was slow of speech and could not give the command","the river had once protected Moses when he was a baby","Aaron was the elder brother, so he had to act first","Pharaoh's magicians had taken Moses' staff from him"],"a":1,"es":{"q":"según Rashi sobre Éxodo 7:19, ¿por qué es Aarón, y no Moisés, quien golpea el Nilo para empezar la plaga de sangre?","o":["Moisés era torpe de palabra y no podía dar la orden","el río había protegido a Moisés cuando era un bebé","Aarón era el hermano mayor, así que debía actuar primero","los magos del faraón le habían quitado la vara a Moisés"]}}],[{"id":"JUDAISM-s04-01","day":235,"d":3,"q":"in Pirkei Avot (1:2), Simon the Just (Shimon HaTzaddik) says the world stands on three things. which three?","o":["justice, truth, and peace among people","repentance, prayer, and giving to the poor","Torah, worship, and acts of loving-kindness","study, the Sabbath, and the holy land of Israel"],"a":2,"es":{"q":"en Pirkei Avot (1:2), Simón el Justo (Shimon HaTzaddik) dice que el mundo se sostiene sobre tres cosas. ¿cuáles son?","o":["la justicia, la verdad y la paz entre las personas","el arrepentimiento, la oración y dar a los pobres","la Torá, el culto y los actos de bondad amorosa","el estudio, el Shabat y la tierra santa de Israel"]}},{"id":"JUDAISM-s04-02","day":264,"d":3,"q":"Rabbi Tarfon says in Pirkei Avot (2:16): \"it is not upon you to finish the work, but you are not free to desist from it.\" what does the saying teach?","o":["each person must keep at the work, though none will finish it","the work counts only once a person has completed it from beginning to end","a person may set the work down once a fair share of it has been done","the work belongs to the sages alone, so others may leave it to them"],"a":0,"es":{"q":"Rabí Tarfón dice en Pirkei Avot (2:16): \"no te corresponde terminar la obra, pero tampoco eres libre de abandonarla\". ¿qué enseña ese dicho?","o":["cada persona debe seguir con la obra, aunque no la termine","la obra solo cuenta cuando una persona la ha completado de principio a fin","una persona puede dejar la obra cuando ya hizo una parte justa de ella","la obra es solo de los sabios, así que los demás pueden dejársela a ellos"]}},{"id":"JUDAISM-s04-03","day":280,"d":3,"q":"in the Talmud's story of the oven of Akhnai (Bava Metzia 59b), Rabbi Yehoshua answers a heavenly voice that sides with Rabbi Eliezer by quoting \"it is not in heaven\" (Deuteronomy 30:12). what does he mean?","o":["the voice came from a spirit, so it carried no authority in the matter","the Torah was given at Sinai; now the sages' majority decides its law","the question about the oven was too small for heaven to rule on it","miracles may settle the law, but only when a prophet is there to confirm them"],"a":1,"es":{"q":"en el relato talmúdico del horno de Ajnai (Bava Metzia 59b), Rabí Yehoshúa responde a una voz celestial que apoya a Rabí Eliezer citando \"no está en el cielo\" (Deuteronomio 30:12). ¿qué quiere decir?","o":["la voz venía de un espíritu, así que no tenía autoridad en el asunto","la Torá se dio en el Sinaí; ahora su ley la decide la mayoría de sabios","la pregunta sobre el horno era muy pequeña para que el cielo la decidiera","los milagros pueden fijar la ley, pero solo si un profeta los confirma"]}},{"id":"JUDAISM-s04-04","day":282,"d":3,"q":"in a study session, a student lays out her opponent's view fully and fairly before giving her own. according to the Talmud (Eruvin 13b), this mirrors the reason the law follows which school?","o":["Shammai's school, because its scholars were sharper","Hillel's school, because they cited Shammai's view first","Shammai's school, because it ruled more strictly","Hillel's school, because they outnumbered Shammai's"],"a":1,"es":{"q":"en una sesión de estudio, una estudiante expone la opinión de su oponente de forma completa y justa antes de dar la suya. según el Talmud (Eruvin 13b), ¿esto refleja la razón por la que la ley sigue a qué escuela?","o":["la Escuela de Shamai, porque sus sabios eran más agudos","la Escuela de Hilel, porque citaban primero a Shamai","la Escuela de Shamai, porque fallaba con más rigor","la Escuela de Hilel, porque eran más que los de Shamai"]}},{"id":"JUDAISM-s04-05","day":289,"d":3,"q":"during the Roman siege of Jerusalem, Rabban Yochanan ben Zakkai is carried out of the city and asks the Roman general for \"Yavneh and its sages\" (Gittin 56b). why is that request remembered as a turning point?","o":["it moved the Temple's sacrifices to a new altar standing at Yavneh","it secured a safe road for the city's people to leave the siege","it kept Torah study and its teachers alive after the Temple fell","it won the Romans' promise to rebuild the Temple once the war ended"],"a":2,"es":{"q":"durante el sitio romano de Jerusalén, Rabán Yojanán ben Zakai es sacado de la ciudad y le pide al general romano \"Yavne y sus sabios\" (Guitín 56b). ¿por qué se recuerda ese pedido como un momento decisivo?","o":["trasladó los sacrificios del Templo a un nuevo altar en Yavne","consiguió un camino seguro para que el pueblo saliera del sitio","mantuvo vivos el estudio de la Torá y sus maestros tras el Templo","obtuvo la promesa romana de reconstruir el Templo al terminar la guerra"]}},{"id":"JUDAISM-s04-06","day":302,"d":3,"q":"which Hasidic master taught, in words later set to a well-known song, that \"the whole world is a very narrow bridge, and the main thing is not to be afraid at all\"?","o":["Israel, the Baal Shem Tov","Dov Ber, the Maggid of Mezritch","Zusya, the rebbe of Hanipol","Nachman, the rebbe of Breslov"],"a":3,"es":{"q":"¿qué maestro jasídico enseñó, con palabras que luego se volvieron una canción muy conocida, que \"el mundo entero es un puente muy angosto, y lo principal es no tener miedo en absoluto\"?","o":["Israel, el Baal Shem Tov","Dov Ber, el Maguid de Mezritch","Zusia, el rebe de Anipoli","Najman, el rebe de Breslov"]}}],[{"id":"JUDAISM-s05-01","day":342,"d":3,"q":"in Exodus 17, during the battle with Amalek at Rephidim, Moses' hands grow heavy as he holds them up. which two men hold up his hands until sunset?","o":["Nadav and Avihu","Joshua and Caleb","Aaron and Hur","Eldad and Medad"],"a":2,"es":{"q":"en Éxodo 17, durante la batalla contra Amalec en Refidim, a Moisés se le cansan las manos de tenerlas en alto. ¿qué dos hombres le sostienen las manos hasta la puesta del sol?","o":["Nadab y Abiú","Josué y Caleb","Aarón y Jur","Eldad y Medad"]}},{"id":"JUDAISM-s05-02","day":417,"d":3,"q":"Leviticus 23:15–16 commands counting seven full weeks, fifty days, from the day the omer, the first sheaf of the new harvest, is brought. which festival falls on the fiftieth day?","o":["Passover, the festival of matzah","Shavuot, the festival of weeks","Sukkot, the festival of booths","Rosh Hashanah, the new year"],"a":1,"es":{"q":"Levítico 23:15–16 manda contar siete semanas completas, cincuenta días, desde el día en que se trae el ómer, la primera gavilla de la nueva cosecha. ¿qué fiesta cae el día cincuenta?","o":["Pésaj, la fiesta del pan ázimo","Shavuot, la fiesta de las semanas","Sucot, la fiesta de las cabañas","Rosh Hashaná, el año nuevo"]}},{"id":"JUDAISM-s05-03","day":352,"d":3,"q":"at Sinai the people answer \"na'aseh v'nishma,\" \"we will do and we will hear\" (Exodus 24:7). in the Talmud (Shabbat 88a), what is praised in the order of those words?","o":["insisting on hearing every law before agreeing to it","agreeing to keep only the laws that were explained","promising to keep the laws once they reached the land","pledging to do before they had heard and understood"],"a":3,"es":{"q":"en el Sinaí el pueblo responde \"naasé venishmá\", \"haremos y escucharemos\" (Éxodo 24:7). en el Talmud (Shabat 88a), ¿qué se elogia en el orden de esas palabras?","o":["exigir escuchar cada ley antes de aceptarla","aceptar cumplir solo las leyes que se explicaron","prometer cumplir las leyes al llegar a la tierra","comprometerse a hacer antes de oír y entender"]}},{"id":"JUDAISM-s05-04","day":408,"d":3,"q":"according to the Mishnah (Yoma 8:9), when one person has wronged another, what does Yom Kippur do for that wrong?","o":["it atones fully, as long as the wrongdoer fasts all day","it atones only once the wrongdoer has made peace with them","it atones once the wrong is confessed aloud in the synagogue","it atones once charity is given in the wronged person's name"],"a":1,"es":{"q":"según la Mishná (Yomá 8:9), cuando una persona le ha hecho daño a otra, ¿qué hace Yom Kipur por esa falta?","o":["la expía del todo, si quien la cometió ayuna todo el día","la expía solo si quien la cometió se reconcilió con el otro","la expía cuando la falta se confiesa en voz alta en la sinagoga","la expía cuando se da caridad a nombre de la persona dañada"]}},{"id":"JUDAISM-s05-05","day":424,"d":3,"q":"in Maimonides' eight levels of giving to the poor (Mishneh Torah, Gifts to the Poor 10:7–14), what is the highest level?","o":["giving so that neither giver nor receiver knows the other","giving the largest sum one can afford, gladly and at once","a gift, loan, partnership or job that makes them self-reliant","giving before being asked, straight into the poor person's hand"],"a":2,"es":{"q":"en los ocho niveles de dar a los pobres de Maimónides (Mishné Torá, Leyes de los dones a los pobres 10:7–14), ¿cuál es el nivel más alto?","o":["dar sin que quien da ni quien recibe sepan uno del otro","dar la suma más grande posible, con alegría y en el acto","un regalo, préstamo, sociedad o empleo que lo haga autónomo","dar antes de que te pidan, directamente en la mano del pobre"]}},{"id":"JUDAISM-s05-06","day":412,"d":3,"q":"a financial adviser steers a client who trusts him into an investment that earns the adviser a fee but is bad for the client. in the rabbinic reading of Leviticus 19 (the Sifra, followed by Rashi), which commandment does this break?","o":["do not put a stumbling block before the blind","do not stand idly by the blood of your neighbor","do not reap the corners of your field fully","do not take vengeance or bear any grudge"],"a":0,"es":{"q":"un asesor financiero lleva a un cliente que confía en él a una inversión que le deja una comisión al asesor pero que es mala para el cliente. en la lectura rabínica de Levítico 19 (el Sifra, seguido por Rashi), ¿qué mandamiento rompe?","o":["no pongas tropiezo delante del ciego","no te quedes quieto ante la sangre de tu prójimo","no siegues del todo las esquinas de tu campo","no te vengues ni guardes rencor alguno"]}}],[{"id":"JUDAISM-s06-01","day":445,"d":2,"q":"in Numbers 12:13, Moses prays a five-word prayer, \"El na, r'fa na lah\" (\"heal her now, O God\"). for whom is he praying?","o":["his sister Miriam","his wife Zipporah","his mother Jochebed","Pharaoh's daughter"],"a":0,"es":{"q":"en Números 12:13, Moisés hace una oración de cinco palabras, \"El na, r'fa na lah\" (\"sánala ahora, oh Dios\"). ¿por quién está orando?","o":["por su hermana Miriam","por su esposa Séfora","por su madre Jocabed","por la hija del faraón"]}},{"id":"JUDAISM-s06-02","day":478,"d":3,"q":"under Numbers 35, a person who killed someone by accident lives in a city of refuge (ir miklat). until when must that person stay there?","o":["until the next Jubilee year is proclaimed","for seven years, one full sabbatical cycle","until the high priest of that time dies","until the victim's family forgives them"],"a":2,"es":{"q":"según Números 35, quien mató a alguien por accidente vive en una ciudad de refugio (ir miklat). ¿hasta cuándo debe quedarse allí?","o":["hasta que se proclame el próximo jubileo","siete años, un ciclo sabático completo","hasta que muera el sumo sacerdote de entonces","hasta que la familia de la víctima lo perdone"]}},{"id":"JUDAISM-s06-03","day":458,"d":3,"q":"at the waters of Meribah (Numbers 20:7–12), Moses learns he will not lead the people into the land. according to Rashi, what was his sin?","o":["he went to the rock before gathering the people","he struck the rock when told to speak to it","he gave water to the people but not the cattle","he prayed for water before the people asked"],"a":1,"es":{"q":"junto a las aguas de Meribá (Números 20:7–12), Moisés sabe que no llevará al pueblo a la tierra. según Rashi, ¿cuál fue su pecado?","o":["fue a la roca antes de reunir al pueblo","golpeó la roca cuando debía hablarle","dio agua al pueblo pero no al ganado","pidió agua antes de que el pueblo la pidiera"]}},{"id":"JUDAISM-s06-04","day":448,"d":3,"q":"in Numbers 14:24, God says that Caleb, one of the twelve scouts, will enter the land of Canaan. what reason does the verse give?","o":["he was of priestly descent, from Aaron's family","he had led Israel in the battle with Amalek","he carried back the great cluster of grapes","he had another spirit and followed God fully"],"a":3,"es":{"q":"en Números 14:24, Dios dice que Caleb, uno de los doce exploradores, entrará en la tierra de Canaán. ¿qué razón da el versículo?","o":["era de linaje sacerdotal, de la familia de Aarón","había guiado a Israel en la batalla contra Amalec","trajo de vuelta el gran racimo de uvas","tenía otro espíritu y siguió a Dios por completo"]}},{"id":"JUDAISM-s06-05","day":489,"d":4,"q":"Mishnah Berakhot 9:5 notes that \"with all thy heart\" in Deuteronomy 6:5 spells heart as levavcha, with a doubled letter. what does it learn from this?","o":["love God in this world and in the world to come","love God with both your good and evil urges","love God with both your mind and your body","love God in the morning and in the evening"],"a":1,"es":{"q":"la Mishná Berajot 9:5 señala que \"con todo tu corazón\" en Deuteronomio 6:5 escribe corazón como levavjá, con una letra doble. ¿qué aprende de esto?","o":["amar a Dios en este mundo y en el mundo por venir","amar a Dios con tus impulsos buenos y malos","amar a Dios con tu mente y con tu cuerpo","amar a Dios en la mañana y en la noche"]}},{"id":"JUDAISM-s06-06","day":467,"d":3,"q":"a man dies leaving a daughter and no sons. under the law given after the daughters of Zelophehad spoke (Numbers 27:8–11), who inherits his land?","o":["his daughter, ahead of any of his kin","his brothers, as next in the family line","his father's brothers, as clan elders","his nearest kinsman, to keep the land"],"a":0,"es":{"q":"un hombre muere y deja una hija y ningún hijo varón. según la ley dada después de que hablaran las hijas de Zelofehad (Números 27:8–11), ¿quién hereda su tierra?","o":["su hija, antes que cualquier pariente","sus hermanos, como siguientes en la familia","los hermanos de su padre, como jefes del clan","su pariente más cercano, para guardar la tierra"]}}],[{"id":"JUDAISM-s07-01","day":539,"d":2,"q":"in the Talmud (Berakhot 26b), Rabbi Yose son of Rabbi Hanina says the patriarchs set the three daily prayers. which patriarch set the afternoon prayer, Minchah?","o":["Abraham","Isaac","Jacob","Moses"],"a":1,"es":{"q":"en el Talmud (Berajot 26b), el rabino Yosé hijo del rabino Janina dice que los patriarcas establecieron las tres oraciones diarias. ¿qué patriarca estableció la oración de la tarde, Minjá?","o":["Abraham","Isaac","Jacob","Moisés"]}},{"id":"JUDAISM-s07-02","day":557,"d":3,"q":"Psalm 145, said daily as Ashrei, runs through the Hebrew alphabet one verse per letter. in the traditional Hebrew text, which letter has no verse?","o":["aleph","samech","tav","nun"],"a":3,"es":{"q":"el Salmo 145, que se dice cada día como Ashrei, recorre el alfabeto hebreo con un verso por letra. en el texto hebreo tradicional, ¿qué letra no tiene verso?","o":["álef","sámej","tav","nun"]}},{"id":"JUDAISM-s07-03","day":567,"d":4,"q":"after the first line of the Shema comes \"baruch shem kevod malchuto le'olam va'ed\" (blessed be the name of His glorious kingdom forever). why, according to the Talmud (Pesachim 56a), is it said quietly?","o":["Jacob said it, but Moses did not write it in the Torah","it is a later poem added by the medieval prayer books","it was sung only by the Levites in the Temple service","it names God in a way that only the high priest may say"],"a":0,"es":{"q":"después de la primera línea del Shemá viene \"baruj shem kevod maljutó leolam vaed\" (bendito sea el nombre de Su glorioso reino por siempre). según el Talmud (Pesajim 56a), ¿por qué se dice en voz baja?","o":["Jacob la dijo, pero Moisés no la escribió en la Torá","es un poema tardío que añadieron los libros de rezo medievales","solo la cantaban los levitas en el servicio del Templo","nombra a Dios de un modo que solo el sumo sacerdote puede decir"]}},{"id":"JUDAISM-s07-04","day":576,"d":3,"q":"Hannah prayed at Shiloh: \"only her lips moved, but her voice could not be heard\" (1 Samuel 1:13). what does the Talmud (Berakhot 31a) learn from this for the Amidah?","o":["pray in the heart alone, keeping the lips still","say it aloud, so the priest can answer amen","form the words with the lips, but too softly to hear","pray it only at a sanctuary, as Hannah did at Shiloh"],"a":2,"es":{"q":"Ana oró en Siló: \"solo se movían sus labios, pero su voz no se oía\" (1 Samuel 1:13). ¿qué aprende de esto el Talmud (Berajot 31a) para la Amidá?","o":["orar solo en el corazón, con los labios quietos","decirla en voz alta, para que el sacerdote responda amén","formar las palabras con los labios, pero sin que se oigan","orarla solo en un santuario, como hizo Ana en Siló"]}},{"id":"JUDAISM-s07-05","day":520,"d":4,"q":"in the Talmud's story of the oven of Akhnai (Bava Metzia 59b), Rabbi Joshua answers a voice from heaven with \"it is not in heaven\" (Deuteronomy 30:12). what does he mean by it?","o":["a voice from heaven outranks any vote of the sages","miracles show which sage holds the correct ruling","the Torah stayed in heaven until Moses brought it","once given, the law is set by the sages' majority"],"a":3,"es":{"q":"en el relato talmúdico del horno de Ajnai (Bava Metzía 59b), el rabino Yehoshúa responde a una voz del cielo con \"no está en el cielo\" (Deuteronomio 30:12). ¿qué quiere decir?","o":["una voz del cielo pesa más que cualquier voto de los sabios","los milagros muestran qué sabio tiene la decisión correcta","la Torá estuvo en el cielo hasta que Moisés la trajo","ya dada la Torá, la ley la decide la mayoría de los sabios"]}},{"id":"JUDAISM-s07-06","day":580,"d":3,"q":"the Talmud (Berakhot 21b) rules that certain prayers are said only with a minyan, a quorum of ten. someone prays the morning Amidah alone. which part is left out?","o":["the Kedushah, the angels' words from Isaiah","the blessing that asks healing for the sick","the closing blessing that asks for peace","the blessing for rain and the year's harvest"],"a":0,"es":{"q":"el Talmud (Berajot 21b) establece que ciertas oraciones solo se dicen con un minián, un quórum de diez. alguien reza solo la Amidá de la mañana. ¿qué parte se omite?","o":["la Kedushá, las palabras de los ángeles en Isaías","la bendición que pide la curación de los enfermos","la bendición final que pide la paz","la bendición por la lluvia y la cosecha del año"]}}],[{"id":"JUDAISM-s08-01","day":608,"d":2,"q":"The Talmud (Berakhot 26b) ties each of the three daily prayers to one of the patriarchs. To whom does it link Mincha, the afternoon prayer?","o":["Abraham, the first patriarch","Isaac, the second patriarch","Jacob, the third patriarch","Joseph, the son of Jacob"],"a":1,"es":{"q":"El Talmud (Berajot 26b) vincula cada una de las tres oraciones diarias con uno de los patriarcas. ¿Con quién vincula Minjá, la oración de la tarde?","o":["Abraham, el primer patriarca","Isaac, el segundo patriarca","Jacob, el tercer patriarca","José, el hijo de Jacob"]}},{"id":"JUDAISM-s08-02","day":621,"d":3,"q":"Musaf, the \"additional\" prayer, is said on Shabbat, festival and new-moon mornings. According to the Talmud, what does it stand in place of?","o":["the second meal the Sabbath adds after prayer","the extra reader called to the Torah that day","the longer Torah reading heard on those mornings","the extra Temple offerings of those days"],"a":3,"es":{"q":"Musaf, la oración \"adicional\", se dice en las mañanas de Shabat, de fiestas y de luna nueva. Según el Talmud, ¿en lugar de qué está?","o":["de la segunda comida que el Shabat añade tras rezar","del lector extra llamado a la Torá ese día","de la lectura más larga de la Torá en esas mañanas","de las ofrendas extra del Templo en esos días"]}},{"id":"JUDAISM-s08-03","day":649,"d":3,"q":"In the Talmud (Rosh Hashanah 16b), three books are opened on Rosh Hashanah. What happens to the beinonim, those in between the righteous and the wicked?","o":["they are written and sealed for life at once","their verdict waits until the end of their life","their judgment is held open until Yom Kippur","their judgment moves to the next Rosh Hashanah"],"a":2,"es":{"q":"En el Talmud (Rosh Hashaná 16b), en Rosh Hashaná se abren tres libros. ¿Qué pasa con los beinonim, los que están entre los justos y los malvados?","o":["se los inscribe y sella para la vida de una vez","su veredicto espera hasta el final de su vida","su juicio queda abierto hasta Yom Kipur","su juicio pasa al siguiente Rosh Hashaná"]}},{"id":"JUDAISM-s08-04","day":666,"d":2,"q":"In the Talmud's account of Hanukkah (Shabbat 21b), what miracle is the eight-day festival linked to?","o":["a single jar of pure oil lasting eight days","the Temple gates opening on their own each night","eight days of rain that broke the long siege","a lamp hidden since Solomon's days found burning"],"a":0,"es":{"q":"En el relato del Talmud sobre Janucá (Shabat 21b), ¿con qué milagro se vincula la fiesta de ocho días?","o":["una sola vasija de aceite puro que duró ocho días","las puertas del Templo abriéndose solas cada noche","ocho días de lluvia que rompieron el largo asedio","una lámpara oculta desde Salomón hallada encendida"]}},{"id":"JUDAISM-s08-05","day":674,"d":3,"q":"Maimonides (Laws of Megillah 2:17) says it is better to spend more on matanot la'evyonim, gifts to the poor, than on the Purim feast and gifts to friends. What reason does he give?","o":["the feast and food portions were added later by the sages","gifts to the poor atone for the sins of the whole year","gladdening the hearts of the poor is the greatest joy","giving to the poor was Queen Esther's own last request"],"a":2,"es":{"q":"Maimónides (Leyes de la Meguilá 2:17) dice que es mejor gastar más en matanot laevionim, los regalos a los pobres, que en el banquete de Purim y los regalos a los amigos. ¿Qué razón da?","o":["los sabios añadieron después el banquete y las porciones","los regalos a los pobres expían los pecados de todo el año","alegrar el corazón de los pobres es la mayor alegría","dar a los pobres fue el último pedido de la reina Ester"]}},{"id":"JUDAISM-s08-06","day":681,"d":3,"q":"At a Passover seder, a grandmother tells her grandson: \"Don't say they were slaves in Egypt. Say I was.\" Which teaching of Mishnah Pesachim 10:5 is she drawing on?","o":["whoever tells the Exodus at length is to be praised","the youngest child must ask the four questions","everyone must recline at the table as free people","each generation must see itself as leaving Egypt"],"a":3,"es":{"q":"En un séder de Pésaj, una abuela le dice a su nieto: \"No digas que ellos fueron esclavos en Egipto. Di que yo lo fui\". ¿En qué enseñanza de la Mishná Pesajim 10:5 se apoya?","o":["quien cuenta el Éxodo con detalle es digno de alabanza","el niño más pequeño debe hacer las cuatro preguntas","todos deben reclinarse a la mesa como gente libre","cada generación debe verse como si saliera de Egipto"]}}],[{"id":"JUDAISM-s09-01","day":747,"d":2,"q":"in the prophet Nathan's parable to King David (2 Samuel 12:1–4), what does the rich man take from the poor man to serve to a traveler?","o":["the poor man's only field of barley","the poor man's ox and its plow","the poor man's one little ewe lamb","the poor man's last jar of oil"],"a":2,"es":{"q":"en la parábola que el profeta Natán le cuenta al rey David (2 Samuel 12:1–4), ¿qué le quita el hombre rico al pobre para servírselo a un viajero?","o":["el único campo de cebada del pobre","el buey y el arado del pobre","la única corderita del pobre","la última vasija de aceite del pobre"]}},{"id":"JUDAISM-s09-02","day":769,"d":2,"q":"at Mount Horeb (1 Kings 19:11–12), the prophet Elijah sees a wind, an earthquake and a fire pass by. in what does the text say the LORD comes to him?","o":["the strong wind that tore the mountains","the earthquake that shook the mountain","the fire that came after the earthquake","a still small voice after the fire"],"a":3,"es":{"q":"en el monte Horeb (1 Reyes 19:11–12), el profeta Elías ve pasar un viento, un terremoto y un fuego. ¿en qué dice el texto que el SEÑOR viene a él?","o":["el viento fuerte que partía los montes","el terremoto que sacudió el monte","el fuego que vino tras el terremoto","una voz suave y delicada tras el fuego"]}},{"id":"JUDAISM-s09-03","day":719,"d":3,"q":"in Judges 7, God has Gideon cut his army from about 32,000 men down to 300 before fighting Midian. what reason does the text give?","o":["so Israel could not boast that its own hand saved it","so the small army could move at night without being seen","because the other tribes refused to send any men","so the few springs could give water to every man"],"a":0,"es":{"q":"en Jueces 7, Dios hace que Gedeón reduzca su ejército de unos 32.000 hombres a 300 antes de pelear contra Madián. ¿qué razón da el texto?","o":["para que Israel no presumiera de salvarse por su mano","para que el pequeño ejército avanzara de noche sin ser visto","porque las demás tribus se negaron a mandar hombres","para que los pocos manantiales dieran agua a todos"]}},{"id":"JUDAISM-s09-04","day":757,"d":3,"q":"at Gibeon, God tells the young King Solomon to ask for anything (1 Kings 3:5–13). why is God pleased with what Solomon asks for?","o":["he asked to see his father's enemies all defeated","he asked for discernment to judge, not riches","he asked for leave to build a house for God","he asked that his sons would rule after him"],"a":1,"es":{"q":"en Gabaón, Dios le dice al joven rey Salomón que pida lo que quiera (1 Reyes 3:5–13). ¿por qué le agrada a Dios lo que pide Salomón?","o":["pidió ver derrotados a todos los enemigos de su padre","pidió discernimiento para juzgar, no riquezas","pidió permiso para construirle una casa a Dios","pidió que sus hijos reinaran después de él"]}},{"id":"JUDAISM-s09-05","day":733,"d":3,"q":"in 1 Samuel 15:22, the prophet Samuel tells King Saul that \"to obey is better than sacrifice.\" what had Saul done in the war against Amalek?","o":["made a peace treaty with the Amalekites to end the war","divided the Amalekite gold among his soldiers","refused to fight the Amalekites when he was sent","spared King Agag and kept the best flocks to offer up"],"a":3,"es":{"q":"en 1 Samuel 15:22, el profeta Samuel le dice al rey Saúl que \"obedecer es mejor que los sacrificios\". ¿qué había hecho Saúl en la guerra contra Amalec?","o":["hizo un tratado de paz con los amalecitas para terminar la guerra","repartió el oro de los amalecitas entre sus soldados","se negó a pelear contra los amalecitas cuando lo enviaron","perdonó al rey Agag y guardó lo mejor del ganado para ofrendas"]}},{"id":"JUDAISM-s09-06","day":720,"d":3,"q":"in a town, each of the most capable people turns down the job of leading, unwilling to leave their own good work, and the post goes to the least fit person, who eagerly accepts. which story from the Former Prophets does this echo?","o":["Nathan's parable of the poor man's little ewe lamb","Jephthah's vow at the start of his campaign","Jotham's fable of the trees choosing a king","Samuel's warning about the ways of a king"],"a":2,"es":{"q":"en un pueblo, cada una de las personas más capaces rechaza el cargo de dirigirlo, porque no quiere dejar su propio buen trabajo, y el puesto queda para la menos apta, que lo acepta con ganas. ¿qué relato de los Profetas Anteriores recuerda esto?","o":["la parábola de Natán sobre la corderita del pobre","el voto que hizo Jefté al comenzar su campaña","la fábula de Jotam sobre los árboles y su rey","la advertencia de Samuel sobre cómo actúa un rey"]}}],[{"id":"JUDAISM-s10-01","day":785,"d":2,"q":"In Isaiah's Temple vision (Isaiah 6), what does one of the seraphim touch to Isaiah's lips before he says \"Here am I; send me\"?","o":["a live coal taken from the altar","a scroll written front and back","oil poured from the anointing horn","water drawn from the bronze basin"],"a":0,"es":{"q":"En la visión de Isaías en el Templo (Isaías 6), ¿qué le toca uno de los serafines en los labios antes de que diga \"Heme aquí; envíame\"?","o":["una brasa encendida tomada del altar","un rollo escrito por delante y por detrás","aceite vertido del cuerno de la unción","agua sacada de la fuente de bronce"]}},{"id":"JUDAISM-s10-02","day":826,"d":3,"q":"In Jonah 4, after Nineveh is spared, what reason does Jonah himself give God for having fled toward Tarshish at the start?","o":["he feared the people of Nineveh would kill him","he knew God was gracious and would relent","he felt too young to speak for God","he thought the king would never listen"],"a":1,"es":{"q":"En Jonás 4, después de que Nínive se salva, ¿qué razón le da el propio Jonás a Dios por haber huido hacia Tarsis al principio?","o":["temía que la gente de Nínive lo matara a él","sabía que Dios era clemente y perdonaría","se sentía muy joven para hablar por Dios","creía que el rey nunca lo escucharía"]}},{"id":"JUDAISM-s10-03","day":840,"d":3,"q":"The Talmud (Moed Katan 28b) draws a rule for comforting mourners from Job's friends, who sat with him seven days in silence. What is the rule?","o":["comforters bring the mourner's first meal","comforters stay no longer than an hour","comforters recite psalms aloud in the mourner's home","comforters may not speak until the mourner does"],"a":3,"es":{"q":"El Talmud (Moed Katán 28b) saca una regla para consolar a los dolientes de los amigos de Job, que se sentaron con él siete días en silencio. ¿Cuál es la regla?","o":["los que consuelan traen la primera comida","los que consuelan no se quedan más de una hora","los que consuelan recitan salmos en voz alta en la casa","los que consuelan no hablan hasta que hable el doliente"]}},{"id":"JUDAISM-s10-04","day":858,"d":2,"q":"In Mishnah Yadayim 3:5, Rabbi Akiva says all the Writings are holy, but one book is the \"holy of holies\". Which book?","o":["the book of Psalms","the book of Ecclesiastes","the Song of Songs","the scroll of Esther"],"a":2,"es":{"q":"En la Mishná Yadáyim 3:5, el rabí Akiva dice que todos los Escritos son santos, pero que un libro es el \"santo de los santos\". ¿Cuál?","o":["el libro de los Salmos","el libro del Eclesiastés","el Cantar de los Cantares","el rollo de Ester"]}},{"id":"JUDAISM-s10-05","day":884,"d":4,"q":"The Talmud (Shabbat 30b) says the sages wanted to store away the book of Ecclesiastes because its words seemed to contradict each other. Why did they keep it?","o":["it begins and ends with words of Torah","Rabbi Akiva called it the holiest of books","it was already read aloud on Sukkot","King Hezekiah's scribes had copied it"],"a":0,"es":{"q":"El Talmud (Shabat 30b) dice que los sabios quisieron guardar el libro del Eclesiastés porque sus palabras parecían contradecirse. ¿Por qué lo conservaron?","o":["empieza y termina con palabras de Torá","el rabí Akiva lo llamó el más santo de los libros","ya se leía en voz alta en Sucot","los escribas del rey Ezequías lo copiaron"]}},{"id":"JUDAISM-s10-06","day":885,"d":3,"q":"Rashi reads Genesis 1:1 as “In the beginning of God’s creating heaven and earth,” a clause that leads into the next verse. In the PaRDeS scheme of Jewish interpretation, which level is that reading?","o":["remez, the allusive hint","derash, the sermonic teaching","peshat, the plain sense","sod, the mystical secret"],"a":2,"es":{"q":"Rashi lee Génesis 1:1 como “Al principio de la creación por Dios del cielo y la tierra”, una cláusula que lleva al versículo siguiente. En el esquema PaRDeS de la interpretación judía, ¿qué nivel es esa lectura?","o":["remez, la alusión o pista","derash, la enseñanza homilética","peshat, el sentido llano","sod, el secreto místico"]}}],[{"id":"JUDAISM-s11-01","day":898,"d":3,"q":"the houses of Hillel and Shammai argued for three years until a heavenly voice ruled that the law follows the house of Hillel. what reason does the Talmud (Eruvin 13b) give for that?","o":["they were the sharper minds and usually won the debates","their rulings were nearly always the stricter of the two","they were humble and taught Shammai's view first","Hillel held the office of high priest in the Temple"],"a":2,"es":{"q":"las casas de Hillel y Shammai discutieron durante tres años, hasta que una voz del cielo dictó que la ley sigue a la casa de Hillel. ¿qué razón da el Talmud (Eruvín 13b)?","o":["eran las mentes más agudas y solían ganar los debates","sus fallos casi siempre eran los más estrictos de los dos","eran humildes y enseñaban primero la opinión de Shammai","Hillel ocupaba el cargo de sumo sacerdote en el Templo"]}},{"id":"JUDAISM-s11-02","day":901,"d":2,"q":"in the Talmud's story (Gittin 56a–b), a sage is carried out of besieged Jerusalem in a coffin and asks the Roman commander Vespasian for \"Yavneh and its sages.\" who is he?","o":["Yochanan ben Zakkai","Akiva ben Yosef","Rabbi Judah the Prince","Shimon bar Yochai"],"a":0,"es":{"q":"en el relato del Talmud (Guitín 56a–b), un sabio sale de Jerusalén sitiada dentro de un ataúd y le pide al comandante romano Vespasiano \"Yavne y sus sabios\". ¿quién es?","o":["Yojanán ben Zakai","Akiva ben Yosef","Rabí Judá el Príncipe","Shimón bar Yojai"]}},{"id":"JUDAISM-s11-03","day":904,"d":3,"q":"dying at the hands of Rome, Rabbi Akiva tells his students he has waited all his life to fulfill \"with all thy soul\" from the Shema. how did the rabbis read that phrase (Mishnah Berakhot 9:5; Berakhot 61b)?","o":["love God with all your money and possessions","love God with both the good and evil inclinations","love God with every hour you spend in Torah study","love God even if God takes your life from you"],"a":3,"es":{"q":"al morir a manos de Roma, Rabí Akiva les dice a sus alumnos que toda su vida esperó cumplir \"con toda tu alma\" del Shemá. ¿cómo leían los rabinos esa frase (Mishná Berajot 9:5; Berajot 61b)?","o":["amar a Dios con todo tu dinero y tus bienes","amar a Dios con la buena y la mala inclinación","amar a Dios con cada hora de estudio de la Torá","amar a Dios aunque Dios te quite la vida"]}},{"id":"JUDAISM-s11-04","day":912,"d":3,"q":"in the 10th century, a Jewish community in Kairouan, North Africa, cannot settle a question of Jewish law. following the practice of the Geonic period, what would it most likely do?","o":["bring the case before the Sanhedrin sitting at Yavneh","write to a Babylonian Gaon and ask for his ruling","look up the ruling in Joseph Karo's Shulchan Aruch","send the question to the high priest in Jerusalem"],"a":1,"es":{"q":"en el siglo X, una comunidad judía de Kairuán, en el norte de África, no logra resolver una pregunta de ley judía. según la práctica de la época de los Gueonim, ¿qué haría con más probabilidad?","o":["llevar el caso ante el Sanedrín reunido en Yavne","escribir a un Gaón de Babilonia y pedirle un fallo","buscar el fallo en el Shuljan Aruj de Yosef Karo","enviar la pregunta al sumo sacerdote en Jerusalén"]}},{"id":"JUDAISM-s11-05","day":916,"d":2,"q":"the Karaites, a Jewish movement that arose in Babylonia around the 8th and 9th centuries, rejected what as binding?","o":["the oral law in Mishnah and Talmud","the books of the Prophets and Writings","the written Torah given at Mount Sinai","the festivals commanded in the Torah"],"a":0,"es":{"q":"los caraítas, un movimiento judío que surgió en Babilonia hacia los siglos VIII y IX, rechazaban como obligatorio ¿qué cosa?","o":["la ley oral de Mishná y Talmud","los libros de los Profetas y los Escritos","la Torá escrita entregada en el monte Sinaí","las fiestas que manda la Torá"]}},{"id":"JUDAISM-s11-06","day":953,"d":3,"q":"Moses Isserles of Kraków (the Rema) wrote the Mappah, \"the tablecloth,\" on Joseph Karo's Shulchan Aruch, \"the set table.\" what is the Mappah?","o":["a long commentary tracing each law back to the Talmud","a mystical reading of the hidden meaning of each law","glosses giving Ashkenazi custom where Karo differs","a shorter summary of the code written for schoolchildren"],"a":2,"es":{"q":"Moisés Isserles de Cracovia (el Remá) escribió la Mapá, \"el mantel\", sobre el Shuljan Aruj de Yosef Karo, \"la mesa servida\". ¿qué es la Mapá?","o":["un comentario largo que remonta cada ley al Talmud","una lectura mística del sentido oculto de cada ley","notas con la costumbre asquenazí donde Karo difiere","un resumen más corto del código escrito para niños"]}}],[{"id":"JUDAISM-s12-01","day":976,"d":3,"q":"Samson Raphael Hirsch's motto, Torah im derekh eretz, comes from Rabban Gamliel's saying in the Mishnah (Pirkei Avot 2:2). in that saying, what does \"derekh eretz\" (literally \"the way of the land\") mean?","o":["settling and farming the Land of Israel","the Oral Torah handed down by the sages","the sacrifices of the Temple service","a worldly occupation, earning a living"],"a":3,"es":{"q":"el lema de Samson Raphael Hirsch, Torá im dérej éretz, viene de un dicho de Rabán Gamliel en la Mishná (Pirkei Avot 2:2). en ese dicho, ¿qué significa \"dérej éretz\" (literalmente \"el camino de la tierra\")?","o":["poblar y cultivar la Tierra de Israel","la Torá oral transmitida por los sabios","los sacrificios del servicio del Templo","un oficio en el mundo, ganarse la vida"]}},{"id":"JUDAISM-s12-02","day":974,"d":3,"q":"a rabbi in nineteenth-century France is asked whether Jews must pay the state's property tax like everyone else. which principle of the Talmudic sage Shmuel answers the question?","o":["pikuach nefesh: saving a life overrides almost every law","dina de-malkhuta dina: the law of the kingdom is the law","kol Yisrael arevim: all Israel are responsible for one another","lo ba-shamayim hi: the Torah is not in heaven"],"a":1,"es":{"q":"a un rabino de la Francia del siglo XIX le preguntan si los judíos deben pagar el impuesto estatal a la propiedad como todos los demás. ¿qué principio del sabio talmúdico Shmuel responde la pregunta?","o":["pikuaj néfesh: salvar una vida pasa por encima de casi toda ley","dina de-maljuta dina: la ley del reino es la ley","kol Israel arevim: todo Israel es responsable el uno del otro","lo ba-shamáyim hi: la Torá no está en el cielo"]}},{"id":"JUDAISM-s12-03","day":983,"d":3,"q":"about fifty days after Yom Kippur, Beta Israel, the Jews of Ethiopia, fast, climb a high place facing Jerusalem, and hear their priests (kessim) read from the Orit to renew the covenant. what is this festival called?","o":["Sigd","Mimouna","Seharane","Hoshana Rabbah"],"a":0,"es":{"q":"unos cincuenta días después de Yom Kipur, Beta Israel, los judíos de Etiopía, ayunan, suben a un lugar alto mirando hacia Jerusalén y escuchan a sus sacerdotes (kessim) leer el Orit para renovar el pacto. ¿cómo se llama esta fiesta?","o":["Sigd","Mimuna","Saharane","Hoshaná Rabá"]}},{"id":"JUDAISM-s12-04","day":990,"d":3,"q":"in George Washington's 1790 letter to the Hebrew Congregation in Newport, Rhode Island, what does he say about \"toleration\"?","o":["it should reach Jews once they become full citizens","it is no longer spoken of, as if rights were a favor","it is a gift the government gives to minority faiths","it covers public worship but not the holding of office"],"a":1,"es":{"q":"en la carta de George Washington de 1790 a la Congregación Hebrea de Newport, Rhode Island, ¿qué dice sobre la \"tolerancia\"?","o":["debe llegar a los judíos cuando sean ciudadanos plenos","ya no se habla de ella, como si los derechos fueran un favor","es un regalo que el gobierno les da a las fes minoritarias","cubre el culto público, pero no el derecho a ocupar cargos públicos"]}},{"id":"JUDAISM-s12-05","day":1000,"d":3,"q":"what did Theodor Herzl argue in his 1896 book The Jewish State (Der Judenstaat)?","o":["Jews should blend fully into European life so the hatred would end","Jews should wait for the Messiah before any return to Zion","hatred of Jews would not fade, so they needed a recognized state","Hebrew must first become the daily language of all Jews"],"a":2,"es":{"q":"¿qué sostuvo Theodor Herzl en su libro de 1896 El Estado judío (Der Judenstaat)?","o":["los judíos debían mezclarse del todo en la vida europea para que el odio acabara","los judíos debían esperar al Mesías antes de volver a Sion","el odio a los judíos no se iría, así que necesitaban un Estado reconocido","el hebreo debía ser primero la lengua diaria de todos los judíos"]}},{"id":"JUDAISM-s12-06","day":1016,"d":3,"q":"who commanded the Jewish Fighting Organization (ZOB) in the Warsaw ghetto uprising, which began on the eve of Passover 1943?","o":["Janusz Korczak","Hannah Senesh","Emanuel Ringelblum","Mordecai Anielewicz"],"a":3,"es":{"q":"¿quién comandó la Organización Judía de Combate (ZOB) en el levantamiento del gueto de Varsovia, que empezó la víspera de Pésaj de 1943?","o":["Janusz Korczak","Hannah Senesh","Emanuel Ringelblum","Mordejái Anielewicz"]}}],[{"id":"JUDAISM-s13-01","day":1080,"d":3,"q":"the Mishnah is arranged in six orders. which order holds tractate Avot (Pirkei Avot), along with the tractates on civil law and courts such as Bava Kamma and Sanhedrin?","o":["Zeraim, the order of seeds","Moed, the order of appointed times","Nezikin, the order of damages","Kodashim, the order of holy things"],"a":2,"es":{"q":"la Mishná está ordenada en seis órdenes. ¿qué orden contiene el tratado Avot (Pirkei Avot), junto con los tratados de derecho civil y tribunales como Bava Kama y Sanedrín?","o":["Zeraim, el orden de las semillas","Moed, el orden de los tiempos señalados","Nezikin, el orden de los daños","Kodashim, el orden de las cosas santas"]}},{"id":"JUDAISM-s13-02","day":1083,"d":3,"q":"Mishnah Bava Metzia opens with two people holding one garment, each saying \"I found it, it is all mine.\" what does the Mishnah rule?","o":["the one who saw it first takes the whole of the garment","each swears to owning at least half, and they divide it","they cast lots, and the winner keeps the garment","the court holds the garment until a witness comes forward"],"a":1,"es":{"q":"la Mishná Bava Metziá empieza con dos personas que sujetan una misma prenda, y cada una dice: \"yo la encontré, es toda mía\". ¿qué dictamina la Mishná?","o":["quien la vio primero se queda con la prenda entera","cada uno jura tener al menos la mitad, y la dividen","echan suertes, y el ganador se queda con la prenda","el tribunal guarda la prenda hasta que llegue un testigo"]}},{"id":"JUDAISM-s13-03","day":1095,"d":3,"q":"a student argues: \"if this work is forbidden on a festival day, which is less strict, then surely it is forbidden on Shabbat, which is stricter.\" which of the rabbis' rules of interpretation is the student using?","o":["gezerah shavah, two verses sharing a word","binyan av, a rule built from one verse","klal u-ferat, a general rule and a detail","kal vachomer, from light to heavy"],"a":3,"es":{"q":"un estudiante argumenta: \"si este trabajo está prohibido en un día de fiesta, que es menos estricto, con más razón está prohibido en Shabat, que es más estricto\". ¿qué regla de interpretación de los rabinos usa el estudiante?","o":["gezerá shavá, dos versículos con una misma palabra","binián av, una regla tomada de un versículo","klal u-ferat, una regla general y un detalle","kal vajómer, de lo leve a lo grave"]}},{"id":"JUDAISM-s13-04","day":1106,"d":3,"q":"the law follows the majority, yet the Mishnah records lone opinions that lost. according to Mishnah Eduyot 1:5, why are those minority opinions written down?","o":["so a later court that agrees with one may rely on it","so the lone sage's students are not shamed in public","because a lone view becomes law outside the land of Israel","so each opinion can be voted on again every new year"],"a":0,"es":{"q":"la ley sigue a la mayoría, pero la Mishná registra opiniones solitarias que perdieron. según la Mishná Eduiot 1:5, ¿por qué se ponen por escrito esas opiniones de la minoría?","o":["para que un tribunal posterior que la comparta pueda apoyarse en ella","para que los alumnos del sabio solitario no sean avergonzados","porque una opinión solitaria es ley fuera de la tierra de Israel","para que cada opinión se pueda volver a votar cada año nuevo"]}},{"id":"JUDAISM-s13-05","day":1110,"d":3,"q":"the blessing over Hanukkah lights thanks God \"who commanded us\" to light them, though Hanukkah is not in the Torah. how does the Talmud (Shabbat 23a) explain where the command comes from?","o":["the prophet Zechariah commanded it in his vision of a lamp","the Torah tells Israel to heed its sages, so their rules bind","the Torah hints at Hanukkah in the tabernacle's menorah","the Maccabees received it as a new law through a heavenly voice"],"a":1,"es":{"q":"la bendición de las luces de Janucá agradece a Dios \"que nos ordenó\" encenderlas, aunque Janucá no está en la Torá. ¿cómo explica el Talmud (Shabat 23a) de dónde viene ese mandato?","o":["el profeta Zacarías lo ordenó en su visión de un candelabro","la Torá manda escuchar a los sabios, y sus normas obligan","la Torá alude a Janucá en la menorá del tabernáculo","los macabeos lo recibieron como ley nueva de una voz celestial"]}},{"id":"JUDAISM-s13-06","day":1157,"d":3,"q":"the Torah speaks of \"the hand of the LORD\" and \"the eyes of the LORD.\" how does Maimonides read such phrases in the Mishneh Torah and the Guide for the Perplexed?","o":["as names of angels who act on God's behalf","as a body of light that only prophets can see","as figures of speech, since God has no body","as a form God takes on only at Mount Sinai"],"a":2,"es":{"q":"la Torá habla de \"la mano del SEÑOR\" y \"los ojos del SEÑOR\". ¿cómo lee Maimónides esas frases en la Mishné Torá y la Guía de los perplejos?","o":["como nombres de ángeles que actúan en nombre de Dios","como un cuerpo de luz que solo los profetas pueden ver","como figuras del lenguaje, porque Dios no tiene cuerpo","como una forma que Dios toma solo en el monte Sinaí"]}}],[{"id":"JUDAISM-s14-01","day":1171,"d":1,"q":"In Hebrew, what does the word kabbalah, the name of Jewish mystical tradition, literally mean?","o":["ascending, or what is lifted up","hiding, or what is concealed","receiving, or what is received","counting, or what is numbered"],"a":2,"es":{"q":"En hebreo, ¿qué significa literalmente la palabra cábala, el nombre de la tradición mística judía?","o":["ascender, o lo que se eleva","ocultar, o lo que está escondido","recibir, o lo que se ha recibido","contar, o lo que se enumera"]}},{"id":"JUDAISM-s14-02","day":1183,"d":3,"q":"In the Kabbalah of Isaac Luria (16th-century Safed), what is the name for God's withdrawal or contraction that makes room for a world to exist?","o":["tzimtzum, a drawing in","shevirah, a shattering","gilgul, a rolling round","devekut, a holding fast"],"a":0,"es":{"q":"En la cábala de Isaac Luria (Safed, siglo XVI), ¿cómo se llama la retirada o contracción de Dios que deja lugar para que exista un mundo?","o":["tzimtzum, un recogerse","shevirá, un quebrarse","guilgul, un girar","devekut, un aferrarse"]}},{"id":"JUDAISM-s14-03","day":1184,"d":3,"q":"In Isaac Luria's teaching, as Chaim Vital recorded it, how did sparks of divine light come to be scattered through the lower worlds?","o":["the first tablets broke at Sinai and let the light out","the sun and moon of day four split the first light apart","angels divided the light among the seventy nations","the vessels made to hold it could not bear it and broke"],"a":3,"es":{"q":"Según la enseñanza de Isaac Luria, tal como la registró Jaim Vital, ¿cómo llegaron a dispersarse chispas de luz divina por los mundos inferiores?","o":["las primeras tablas se rompieron en el Sinaí y la luz salió","el sol y la luna del cuarto día partieron la primera luz","los ángeles repartieron la luz entre las setenta naciones","las vasijas hechas para contenerla no la soportaron y se rompieron"]}},{"id":"JUDAISM-s14-04","day":1182,"d":4,"q":"The Zohar (3:152a) calls the Torah's stories its garment. According to that passage, what lies beneath the garment?","o":["the Hebrew letters as its body, and their numbers within","the commandments as its body, and a soul within that","the prophets as its body, and the Writings within that","the Oral Torah as its body, and the Talmud within that"],"a":1,"es":{"q":"El Zóhar (3:152a) llama a los relatos de la Torá su vestido. Según ese pasaje, ¿qué hay debajo del vestido?","o":["las letras hebreas como cuerpo, y sus números por dentro","los mandamientos como cuerpo, y un alma dentro de él","los profetas como cuerpo, y los Escritos dentro de él","la Torá oral como cuerpo, y el Talmud dentro de ella"]}},{"id":"JUDAISM-s14-05","day":1221,"d":3,"q":"Conservative (Masorti) Judaism grew from Zecharias Frankel's \"positive-historical\" school. How does the movement itself describe halakha, Jewish law?","o":["a guide each Jew may take up or set aside by choice","a folkway of the people that each age may remake","binding on Jews, and developing through history","binding on Jews, and fixed since Sinai unchanged"],"a":2,"es":{"q":"El judaísmo conservador (masortí) nació de la escuela \"histórico-positiva\" de Zacharias Frankel. ¿Cómo describe el propio movimiento la halajá, la ley judía?","o":["una guía que cada judío puede tomar o dejar a su elección","una costumbre del pueblo que cada época puede rehacer","obligatoria para los judíos, y en desarrollo con la historia","obligatoria para los judíos, y fija e inmutable desde el Sinaí"]}},{"id":"JUDAISM-s14-06","day":1194,"d":3,"q":"A Hasid holds that a meal, eaten with a blessing and the right intention, is itself an act of worship rather than a pause from it. Which Hasidic teaching is this?","o":["avodah b'gashmiyut, serving God through the physical","tzimtzum, God's drawing in to make room for a world","gilgul, the return of a soul in a new lifetime","hitbodedut, praying alone in the fields or woods"],"a":0,"es":{"q":"Un jasid sostiene que una comida, tomada con una bendición y la intención correcta, es en sí misma un acto de culto y no una pausa en él. ¿Qué enseñanza jasídica es esta?","o":["avodá begashmiut, servir a Dios a través de lo físico","tzimtzum, el recogerse de Dios para dejar lugar al mundo","guilgul, el regreso de un alma en una nueva vida","hitbodedut, orar a solas en los campos o el bosque"]}}],[{"id":"JUDAISM-s15-01","day":1279,"d":3,"q":"Who wrote Mesillat Yesharim (The Path of the Just), the 18th-century Mussar classic that climbs a ladder of traits beginning with watchfulness?","o":["Rabbi Israel Salanter","Mendel Lefin of Satanov","Moshe Chaim Luzzatto","Rabbi Israel Meir Kagan"],"a":2,"es":{"q":"¿Quién escribió Mesilat Yesharim (El sendero de los justos), el clásico del Musar del siglo XVIII que sube por una escalera de virtudes que empieza con la vigilancia?","o":["El rabino Israel Salanter","Mendel Lefin de Satanov","Moshé Jaim Luzzatto","El rabino Israel Meir Kagan"]}},{"id":"JUDAISM-s15-02","day":1306,"d":2,"q":"At a traditional Jewish wedding, what is the ketubah that is read aloud under the chuppah (the wedding canopy)?","o":["a contract setting out the husband's duties to his wife","a set of blessings sung over the couple and a cup of wine","a record of both families' lineage back to their tribes","the couple's vows to keep a kosher home and keep Shabbat"],"a":0,"es":{"q":"En una boda judía tradicional, ¿qué es la ketubá que se lee en voz alta bajo la jupá (el palio nupcial)?","o":["un contrato con los deberes del esposo hacia su esposa","bendiciones cantadas sobre la pareja y una copa de vino","un registro del linaje de ambas familias hasta su tribu","los votos de la pareja de tener hogar kosher y guardar Shabat"]}},{"id":"JUDAISM-s15-03","day":1272,"d":3,"q":"In the laws of speech set out by the Chafetz Chaim (Rabbi Israel Meir Kagan), what makes motzi shem ra (\"bringing out a bad name\") different from lashon hara (harmful speech)?","o":["the report is said to the person's face","the report is spread to a large crowd","the report is written rather than spoken","the damaging report is false, not true"],"a":3,"es":{"q":"En las leyes del habla que expone el Jafetz Jaim (el rabino Israel Meir Kagan), ¿qué distingue al motzí shem ra (\"sacar un mal nombre\") del lashón hará (habla dañina)?","o":["el relato se dice a la cara de la persona","el relato se difunde ante una gran multitud","el relato se escribe en lugar de decirse","el relato dañino es falso, no verdadero"]}},{"id":"JUDAISM-s15-04","day":1252,"d":3,"q":"In Hilkhot De'ot, Maimonides' laws of character traits (middot), where does he place the right measure for most traits?","o":["at the strictest end, as far as one can go","in the middle, between the two extremes","wherever one's own teacher's measure lies","at whatever level comes most naturally"],"a":1,"es":{"q":"En Hiljot Deot, las leyes de Maimónides sobre los rasgos de carácter (midot), ¿dónde sitúa la medida correcta para la mayoría de los rasgos?","o":["en el extremo más estricto, lo más lejos posible","en el medio, entre los dos extremos","donde esté la medida de tu propio maestro","en el nivel que resulte más natural"]}},{"id":"JUDAISM-s15-05","day":1266,"d":3,"q":"The Talmud (Sukkah 49b) names ways that gemilut chasadim, acts of loving-kindness, is greater than tzedakah, charity. Which is one of them?","o":["it reaches the dead as well as the living","it must be given in secret to count","it is owed first to one's closest relatives","it frees the giver from the year's tithes"],"a":0,"es":{"q":"El Talmud (Sucá 49b) nombra formas en que la guemilut jasadim, los actos de bondad, es mayor que la tzedaká, la caridad. ¿Cuál es una de ellas?","o":["alcanza a los muertos y también a los vivos","hay que darla en secreto para que cuente","se debe primero a los parientes más cercanos","libera a quien la da de los diezmos del año"]}},{"id":"JUDAISM-s15-06","day":1278,"d":3,"q":"Pirkei Avot 1:6 teaches, in the name of Joshua ben Perachiah, to judge every person on the side of merit. A neighbor who promised to help on moving day never arrives and sends no word. What reading of the neighbor does this teaching call for?","o":["suspect he chose not to come, but stay polite","ask other neighbors whether he often does this","hold it against him until he says he is sorry","assume a good reason kept him away for now"],"a":3,"es":{"q":"Pirkei Avot 1:6 enseña, en nombre de Iehoshúa ben Perajiá, a juzgar a toda persona por el lado del mérito. Un vecino que prometió ayudar el día de la mudanza nunca llega y no avisa. ¿Qué lectura del vecino pide esta enseñanza?","o":["sospechar que decidió no venir, pero ser cortés","preguntar a otros vecinos si lo hace a menudo","guardárselo hasta que él pida perdón","suponer que una buena razón lo detuvo por ahora"]}}],[{"id":"JUDAISM-s16-01","day":1342,"d":4,"q":"In the Talmud (Berakhot 4b), Rabbi Yochanan asks why Psalm 145, the Ashrei, has no verse beginning with the letter nun. What is his answer?","o":["nun's bent shape was a sign of pride, unfit for a psalm of praise","the nun verse was lost from the scrolls when the Temple was burned","a nun verse would open with Amos's word for Israel falling","nun's number, fifty, was set aside for counting the Omer days"],"a":2,"es":{"q":"En el Talmud (Berajot 4b), Rabí Yojanán pregunta por qué el Salmo 145, el Ashrei, no tiene ningún verso que empiece con la letra nun. ¿Cuál es su respuesta?","o":["la forma doblada de la nun era señal de orgullo, impropia de una alabanza","el verso de la nun se perdió de los rollos cuando se quemó el Templo","un verso con nun abriría con la palabra de Amós para la caída de Israel","el número de la nun, cincuenta, se reservaba para contar los días del Omer"]}},{"id":"JUDAISM-s16-02","day":1331,"d":3,"q":"In the Talmud (Shabbat 104a), why is the letter gimel drawn with its foot stretched toward the letter dalet?","o":["because one who is kind to the poor runs after them","because a student must run after a teacher to learn","because the strong must carry the weak like a camel","because a giver waits at home for the poor to knock"],"a":0,"es":{"q":"En el Talmud (Shabat 104a), ¿por qué la letra guímel se dibuja con el pie estirado hacia la letra dálet?","o":["porque quien es bondadoso con los pobres corre tras ellos","porque el alumno debe correr tras el maestro para aprender","porque el fuerte debe cargar al débil como lo hace un camello","porque quien da espera en casa a que el pobre toque la puerta"]}},{"id":"JUDAISM-s16-03","day":1363,"d":2,"q":"Which three Hebrew letters spell emet, the word for truth?","o":["shin, kuf, resh","alef, mem, tav","alef, mem, nun","mem, vav, tav"],"a":1,"es":{"q":"¿Qué tres letras hebreas forman emet, la palabra para verdad?","o":["shin, kuf, resh","álef, mem, tav","álef, mem, nun","mem, vav, tav"]}},{"id":"JUDAISM-s16-04","day":1350,"d":3,"q":"In the Talmud (Shabbat 104a), the letters of sheker, falsehood, each stand on one foot, while the letters of emet, truth, stand on broad bases. What does the Talmud draw from this?","o":["falsehood spreads faster than truth can follow it","truth needs two witnesses before it can stand firm","falsehood hides itself, while truth is seen by all","truth stands firm, and falsehood does not stand"],"a":3,"es":{"q":"En el Talmud (Shabat 104a), las letras de sheker, la mentira, se apoyan cada una en un solo pie, mientras que las de emet, la verdad, se apoyan en bases anchas. ¿Qué enseña el Talmud con esto?","o":["la mentira se extiende más rápido de lo que la verdad la alcanza","la verdad necesita dos testigos para poder mantenerse firme","la mentira se esconde, mientras que la verdad está a la vista","la verdad se mantiene firme, y la mentira no se sostiene"]}},{"id":"JUDAISM-s16-05","day":1405,"d":3,"q":"The rabbinic word Shechinah, God's indwelling presence, shares its three-letter root Sh-K-N with which word from the Torah's account of the wilderness?","o":["mishkan, the tabernacle","kapporet, the ark-cover","mizbe'ach, the altar","menorah, the lampstand"],"a":0,"es":{"q":"La palabra rabínica Shejiná, la presencia de Dios que habita, comparte su raíz de tres letras Sh-J-N con ¿qué palabra del relato de la Torá sobre el desierto?","o":["mishkán, el tabernáculo","kaporet, la tapa del arca","mizbéaj, el altar","menorá, el candelabro"]}},{"id":"JUDAISM-s16-06","day":1391,"d":3,"q":"Before Yom Kippur, a man realizes he insulted a coworker in the spring. According to the Mishnah (Yoma 8:9), what is needed for this wrong to be atoned?","o":["the fast and his confession atone for it by themselves","the day atones once he has made peace with the coworker","the high priest's confession atones for it on his behalf","a wrong done to a person cannot be atoned for at all"],"a":1,"es":{"q":"Antes de Iom Kipur, un hombre se da cuenta de que insultó a un compañero de trabajo en la primavera. Según la Mishná (Iomá 8:9), ¿qué hace falta para que se expíe esa falta?","o":["el ayuno y su confesión la expían por sí mismos","el día la expía cuando haya hecho las paces con su compañero","la confesión del sumo sacerdote la expía en su nombre","una falta contra una persona no se puede expiar de ningún modo"]}}]],"SIKHISM":[[{"id":"SIKHISM-s00-01","day":18,"d":1,"q":"of the five Ks that an initiated Sikh keeps, as listed in the Sikh Rehat Maryada, which one is the small wooden comb worn in the hair?","o":["kara","kanga","kachera","kirpan"],"a":1,"es":{"q":"de las cinco K que guarda un sij iniciado, tal como las enumera el Sikh Rehat Maryada, ¿cuál es el pequeño peine de madera que se lleva en el cabello?","o":["kara","kanga","kachera","kirpan"]}},{"id":"SIKHISM-s00-02","day":20,"d":2,"q":"which Guru gathered the hymns of the Gurus before him, added his own, and installed the first Sikh scripture, the Adi Granth, at the Harmandir Sahib in Amritsar in 1604?","o":["Guru Angad","Guru Ram Das","Guru Arjan","Guru Hargobind"],"a":2,"es":{"q":"¿qué Guru reunió los himnos de los Gurus anteriores, añadió los suyos e instaló la primera escritura sij, el Adi Granth, en el Harmandir Sahib de Amritsar en 1604?","o":["Guru Angad","Guru Ram Das","Guru Arjan","Guru Hargobind"]}},{"id":"SIKHISM-s00-03","day":2,"d":1,"q":"in the langar, the free kitchen of every gurdwara, people sit on the floor in rows called pangat and are served by volunteers. what is sitting in pangat mainly meant to teach?","o":["that no one ranks above another, whatever their caste or wealth","that the eldest are seated nearest the Guru and served first","that the meal is karah prashad, the blessed food of worship","that sharing a meal earns merit toward a better next birth"],"a":0,"es":{"q":"en el langar, la cocina gratuita de cada gurdwara, la gente se sienta en el suelo en filas llamadas pangat y la sirven voluntarios. ¿qué busca enseñar sobre todo sentarse en pangat?","o":["que nadie está por encima de otro, sea cual sea su casta o riqueza","que los mayores se sientan más cerca del Guru y se les sirve primero","que la comida es karah prashad, el alimento bendito del culto","que compartir una comida gana mérito para un mejor renacimiento"]}},{"id":"SIKHISM-s00-04","day":9,"d":1,"q":"the Guru Granth Sahib opens with Ik Onkar, written with the numeral one followed by the sign for Onkar. what does Ik Onkar affirm?","o":["that Guru Nanak was the first of the ten Gurus","that the first hymn is sung before every other","that God stands apart from the world, far above it","that there is one God, one reality present in all"],"a":3,"es":{"q":"el Guru Granth Sahib se abre con Ik Onkar, escrito con el numeral uno seguido del signo de Onkar. ¿qué afirma Ik Onkar?","o":["que Guru Nanak fue el primero de los diez Gurus","que el primer himno se canta antes que todos los demás","que Dios está apartado del mundo, muy por encima de él","que hay un solo Dios, una realidad presente en todo"]}},{"id":"SIKHISM-s00-05","day":7,"d":2,"q":"Guru Hargobind, the sixth Guru, wore two swords, called miri and piri. what did the two swords stand for?","o":["justice for the poor and mercy for the guilty","temporal authority and spiritual authority","his father's martyrdom and his own coming","the defense of Punjab and of the Harmandir"],"a":1,"es":{"q":"Guru Hargobind, el sexto Guru, llevaba dos espadas, llamadas miri y piri. ¿qué representaban las dos espadas?","o":["justicia para los pobres y misericordia para los culpables","la autoridad temporal y la autoridad espiritual","el martirio de su padre y su propia llegada","la defensa del Punyab y la del Harmandir"]}},{"id":"SIKHISM-s00-06","day":13,"d":2,"q":"a Sikh shopkeeper sets aside a tenth of what he earns (dasvandh) for the langar and for people in need. which of the three teachings often traced to Guru Nanak does this most directly carry out?","o":["kirat karni, earning by honest labor","naam japna, remembering God's name","vand chakna, sharing one's earnings","chardi kala, keeping rising spirits"],"a":2,"es":{"q":"un comerciante sij aparta la décima parte de lo que gana (dasvandh) para el langar y para quienes lo necesitan. ¿cuál de las tres enseñanzas que suelen atribuirse a Guru Nanak pone en práctica de forma más directa?","o":["kirat karni, ganarse la vida con trabajo honrado","naam japna, recordar el nombre de Dios","vand chakna, compartir lo que se gana","chardi kala, mantener el ánimo en alto"]}}],[{"id":"SIKHISM-s01-01","day":44,"d":2,"q":"Guru Nanak chose his disciple Lehna, not either of his own sons, to succeed him. What name did he give Lehna?","o":["Guru Amar Das","Guru Angad","Guru Ram Das","Guru Arjan"],"a":1,"es":{"q":"Guru Nanak eligió a su discípulo Lehna, y no a uno de sus propios hijos, para sucederlo. ¿Qué nombre le dio a Lehna?","o":["Guru Amar Das","Guru Angad","Guru Ram Das","Guru Arjan"]}},{"id":"SIKHISM-s01-02","day":56,"d":2,"q":"The lavan, the four hymns in raag Suhi sung as a couple walks around the Guru Granth Sahib in the Anand Karaj wedding, were written by which Guru?","o":["Guru Amar Das","Guru Arjan","Guru Ram Das","Guru Nanak"],"a":2,"es":{"q":"Los lavan, los cuatro himnos en raag Suhi que se cantan mientras la pareja camina alrededor del Guru Granth Sahib en la boda Anand Karaj, ¿qué Guru los escribió?","o":["Guru Amar Das","Guru Arjan","Guru Ram Das","Guru Nanak"]}},{"id":"SIKHISM-s01-03","day":27,"d":2,"q":"In the janamsakhi story of Guru Nanak as storekeeper at Sultanpur, he weighs out grain and, on reaching thirteen, keeps repeating that number. What is the point of the story?","o":["thirteen marked the measure where a storekeeper took his own share","thirteen was the number of measures owed as tax to the governor","terah sounds like a word for enough, so he stopped weighing grain","terah, thirteen, sounds like tera, yours: all of it is God's"],"a":3,"es":{"q":"En el relato de las janamsakhis sobre Guru Nanak como encargado del almacén de Sultanpur, él pesa el grano y, al llegar al trece, sigue repitiendo ese número. ¿Cuál es el sentido del relato?","o":["el trece marcaba la medida en que el encargado tomaba su propia parte","el trece era el número de medidas que se debían de impuesto al gobernador","terah suena como una palabra para basta, así que dejó de pesar el grano","terah, trece, suena como tera, tuyo: todo le pertenece a Dios"]}},{"id":"SIKHISM-s01-04","day":66,"d":3,"q":"Guru Hargobind wore two swords, for miri and piri, and built the Akal Takht facing the Harmandir Sahib. In that pairing, what does the Akal Takht stand for?","o":["miri, the community's temporal and worldly affairs","piri, the spiritual life of hymns and the Name","the emperor's rule, which the Guru accepted over the Sikhs","the Guru's family court, handed down to his heirs"],"a":0,"es":{"q":"Guru Hargobind llevaba dos espadas, por miri y piri, y construyó el Akal Takht frente al Harmandir Sahib. En esa pareja, ¿qué representa el Akal Takht?","o":["miri, los asuntos temporales y mundanos de la comunidad","piri, la vida espiritual de los himnos y del Nombre","el gobierno del emperador, que el Guru aceptaba sobre los sijs","la corte familiar del Guru, heredada por sus hijos"]}},{"id":"SIKHISM-s01-05","day":51,"d":2,"q":"At Goindval, Guru Amar Das kept the rule \"pehlan pangat, pichhon sangat,\" which tradition says even the emperor Akbar followed. What does the rule require?","o":["the emperor's land grant must fund the kitchen before the hymns","the hymns are sung first, and the shared meal is served after","all eat in langar, in a row as equals, before seeing the Guru","rulers and priests are seated first, and then everyone else eats"],"a":2,"es":{"q":"En Goindval, Guru Amar Das mantenía la regla \"pehlan pangat, pichhon sangat\", que según la tradición siguió incluso el emperador Akbar. ¿Qué pide la regla?","o":["la tierra donada por el emperador debe pagar la cocina antes de los himnos","primero se cantan los himnos y después se sirve la comida compartida","todos comen en el langar, en fila como iguales, antes de ver al Guru","los gobernantes y sacerdotes se sientan primero, y luego comen los demás"]}},{"id":"SIKHISM-s01-06","day":94,"d":3,"q":"A Sikh medic in a war zone treats injured fighters from the side that attacked her own town. Which story from the time of the Gurus is the closest precedent?","o":["Mai Bhago leading the forty back to fight at Khidrana","Bhai Kanhaiya giving water to the fallen of both sides","Bhai Jaita carrying the Guru's head home to Anandpur","Bhai Lalo sharing his coarse bread with Nanak at Saidpur"],"a":1,"es":{"q":"Una médica sij en una zona de guerra atiende a combatientes heridos del bando que atacó su propio pueblo. ¿Qué relato de la época de los Gurus es el precedente más cercano?","o":["Mai Bhago llevando a los cuarenta de vuelta a luchar en Khidrana","Bhai Kanhaiya dando agua a los caídos de ambos bandos","Bhai Jaita llevando la cabeza del Guru de vuelta a Anandpur","Bhai Lalo compartiendo su pan sencillo con Nanak en Saidpur"]}}],[{"id":"SIKHISM-s02-01","day":98,"d":2,"q":"At a gurdwara, what is the joda ghar?","o":["the room where shoes are left and minded","the hall where langar is served in rows","the room where the Granth is kept at night","the pool where pilgrims bathe at dawn"],"a":0,"es":{"q":"En un gurdwara, ¿qué es el joda ghar?","o":["el cuarto donde se dejan y cuidan los zapatos","la sala donde se sirve el langar en filas","el cuarto donde se guarda el Granth de noche","el estanque donde se bañan los peregrinos"]}},{"id":"SIKHISM-s02-02","day":102,"d":3,"q":"In the Guru Granth Sahib (Ang 466, Asa di Var), Guru Angad calls haumai, ego, a long and deep illness. What does the same verse say about its cure?","o":["its cure is found at holy rivers","its cure is found in long fasting","its cure also lies within it","its cure is found in the forest"],"a":2,"es":{"q":"En el Guru Granth Sahib (Ang 466, Asa di Var), Guru Angad llama al haumai, el ego, una enfermedad larga y profunda. ¿Qué dice el mismo verso sobre su cura?","o":["su cura está en los ríos sagrados","su cura está en los ayunos largos","su cura también está dentro de él","su cura se halla en el bosque"]}},{"id":"SIKHISM-s02-03","day":105,"d":2,"q":"After its opening prayers, the Guru Granth Sahib is arranged in 31 raag sections. Which raag comes first?","o":["Raag Majh","Sri Raag","Raag Gauri","Raag Asa"],"a":1,"es":{"q":"Después de sus oraciones iniciales, el Guru Granth Sahib se ordena en 31 secciones de raag. ¿Qué raag va primero?","o":["Raag Majh","Sri Raag","Raag Gauri","Raag Asa"]}},{"id":"SIKHISM-s02-04","day":124,"d":3,"q":"In the fourth pauri of Japji Sahib, Guru Nanak speaks of amrit vela, the ambrosial hour before dawn. What does he say that hour is for?","o":["giving alms to the needy at the door","keeping a fast until the sun has risen","reciting the whole scripture aloud","dwelling on the true Name's greatness"],"a":3,"es":{"q":"En la cuarta pauri del Japji Sahib, Guru Nanak habla del amrit vela, la hora ambrosial antes del amanecer. ¿Para qué dice que es esa hora?","o":["dar limosna a los necesitados en la puerta","ayunar hasta que haya salido el sol","recitar en voz alta toda la escritura","meditar en la grandeza del Nombre verdadero"]}},{"id":"SIKHISM-s02-05","day":142,"d":2,"q":"In a gurdwara, why is karah prashad given to everyone in the sangat from the same bowl, without distinction?","o":["it marks the breaking of a fast kept that morning","it repays the families who donated the flour","it sets aside caste rules on who may eat together","it honors the day's readers of the Guru Granth Sahib"],"a":2,"es":{"q":"En un gurdwara, ¿por qué se da karah prashad a todos en la sangat del mismo recipiente, sin distinción?","o":["marca el final de un ayuno guardado esa mañana","paga a las familias que donaron la harina","deja de lado las reglas de casta sobre quién come junto","honra a quienes leyeron ese día el Guru Granth Sahib"]}},{"id":"SIKHISM-s02-06","day":133,"d":3,"q":"A guest hears the same short hymn near the close of a Sikh wedding and of a memorial a week later, sung just before everyone stands for Ardas. Which bani is it most likely to be?","o":["Japji Sahib, by Guru Nanak Dev","Anand Sahib, by Guru Amar Das","Jaap Sahib, by Guru Gobind Singh","Chaupai Sahib, by Guru Gobind Singh"],"a":1,"es":{"q":"Una invitada oye el mismo himno corto cerca del final de una boda sij y de un servicio en memoria una semana después, cantado justo antes de que todos se pongan de pie para el Ardas. ¿Qué bani es lo más probable?","o":["Japji Sahib, de Guru Nanak Dev","Anand Sahib, de Guru Amar Das","Jaap Sahib, de Guru Gobind Singh","Chaupai Sahib, de Guru Gobind Singh"]}}],[{"id":"SIKHISM-s03-01","day":157,"d":2,"q":"Sikh tradition credits which Guru with shaping and settling the Gurmukhi script in which the Gurus' hymns are written?","o":["Guru Angad, the second Guru","Guru Amar Das, the third Guru","Guru Ram Das, the fourth Guru","Guru Arjan, the fifth Guru"],"a":0,"es":{"q":"La tradición sij atribuye a ¿qué Guru haber dado forma y fijado la escritura gurmukhi, en la que están escritos los himnos de los Gurus?","o":["Guru Angad, el segundo Guru","Guru Amar Das, el tercer Guru","Guru Ram Das, el cuarto Guru","Guru Arjan, el quinto Guru"]}},{"id":"SIKHISM-s03-02","day":159,"d":2,"q":"In the Mool Mantar, the opening lines of the Guru Granth Sahib (Ang 1), what does the word nirbhau mean?","o":["without enmity","self-existent","without fear","beyond time"],"a":2,"es":{"q":"En el Mool Mantar, las líneas con que abre el Guru Granth Sahib (Ang 1), ¿qué significa la palabra nirbhau?","o":["sin enemistad","existente por sí mismo","sin temor alguno","más allá del tiempo"]}},{"id":"SIKHISM-s03-03","day":164,"d":3,"q":"In the first pauri of Japji Sahib (Guru Granth Sahib, Ang 1), how does Guru Nanak say one becomes truthful (sachiaara) and the wall of falsehood is torn down?","o":["by thinking it over a hundred thousand times","by keeping outward silence for endless hours","by walking in the hukam, the divine will","by piling up the goods of all the worlds"],"a":2,"es":{"q":"En la primera pauri del Japji Sahib (Guru Granth Sahib, Ang 1), ¿cómo dice Guru Nanak que uno se vuelve veraz (sachiaara) y se derriba el muro de la falsedad?","o":["pensándolo cien mil veces sin descanso","guardando silencio exterior horas sin fin","caminando en el hukam, la voluntad divina","acumulando los bienes de todos los mundos"]}},{"id":"SIKHISM-s03-04","day":188,"d":3,"q":"In Pauri 16 of Japji Sahib (Guru Granth Sahib, Ang 3), what does Guru Nanak say the mythic bull (dhaul) holding up the earth really is?","o":["seva, selfless service, the child of true humility","dharam, right living, the child of compassion","naam, the Name, the child of the true Guru","hukam, the order, the child of the Creator"],"a":1,"es":{"q":"En la pauri 16 del Japji Sahib (Guru Granth Sahib, Ang 3), ¿qué dice Guru Nanak que es en verdad el toro mítico (dhaul) que sostiene la tierra?","o":["seva, el servicio desinteresado, hijo de la humildad","dharam, la vida recta, hijo de la compasión","naam, el Nombre, hijo del verdadero Guru","hukam, el orden, hijo del Creador"]}},{"id":"SIKHISM-s03-05","day":210,"d":3,"q":"Someone reads Pauri 28 of Japji Sahib (Guru Granth Sahib, Ang 6), with its yogi's earrings, begging bag and ashes. What does Guru Nanak do with those items there?","o":["requires Sikhs to wear them at the dawn prayer","allows them only for Sikhs who leave their homes","lists them as the dress of the five beloved ones","makes each an inner virtue, like contentment"],"a":3,"es":{"q":"Alguien lee la pauri 28 del Japji Sahib (Guru Granth Sahib, Ang 6), con los aretes, la bolsa de limosna y las cenizas del yogui. ¿Qué hace Guru Nanak allí con esos objetos?","o":["obliga a los sijs a llevarlos en la oración del alba","los permite solo a los sijs que dejan su hogar","los nombra como atuendo de los cinco amados","hace de cada uno una virtud, como el contento"]}},{"id":"SIKHISM-s03-06","day":221,"d":3,"q":"In Pauri 34 of Japji Sahib (Guru Granth Sahib, Ang 7), Guru Nanak calls the earth a dharamsaal. What does that picture say the earth is?","o":["a prison the soul must break out of","a home set up for right action","a waiting room before the next realm","a marketplace where all is sold"],"a":1,"es":{"q":"En la pauri 34 del Japji Sahib (Guru Granth Sahib, Ang 7), Guru Nanak llama a la tierra dharamsaal. ¿Qué dice esa imagen que es la tierra?","o":["una prisión de la que el alma debe huir","un hogar dispuesto para el obrar recto","una sala de espera antes del otro reino","un mercado donde todo se vende"]}}],[{"id":"SIKHISM-s04-01","day":232,"d":3,"q":"after its opening daily prayers, the main body of the Guru Granth Sahib is divided into large sections. what are those sections named for?","o":["the ten Gurus, in their order","the hours of the Sikh daily round","musical measures called raags","the twelve months of the year"],"a":2,"es":{"q":"después de sus oraciones diarias de apertura, el cuerpo principal del Guru Granth Sahib se divide en grandes secciones. ¿por qué llevan su nombre esas secciones?","o":["por los diez Gurus, en su orden","por las horas de la rutina sij diaria","por modos musicales llamados raags","por los doce meses del año"]}},{"id":"SIKHISM-s04-02","day":236,"d":3,"q":"in a salok of Guru Angad in Asa di Var (ang 466), how is haumai, the ego of \"I, me\", described?","o":["a sin that a pilgrimage bath can wash away","a chronic illness that holds its own cure within","a passing mood that simply fades away with age","a fault found only in the worldly, never in seekers"],"a":1,"es":{"q":"en un salok de Guru Angad en Asa di Var (ang 466), ¿cómo se describe el haumai, el ego del \"yo, mí\"?","o":["un pecado que un baño de peregrinación puede lavar","una enfermedad crónica que lleva dentro su propia cura","un estado de ánimo pasajero que se va con la edad","una falta que solo tienen los mundanos, nunca los buscadores"]}},{"id":"SIKHISM-s04-03","day":242,"d":3,"q":"in the Guru Granth Sahib, what separates a gurmukh from a manmukh?","o":["the gurmukh faces the Guru; the manmukh follows their own mind","the gurmukh has taken amrit; the manmukh has not yet taken it","the gurmukh can read Gurmukhi script; the manmukh cannot read it","the gurmukh descends from a Guru's family; the manmukh does not"],"a":0,"es":{"q":"en el Guru Granth Sahib, ¿qué distingue a un gurmukh de un manmukh?","o":["el gurmukh mira al Guru; el manmukh sigue su propia mente","el gurmukh ha tomado amrit; el manmukh todavía no lo ha tomado","el gurmukh sabe leer la escritura gurmukhi; el manmukh no sabe","el gurmukh desciende de la familia de un Guru; el manmukh no"]}},{"id":"SIKHISM-s04-04","day":258,"d":3,"q":"Sheikh Farid, whose saloks and hymns appear in the Guru Granth Sahib, was who?","o":["a Sikh scribe who wrote down Guru Arjan's hymns","a court poet who served Guru Gobind Singh at Anandpur","a son of Guru Nanak who founded the Udasi order","a Chishti Sufi of Pakpattan who wrote in Punjabi"],"a":3,"es":{"q":"el jeque Farid, cuyos saloks e himnos aparecen en el Guru Granth Sahib, ¿quién fue?","o":["un escriba sij que puso por escrito los himnos de Guru Arjan","un poeta de la corte de Guru Gobind Singh en Anandpur","un hijo de Guru Nanak que fundó la orden udasi","un sufí chishti de Pakpattan que escribió en panyabí"]}},{"id":"SIKHISM-s04-05","day":272,"d":3,"q":"at a gurdwara, a young man keeps his hair uncut under a patka and has not yet taken amrit. which term do Sikhs commonly use for him?","o":["keshdhari, one who keeps uncut hair","amritdhari, one who has taken amrit","sahajdhari, one not yet keeping kesh","Nihang, one of the blue-robed orders"],"a":0,"es":{"q":"en un gurdwara, un joven lleva el cabello sin cortar bajo un patka y todavía no ha tomado amrit. ¿qué término usan comúnmente los sijs para él?","o":["keshdhari, quien no se corta el cabello","amritdhari, quien ya ha tomado amrit","sahajdhari, quien aún no guarda el kesh","nihang, de las órdenes de túnica azul"]}},{"id":"SIKHISM-s04-06","day":295,"d":3,"q":"the Singh Sabha movement, begun in Amritsar in 1873, met the worry that Sikhs were losing touch with their tradition mainly through what?","o":["an armed revolt to restore Ranjit Singh's kingdom","schools, Gurmukhi teaching and Sikh publishing","petitions asking the British to leave Punjab","missions sending preachers to Britain and Canada"],"a":1,"es":{"q":"el movimiento Singh Sabha, iniciado en Amritsar en 1873, respondió a la preocupación de que los sijs perdían el contacto con su tradición, sobre todo ¿por qué medio?","o":["una revuelta armada para restaurar el reino de Ranjit Singh","escuelas, enseñanza del gurmukhi y publicaciones sijs","peticiones para que los británicos dejaran el Punyab","misiones que enviaban predicadores a Gran Bretaña y Canadá"]}}],[{"id":"SIKHISM-s05-01","day":336,"d":3,"q":"Jaap Sahib, Guru Gobind Singh's morning praise, moves for long stretches in a meter called bhujang prayat. What motion is that meter named after?","o":["a galloping horse","a gliding snake","a flying eagle","a charging elephant"],"a":1,"es":{"q":"Jaap Sahib, la alabanza matutina de Guru Gobind Singh, avanza por largos tramos en un metro llamado bhujang prayat. ¿En qué movimiento se inspira el nombre de ese metro?","o":["un caballo al galope","una serpiente que se desliza","un águila en vuelo","un elefante que embiste"]}},{"id":"SIKHISM-s05-02","day":335,"d":3,"q":"Jaap Sahib's opening stanza says no one can tell all of the One's names. By what, it says, do the wise name the One?","o":["by the One's form and outward look","by the One's caste and family line","by a secret name told to a few","by the One's deeds in the world"],"a":3,"es":{"q":"La estrofa inicial de Jaap Sahib dice que nadie puede decir todos los nombres del Uno. Según ella, ¿por qué nombran los sabios al Uno?","o":["por la forma y el aspecto exterior del Uno","por la casta y el linaje del Uno","por un nombre secreto que solo saben unos pocos","por las obras del Uno en el mundo"]}},{"id":"SIKHISM-s05-03","day":368,"d":2,"q":"In the Tav Prasad Savaiye, Guru Gobind Singh describes ascetics, yogis and mighty kings, then says \"saach kahoon sun leho sabhai\": I tell the truth, all of you listen. What truth follows?","o":["those who loved found the Lord","those who fasted found the Lord","those who conquered found the Lord","those who studied found the Lord"],"a":0,"es":{"q":"En los Tav Prasad Savaiye, Guru Gobind Singh describe ascetas, yoguis y reyes poderosos, y luego dice \"saach kahoon sun leho sabhai\": digo la verdad, escuchen todos. ¿Qué verdad sigue?","o":["los que amaron encontraron al Señor","los que ayunaron encontraron al Señor","los que conquistaron encontraron al Señor","los que estudiaron encontraron al Señor"]}},{"id":"SIKHISM-s05-04","day":380,"d":2,"q":"Anand Sahib, the hymn of forty pauris in Raag Ramkali in the Guru Granth Sahib, was composed by which Guru?","o":["Guru Nanak, the first Guru","Guru Arjan Dev, the fifth Guru","Guru Amar Das, the third Guru","Guru Ram Das, the fourth Guru"],"a":2,"es":{"q":"Anand Sahib, el himno de cuarenta pauris en Raag Ramkali del Guru Granth Sahib, ¿qué Guru lo compuso?","o":["Guru Nanak, el primer Guru","Guru Arjan Dev, el quinto Guru","Guru Amar Das, el tercer Guru","Guru Ram Das, el cuarto Guru"]}},{"id":"SIKHISM-s05-05","day":386,"d":3,"q":"The sixth pauri of Anand Sahib begins \"anand anand sabh ko kahai\": everyone speaks of bliss. How does it say true bliss is known?","o":["known through wealth and family","known through the True Guru","known through a pilgrimage","known through the forest's quiet"],"a":1,"es":{"q":"La sexta pauri de Anand Sahib empieza \"anand anand sabh ko kahai\": todos hablan de dicha. ¿Cómo dice que se conoce la verdadera dicha?","o":["a través de la riqueza y la familia","a través del Verdadero Guru","a través de una peregrinación","a través de la calma del bosque"]}},{"id":"SIKHISM-s05-06","day":412,"d":3,"q":"Someone says a human life is just a waiting room before the next one. What does Guru Arjan's shabad \"bhaee paraapat maanukh dehureeaa\" (Raag Asa, Ang 12) say a human life is?","o":["a burden to escape from quickly","a matter less than the next birth","the chance to meet the Lord","a test that most people fail"],"a":2,"es":{"q":"Alguien dice que una vida humana es solo una sala de espera antes de la siguiente. ¿Qué dice el shabad de Guru Arjan \"bhaee paraapat maanukh dehureeaa\" (Raag Asa, Ang 12) que es una vida humana?","o":["una carga de la que escapar pronto","algo que importa menos que la próxima vida","la oportunidad de encontrarse con el Señor","una prueba que casi todos reprueban"]}}],[{"id":"SIKHISM-s06-01","day":421,"d":2,"q":"Kirtan Sohila is a short bani of five hymns on Angs 12–13 of the Guru Granth Sahib. According to the Sikh Rehat Maryada, at what time of day is it recited?","o":["at dawn, during the amrit vela","at night, before going to sleep","at midday, before the main daily meal","at sunset, together with Rehras"],"a":1,"es":{"q":"Kirtan Sohila es una bani corta de cinco himnos, en los Ang 12–13 del Guru Granth Sahib. Según el Sikh Rehat Maryada, ¿a qué hora del día se recita?","o":["al amanecer, durante el amrit vela","de noche, antes de irse a dormir","al mediodía, antes de la comida principal","al atardecer, junto con el Rehras"]}},{"id":"SIKHISM-s06-02","day":429,"d":3,"q":"In Guru Nanak's hymn \"Gagan mai thaal\" (Raag Dhanasari, sung in Kirtan Sohila), the sky is the platter, the sun and moon are the lamps and the stars are the pearls. What is the hymn describing?","o":["the heavens the soul crosses after death","the first day on which the world was made","the aarti all creation offers the Creator","the night sky over Guru Nanak's last journey"],"a":2,"es":{"q":"En el himno de Guru Nanak \"Gagan mai thaal\" (Raag Dhanasari, cantado en Kirtan Sohila), el cielo es la bandeja, el sol y la luna son las lámparas y las estrellas son las perlas. ¿Qué describe el himno?","o":["los cielos que cruza el alma tras la muerte","el primer día en que fue hecho el mundo","el aarti que toda la creación ofrece al Creador","el cielo nocturno del último viaje de Guru Nanak"]}},{"id":"SIKHISM-s06-03","day":436,"d":2,"q":"Sukhmani Sahib, the \"jewel of peace,\" begins on Ang 262 of the Guru Granth Sahib in Raag Gauri. Which Guru composed it?","o":["Guru Nanak","Guru Angad","Guru Ram Das","Guru Arjan"],"a":3,"es":{"q":"Sukhmani Sahib, la \"joya de la paz\", comienza en el Ang 262 del Guru Granth Sahib, en Raag Gauri. ¿Qué Gurú la compuso?","o":["Guru Nanak","Guru Angad","Guru Ram Das","Guru Arjan"]}},{"id":"SIKHISM-s06-04","day":457,"d":3,"q":"In Sukhmani Sahib's fifth ashtpadi, a banker lends a man his capital, then takes a little of it back, and the man flies into a rage. What does Guru Arjan use this picture to teach?","o":["all we have is God's trust, to give back without anger","a debt to a lender has to be repaid with full interest","wealth comes from a person's own hard work and effort","God punishes all those who waste what they have been given"],"a":0,"es":{"q":"En la quinta ashtpadi de Sukhmani Sahib, un prestamista le presta su capital a un hombre, luego le pide de vuelta una parte, y el hombre se enfurece. ¿Qué enseña Guru Arjan con esta imagen?","o":["todo lo que tenemos es un préstamo de Dios, para devolverlo sin enojo","una deuda con un prestamista se paga con todos sus intereses","la riqueza viene del propio trabajo y esfuerzo de cada persona","Dios castiga a quienes malgastan lo que se les ha dado"]}},{"id":"SIKHISM-s06-05","day":485,"d":3,"q":"In Sukhmani Sahib's twelfth ashtpadi, Guru Arjan says that as long as a person thinks \"something gets done by me,\" no peace comes to them. Which of the five thieves of Gurbani is he naming?","o":["kaam, lust of the senses","karodh, anger in the mind","lobh, greed for still more","ahankaar, ego and pride"],"a":3,"es":{"q":"En la duodécima ashtpadi de Sukhmani Sahib, Guru Arjan dice que mientras alguien piense \"algo se hace por mí\", no le llega la paz. ¿Cuál de los cinco ladrones del Gurbani está nombrando?","o":["kaam, la lujuria de los sentidos","karodh, la ira en la mente","lobh, la codicia de más y más","ahankaar, el ego y el orgullo"]}},{"id":"SIKHISM-s06-06","day":493,"d":3,"q":"A carpenter earns his bread by fair, hard labor, never by cheating or exploiting anyone, like Bhai Lalo in the janamsakhis. Which of the three pillars of Sikh life does this describe?","o":["naam japna, remembering God","vand chhakna, sharing with all","kirat karni, honest toil","dasvandh, giving a tenth"],"a":2,"es":{"q":"Un carpintero se gana el pan con trabajo justo y duro, sin engañar ni explotar a nadie, como Bhai Lalo en las janamsakhis. ¿Cuál de los tres pilares de la vida sij describe esto?","o":["naam japna, recordar a Dios","vand chhakna, compartir con todos","kirat karni, el trabajo honrado","dasvandh, dar la décima parte"]}}],[{"id":"SIKHISM-s07-01","day":532,"d":1,"q":"Sukhmani Sahib, the \"psalm of peace\" of twenty-four ashtpadis in Raag Gauri of the Guru Granth Sahib, was composed by which Guru?","o":["Guru Nanak Dev","Guru Ram Das","Guru Arjan Dev","Guru Tegh Bahadur"],"a":2,"es":{"q":"Sukhmani Sahib, el \"salmo de la paz\" de veinticuatro ashtpadis en el Raag Gauri del Guru Granth Sahib, fue compuesto por ¿qué Gurú?","o":["Gurú Nanak Dev","Gurú Ram Das","Gurú Arjan Dev","Gurú Tegh Bahadur"]}},{"id":"SIKHISM-s07-02","day":550,"d":3,"q":"A salok in Asa di Var (ang 469) says \"dukh daaroo sukh rog\": pain has become the medicine and pleasure the disease. According to the same salok, why is pleasure called a disease?","o":["pleasure is a punishment for past wrongs","in comfort a person stops longing for the Lord","every kind of enjoyment slowly weakens the body","only those who seek suffering are accepted"],"a":1,"es":{"q":"Un salok del Asa di Var (ang 469) dice \"dukh daaroo sukh rog\": el dolor se volvió la medicina y el placer la enfermedad. Según ese mismo salok, ¿por qué al placer se le llama enfermedad?","o":["el placer es un castigo por faltas pasadas","en la comodidad uno deja de anhelar al Señor","todo disfrute va dañando poco a poco el cuerpo","solo se acepta a quien busca el sufrimiento"]}},{"id":"SIKHISM-s07-03","day":554,"d":3,"q":"In a salok of Asa di Var (ang 471), Guru Nanak asks for a janeu, a sacred thread, with compassion as its cotton, contentment its thread, restraint its knot and truth its twist. What point does the salok make?","o":["a cotton thread must be renewed yearly to stay pure","only those who have taken amrit may wear such a thread","a thread takes effect only once a priest has blessed it","the true thread is made of virtues and never breaks"],"a":3,"es":{"q":"En un salok del Asa di Var (ang 471), Gurú Nanak pide un janeu, un hilo sagrado, con la compasión como algodón, el contento como hilo, la templanza como nudo y la verdad como torsión. ¿Qué enseña el salok?","o":["el hilo de algodón debe renovarse cada año para ser puro","solo quien ha tomado amrit puede usar un hilo así","el hilo solo surte efecto si un sacerdote lo bendice","el hilo verdadero está hecho de virtudes y no se rompe"]}},{"id":"SIKHISM-s07-04","day":587,"d":4,"q":"Which raag section of the Guru Granth Sahib holds hymns by Guru Tegh Bahadur and by no other Guru or saint?","o":["Raag Jaijavanti","Raag Gauri","Raag Sorath","Raag Dhanasri"],"a":0,"es":{"q":"¿Qué sección de raag del Guru Granth Sahib contiene himnos de Gurú Tegh Bahadur y de ningún otro Gurú ni santo?","o":["Raag Jaijavanti","Raag Gauri","Raag Sorath","Raag Dhanasri"]}},{"id":"SIKHISM-s07-05","day":600,"d":3,"q":"Guru Tegh Bahadur's salok \"jag rachnaa sabh jhooth hai\" (ang 1429) calls the created world jhooth, often translated \"false.\" How does the couplet itself explain the word?","o":["it is a trick and does not really exist","it does not stay, like a wall of sand","it is evil and should be fled for the forest","it was made by a power lesser than God"],"a":1,"es":{"q":"El salok de Gurú Tegh Bahadur \"jag rachnaa sabh jhooth hai\" (ang 1429) llama jhooth al mundo creado, palabra que suele traducirse como \"falso\". ¿Cómo explica la palabra el propio dístico?","o":["es un engaño y en realidad no existe","no permanece, como un muro de arena","es malo y hay que huir de él al bosque","lo hizo un poder menor que el de Dios"]}},{"id":"SIKHISM-s07-06","day":595,"d":3,"q":"A manager refuses to intimidate the people who work under her, and also refuses to be intimidated into wrongdoing by a powerful client. Which line of Guru Tegh Bahadur's saloks (ang 1427–1429) does she most closely live out?","o":["one frightens no one and fears no one","the Name is the boat across the world's ocean","praise and blame, gold and iron are alike","whatever is born must perish in time"],"a":0,"es":{"q":"Una gerente se niega a intimidar a quienes trabajan con ella, y también se niega a dejarse intimidar por un cliente poderoso para hacer algo indebido. ¿Qué verso de los saloks de Gurú Tegh Bahadur (ang 1427–1429) vive más de cerca?","o":["no asustar a nadie ni temer a nadie","el Nombre es la barca para cruzar el océano","alabanza y culpa, oro y hierro, son iguales","todo lo que nace ha de perecer un día"]}}],[{"id":"SIKHISM-s08-01","day":691,"d":3,"q":"In 1708 Guru Gobind Singh passed the guruship to the Granth, declaring that there would be no human Guru after him. Where did this happen?","o":["Nanded, by the Godavari river","Anandpur, in the Shivalik hills","Talwandi Sabo, in southern Punjab","Patna, by the Ganges in Bihar"],"a":0,"es":{"q":"En 1708, Guru Gobind Singh entregó la guía de Gurú al Granth y declaró que después de él no habría un Gurú humano. ¿Dónde ocurrió?","o":["Nanded, junto al río Godavari","Anandpur, en los montes Shivalik","Talwandi Sabo, en el sur del Punyab","Patna, junto al Ganges, en Bihar"]}},{"id":"SIKHISM-s08-02","day":618,"d":3,"q":"The opening stanza of the Ardas names the Gurus one by one. What does it say comes to the one who remembers Guru Tegh Bahadur?","o":["pain departs at the very sight of him","the nine treasures come running home","every enemy turns and flees the door","the eighteen powers settle in the house"],"a":1,"es":{"q":"La primera estrofa del Ardas nombra a los Gurús uno por uno. ¿Qué dice que llega a quien recuerda a Guru Tegh Bahadur?","o":["el dolor se va con solo verlo a él","los nueve tesoros llegan corriendo a casa","todo enemigo da la vuelta y huye","los dieciocho poderes se quedan en casa"]}},{"id":"SIKHISM-s08-03","day":621,"d":3,"q":"The Ardas remembers the \"chaalee mukte\", the forty liberated ones. Who were they?","o":["the first forty Sikhs given amrit at Anandpur in 1699","scribes who copied the Adi Granth for distant sangats","Sikhs who left the Guru, came back, fell at Muktsar","Sikhs who dug the sacred pool at Amritsar for Ram Das"],"a":2,"es":{"q":"El Ardas recuerda a los \"chaalee mukte\", los cuarenta liberados. ¿Quiénes fueron?","o":["los primeros cuarenta sijs que recibieron amrit en 1699","escribas que copiaron el Adi Granth para sangats lejanas","sijs que dejaron al Gurú, volvieron, cayeron en Muktsar","sijs que cavaron el estanque sagrado de Amritsar"]}},{"id":"SIKHISM-s08-04","day":635,"d":3,"q":"The Ardas ends \"Nanak naam chardi kala, tere bhaane sarbat da bhala.\" What does its second half, \"tere bhaane sarbat da bhala,\" ask for?","o":["victory for the Khalsa over all its foes","pardon for any slip made in the prayer","the good of all, within God's will","rising spirits for the Sikh sangat alone"],"a":2,"es":{"q":"El Ardas termina \"Nanak naam chardi kala, tere bhaane sarbat da bhala\". ¿Qué pide su segunda mitad, \"tere bhaane sarbat da bhala\"?","o":["la victoria del Khalsa sobre sus enemigos","perdón por cualquier error en la oración","el bien de todos, en la voluntad de Dios","ánimo en alto solo para la sangat sij"]}},{"id":"SIKHISM-s08-05","day":665,"d":3,"q":"In Guru Ram Das's laavan (Raag Suhi, Ang 773–774), the four stanzas sung at the Anand Karaj, what does the fourth round describe?","o":["the call to live a householder's life of dharma","the mind freed of fear by meeting the true Guru","a deep longing for the Lord rising in the heart","the mind at ease in sahaj, one with the Lord"],"a":3,"es":{"q":"En las laavan de Guru Ram Das (Raag Suhi, Ang 773–774), las cuatro estrofas que se cantan en el Anand Karaj, ¿qué describe la cuarta vuelta?","o":["el llamado a vivir el dharma como jefe de hogar","la mente libre de miedo al encontrar al Gurú verdadero","un hondo anhelo del Señor que crece en el corazón","la mente en calma en sahaj, unida al Señor"]}},{"id":"SIKHISM-s08-06","day":640,"d":3,"q":"A Sikh family is about to open a new shop and wants to follow the Sikh Rehat Maryada. What does the Rehat Maryada say is offered before beginning any task?","o":["the Laavan, the four rounds","an Ardas, the standing prayer","the Sohila, the night prayer","the Mool Mantar, said five times"],"a":1,"es":{"q":"Una familia sij está por abrir una tienda nueva y quiere seguir el Sikh Rehat Maryada. ¿Qué dice el Rehat Maryada que se ofrece antes de empezar cualquier tarea?","o":["las Laavan, las cuatro vueltas","un Ardas, la oración de pie","el Sohila, la oración de la noche","el Mool Mantar, dicho cinco veces"]}}],[{"id":"SIKHISM-s09-01","day":697,"d":2,"q":"By Sikh tradition, who wrote out the Adi Granth as its scribe while Guru Arjan compiled it in 1604?","o":["Baba Buddha","Bhai Mani Singh","Bhai Gurdas","Bhai Nand Lal"],"a":2,"es":{"q":"Según la tradición sij, ¿quién escribió como escriba el Adi Granth mientras Gurú Arjan lo compilaba en 1604?","o":["Baba Buddha","Bhai Mani Singh","Bhai Gurdas","Bhai Nand Lal"]}},{"id":"SIKHISM-s09-02","day":718,"d":3,"q":"Besides Gurbani, the Sikh Rehat Maryada allows kirtan in the congregation from the works of which two poets?","o":["Bhai Gurdas and Bhai Nand Lal","Bhai Mani Singh and Bhai Gurdas","Bhai Nand Lal and Bhai Mani Singh","Bhai Santokh Singh and Bhai Gurdas"],"a":0,"es":{"q":"Además del Gurbani, el Sikh Rehat Maryada permite el kirtan en la congregación con las obras de ¿cuáles dos poetas?","o":["Bhai Gurdas y Bhai Nand Lal","Bhai Mani Singh y Bhai Gurdas","Bhai Nand Lal y Bhai Mani Singh","Bhai Santokh Singh y Bhai Gurdas"]}},{"id":"SIKHISM-s09-03","day":706,"d":3,"q":"In the sakhi of Guru Nanak at Multan, the city's holy men send him a cup brimming with milk. What does his floating a jasmine flower on it say?","o":["he will leave Multan without entering the city","he will stay lightly, adding fragrance, crowding no one","he claims the city's holy seat for his own teaching","he returns their gift to show he needs nothing at all"],"a":1,"es":{"q":"En la sakhi de Gurú Nanak en Multán, los santones de la ciudad le envían una taza llena de leche hasta el borde. ¿Qué dice él al hacer flotar una flor de jazmín encima?","o":["que se irá de Multán sin entrar en la ciudad","que se quedará con ligereza, dando aroma, sin desplazar a nadie","que reclama el asiento santo de la ciudad para su enseñanza","que les devuelve el regalo para mostrar que no necesita nada"]}},{"id":"SIKHISM-s09-04","day":740,"d":2,"q":"In the Sikh story of the cowherd boy who became Baba Buddha, why does Guru Nanak call him 'buddha', the old one?","o":["he was the eldest of Nanak's first circle of disciples","he had been born, the story says, with white hair","he was chosen as headman of his village council","he saw that death takes the young as well as the old"],"a":3,"es":{"q":"En la historia sij del niño pastor que llegó a ser Baba Buddha, ¿por qué Gurú Nanak lo llama 'buddha', el viejo?","o":["era el mayor del primer círculo de discípulos de Nanak","según la historia, había nacido con el pelo blanco","lo eligieron jefe del consejo de su aldea","vio que la muerte se lleva a jóvenes y viejos por igual"]}},{"id":"SIKHISM-s09-05","day":758,"d":3,"q":"In his hymns in the Guru Granth Sahib, Kabir leaves Kashi to die at Maghar. What point does that move make?","o":["Maghar was the town where his teacher Ramanand lived","the rulers of Kashi had banished him from their city","release comes from the Lord, not where one dies","he wished to be buried among his weaver kinsfolk"],"a":2,"es":{"q":"En sus himnos del Gurú Granth Sahib, Kabir deja Kashi para morir en Maghar. ¿Qué quiere mostrar con eso?","o":["Maghar era el pueblo donde vivía su maestro Ramanand","los gobernantes de Kashi lo habían desterrado","la liberación viene del Señor, no de dónde se muere","quería ser enterrado entre sus parientes tejedores"]}},{"id":"SIKHISM-s09-06","day":763,"d":3,"q":"Farid's salok on Ang 1378 says not to write black marks against others. A friend keeps a running list of a coworker's faults. Where would that salok turn the friend?","o":["to taking the list to an elder to judge it fairly","to praying each day that the coworker will change","to forgiving the faults but keeping the list safe","to looking at the faults under their own collar"],"a":3,"es":{"q":"El salok de Farid en el Ang 1378 dice que no escribas marcas negras contra otros. Un amigo lleva una lista de las faltas de un compañero de trabajo. ¿Hacia dónde lo dirigiría ese salok?","o":["a llevar la lista a un mayor para que la juzgue","a orar cada día para que el compañero cambie","a perdonar las faltas pero guardar la lista","a mirar las faltas bajo su propio cuello"]}}],[{"id":"SIKHISM-s10-01","day":782,"d":2,"q":"The Guru Granth Sahib keeps a hymn by Bhagat Dhanna in Raag Dhanasri (Ang 695) that asks God plainly for lentils, flour, ghee, shoes and a milk cow. What does Sikh tradition remember Dhanna as by trade?","o":["a farmer who worked his own fields","a weaver who worked at a handloom","a barber who served at a king's court","a cobbler who worked with leather"],"a":0,"es":{"q":"El Guru Granth Sahib guarda un himno de Bhagat Dhanna en Raag Dhanasri (Ang 695) que le pide a Dios, sin rodeos, lentejas, harina, ghee, zapatos y una vaca lechera. ¿Qué oficio le atribuye la tradición sij a Dhanna?","o":["un campesino que trabajaba sus tierras","un tejedor que trabajaba en un telar","un barbero que servía en la corte de un rey","un zapatero que trabajaba el cuero"]}},{"id":"SIKHISM-s10-02","day":791,"d":3,"q":"Near the end of the Guru Granth Sahib (from Ang 1389), the Bhatts' swayye praise the Gurus one after another, and Bhatt Mathura describes the light passing from Guru Nanak to Angad, Amar Das, Ram Das and Arjan. What teaching do these verses express?","o":["each Guru founded a separate school with its own teaching","the Gurus were kings to be praised for their wealth and rule","only Guru Nanak's own verses carry the light of the Guru","the Guru is one light, the same in each Guru who follows"],"a":3,"es":{"q":"Cerca del final del Guru Granth Sahib (desde el Ang 1389), los swayye de los Bhatts alaban a los Gurús uno tras otro, y Bhatt Mathura describe la luz que pasa de Guru Nanak a Angad, Amar Das, Ram Das y Arjan. ¿Qué enseñanza expresan estos versos?","o":["cada Gurú fundó una escuela distinta con su propia enseñanza","los Gurús eran reyes alabados por su riqueza y su poder","solo los versos de Guru Nanak llevan la luz del Gurú","el Gurú es una sola luz, la misma en cada Gurú que sigue"]}},{"id":"SIKHISM-s10-03","day":829,"d":3,"q":"At Khidrana in 1705, the dying Mahan Singh asked Guru Gobind Singh to tear up the bedava, and the place became Muktsar. What was the bedava?","o":["a treaty the Guru had made with the Mughal commanders","a list of Sikhs the Sirhind governor had ordered seized","a letter the Majha Sikhs had signed disowning the Guru","a hukamnama calling the Sikhs of Majha to Anandpur"],"a":2,"es":{"q":"En Khidrana, en 1705, Mahan Singh, moribundo, le pidió a Guru Gobind Singh que rompiera el bedava, y el lugar pasó a llamarse Muktsar. ¿Qué era el bedava?","o":["un tratado que el Gurú había hecho con los jefes mogoles","una lista de sijs que el gobernador de Sirhind mandó apresar","una carta firmada por los sijs de Majha que renegaba del Gurú","un hukamnama que llamaba a los sijs de Majha a Anandpur"]}},{"id":"SIKHISM-s10-04","day":838,"d":3,"q":"When Guru Gobind Singh sent Banda Singh Bahadur from Nanded to Punjab in 1708, tradition says he gave him five arrows from his quiver, along with five Sikhs, a drum, a banner and letters (hukamnamas). What did the arrows mainly signify?","o":["the weapons he was to use in his first battle at Samana","that Banda was sent with the Guru's blessing and authority","that Banda had been named as the next Guru of the Sikh panth","payment for his years of service to the Guru at Nanded"],"a":1,"es":{"q":"Cuando Guru Gobind Singh envió a Banda Singh Bahadur de Nanded al Punyab en 1708, la tradición dice que le dio cinco flechas de su carcaj, junto con cinco sijs, un tambor, un estandarte y cartas (hukamnamas). ¿Qué significaban sobre todo las flechas?","o":["las armas que debía usar en su primera batalla, en Samana","que Banda iba con la bendición y la autoridad del Gurú","que Banda había sido nombrado el siguiente Gurú de los sijs","el pago por sus años de servicio al Gurú en Nanded"]}},{"id":"SIKHISM-s10-05","day":842,"d":3,"q":"A landlord keeps most of the harvest that tenant farmers plowed, sowed and reaped. In the janamsakhi story of Guru Nanak at Saidpur, which food would that grain be most like?","o":["the rich feast Malik Bhago held for holy men","the coarse bread Bhai Lalo the carpenter offered","the langar food Mata Khivi served at Khadur","the karah parshad shared at the close of a diwan"],"a":0,"es":{"q":"Un terrateniente se queda con la mayor parte de la cosecha que los campesinos arrendatarios araron, sembraron y segaron. En el relato de los janamsakhis sobre Guru Nanak en Saidpur, ¿a qué comida se parecería más ese grano?","o":["al rico banquete que Malik Bhago ofreció a los santos","al pan sencillo que ofreció Bhai Lalo, el carpintero","a la comida del langar que Mata Khivi servía en Khadur","al karah parshad que se reparte al cierre de un diwan"]}},{"id":"SIKHISM-s10-06","day":851,"d":3,"q":"Bhai Mani Singh had promised the Lahore governor a fee for letting Sikhs gather at Amritsar for Diwali, to be paid from the offerings. Why could he not pay it?","o":["he spent the offerings on feeding the large crowds who came","he told Sikhs to stay away on hearing of a planned attack","the governor raised the fee once the gathering began","heavy rains kept the Sikhs from reaching Amritsar"],"a":1,"es":{"q":"Bhai Mani Singh le había prometido al gobernador de Lahore una cuota por dejar que los sijs se reunieran en Amritsar para Diwali, que pagaría con las ofrendas. ¿Por qué no pudo pagarla?","o":["gastó las ofrendas en dar de comer a la gente que vino","pidió a los sijs no ir al saber de un ataque planeado","el gobernador subió la cuota cuando empezó la reunión","unas lluvias fuertes impidieron a los sijs llegar a Amritsar"]}}],[{"id":"SIKHISM-s11-01","day":905,"d":2,"q":"When his father Maha Singh died in 1792, the twelve-year-old Ranjit Singh became chief of which misl?","o":["the Bhangi misl","the Kanhaiya misl","the Sukerchakia misl","the Faizullapuria misl"],"a":2,"es":{"q":"Cuando murió su padre, Maha Singh, en 1792, Ranjit Singh, con doce años, quedó como jefe de ¿qué misl?","o":["el misl Bhangi","el misl Kanhaiya","el misl Sukerchakia","el misl Faizullapuria"]}},{"id":"SIKHISM-s11-02","day":900,"d":3,"q":"In the misl period, the Sarbat Khalsa met at Amritsar, usually at Vaisakhi and Diwali, and made decisions before the Guru Granth Sahib that bound every band. What was such a decision called?","o":["a gurmata","a rehitnama","a janamsakhi","a dharamsal"],"a":0,"es":{"q":"En la época de los misls, el Sarbat Khalsa se reunía en Amritsar, por lo general en Vaisakhi y Diwali, y tomaba decisiones ante el Guru Granth Sahib que obligaban a todas las bandas. ¿Cómo se llamaba una decisión así?","o":["un gurmata","un rehitnama","un janamsakhi","un dharamsal"]}},{"id":"SIKHISM-s11-03","day":910,"d":3,"q":"Maharaja Ranjit Singh ruled Punjab as the Sarkar-e-Khalsa, yet his Nanakshahi coins left off his own name. What did their Persian verse do in its place?","o":["named the Mughal emperor in Delhi as the true sovereign","listed the misl chiefs who shared the rule of Punjab","recorded his treaty of friendship with the British","gave the victory to Guru Nanak and Guru Gobind Singh"],"a":3,"es":{"q":"El Maharaja Ranjit Singh gobernó el Panyab como el Sarkar-e-Khalsa, pero sus monedas nanakshahi no llevaban su propio nombre. ¿Qué hacía en su lugar su verso persa?","o":["nombraba al emperador mogol de Delhi como el verdadero soberano","enumeraba a los jefes de misl que compartían el gobierno del Panyab","registraba su tratado de amistad con los británicos","daba la victoria a Guru Nanak y a Guru Gobind Singh"]}},{"id":"SIKHISM-s11-04","day":915,"d":3,"q":"Sikh tradition says Akali Phula Singh, serving at the Akal Takht, summoned Maharaja Ranjit Singh for a breach of Sikh discipline, and the Maharaja came and accepted his penance. What does the story show?","o":["the Maharaja could appoint and dismiss the Akal Takht's leaders","even the ruler was answerable to the Khalsa at the Akal Takht","the Akal Takht dealt only with war and land, never with conduct","a penance at the Akal Takht could be bought off with a gift of land"],"a":1,"es":{"q":"La tradición sij cuenta que Akali Phula Singh, que servía en el Akal Takht, llamó al Maharaja Ranjit Singh por faltar a la disciplina sij, y que el Maharaja acudió y aceptó su penitencia. ¿Qué muestra el relato?","o":["el Maharaja podía nombrar y destituir a los líderes del Akal Takht","aun el gobernante respondía ante el Khalsa en el Akal Takht","el Akal Takht trataba solo de guerra y tierras, nunca de conducta","una penitencia del Akal Takht se podía saldar con un regalo de tierras"]}},{"id":"SIKHISM-s11-05","day":925,"d":4,"q":"In a salok in the Guru Granth Sahib (Ang 787, Var Suhi), Guru Amar Das says that women who burn on their husband's pyre are not true satis. Who does he say is truly called a sati?","o":["a woman who burns with her husband to prove her loyalty","a woman who lives in virtue and contentment, serving God","a woman who leaves her home to wander as a renunciant","a woman who keeps a vow of silence for the rest of her life"],"a":1,"es":{"q":"En un salok del Guru Granth Sahib (Ang 787, Var Suhi), Guru Amar Das dice que las mujeres que se queman en la pira de su esposo no son verdaderas satis. ¿A quién llama él de verdad sati?","o":["a la mujer que arde con su esposo para probar su lealtad","a la que vive con bondad y contento, sirviendo al Señor","a la mujer que deja su casa para vagar como renunciante","a la que guarda un voto de silencio por el resto de su vida"]}},{"id":"SIKHISM-s11-06","day":895,"d":2,"q":"A traveller in an unfamiliar town sees a tall pole wrapped in saffron cloth, flying a triangular saffron flag with the Khanda emblem. Going by the Sikh Rehat Maryada, what does it tell her?","o":["a Sikh family nearby is mourning a death","a Sikh regiment is stationed in the town","a gurdwara is here, open to all who come","a Gurpurab fair will be held here this week"],"a":2,"es":{"q":"Una viajera, en un pueblo que no conoce, ve un poste alto envuelto en tela azafrán, con una bandera triangular azafrán que lleva el emblema del Khanda. Según el Sikh Rehat Maryada, ¿qué le indica?","o":["una familia sij cercana está de luto por una muerte","un regimiento sij está acuartelado en el pueblo","aquí hay un gurdwara, abierto a todos","esta semana habrá aquí una feria de Gurpurab"]}}],[{"id":"SIKHISM-s12-01","day":974,"d":2,"q":"In the Sikh wedding rite, Anand Karaj, the four lavan sung as the couple walks around the Guru Granth Sahib were composed by which Guru?","o":["Guru Amar Das, the third Guru","Guru Arjan Dev, the fifth Guru","Guru Ram Das, the fourth Guru","Guru Nanak Dev, the first Guru"],"a":2,"es":{"q":"En el rito de boda sij, el Anand Karaj, ¿qué Gurú compuso las cuatro lavan que se cantan mientras la pareja camina alrededor del Gurú Granth Sahib?","o":["Gurú Amar Das, el tercer Gurú","Gurú Arjan Dev, el quinto Gurú","Gurú Ram Das, el cuarto Gurú","Gurú Nanak Dev, el primer Gurú"]}},{"id":"SIKHISM-s12-02","day":985,"d":3,"q":"In the Nankana Sahib massacre of February 1921, which leader of a band of gurdwara reformers does Sikh memory say was tied to a jand tree and burned?","o":["Bhai Lachhman Singh","Baba Kharak Singh","Master Tara Singh","Professor Teja Singh"],"a":0,"es":{"q":"En la masacre de Nankana Sahib de febrero de 1921, ¿a qué líder de un grupo de reformistas de los gurdwaras, según la memoria sij, ataron a un árbol jand y quemaron?","o":["Bhai Lachhman Singh","Baba Kharak Singh","Master Tara Singh","el profesor Teja Singh"]}},{"id":"SIKHISM-s12-03","day":976,"d":3,"q":"In 1913 an outer wall of Gurdwara Rakab Ganj in Delhi was torn down to make way for the new capital. Why is that ground so sacred to Sikhs?","o":["It is where Guru Tegh Bahadur was beheaded in 1675","It is where Guru Tegh Bahadur's body was cremated","It is where Guru Har Krishan tended the sick of Delhi","It is where Mata Sundari lived after leaving Anandpur"],"a":1,"es":{"q":"En 1913 se derribó un muro exterior del Gurdwara Rakab Ganj, en Delhi, para abrir paso a la nueva capital. ¿Por qué ese terreno es tan sagrado para los sijs?","o":["Es donde decapitaron a Gurú Tegh Bahadur en 1675","Es donde se cremó el cuerpo de Gurú Tegh Bahadur","Es donde Gurú Har Krishan atendió a los enfermos de Delhi","Es donde vivió Mata Sundari después de dejar Anandpur"]}},{"id":"SIKHISM-s12-04","day":986,"d":3,"q":"In the 1921-22 'keys affair', how did Sikhs win back the keys of the toshakhana (treasury) of the Golden Temple, Harmandir Sahib, from the British government?","o":["through a ruling of the Lahore High Court","through a payment raised by the sangat","through an appeal by the Maharaja of Patiala","through peaceful protest and mass arrests"],"a":3,"es":{"q":"En el 'asunto de las llaves' de 1921-22, ¿cómo recuperaron los sijs, del gobierno británico, las llaves del toshakhana (tesoro) del Templo Dorado, Harmandir Sahib?","o":["con un fallo del Tribunal Superior de Lahore","con un pago reunido entre toda la sangat","con una petición del maharajá de Patiala","con protesta pacífica y arrestos masivos"]}},{"id":"SIKHISM-s12-05","day":1054,"d":3,"q":"In the Sikh story recalled each Maghi at Muktsar, why does Guru Gobind Singh tear up the bedava, the letter in which a band of Sikhs disowned him?","o":["The Mughal governor had sworn to grant them safe passage","The men who signed it came back and died defending him","Mai Bhago had paid a fine on the deserters' behalf","The signers had all taken amrit again at Anandpur"],"a":1,"es":{"q":"En la historia sij que se recuerda cada Maghi en Muktsar, ¿por qué Gurú Gobind Singh rompe el bedava, la carta en que un grupo de sijs renegó de él?","o":["El gobernador mogol les había jurado un paso seguro","Los firmantes volvieron y murieron defendiéndolo","Mai Bhago había pagado una multa por los desertores","Los firmantes habían vuelto a tomar amrit en Anandpur"]}},{"id":"SIKHISM-s12-06","day":990,"d":4,"q":"The hereditary custodian of a historic gurdwara listed under the Sikh Gurdwaras Act of 1925 says he may pass the shrine to his son. Under the Act, who oversees the shrine's management instead?","o":["a manager named by the Punjab government","the son, once the town's sangat agrees","a board whose members Sikh voters elect","the Jathedar of the Akal Takht alone"],"a":2,"es":{"q":"El custodio hereditario de un gurdwara histórico incluido en la Ley de Gurdwaras Sijs de 1925 dice que puede dejarle el santuario a su hijo. Según la ley, ¿quién supervisa en cambio la administración del santuario?","o":["un administrador nombrado por el gobierno del Panyab","el hijo, si la sangat del pueblo está de acuerdo","una junta cuyos miembros eligen los votantes sijs","el Jathedar del Akal Takht, por su propia cuenta"]}}],[{"id":"SIKHISM-s13-01","day":1063,"d":2,"q":"In a shabad of the Guru Granth Sahib, what does the word 'rahao' written after a line mark?","o":["the Guru who wrote it, given by number","the raga in which the hymn is to be sung","the refrain, the hymn's central line","the last verse, where the poet signs it"],"a":2,"es":{"q":"En un shabad del Guru Granth Sahib, ¿qué marca la palabra 'rahao' escrita después de una línea?","o":["el Gurú que lo escribió, dado por número","el raga en que debe cantarse el himno","el estribillo, el centro del himno","el último verso, donde firma el poeta"]}},{"id":"SIKHISM-s13-02","day":1065,"d":3,"q":"Inside each raga section of the Guru Granth Sahib, how are the hymns ordered?","o":["the Bhagats' hymns first, then the Gurus' after them","the Gurus' hymns by Mahala, then the Bhagats'","by year of writing, Gurus and Bhagats mixed together","by the first letter of each hymn, in Gurmukhi order"],"a":1,"es":{"q":"Dentro de cada sección de raga del Guru Granth Sahib, ¿cómo están ordenados los himnos?","o":["primero los himnos de los Bhagats, luego los de los Gurús","primero los de los Gurús, por Mahala, luego los Bhagats","por año de escritura, Gurús y Bhagats mezclados","por la primera letra de cada himno, en orden gurmukhi"]}},{"id":"SIKHISM-s13-03","day":1126,"d":3,"q":"In the Guru Granth Sahib, whose hymns make up the whole of Raag Jaijavanti, the last raga section?","o":["Guru Tegh Bahadur, the ninth Guru","Guru Arjan Dev, the fifth Guru","Bhagat Kabir, the weaver of Banaras","Guru Nanak Dev, the first Guru"],"a":0,"es":{"q":"En el Guru Granth Sahib, ¿de quién son todos los himnos de Raag Jaijavanti, la última sección de raga?","o":["Guru Tegh Bahadur, el noveno Gurú","Guru Arjan Dev, el quinto Gurú","Bhagat Kabir, el tejedor de Benarés","Guru Nanak Dev, el primer Gurú"]}},{"id":"SIKHISM-s13-04","day":1114,"d":3,"q":"A gurdwara is planning kirtan for the coming of spring. Which raga of the Guru Granth Sahib does Sikh tradition sing in that season?","o":["Raag Malar","Raag Prabhati","Raag Basant","Raag Sarang"],"a":2,"es":{"q":"Un gurdwara prepara el kirtan para la llegada de la primavera. ¿Qué raga del Guru Granth Sahib canta la tradición sij en esa estación?","o":["Raag Malar","Raag Prabhati","Raag Basant","Raag Sarang"]}},{"id":"SIKHISM-s13-05","day":1136,"d":3,"q":"In the Sidh Gosht (Raag Ramkali), when the yogis urge Guru Nanak to take up their earrings and patched coat, how does he answer?","o":["he wears them for a while to honor his hosts","he asks the yogis to answer his questions first","he accepts them as a gift and joins their order","he makes them inner: the Word is the earring"],"a":3,"es":{"q":"En el Sidh Gosht (Raag Ramkali), cuando los yoguis animan a Guru Nanak a llevar sus aretes y su manto de retazos, ¿cómo responde?","o":["los usa un tiempo para honrar a sus anfitriones","pide a los yoguis que antes respondan sus preguntas","los acepta como regalo y se une a su orden","los vuelve signos internos: la Palabra es el arete"]}},{"id":"SIKHISM-s13-06","day":1139,"d":3,"q":"In the Sidh Gosht, Guru Nanak answers the yogis' question about his guru with 'sabad guru, surat dhun chela.' What does this line say?","o":["the Word is the Guru; attention to it the disciple","a living sage is the Guru; Nanak is his disciple","the breath is the Guru; holding it still the disciple","the pandit is the Guru; his student is the disciple"],"a":0,"es":{"q":"En el Sidh Gosht, Guru Nanak responde a la pregunta de los yoguis sobre su gurú con 'sabad guru, surat dhun chela'. ¿Qué dice esta línea?","o":["la Palabra es el Gurú; la atención a ella, el discípulo","un sabio vivo es el Gurú; Nanak es su discípulo","la respiración es el Gurú; retenerla, el discípulo","el pandit es el Gurú; su alumno es el discípulo"]}}],[{"id":"SIKHISM-s14-01","day":1159,"d":2,"q":"Guru Nanak's Babarvani hymns (in Raag Asa and Raag Tilang) respond to which historical event?","o":["Babur's invasion of Punjab and the sack of Saidpur","Aurangzeb's order to execute Guru Tegh Bahadur in Delhi","Nadir Shah's raid that plundered Delhi and the Punjab","Ahmad Shah Abdali's attack on the Harmandir at Amritsar"],"a":0,"es":{"q":"¿A qué hecho histórico responden los himnos Babarvani de Guru Nanak (en Raag Asa y Raag Tilang)?","o":["La invasión del Punyab por Babur y el saqueo de Saidpur","La orden de Aurangzeb de ejecutar a Guru Tegh Bahadur en Delhi","El ataque de Nadir Shah que saqueó Delhi y el Punyab","El ataque de Ahmad Shah Abdali al Harmandir de Amritsar"]}},{"id":"SIKHISM-s14-02","day":1180,"d":3,"q":"In a salok of Guru Angad in Asa di Var (Ang 466), how is haumai, ego, described?","o":["a passing mood that fades away on its own with age","a curse that only fasting and pilgrimage can remove","a useful strength once it is turned toward service","a deep, chronic illness whose cure lies within it"],"a":3,"es":{"q":"En un salok de Guru Angad en la Asa di Var (Ang 466), ¿cómo se describe haumai, el ego?","o":["un estado de ánimo pasajero que se va solo con la edad","una maldición que solo el ayuno y la peregrinación quitan","una fuerza útil cuando se dirige hacia el servicio","una enfermedad honda y crónica que lleva su cura dentro"]}},{"id":"SIKHISM-s14-03","day":1185,"d":3,"q":"In his Var in Raag Suhi (Ang 787), Guru Amar Das takes up the word sati, used for a widow who died on her husband's funeral pyre. Whom does he call a true sati?","o":["one who burns with her husband's body to prove her loyalty","one who lives in virtue and contentment, serving her Lord","one who leaves her home for a life of wandering and begging","one who gives all her wealth to priests in her husband's name"],"a":1,"es":{"q":"En su Var en Raag Suhi (Ang 787), Guru Amar Das retoma la palabra sati, usada para la viuda que moría en la pira funeraria de su esposo. ¿A quién llama una verdadera sati?","o":["a la que arde con el cuerpo de su esposo para probar su lealtad","a la que vive con virtud y contento, sirviendo a su Señor","a la que deja su hogar para vivir errante y pidiendo limosna","a la que da sus bienes a los sacerdotes en nombre del esposo"]}},{"id":"SIKHISM-s14-04","day":1186,"d":3,"q":"A man keeps steering by his own will and cleverness and turns away from the Guru's word. In Guru Amar Das's hymns, what is such a person called?","o":["a manmukh, one turned to the self","a gurmukh, one turned toward the Guru","a sachiara, one who lives in truth","a sevadar, one who serves the sangat"],"a":0,"es":{"q":"Un hombre se guía por su propia voluntad y astucia y le da la espalda a la palabra del Guru. En los himnos de Guru Amar Das, ¿cómo se llama a esa persona?","o":["un manmukh, alguien vuelto hacia sí mismo","un gurmukh, alguien vuelto hacia el Guru","un sachiara, alguien que vive en la verdad","un sevadar, alguien que sirve a la sangat"]}},{"id":"SIKHISM-s14-05","day":1208,"d":2,"q":"In the Mundavani, Guru Arjan's seal near the close of the Guru Granth Sahib (Ang 1429), which three things are placed on the plate (thal)?","o":["honest work, remembrance and sharing","service, humility and fearlessness","truth, contentment and reflection","prayer, fasting and holy pilgrimage"],"a":2,"es":{"q":"En el Mundavani, el sello de Guru Arjan cerca del final del Guru Granth Sahib (Ang 1429), ¿qué tres cosas se ponen en el plato (thal)?","o":["trabajo honesto, recordar y dar","servicio, humildad y valentía","verdad, contento y reflexión","oración, ayuno y peregrinación"]}},{"id":"SIKHISM-s14-06","day":1220,"d":3,"q":"Near the end of the Guru Granth Sahib (Ang 1429), Guru Tegh Bahadur's saloks say that even Ram and Ravan have passed away. What contrast do these saloks draw?","o":["evil kings pass, but righteous kings like Ram live on","the body passes, but a family's name lives on in its sons","kingdoms pass, but the Name and the holy ones remain","the world passes, but heroes' fame lives on in the epics"],"a":2,"es":{"q":"Cerca del final del Guru Granth Sahib (Ang 1429), los saloks de Guru Tegh Bahadur dicen que hasta Ram y Ravan ya pasaron. ¿Qué contraste trazan esos saloks?","o":["los reyes malos pasan, pero los justos como Ram perduran","el cuerpo pasa, pero el apellido perdura en los hijos","reyes y reinos pasan, pero el Nombre y los santos quedan","el mundo pasa, pero la fama de los héroes vive en las epopeyas"]}}],[{"id":"SIKHISM-s15-01","day":1258,"d":3,"q":"Under the Sikh Rehat Maryada, kirtan in the sangat is to be of Gurbani or of the works that explain it, written by which two Sikh poets?","o":["Bhai Mani Singh and Bhai Bala","Bhai Vir Singh and Kahn Singh","Bhai Gurdas and Bhai Nand Lal","Bhai Santokh Singh and Sainapati"],"a":2,"es":{"q":"Según el Sikh Rehat Maryada, el kirtan en la sangat debe ser de Gurbani o de las obras que lo explican, escritas por ¿qué dos poetas sijs?","o":["Bhai Mani Singh y Bhai Bala","Bhai Vir Singh y Kahn Singh","Bhai Gurdas y Bhai Nand Lal","Bhai Santokh Singh y Sainapati"]}},{"id":"SIKHISM-s15-02","day":1262,"d":2,"q":"According to the Sikh Rehat Maryada, what is karah prashad, the sacred sweet shared in the gurdwara, made from?","o":["wheat flour, sugar and clarified butter in equal parts","rice, milk and sugar, simmered slowly in an iron pan","semolina, jaggery and sesame oil, with cardamom added","chickpea flour, honey and butter, flavored with saffron"],"a":0,"es":{"q":"Según el Sikh Rehat Maryada, ¿de qué se hace el karah prashad, el dulce sagrado que se comparte en el gurdwara?","o":["harina, azúcar y mantequilla clarificada en partes iguales","arroz, leche y azúcar, cocidos despacio en una olla de hierro","sémola, jaggery y aceite de sésamo, con cardamomo añadido","harina de garbanzo, miel y mantequilla, con sabor a azafrán"]}},{"id":"SIKHISM-s15-03","day":1306,"d":3,"q":"A pilgrim bathes in sacred waters a hundred thousand times, hoping to make the mind pure. Reading soch in the first pauri of the Japji (Ang 1) as ritual cleansing, what does Guru Nanak say of this?","o":["outward washing, however often, cannot purify the mind","a hundred thousand baths will at last purify the mind","bathing cleans the body, and silence then cleans the mind","bathing purifies the mind when done on holy festival days"],"a":0,"es":{"q":"Un peregrino se baña en aguas sagradas cien mil veces, esperando purificar la mente. Si se lee soch en el primer pauri del Japji (Ang 1) como limpieza ritual, ¿qué dice Guru Nanak de esto?","o":["lavarse por fuera, por más veces que sea, no purifica la mente","cien mil baños terminarán al fin por purificar la mente","el baño limpia el cuerpo, y luego el silencio limpia la mente","el baño purifica la mente si se hace en días de fiesta sagrados"]}},{"id":"SIKHISM-s15-04","day":1334,"d":3,"q":"The town of Muktsar, once called Khidrana, takes its name (\"pool of liberation\") from which event in Guru Gobind Singh's life?","o":["the founding of the Khalsa with the first five initiated","his blessing of the forty who came back and fell there","the martyrdom of his two younger sons at Sirhind","his completion of the Granth with Bhai Mani Singh"],"a":1,"es":{"q":"La ciudad de Muktsar, antes llamada Khidrana, toma su nombre (\"estanque de la liberación\") de ¿qué hecho en la vida de Guru Gobind Singh?","o":["la fundación del Khalsa con los primeros cinco iniciados","su bendición a los cuarenta que volvieron y cayeron allí","el martirio de sus dos hijos menores en Sirhind","la terminación del Granth junto a Bhai Mani Singh"]}},{"id":"SIKHISM-s15-05","day":1338,"d":3,"q":"At Bakala, after Guru Har Krishan's death, many men claimed to be the next Guru. In Sikh tradition, why did the trader Makhan Shah proclaim Tegh Bahadur the true Guru?","o":["Tegh Bahadur was named in a letter from Guru Har Krishan","Tegh Bahadur won a public debate against the other claimants","Tegh Bahadur was chosen by a vote of the Bakala sangat","Tegh Bahadur alone asked for the full offering he had vowed"],"a":3,"es":{"q":"En Bakala, tras la muerte de Guru Har Krishan, muchos hombres decían ser el siguiente Guru. Según la tradición sij, ¿por qué el comerciante Makhan Shah proclamó a Tegh Bahadur como el verdadero Guru?","o":["Tegh Bahadur fue nombrado en una carta de Guru Har Krishan","Tegh Bahadur ganó un debate público contra los otros aspirantes","Tegh Bahadur fue elegido por votación de la sangat de Bakala","solo Tegh Bahadur le pidió la ofrenda entera prometida"]}},{"id":"SIKHISM-s15-06","day":1342,"d":4,"q":"The Guru Granth Sahib holds a var (ballad) in Raag Ramkali credited to the minstrels Satta and Balwand (Ang 966). What is its main theme?","o":["Guru Nanak's long journeys to Mecca and Baghdad","the building of the Harmandir's pool at Amritsar","the one light passing from each Guru to the next","Guru Hargobind's battles against Mughal forces"],"a":2,"es":{"q":"El Guru Granth Sahib contiene una var (balada) en Raag Ramkali atribuida a los juglares Satta y Balwand (Ang 966). ¿Cuál es su tema principal?","o":["los largos viajes de Guru Nanak a La Meca y Bagdad","la construcción del estanque del Harmandir en Amritsar","la misma luz que pasa de cada Guru al siguiente","las batallas de Guru Hargobind contra fuerzas mogolas"]}}],[{"id":"SIKHISM-s16-01","day":1363,"d":4,"q":"Near the end of the Guru Granth Sahib, the name Waheguru rings out again and again in Swayye (praise verses) by whom?","o":["the Bhatts, bards of the Gurus' court","Bhagat Kabir, the weaver of Banaras","Sheikh Farid, the Sufi of Pakpattan","Balwand and Satta, the court musicians"],"a":0,"es":{"q":"Cerca del final del Guru Granth Sahib, el nombre Waheguru resuena una y otra vez en los Swayye (versos de alabanza) de ¿quién?","o":["los Bhatts, bardos de la corte de los Gurús","Bhagat Kabir, el tejedor de Benarés","Sheikh Farid, el sufí de Pakpattan","Balwand y Satta, los músicos de la corte"]}},{"id":"SIKHISM-s16-02","day":1412,"d":2,"q":"Sikh tradition credits which Guru with shaping the Gurmukhi script, in which the Guru Granth Sahib is written?","o":["Guru Arjan, the Fifth Guru","Guru Angad, the Second Guru","Guru Ram Das, the Fourth Guru","Guru Amar Das, the Third Guru"],"a":1,"es":{"q":"La tradición sij atribuye a ¿qué Gurú haber dado forma a la escritura gurmukhi, en la que está escrito el Guru Granth Sahib?","o":["Guru Arjan, el quinto Gurú","Guru Angad, el segundo Gurú","Guru Ram Das, el cuarto Gurú","Guru Amar Das, el tercer Gurú"]}},{"id":"SIKHISM-s16-03","day":1364,"d":3,"q":"In Sikh teaching, as in Guru Arjan's Sukhmani Sahib, what do the paired words nirgun and sargun say about the One?","o":["the soul is bound before and freed after the Name","the Guru's teaching is partly hidden, partly open","the One is past all qualities and in every form","two gods rule together, one far and one near"],"a":2,"es":{"q":"En la enseñanza sij, como en el Sukhmani Sahib de Guru Arjan, ¿qué dicen sobre el Uno las palabras pareadas nirgun y sargun?","o":["el alma está atada antes del Nombre y libre después","la enseñanza del Gurú es en parte oculta y en parte abierta","el Uno está más allá de toda cualidad y en toda forma","dos dioses reinan juntos, uno lejano y otro cercano"]}},{"id":"SIKHISM-s16-04","day":1375,"d":3,"q":"In Raag Nat, Guru Ram Das sings 'bani guru, guru hai bani'. What does that line say about the Guru?","o":["the hymns count only when a living Guru sings them","the hymns are a lesser copy of a Guru in a body","the hymns must be read aloud by a Guru's own family","the Word sung in the hymns is itself the Guru"],"a":3,"es":{"q":"En el Raag Nat, Guru Ram Das canta 'bani guru, guru hai bani'. ¿Qué dice ese verso sobre el Gurú?","o":["los himnos solo cuentan si los canta un Gurú vivo","los himnos son una copia menor de un Gurú en un cuerpo","los himnos debe leerlos en voz alta la familia del Gurú","la Palabra cantada en los himnos es en sí el Gurú"]}},{"id":"SIKHISM-s16-05","day":1391,"d":4,"q":"In a salok of Asa di Var, Guru Nanak gives each of the four ages (yugas) a chariot and a charioteer. What do the chariots and drivers stand for?","o":["the kings who ruled the land in each age","the virtues or vices that move people","the length of a human life in each age","the holy places people visited in each age"],"a":1,"es":{"q":"En un salok del Asa di Var, Guru Nanak da a cada una de las cuatro edades (yugas) un carro y un auriga. ¿Qué representan los carros y sus aurigas?","o":["los reyes que gobernaron la tierra en cada edad","las virtudes o los vicios que mueven a la gente","la duración de la vida humana en cada edad","los lugares santos que se visitaban en cada edad"]}},{"id":"SIKHISM-s16-06","day":1384,"d":4,"q":"A Sikh village is in a bitter land dispute with a neighbouring chief, and no talks have been tried yet. Which course fits the Tenth Guru's teaching in his Zafarnama?","o":["take up arms now, since the cause is just","refuse all force, even if every talk fails","try every peaceful means first, arms last","let the emperor's court settle it for them"],"a":2,"es":{"q":"Una aldea sij tiene una dura disputa de tierras con un jefe vecino, y aún no se ha intentado dialogar. ¿Qué camino concuerda con la enseñanza del décimo Gurú en su Zafarnama?","o":["tomar las armas ya, porque la causa es justa","rechazar toda fuerza, aunque falle todo diálogo","intentar antes toda vía pacífica; armas al final","dejar que el tribunal del emperador lo resuelva"]}}]]};
